            "promptText": "Component 00a-01: ProvenanceMark. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nIt comes first because every other component embeds its marks, and it gets a full light and dark set.\n\nARTBOARDS (8, exact names; the batch plan gives the order)\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark\nPlus 00a · Notes, created in batch 2.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark\n 6. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark\nThen stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2:\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark\n 3. 00a · Notes (create it with the \"Board\" entries from the setup message and the 01 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): The only way the product says how sure it is about a fact: three shapes, one meaning each, used everywhere.\nUSED IN (print): x-provenance-sheet, x-date-sheet, x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, f1-today-tab, f3-household-calendar, f3-household-notifications, f8-scale-strips, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-sheet, f8-og-compare-card, f8-seasonal-aha, f6-place-section-details, f10-extraction-confirm, f10-bill-provenance, f10-bill-trend, f10-mail-day-triage, f11-keeper-strip, f1-claim-receipt.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: each silhouette at L 56pt with callouts, then all sizes in a row)\n- OFFICIAL: a solid disc. The diameter equals the size.\n- UNCONFIRMED: a ring with the same outer diameter and a transparent centre. Stroke width: XS 12 → 1.5px, S 16 → 2px, M 24 → 3px, L 56 → 7px. Never thinner than 1.5px.\n- YOU ADDED: a solid disc with a tick KNOCKED OUT of it. The tick is a true cut-out that shows the surface behind, not a second colour painted on top. The tick spans the middle 56% of the diameter. Its stroke width equals the ring stroke for that size (XS 1.5, S 2, M 3, L 7), with round caps and joins. This drawing survives one-colour tinting.\n- Ink: text.secondary (4.83:1 on base) or darker in light mode; dark text.secondary in dark mode. Add a crossed-out swatch row labelled \"never border.* · never text.muted\" (border.default is 1.24:1, text.muted is 2.54:1).\n- Sizes, each with its use printed:\n  XS 12pt / 12dp / 12px: the smallest size at which the three shapes can still be told apart (strip cells, widget, tray previews).\n  S 16pt: list rows and captions.\n  M 24pt: the sheet legend.\n  L 56pt: the provenance sheet header.\n  OG 28px at 1200 wide: the share-card minimum.\n- Below 12pt, no mark is drawn. Show a row labelled \"10pt → no mark\" that prints the words instead: \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\".\n- Spacing: 8pt (spacing.2) between the mark and its text, shown with a dimension line.\n- LEGEND specimen (at M 24pt, stacked): [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\". Where a legend is written \"● Official · ○ … · ✓ …\", those characters stand for the drawn marks: always render the vector mark, never a font character.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy, light and dark)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83:1 on base · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96:1 on dark base, 5.71:1 on dark raised · stale: text.primary #111827 at 50% (the B7 50% figures) · dark stale: dark text.primary #E5E7EB at 50% (B7) · tinted widget: primary.700 #0369a1 on surface.base 5.93:1 (light) and primary.500 #0ea5e9 on dark surface.raised 5.28:1 (dark), never dimmed (at 50% they drop to 2.24:1 and 2.36:1) · never: primary.500 on surface.base 2.77:1, border.default 1.24:1, text.muted 2.54:1, text.secondary at 50% 1.98:1.\n01-anatomy · dark carries the three silhouettes, the size row, the legend and this table in dark tokens only. It has no text blocks.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 6 rows × 5 columns; each cell is a 358-wide row at S 16pt on surface.base unless a column rule says otherwise)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (dimmed + age words) → stale · inside tap target → in-target · tinted/accented widget rendering (silhouette only) → tinted-widget · greyscale → greyscale.\nRows (label → key), used in every column unless a column rule says otherwise:\n R1 official (filled) → official: \"Flood zone\" / \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\", caption \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n R2 unconfirmed (hollow) → unconfirmed: \"Pickup day\" / \"Thursday\", caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" (Place B).\n R3 you-added (filled + knocked-out tick) → you-added: \"Warranty ends\" / \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\", caption \"You added this\" (Home A).\n R4 read-from-your-photo → read-from-photo: a machine read before the user commits it, drawn with the UNCONFIRMED ring. Row \"Clark Public Utilities\" / \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". Under the uncertain value only (the due date), add the flag line \"We weren't sure — check this\" in caption 12/16 text.strong with a 12pt text.strong pencil glyph (not a circle). Beside the cell, draw a small arrow to a copy of the row after commit, where the mark becomes YOU ADDED, labelled \"on commit → you-added\".\n R5 stale → stale: the fact's own provenance shape (the official disc for air) in text.primary at 50% (3.39:1). Row \"Air quality\" / \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17), with the words \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\" in caption text.secondary.\n R6 reported → reported: shape unchanged (the unconfirmed ring for the Place B pickup row), plus a status line under the row, \"You reported this · checking\", in caption 12/16 text.secondary with no glyph.\nColumn rules:\n - default: as above.\n - stale: dim the mark to text.primary at 50% and replace the caption with that row's own stale caption. The dimming is never the only cue: the age words always appear. Per row:\n   R1: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   R2: dimmed ring, caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\".\n   R3: Does not apply — your own entry does not age.\n   R4: Does not apply — a pre-commit read is not refreshed.\n   R5: print \"same as stale variant\" (R5 is already stale) and draw the R5 row.\n   R6: dimmed ring, the R2 stale caption, and the \"You reported this · checking\" line under it.\n - in-target: draw the whole row at a 44pt minimum height (iOS), with the dashed target (B13) around the row and a \"not a target\" label on the mark. Add \"48dp on Android · 44px on web\".\n - tinted-widget: draw the row at XS 12pt inside a 158×158 widget crop rendered in one accent hue. Light cell: widget background surface.base, tint primary.700, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.93:1\" (never primary.500: 2.77:1). All silhouettes are one colour; the YOU ADDED tick stays a cut-out showing the widget background. Print the word next to every mark (a widget is a standalone surface).\n   R5 tinted-widget: no dimming under tinted rendering. Draw the full-strength tint (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and let the age words \"— 11 hours ago\" carry the stale state. Label it \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\".\n - greyscale: the default cell at 0% saturation, labelled \"shape carries the meaning\".\nDark twin: the same 30 cells in dark tokens. The tinted column uses widget background dark surface.raised with tint primary.500, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.28:1\". Its R5 cell follows the same no-dimming rule.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1, R2 and R3 stacked. The mark scales with Dynamic Type relative to the caption style, capped at 32pt. The row text wraps, and the mark top-aligns to the first line. The legend becomes one entry per line.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same three rows with sp scaling, mark capped at 32dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same, with the SVG sized in em.\n- XS legibility strip: the three marks at XS 12pt on surface.base, surface.sunken, dark surface.base and dark surface.raised, plus both tinted-widget backgrounds from the grid, labelled \"must be told apart at 12pt\".\n- GREYSCALE (this component overrides B10): do not redraw the grid. Print \"Greyscale: see the greyscale column on 02-variants-states — every cell reads yes — shape\". Draw one deliberate FAIL example labelled \"WRONG\": two discs that differ only in hue, with the fix label \"fix: shape, not colour\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: the three marks in text.strong, labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\".\nDark twin (03 · dark): the AX5 and 200% frames in dark tokens, the XS strip, and the three marks in dark text.strong labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\". It leaves out the web zoom frame and the greyscale pointer, because greyscale does not depend on theme.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Spoken names are fixed: \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\", \"you added this\". The name is appended to the row's merged label:\n  \"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, FEMA, official\"\n  \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\"\n  \"Warranty ends, water heater, in 54 days, Saturday 12 December, you added this\"\n- Non-colour encoding: the shape; colour never tells the marks apart.\n- Target rule: the mark is never a tap target on its own. The enclosing row or cell is the target (B13).\n- Contrast: at least 3:1 in both themes, including the tinted widget. Scales with Dynamic Type or sp up to AX5 / 200%.\n- Each surface shows a legend or a first-occurrence word once.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Legend strings, exactly: \"Official\" · \"On record, not confirmed\" · \"You added this\".\n- Print the word next to the mark once per surface. On standalone surfaces (widget, OG card, push landing), print it next to every mark.\n- In a push, the caveat goes at the front of the title: \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\".\n- Glossary: never \"verified\", \"confirmed\" or \"trusted\" for official data; never \"unverified\", \"estimated\", \"guessed\", \"pending\" or \"probable\" for the hollow mark; never \"user-entered\", \"self-reported\" or \"manual\" for the tick.\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- iOS widgets: the mark is widgetAccentable, and the tick stays knocked out under accented rendering.\n- Android widgets: fixed ink (text.secondary / dark text.secondary), not a Material dynamic colour role.\n- Web: inline SVG with role=\"img\" and an aria-label holding the spoken name.\n- OG card: at least 28px at 1200 wide.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three 390-wide crops; the dark twin has the same three crops)\n a) x-place-file, Place B. A legend strip at the top (\"Official · On record, not confirmed · You added this\" with drawn M-size marks), then these rows: \"Flood zone · Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" (official); \"Radon zone · Zone 1 — highest potential\" (official, caption \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"); \"Pickup day · Thursday\" (unconfirmed); \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" (no mark, because nothing is on record).\n b) f5-today-calendar-strip, Home A. At the top of the crop, above the strip, a legend line: [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\", with the marks at S 16pt, labelled \"legend once per surface\". Then a 14-cell FourteenDayStrip from Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov, with marks at XS 12pt in one ink colour. Draw every fixture date in the window:\n   Tue 20 Oct: unconfirmed ring (recycling and garbage, city schedule).\n   Fri 23 Oct: you-added mark (Clark Public Utilities bill).\n   Mon 26 Oct: voter registration, a statewide rule, drawn as a full-height bar spanning the cell with no mark. Label it \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\".\n   Tue 27 Oct: unconfirmed ring (garbage only).\n   Wed 28 Oct: you-added mark (City of Vancouver water bill).\n   Sun 1 Nov: you-added mark (HOA dues).\n   All other cells are empty. Beside the strip print \"at most 3 marks per cell, then +N\".\n  Under the strip, draw the matching rows at S 16pt, each with its mark:\n   \"Recycling and garbage\" / \"Tomorrow\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\" / \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" / \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (official)\n   \"Garbage only\" / \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00\" / \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"HOA dues · $285\" / \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" (you added)\n  Label: \"the strip is one element; rows are the targets\".\n c) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\". Marks at XS 12pt, each with its word printed beside it, for example \"On record, not confirmed\" next to \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Instead of filled vs hollow for any other meaning (sender vs you in compare, taken vs open founding slots, density), draw labelled pointers, or solid vs hatched segments plus a numeral — because filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage, bar or star, draw one of the three marks plus its word — because the product never grades certainty.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on an official public dataset (EPA radon zone, USFS wildfire hazard), draw the filled mark and put the limit in the caption's scope word (\"county-wide estimate\") — because hollow means \"not confirmed\", not \"coarse\".\n- Instead of a tick painted in a second colour on top of the disc, knock the tick out — because a second colour disappears under one-colour widget tinting.\n- Instead of a light tinted widget in primary.500, use primary.700 on surface.base — because primary.500 is 2.77:1 on white and marks need 3:1.\n- Instead of dimming a tinted widget mark for stale, keep the full tint and add the age words — because a dimmed tint drops below 3:1.\n- Instead of making an 8px dot the tap target, make the enclosing row or cell the target — because a small mark cannot be hit reliably.\n- Instead of a bare \"Unverified\" suffix on every row, show the word once per surface in a legend — because repetition is noise and \"unverified\" is forbidden.\n- Instead of text.secondary at 50% for stale, use text.primary at 50% — because the first drops to 1.98:1.\n- Instead of one age suffix on every row, give each fact its own stale caption — because an effective date or your own entry does not age.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: official · unconfirmed · you-added · read-from-photo · stale · reported. States: default · stale · in-target · tinted-widget · greyscale.\n<size|platform> is the size the cell is drawn at (XS, S, M, L, OG); tinted-widget cells are XS. Examples: \"ProvenanceMark / official / default / S / light\" · \"ProvenanceMark / you-added / tinted-widget / XS / dark\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"01 ProvenanceMark\")\n 01.A1 Stale ink is text.primary at 50% (3.39:1 on base), not a plain \"50% opacity\", because text.secondary at 50% is 1.98:1 and marks need 3:1.\n 01.A2 Stale captions are per row, not one shared suffix. The pickup schedule reads \"as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\". The official effective-date row, your own entry and a pre-commit photo read \"does not apply\", because they do not age.\n 01.A3 The tinted widget is never dimmed for stale. The full tint stays (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and the age words carry the state, because a 50% tint drops to 2.24:1 (light) and 2.36:1 (dark).\n 01.A4 Tinted-widget stand-in: primary.700 on surface.base in light (5.93:1) and primary.500 on dark surface.raised in dark (5.28:1). primary.500 on white is 2.77:1, so it is not used in light mode.\n 01.A5 The ring and tick stroke widths per size (1.5 / 2 / 3 / 7) and the 56% tick span are this board's geometry. The source spec sets only the 1.5px minimum.\n 01.A6 The spoken example \"Trash day Tuesday, City of Camas, …\" became \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\", following the glossary (\"Pickup day\") and the Place B fixture.\n 01.A7 In the calendar-strip crop, Mon 26 Oct voter registration is FourteenDayStrip's full-height civic bar (a civic, state or county rule is a full-height bar spanning the cell), not a mark. Its row uses the \"must arrive by\" wording.\n 01.A8 The calendar-strip crop prints the legend once above the strip, so that surface shows each mark's word once (invariant 1).\n 01.B1 \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" · \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\" · \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" · \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\" · \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\".\n 01.B2 The six calendar-strip rows under crop b, each quoted exactly as written there.\n 01.B3 Annotations: \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\" · \"legend once per surface\" · \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\" · \"on commit → you-added\".\n 01.B4 The flood-zone and warranty spoken labels from ACCESSIBILITY.\n 01.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 01.E Every ProvenanceMark name, by the grammar and keys above.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 8 artboards and 00a · Notes (Board and 01 entries) exist with exact names.\n- Both 02 grids have 6 × 5 cells with printed keys; \"Does not apply\" cells print their reasons; the stale column uses each row's own caption; both R5 tinted cells are at full tint.\n- No mark is under 12pt, no ring stroke under 1.5px, and the tick is a cut-out everywhere, including both tinted cells (each printing its background, tint and ratio).\n- Crops a and b print the legend once; the widget crop prints the word beside every mark.\n- The strip is named \"FourteenDayStrip\" and nothing else. No mark is a target on its own."
