            "promptText": "Component 00a-02: SourceCaption. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nSourceCaption embeds the ProvenanceMark you drew in 00a-01. Reuse those marks exactly.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light: the caption pattern with callouts, base vs sunken ink, the wrap example, link vs no-link, the OG strip, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light: the 6 × 3 grid plus the dated-static-link twin\n3. 00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light: f8-scale-strips, f1-today-air-band (default and alert, no track), f8-compare-arrival-header frozen row\n4. 00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark: the same cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 02 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): Puts the minimum provenance on the value itself: who says it, what it covers, and when.\nPrint this rationale under the purpose: \"Almost nobody opens the provenance sheet, so the caption carries the caveat.\"\nUSED IN (print): f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f1-today-air-band, f8-seasonal-aha, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-og-compare-card, f8-compare-sheet, x-provenance-sheet, x-place-file, f4-today-pickup-card, f5-today-calendar-strip, f3-household-calendar, f10-bill-trend.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on a 358-wide specimen, \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\", with the external-link glyph)\n- ① ProvenanceMark at S 16pt, leading, top-aligned to the first line, with an 8pt gap.\n- ② Authority, ③ \" · \" separator, ④ scope word, ⑤ \" · \", ⑥ as-of. All in caption 12/16/400.\n- Ink: text.secondary on base, raised or app surfaces; text.strong on sunken (text.secondary on sunken is 4.39:1). Draw two copies side by side, one on base and one on sunken, each labelled with its token and ratio.\n- The caption wraps to two lines at default size and never cuts the authority short with an ellipsis. Draw a 240-wide wrap example: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\n- ⑦ Optional trailing external-link glyph (12pt, an arrow out of a square, not a circle), shown only when a source URL exists. When a URL exists, the authority word is primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)) with an underline, and the caption line's hit area is a target (B13). When no URL exists, everything is text.secondary, with no underline, no glyph and no target.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83 base / 4.63 raised / 4.51 app · text.strong #374151 9.37 on sunken · primary.700 #0369a1 5.93 on base · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 8.33 on dark base · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96 on dark base.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 6 rows × 3 columns; each cell shows the value line in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary above the caption)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (the as-of age appended) → stale · offline (\"as of\" date) → offline.\n R1 dated static → dated-static. Value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n   default: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n   stale: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   offline: unchanged. Draw the default caption and label it \"static captions do not change offline\".\n R2 live → live. Value \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17).\n   default: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today\".\n   stale: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\".\n   offline: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\".\n R3 frozen token (a compare card's saved reading) → frozen. Value \"AQI 42 · Good\".\n   default: \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n   stale: Does not apply — a frozen reading is dated, never \"ago\".\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\n R4 county scope → county. Value \"Zone 1 — highest potential\".\n   default: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\n   stale: Does not apply — a county zone does not age.\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\n R5 collapsed sources line, only at 320–360 wide → collapsed. Draw it in a 320-wide cell under four value rows (Flood, Wildfire, Air, Radon).\n   default: \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\". The air row keeps its own time on its row: \"observed 7:00 AM today\".\n   stale: the sources line is unchanged; only the air row appends \"— 11 hours ago\".\n   offline: the sources line is unchanged; the air row reads \"as of 7:00 AM\".\n R6 no URL: a flat caption, not tappable → no-url. Value \"Thursday\" (Place B pickup day).\n   default: \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\", with no glyph and no underline, labelled \"not a target\".\n   stale: Does not apply — the schedule is dated by its as-of, which is already shown.\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\nNext to R1, also draw a \"with URL\" twin (label \"dated static, with URL\", key: dated-static-link), default state only, showing the underlined authority and trailing glyph, so the difference between R1 and R6 is visible.\nDark twin: all 18 cells and the twin in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R2 and R4 at caption 40pt with the mark at 32pt, wrapping to as many lines as needed and never ending in an ellipsis.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same at 24sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): every cell. The link still reads by its underline and glyph: \"yes — underline + glyph\". Other cells: \"yes — words; the mark's shape\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R2 default with the caption in text.strong; the link stays primary.700 with its underline.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Contrast is at least 4.5:1 (see the table).\n- The caption is read after the value in the row's merged label: \"Air quality, AQI 42, Good, AirNow, nearest monitors, observed 7:00 AM today, official\".\n- The non-colour cue for a link is the underline plus the external-link glyph.\n- Target rule: a caption is a target (B13) only when a URL exists. A caption with no URL is never a target.\n- There is no hover-only content.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Always authority · scope · as-of.\n- Use the authority's own word, \"hazard\" or \"potential\"; never \"risk\" unless the source says risk.\n- Deadlines received by a date say \"must arrive by\" (\"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\").\n- Never write \"Sources:\" at widths above 360.\n- Never write \"provider\", \"feed\" or \"partner\" for the source.\n- Never label a frozen reading \"today\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Same on iOS, Android and web.\n- On the OG image, the caption is at least 28px and may be merged into one sources line; the full captions go in og:description. Draw a 1200-wide strip crop showing \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" at 28px.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three 390-wide crops)\n a) f8-scale-strips, Place B: the flood row \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" with the R1 caption under the strip.\n b) f1-today-air-band, Place B: \"AQI 42 · Good\" with the R2 caption. Beside it, an alert-variant copy: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" with \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM today\". Both show the value line and caption only; label them \"track omitted: AqiBand\" (B17).\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, Friend C: a \"Dana · Camas, WA\" card with the row \"Air on Sat 12 Sep\" and the R3 caption \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of hiding the source behind a tooltip or \"learn more\", print authority · scope · as-of on the value — because almost nobody opens the sheet.\n- Instead of labelling a frozen reading \"today\", write \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" — because a shared card is read days later.\n- Instead of making a caption with no URL tappable, draw it flat — because a target that goes nowhere breaks trust.\n- Instead of \"Sources:\" on wide layouts, give every row its own caption — because the collapsed line exists only for 320–360 widths.\n- Instead of cutting a long authority short with an ellipsis, wrap to a second line — because the authority is the caveat.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: dated-static · dated-static-link · live · frozen · county · collapsed · no-url. States: default · stale · offline. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"SourceCaption / live / stale / any / light\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"02 SourceCaption\")\n 02.A1 Source example strings were re-dated to the house-style fixtures (TODAY Mon 19 Oct 2026) and the weekday date format: \"effective Sep 24, 2021\" → \"effective Sep 2021\"; \"observed 3:10 PM today\" → \"observed 7:00 AM today\"; \"on Sep 12, 2026\" → \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\"; \"— 9 hours ago\" → \"— 11 hours ago\"; \"as of Sep 15\" → \"as of 7:00 AM\".\n 02.A2 SourceCaption adds a dated-static-link key for the with-URL twin, so the link form can be published separately from the no-URL form.\n 02.B1 \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\" · \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM today\" · \"track omitted: AqiBand\" · \"static captions do not change offline\". \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" is already listed under 01.\n 02.B2 Spoken label: \"Air quality, AQI 42, Good, AirNow, nearest monitors, observed 7:00 AM today, official\".\n 02.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 02.E Every SourceCaption name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 02 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have 6 rows × 3 columns plus the dated-static-link twin, with printed keys, and every \"Does not apply\" cell prints its reason.\n- No caption without a URL shows an underline, glyph or target; every caption with a URL shows all three.\n- Text on sunken is text.strong. No authority is cut short with an ellipsis. \"Sources:\" appears only in the 320-wide cell and on the OG strip.\n- No frozen reading says \"today\", and no air crop draws a track or an EPA hue."
