            "promptText": "Component 00a-03: ScopeChip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · ScopeChip · 01-anatomy · light: the pill with callouts, the glyphs, target vs label-only, the footer sentence, the retired wording, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · light: the 5 × 4 grid\n3. 00a · ScopeChip · 04-in-context · light: the f1-today-tab location row, the x-date-sheet footer above Save, the f1-claim-receipt pairs and consent\n4. 00a · ScopeChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · dark: the same 20 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · ScopeChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · ScopeChip · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · ScopeChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 03 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): States who can see this address data, only you or your household, on every surface that shows address data.\nUSED IN (print): f1-today-tab, f1-today-air-band, f1-your-places, f1-add-place-sheet, f1-save-confirmation, f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-claim-receipt, x-date-sheet, x-place-file, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-widget-tap-landing, f9-privacy-mirror, f11-keeper-naming, f11-keeper-strip, f3-household-notifications, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-snap-capture-tray, f10-mail-snap-privacy, f10-mail-piece-photo.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on \"Saved place · Only you\" and \"Your household\")\n- ① Pill, radius pill, height 24pt / 24dp / 24px.\n- ② Horizontal padding 8 (spacing.2) and a 4 (spacing.1) gap between glyph and label.\n- ③ A 12pt glyph: a person means Only you; a house means household. It is a line glyph with a 1.5px stroke in text.strong. The house glyph could use identity.home only if it reached 3:1, but identity.home on surface.sunken is 2.99:1, so draw it in text.strong and print \"identity.home fails 3:1 on sunken (2.99) → text.strong\".\n- ④ Label in label 13/18/600, text.strong (9.37:1 on sunken). The \" · \" separator is a typographic middle dot with a space on each side.\n- ⑤ Fill surface.sunken, with no border (dark: the sunken-fill rule in B6).\n- ⑥ Hit area: a target (B13) only when the chip opens the control that changes scope. Draw a \"label only, no target\" copy and an \"opens scope control\" copy with the dashed target and a trailing 12pt chevron in text.strong.\n- Footer sentence form (used in sheets): a 16pt glyph and a sentence in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary on base, with no pill.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37 · identity.home #16A34A on sunken 2.99 (not used) · text.secondary #6B7280 on base 4.83 · dark text.strong #F1F5F9 on dark raised 13.35.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 5 rows × 4 columns)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · pending share (dashed house glyph) → pending · declined share (person → person) → declined · struck (old scope on the claim receipt) → struck.\n R1 saved place → saved-place: \"Saved place · Only you\" with the person glyph.\n   default: as specified.\n   pending and declined: Does not apply — pending and declined exist only in the scope-change pair (R4).\n   struck: the chip with a 1px text.strong strike line through the label, then a 4pt gap, a 12pt arrow glyph, another 4pt gap and a \"Your household\" chip, captioned \"old scope on the claim receipt\". The strike is never the only cue: the new chip is always beside it.\n R2 claimed home → claimed-home: \"Your household\" with the house glyph.\n   default: as specified.\n   pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — a claimed home's chip has no pending share or older scope of its own.\n R3 named home (multi-home contexts) → named-home: \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" with the house glyph.\n   default: as specified.\n   pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — same reason as R2.\n R4 scope-change pair (claim receipt, trailing edge of a carried row) → scope-change-pair: glyphs only, a 12pt person glyph → 12pt arrow → 12pt house glyph, in text.strong. Show it on the row \"Warranty ends · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\".\n   default: person → house, both in solid lines (shared).\n   pending: person → house, with the house drawn in a DASHED 1.5px stroke (2px dash, 2px gap), shown until the user chooses. Under the row, the consent question \"Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?\" and two equal-weight buttons, \"Share with the household\" and \"Keep them private to me\" (the glossary tension is flagged on Notes).\n   declined: person → person, both solid.\n   struck: Does not apply — the pair itself shows the change.\n R5 footer sentence form (sheets) → footer-sentence:\n   default: two copies, the person glyph with \"Only you will see this.\" and the house glyph with \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n   pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — the sentence describes the current scope only.\nDark twin: all 20 cells in dark tokens, using the sunken-fill rule from B6.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 and R3 at label 44pt. The chip wraps to two lines and becomes a rounded rectangle (radius lg 12), with the glyph scaled to 24pt and top-aligned. The height grows to fit. Nothing is truncated.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same at 26sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): every cell reads \"yes — glyph + words\". The dashed house still reads as dashed: \"yes — dashed stroke + consent words\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: the chip is unchanged (it is already text.strong); the R5 footer sentence becomes text.strong.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Spoken: \"Visible to only you\" (R1); \"Visible to your household\" (R2 and R3; R3 is prefixed with \"Larkspur Loop,\"). Pair, default: \"Visible to your household\". Pair, pending: \"Visible to only you; will be visible to your household if you share\". Pair, declined: \"Visible to only you\".\n- Never colour-only: the glyph plus the words.\n- Target rule: a target (B13) only when it opens the scope control; otherwise it is not a target.\n- It wraps at AX sizes.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Exactly these chip strings: \"Saved place · Only you\" and \"Your household\" (with an optional leading home label, as in \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\").\n- Exactly these sentences: \"Only you will see this.\" and \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n- Draw a crossed-out \"Retired wording\" list: \"Only you see this\" · \"Only you can see these\" · \"private to your home\" · \"Saved place - Only you\" (a hyphen instead of a middle dot).\n- A saved place never uses the words home, household or claim.\n- Where finance permissions differ, name the people instead: \"You and Sam can see these photos\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Identical on iOS, Android and web.\n- On push landings, it sits next to the address in the location row.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three 390-wide crops)\n a) f1-today-tab, Place B: the location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with \"Saved place · Only you\" beside it (wrapping under it if the row is too narrow), and the FreshnessLine words \"Updated 12m ago\" below it.\n b) x-date-sheet, Home A: the sheet title \"Add a date\" at the top of the crop, then (with the sheet body cropped out between) the footer sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" directly above the sheet's primary button \"Save\".\n c) f1-claim-receipt, Home A: the header with the struck \"Saved place · Only you\" → \"Your household\", then two carried rows with pending pairs and the consent block from R4.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of a green \"verified-looking\" chip to mean membership, draw the neutral sunken chip with the house glyph — because green reads as verification, which is a different thing.\n- Instead of dropping the chip from an alert landing, keep it next to the address — because an alert is when people most need to know who else sees it.\n- Instead of \"Everyone in this household\" where finance permissions differ, name the people (\"You and Sam can see these photos\") — because the sentence would be false.\n- Instead of an identity.home fill, use surface.sunken with text.strong — because the colour is not the message and fails contrast on sunken.\n- Instead of any new wording, use the two chip strings and two sentences — because five earlier wordings drifted.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: saved-place · claimed-home · named-home · scope-change-pair · footer-sentence. States: default · pending · declined · struck. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"ScopeChip / scope-change-pair / pending / any / light\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"03 ScopeChip\")\n 03.A1 The house glyph is text.strong, because identity.home is 2.99:1 on surface.sunken.\n 03.A2 Footer sentence type is bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary with a 16pt glyph; the source spec sets no type style.\n 03.A3 The named-home example \"Maple St · Your household\" became \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" (the Home A fixture label).\n 03.A4 Glossary tension: the sourced consent button \"Keep them private to me\" is close to the glossary's forbidden \"private to you\" and the retired \"private to your home\". Proposed alternative: \"Just me\" (the house style's neutral decline).\n 03.B1 \"Warranty ends · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"old scope on the claim receipt\" · \"label only, no target\" · \"opens scope control\".\n 03.B2 Spoken labels: \"Visible to only you; will be visible to your household if you share\".\n 03.B3 Sourced, not invented: \"Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?\", \"Share with the household\" and \"Keep them private to me\" (f1-claim-receipt research); \"Add a date\" and \"Save\" (the DateSheet title and primary button).\n 03.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 03.D Keep \"Keep them private to me\", or use \"Just me\"? (03.A4)\n 03.E Every ScopeChip name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 03 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have 5 rows × 4 columns with printed keys, and every \"Does not apply\" cell prints its reason.\n- Only the two chip strings and the two sentences appear as scope wording; the retired list is crossed out.\n- No chip uses a green or identity.home fill; the house glyph is text.strong.\n- A strike never appears without the new chip beside it, and the pending pair is dashed with its consent block.\n- The x-date-sheet crop's primary button reads \"Save\"; \"Add a date\" is the sheet title.\n- Dark chips on dark base use dark surface.raised (B6)."
