            "promptText": "Component 00a-05: OfflineNotice. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nOfflineNotice embeds the FreshnessLine you drew in 00a-04. Reuse its offline line exactly.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light: the offline line, a disabled control with its reason, plain vs sunken, the focusable disabled control, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light: the 3 × 3 grid\n3. 00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light: f8-native-share-compare, f1-add-place-sheet, f10-snap-capture-tray\n4. 00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark: the same 9 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 05 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One pattern for no connection: cached content stays readable, and actions are disabled with a stated reason.\nUSED IN (print exactly this sentence; do not list ids): every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on a 390-wide Today crop for Place B)\n- ① FreshnessLine in its offline variant at the top: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", with the offline glyph.\n- ② Cached content at full ink, not dimmed: the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17).\n- ③ A disabled control, the secondary button \"Compare with a friend\", 44pt tall: its label in text.muted on surface.sunken (disabled is the one allowed use of text.muted).\n- ④ A reason caption directly under that control, 4pt below: \"Compare needs a connection.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary (4.83:1).\n- ⑤ Background: no banner colour. Either plain (on base or app) or a surface.sunken strip with text.strong. Draw both and label them \"plain\" and \"sunken strip\".\n- ⑥ The disabled control keeps a focus ring when focused (B14), which shows that it stays focusable.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83 on base · text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37 · text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled label only) · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96 on dark base.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 3 rows × 3 columns; each cell is a 390-wide crop; all 9 cells apply)\nColumns (label → key): offline → offline · reconnecting → reconnecting · back online (the line reverts to FreshnessLine) → back-online.\n R1 read-only cached screen → cached-screen: f1-today-tab, Place B, with the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17) and the \"Compare with a friend\" button.\n   offline: as in the anatomy.\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the button is still disabled with its reason.\n   back-online: two sub-cells. First the line reads \"Updating…\", then \"Updated just now\". The button is enabled and the reason caption is gone.\n R2 queued writes → queued-writes: f10-snap-capture-tray, Home A, with three mail-snap thumbnails.\n   offline: the line \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", and under it \"You're offline. You can keep taking photos.\"; each thumbnail has the caption \"Will upload when you're back online\".\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the thumbnails keep their captions.\n   back-online: the live status line \"Uploading 1 of 3\". The thumbnail captions disappear one by one; draw the moment after the first upload.\n R3 form offline → form: f1-add-place-sheet, signed in. A disabled address field with the message \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.strong on a surface.sunken strip above the field. The sheet keeps a visible \"Close\".\n   offline: as described.\n   reconnecting: the same message, with \"Reconnecting\" as a caption under it.\n   back-online: the field is enabled and the message is gone. No FreshnessLine appears, because a form has no content age; print that note on the cell.\nDark twin: all 9 cells in dark tokens (disabled label in dark text.muted, 3.75:1; sunken strips follow B6).\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 offline. The line wraps, the button goes full width, and the reason caption wraps under it at 40pt.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same, with the button at 48dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): every cell reads \"yes — words; disabled is stated, not only greyed\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 offline with the reason caption in text.strong. The disabled label stays text.muted, because the reason caption carries the meaning (B11).\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Disabled controls stay focusable and read their reason:\n  iOS: \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Android: \"Compare with a friend, disabled, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Web: aria-disabled=\"true\" (not the disabled attribute), with aria-describedby pointing at the reason caption.\n- Status changes are announced politely.\n- Target rule: the disabled control keeps its target size (B13).\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Start with \"You're offline.\" and then say what still works.\n- Exact strings: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Compare needs a connection.\" · \"Will upload when you're back online\" · \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\"\n- Never \"No internet\", \"Connection lost\" or \"Network error\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy): the same on iOS, Android and web.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops)\n a) f8-native-share-compare, iOS 393: \"Compare with a friend\" disabled, with \"Compare needs a connection.\" under it and the offline line at the top.\n b) f1-add-place-sheet, Android 412: R3 offline, with the sheet's visible \"Close\".\n c) f10-snap-capture-tray, Home A, iOS 393: R2 offline.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of a full-page offline illustration, keep the cached screen readable with the offline line on top — because people still need what they already had.\n- Instead of silent dead buttons, disable the control and put the reason under it — because a button that does nothing looks broken.\n- Instead of a red or amber banner, use plain or surface.sunken with text.strong — because being offline is a condition, not an error.\n- Instead of blanking stale data, keep it with \"as of 7:04 AM\" — because a blank throws away true information.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: cached-screen · queued-writes · form. States: offline · reconnecting · back-online. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"OfflineNotice / form / reconnecting / any / dark\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"05 OfflineNotice\")\n 05.A1 The form variant shows no FreshnessLine when back online, because a form has no content age.\n 05.A2 The used-in line is the sentence \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\", not a list of ids.\n 05.B1 \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Reconnecting\" · \"You're offline. You can keep taking photos.\" · \"plain\" · \"sunken strip\".\n 05.B2 Spoken labels: \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\" · \"Compare with a friend, disabled, Compare needs a connection.\"\n 05.B3 Sourced, not invented: \"Uploading 1 of 3\" (the live-status pattern from the research brief, section 5).\n 05.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 05.E Every OfflineNotice name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 05 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have all 9 cells with printed keys, and R1 back-online shows both sub-cells.\n- Cached content is never dimmed or blanked; no frame uses a red, amber or other semantic banner.\n- Every disabled control has its reason caption under it, stays focusable (a focus ring is drawn once), and keeps its 44pt / 48dp / 44px target.\n- text.muted appears only on disabled labels; text on sunken strips is text.strong.\n- The used-in line reads exactly \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\"."
