            "promptText": "Component 00a-07: KindGlyph. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · KindGlyph · 01-anatomy · light: the grid, stroke, tile, label and 2-column target cell, the 17-glyph set with keys, the TILE → GLYPH map, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · light: Part A (17 glyphs × row, tile, widget, tray), Part B (4 × 5 states), and the 10-tile 2-column picker\n3. 00a · KindGlyph · 04-in-context · light: the x-date-sheet picker, f4-today-pickup-card (42pt tile), f7-today-widget\n4. 00a · KindGlyph · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: the AX5 one-column list (trailing check), the Android 200% list (Material 3 radios), web zoom, the greyscale subset, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · dark: Parts A and B and the picker in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · KindGlyph · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · KindGlyph · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · KindGlyph · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 07 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One drawn glyph per dated kind, used in tiles, rows, the pickup card and the widget.\nUSED IN (print): x-date-sheet, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f10-extraction-confirm, f3-household-calendar, x-place-file.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on \"Recycling\" at 24pt, which shows glyph 2, and on the \"Pickup day\" tile at 42pt, which shows glyph 3, garbage+recycling)\n- ① A line icon on a 24pt / 24dp / 24px grid, 2pt stroke, round caps and joins, in text.strong. Use the Pantopus design system's icon style; if the set lacks a glyph, draw it in that style.\n- ② Tile variant: a 42pt rounded square, radius lg 12, fill surface.sunken, with the 24pt glyph centred.\n- ③ The tile label, 8pt below the tile, in label 13/18/600 text.strong. It is centred and wraps to two lines.\n- ④ The whole tile-plus-label cell is the target (B13). The kind picker is a 2-column grid inside the date sheet, with 8pt gaps between cells, so each cell is half the sheet's content width minus half a gap: 176 wide on iOS 393 (16pt side margins), 186 wide on Android 412, and 175 wide on web 390. Every cell is 88 tall. Draw the dimension lines for the iOS cell.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.strong #374151 on base 10.31 and on sunken 9.37 · text.primary #111827 (selected label) · text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled only) · primary.700 #0369a1 on primary.50 5.57 · dark text.strong #F1F5F9 13.35 on dark raised · dark text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 #0c4a6e 7.64 · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (radio and check only).\n\nTHE SET (on 01-anatomy: draw all 17 in this order, each labelled with its kind name and \"key: <key>\")\n 1 garbage (key garbage): a lidded wheeled cart\n 2 recycling (key recycling): a cart with three chasing arrows on its body\n 3 garbage+recycling (key garbage-recycling): two carts overlapping\n 4 bulk (key bulk): an armchair\n 5 move-in (key move-in): an open box with an arrow entering it\n 6 lease ends (key lease-ends): a key over a door outline\n 7 notice deadline (key notice-deadline): an envelope with a small flag\n 8 insurance renews (key insurance-renews): a shield with a circular arrow drawn as an open arc\n 9 warranty ends (key warranty-ends): a tag with a wrench\n 10 HOA dues (key hoa-dues): three adjoining rooftops\n 11 property-tax appeal (key property-tax-appeal): a document with an upward arrow\n 12 property-tax due (key property-tax-due): a document with a dollar sign\n 13 voter registration (key voter-registration): a ballot entering a slotted box\n 14 bill (key bill): a receipt with a zigzag bottom edge\n 15 home event (key home-event): a house outline with a small calendar page\n 16 task (key task): a rounded-square checkbox with a check stroke\n 17 package (key package): a parcel with tape\nProperty tax is one kind with two uses, appeal and due; draw it as two glyphs sharing the document base. Cart wheels are round sub-parts of a larger glyph, which B8 allows.\n\nTILE → GLYPH MAP (print this table on 01-anatomy)\n Pickup day → 3 garbage+recycling\n Move-in date → 5 move-in\n Lease ends → 6 lease ends\n Notice deadline → 7 notice deadline\n Insurance renews → 8 insurance renews\n Warranty ends → 9 warranty ends\n HOA dues → 10 HOA dues\n Property-tax appeal → 11 property-tax appeal\n Voter registration → 13 voter registration\n Bill → 14 bill\n No tile (used in rows, the pickup card, the widget and the tray only):\n  Pickup rows and the pickup card choose by which bins go out: \"Garbage only\" → 1 garbage; \"Recycling and garbage\" → 3 garbage+recycling; a recycling-only pickup (a city that collects recycling on its own day, which is not the case at Home A or Place B) → 2 recycling.\n  Also without a tile: 4 bulk, 12 property-tax due, 15 home event, 16 task and 17 package.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states)\nPart A, variants: 17 glyph rows × 4 variant columns, all in the default state. Column keys: row · tile · widget · tray.\n - row 24pt (key row): the glyph with a visible kind label in bodySmall to its right.\n - tile 42pt (key tile): tile plus label. Glyphs with no tile get \"Does not apply — no picker tile; see the map\".\n - widget 16pt (key widget): the glyph at 16pt with a 1.5pt stroke, with its word beside it in caption.\n - tray, monochrome (key tray): 16pt, one ink, drawn on the dark mail-snap tray (dark surface.raised) in dark text.primary. Label it \"tray: monochrome, one ink\".\nPart B, states, drawn for the \"Pickup day\" kind (glyph 3): 4 rows (row · tile · widget · tray) × 5 columns. Columns (label → key): default → default · selected tile → selected · disabled → disabled · focused, not selected → focus · selected + focused → selected-focus. Every row has all five columns, and every \"does not apply\" cell carries its reason.\n - tile row:\n   default: as specified. No indicator is drawn on an unselected tile.\n   selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900). The label keeps label 13/18/600 and its ink changes from text.strong to text.primary (dark: dark text.primary). In the tile's top-right corner, a 16pt radio indicator in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)): a 1.5px ring with an 8pt filled centre (a flagged B8 exception, recorded on Notes). Print \"selected = fill + radio dot + label ink\".\n   disabled: glyph and label in text.muted, fill surface.muted, with the reason caption \"Already on file\" under the label in caption text.secondary.\n   focus: the B14 focus ring only, with no fill and no dot.\n   selected-focus: the selected tile plus the B14 focus ring.\n - row 24pt:\n   default: as specified.\n   selected: Does not apply — rows are not selectable.\n   disabled: glyph and label in text.muted, with the reason \"Already on file\" as a caption in text.secondary.\n   focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the glyph is decorative; its DateRow owns focus.\n - widget 16pt: default as specified. selected, disabled, focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the widget is read-only.\n - tray (monochrome): default as specified. selected, disabled, focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the tray is read-only.\nThen draw all 10 tile labels in the default state as one 2-column kind-picker grid, in the order of the map.\nDark twin: Parts A and B and the picker in dark tokens (tile fill follows the sunken-fill rule in B6).\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): the kind picker drops from two columns to one. Each tile becomes a full-width list row: the 42pt tile on the leading edge and the label at 44pt wrapping to its right. Draw \"Warranty ends\" selected and the rest unselected. The selected row gets the primary.50 fill, the text.primary label and a trailing 24pt check stroke in primary.700. Unselected rows show no indicator at all (native iOS list selection). No ring is drawn on iOS. The row glyph scales to 48pt at most.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same one-column list at 26sp, with Material 3 radio buttons on the trailing edge, because they are the Android platform control. The selected row shows a 2px primary.700 ring with a 12pt filled centre; unselected rows show an empty 2px ring in text.secondary (both are flagged B8 exceptions, recorded on Notes).\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the one-column list in the iOS form (trailing check on the selected row, nothing on the others), built as role=\"radio\" rows.\n- GREYSCALE (this component narrows B10 to a subset): the 17 row-variant glyphs and all of Part B. Verdict: \"yes — shape + label\". Selected reads by the radio dot (tile) or the check (iOS and web rows) plus the fill and label ink, not by fill hue alone.\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: print \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — glyphs and labels are already text.strong; on Android, the unselected radio ring becomes text.strong\", and draw that Android ring.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Decorative (hidden) when a text label is adjacent.\n- Otherwise labelled with the kind name (for example \"Recycling\").\n- Always paired with visible text; the widget and tray glyphs carry their word.\n- Each tile is one element: \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\" (iOS: a button with the selected trait; Android: RadioButton semantics; web: role=\"radio\" inside role=\"radiogroup\").\n- Non-colour: shape plus label; selection is the dot or check plus the fill and ink change.\n- Target rule: the tile cell or row, never the glyph alone, is the target (B13).\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Tile labels, exactly: Pickup day · Move-in date · Lease ends · Notice deadline · Insurance renews · Warranty ends · HOA dues · Property-tax appeal · Voter registration · Bill.\n- Glossary: \"Pickup day\", never \"trash day\", \"garbage day\" or \"bin day\"; \"Date\", never \"event\" or \"deadline item\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Draw the same glyph on all three platforms. The widget glyph follows the same silhouette-safe drawing as ProvenanceMark: one ink, any inner detail cut out, so it survives one-colour accented rendering.\n- The one-column large-text list differs by platform: a trailing check on iOS and web, Material 3 radio buttons on Android.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops)\n a) x-date-sheet, iOS 393, Home A: the sheet title \"Add a date\", the 10-tile kind picker in 2 columns with \"Warranty ends\" selected, the sheet's visible \"Close\", and its primary button \"Save\".\n b) f4-today-pickup-card, Home A, Android 412: the pickup card on surface.base, radius lg. Top to bottom: the 42pt tile with glyph 3 (garbage+recycling); the h3 headline \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\"; the instruction \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\"; a SourceCaption with the unconfirmed mark reading \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct\", with the words \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" printed once beside the mark; then two outlined peer buttons of identical weight, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n c) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\": 16pt glyphs, each with its words: glyph 3 with \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\", bill with \"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", and HOA dues with \"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of hue-coded glyphs as the only class cue, give each kind its own silhouette plus a label — because hue alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind users.\n- Instead of an unlabelled glyph, always show the kind name beside it — because the glyphs are not universal.\n- Instead of guessing a tile's glyph, use the TILE → GLYPH map — because every later picker copies this one.\n- Instead of showing selection with the focus ring, use fill + radio dot + label ink — because selection must look different from focus.\n- Instead of an empty-ring radio on iOS or web large-text rows, use a trailing check on the selected row and nothing on the others — because iOS has no radio control and an empty ring is the unconfirmed mark's shape.\n- Instead of emoji or a second icon set, use the Pantopus icon style — because the house style forbids a new icon set.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\n<variant> is the kind key (the 17 keys above). <state> is default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus (Part A cells are default). <size|platform> is the variant key: row · tile · widget · tray. Examples: \"KindGlyph / garbage-recycling / selected / tile / light\" · \"KindGlyph / bill / default / widget / dark\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"07 KindGlyph\")\n 07.A1 Radio indicators vs invariant 1 (\"filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else\"). Two flagged exceptions: (a) the selected tile's corner indicator, a ring with a filled centre (unselected tiles show nothing), which the source spec asks for as a \"filled radio dot\"; (b) Android Material 3 radio buttons in the 200% one-column list, where they are the platform control and the unselected option is an empty ring, the same silhouette as the UNCONFIRMED mark. iOS (AX5) and web (200% zoom) lists use a trailing check on the selected row and nothing on the others, because iOS has no native radio control.\n 07.A2 The selected tile label keeps weight 600 (label 13/18/600, the type scale) and changes ink from text.strong to text.primary. The source spec asks for a \"bold label\"; this board shows selection with the fill, the corner dot and the ink change instead of an off-scale 700 weight. Alternative if rejected: record weight 700 as a type-scale deviation.\n 07.A3 Part B has five state columns for every variant (default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus). The source spec lists default · selected tile · disabled; focus is added to show that selection differs from focus.\n 07.A4 The widget glyph stroke is 1.5pt at 16pt, and the widget glyph uses ProvenanceMark's silhouette-safe accented rendering. The source spec has no platform notes for KindGlyph.\n 07.A5 \"property-tax (appeal / due)\" is drawn as two glyphs sharing a document base.\n 07.A6 Glyph 2 (recycling) has no tile. It is used for a recycling-only pickup row and in the anatomy specimen. Neither Home A nor Place B has a recycling-only day.\n 07.A7 The kind picker is 2 columns (from the DateSheet anatomy), with the TILE → GLYPH map on 01-anatomy. \"Pickup day\" uses glyph 3, garbage+recycling.\n 07.A8 The f4-today-pickup-card crop follows the PickupCard anatomy (42pt tile, the words \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" once), with the Home A instruction adapted to the fixture's \"carts out by 6:30 AM\". Its headline names tomorrow's pickup, so it shows the weekday date alone.\n 07.B1 \"Already on file\" · \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\" (source pattern with the fixture time) · \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\" · the widget rows (\"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\") · \"tray: monochrome, one ink\" · \"selected = fill + radio dot + label ink\" · the glyph descriptions and keys for the 17 kinds.\n 07.B2 Spoken label: \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\".\n 07.B3 Sourced, not invented: \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\", \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\" (PickupCard); \"Add a date\" and \"Save\" (DateSheet).\n 07.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 07.D Radio indicators (07.A1): keep (b) as platform-native, or use the trailing-check form on Android too? And should (a) become a check stroke in the tile corner?\n 07.E Every KindGlyph name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 07 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- All 17 glyphs are drawn with their keys. Part A has 17 × 4 cells; Part B has 4 × 5 cells, every one drawn or carrying its \"Does not apply\" reason.\n- The kind picker is 2 columns, and every tile shows the glyph from the TILE → GLYPH map.\n- The only rings are the selected tile's corner indicator and the Android 200% radios. No iOS or web frame draws an empty ring.\n- The selected tile has the fill, the corner dot and the text.primary label at weight 600; focus is a ring only.\n- No glyph is a target on its own, and every glyph has its word beside it or an adjacent label."
