            "promptText": "Component 00a-08: AddressChip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nAddressChip is paired with the ScopeChip sentence you drew in 00a-03. Reuse that sentence exactly.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · AddressChip · 01-anatomy · light: the chip with callouts, the Save it action, the scope sentence and its sender exception, the dark edge rule, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · light: the 4 × 3 grid\n3. 00a · AddressChip · 04-in-context · light: f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-save-confirmation, f8-compare-arrival-header\n4. 00a · AddressChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · dark: the same 12 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · AddressChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · AddressChip · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · AddressChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 08 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): Shows a held or selected address as a label: never a map, never coordinates.\nUSED IN (print): f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-save-confirmation, f1-add-place-sheet, f8-compare-arrival-header.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on the held chip for Place B)\n- ① Pill, radius pill, fill surface.raised, with a 1px border.default edge as decoration (1.24:1). The chip's meaning never depends on its edge.\n- ② A 16pt pin glyph in text.strong, with an 8pt gap. Its round hole is a sub-part (B8).\n- ③ Street \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" in bodySmallMedium 14/20/500, text.primary.\n- ④ City \"Camas, WA 98607\" in caption 12/16, text.secondary (4.63:1 on raised), on the line below the street.\n- ⑤ Padding 12 horizontal and 8 vertical; minimum height 44pt.\n- ⑥ At 390 wide it wraps: street and city each wrap and are never truncated.\n- ⑦ Optional \"Save it\" action, used only when the chip is a selectable suggestion row: a text button in label 13/18/600 primary.700, with a target (B13).\n- ⑧ The ScopeChip sentence follows 8pt below: \"Only you will see this.\" The one exception is the sender label (R4). It describes someone else's place, so it carries no sentence; the sentence goes under the recipient's own address field instead (see in-context c).\n- Dark: fill dark surface.raised. dark border.default on dark raised is invisible (1.00:1), so dark mode uses no border; the pin and text carry the chip. Draw a light and a dark chip side by side labelled \"dark: no border\".\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.primary #111827 on raised · text.secondary #6B7280 on raised 4.63 · text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37 · primary.700 #0369a1 on base 5.93 and on primary.50 5.57 · border.default #E5E7EB 1.24 (decoration only) · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 on dark raised 5.71 · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (edge and check only) · dark text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 7.64.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 4 rows × 3 columns)\nThe addresses in these rows are specimens only. R1–R3 all use the Place B address to show each form, even though in the fixture story Jordan has already saved it (recorded on Notes).\nColumns (label → key): default → default · selected → selected · expired (neutral) → expired.\n R1 held → held (f1-email-verify-handoff): the chip, then \"We're holding it for 7 days\", then \"Only you will see this.\"\n   default: as described.\n   selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900), a 1.5px primary.700 edge (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), and a trailing 16pt check stroke in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)). Text stays text.primary (dark: dark text.primary).\n   expired: fill surface.sunken, text in text.strong, the caption \"We're no longer holding this address.\" and a text button \"Search again\", which opens search already filled with \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\". Use no warning or error hue.\n R2 selectable recovery row → recovery-row (f1-save-confirmation): a full-width 44pt row reading \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\", where \"Save it\" is the action. Followed by \"Only you will see this.\"\n   default: as described.\n   selected: the selected treatment from R1, with \"Save it\" replaced by the check.\n   expired: the R1 expired treatment in row form.\n R3 duplicate → duplicate (f1-add-place-sheet): the chip, then You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today, where \"Use for Today\" is a 44pt text button. Followed by \"Only you will see this.\"\n   default: as described.\n   selected: the selected treatment, after \"Use for Today\" is chosen.\n   expired: Does not apply — a saved place does not expire.\n R4 sender label → sender (f8-compare-arrival-header): the chip with the pin glyph, reading \"Dana\" in bodySmallMedium and \"Camas, WA\" in caption. Its compact form reads \"Dana · Camas, WA\". No scope sentence under it (anatomy ⑧); print \"no scope sentence: not your place\".\n   default: as described.\n   selected and expired: Does not apply — a sender label is neither selectable nor held.\nDark twin: all 12 cells in dark tokens, with no chip border.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 and R2. The street and city wrap onto several lines, the pill becomes a rounded rectangle (radius lg 12), and \"Save it\" moves under the address as a full-width 44pt button. The pin glyph scales to 32pt.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same, with the button at 48dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): \"yes — pin + text; selected = check + edge\"; expired cells: \"yes — words\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 default with the city line in text.strong; the decorative border is unchanged.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Reads the full address: \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, Washington 98607\". Selected: \"…, selected\". Sender: \"Dana, Camas, Washington\".\n- Non-colour: selected is the check plus the edge; expired is stated in words.\n- Target rule: the chip itself is a label. Its actions (\"Save it\", \"Use for Today\", \"Search again\") are targets (B13).\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Always paired with the ScopeChip sentence, except the sender label.\n- Exact strings: \"We're holding it for 7 days\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" · You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today · \"Dana · Camas, WA\".\n- Glossary: \"Saved place\", never \"bookmark\", \"preview\" or \"draft\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy): no platform differences. Draw the same chip on all three platforms.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops)\n a) f1-email-verify-handoff, web 390: the \"Check your email\" context, with R1 default under it.\n b) f1-save-confirmation, iOS 393: R2 default.\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, web 1440 cropped to 720 wide: the R4 sender chip over Dana's column (no scope sentence), and in the empty second column the recipient's own address field with \"Only you will see this.\" under it.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of a blank retype field when the server holds the address, show the held AddressChip — because retyping loses people between steps.\n- Instead of a map or coordinates, show the street and city as text — because a label is enough and a map leaks location.\n- Instead of an alarm colour for an expired hold, use a neutral sunken chip with \"Search again\" — because expiry is not an error.\n- Instead of a held or selectable chip without its scope sentence, always add \"Only you will see this.\" — because a held address must say who sees it.\n- Instead of \"Only you will see this.\" under a sender's chip, put it under the recipient's own field — because the sentence would be false about the sender's place.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: held · recovery-row · duplicate · sender. States: default · selected · expired. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"AddressChip / held / expired / any / light\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"08 AddressChip\")\n 08.A1 Dark mode has no border, because dark border.default on dark raised is 1.00:1.\n 08.A2 The sender label (R4) has no ScopeChip sentence, because \"Only you will see this.\" would be false about the sender's place; the sentence sits under the recipient's own address field. The source spec says the chip is always paired with the sentence.\n 08.A3 Rows R1–R3 all use the Place B address as specimens, although in the fixture story Jordan already saved it on Sat 10 Oct. The duplicate string (You already saved this as “Mom’s house”) is kept verbatim, with curly inner quotes, for the specimen only.\n 08.A4 The recovery-row example \"1402 NE 3rd Ave, Camas — Save it\" became \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" (the Place B fixture).\n 08.B1 \"We're no longer holding this address.\" · \"Search again\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\" (the prefilled search) · \"no scope sentence: not your place\" · \"dark: no border\".\n 08.B2 Spoken labels: \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, Washington 98607\" · \"Dana, Camas, Washington\".\n 08.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 08.E Every AddressChip name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 08 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have 4 rows × 3 columns with printed keys, and every \"Does not apply\" cell prints its reason.\n- Every held, recovery and duplicate specimen has \"Only you will see this.\" under it; the sender chip never does, and in-context c puts the sentence under the recipient's field.\n- The selected state has the fill, the 1.5px edge and the check; expired uses no warning or error hue.\n- No street or city is truncated, no map or coordinates appear, and no dark chip has a border."
