            "promptText": "Component 00a-09: ChoiceChip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nThis is the last component. After this batch, the board is complete.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · ChoiceChip · 01-anatomy · light: the chip with callouts, selected vs unselected vs focus vs disabled, the outline decisions, the iOS / Android / web comparison for R5 and R3, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · light: the 5 × 5 grid\n3. 00a · ChoiceChip · 04-in-context · light: f3-invite-composer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f3-bills-list (web chips vs the iOS segmented control)\n4. 00a · ChoiceChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5 rows (trailing check), Android 200% (Material 3 radios), web zoom at 390 and 1440, the greyscale grid and WRONG example, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · dark: the same 25 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes (final).\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · ChoiceChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · ChoiceChip · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · ChoiceChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 09 entries below; this is the final version)\nThen stop and say the board is complete.\n\nPURPOSE (print): Small single-choice chips for channel, role, time and filter; they are never status badges.\nUSED IN (print): f3-invite-composer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f10-mail-piece-photo, f3-bills-list, f4-notification-settings.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on the time group \"6:30 AM · 7:00 AM · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM\" with 7:00 AM selected)\n- ① Height 32pt / 32dp / 32px visual, with a target (B13) around it. Draw both outlines.\n- ② Radius pill, padding 12 horizontal, 8 gap between chips.\n- ③ Label 13/18/600.\n- ④ Selected: fill primary.50, a 1px primary.700 outline (5.93:1 against base, so the shape stays visible although the fill is only 1.07:1), text primary.700 (5.57:1 on the fill), and a leading 12pt check stroke in primary.700 with a 4pt gap. Dark: fill primary.900, a 1px primary.400 (dark link) outline (8.33:1 on dark base), text in dark text.primary, check in primary.400 (dark link).\n- ⑤ Unselected: a 1px outline and text.strong. The source spec names border.strong for the outline, but border.strong is 1.47:1 and the house style says an input's only edge uses text.secondary ink or darker. Draw the outline in text.secondary (4.83:1; dark: dark text.secondary) and print \"spec border.strong → text.secondary (see Notes)\".\n- ⑥ Focus: the B14 ring, drawn on an unselected and on a selected chip.\n- ⑦ Disabled: the text and a 1px outline, both in text.muted (2.54:1 on base; dark text.muted, 3.75:1 on dark base), no check, plus a reason caption under the group in text.secondary. No border token is used as the edge. Print \"disabled controls are exempt from WCAG contrast; the reason caption carries the meaning (see Notes)\".\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\nprimary.700 #0369a1 on primary.50 5.57 and on base 5.93 (selected outline) · primary.50 #f0f9ff on base 1.07 (fill only) · text.strong #374151 on base 10.31 · text.secondary #6B7280 4.83 (unselected outline) · text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled text and outline) · border.strong #D1D5DB 1.47 (not used as the edge) · border.focus #0284c7 4.10 · dark: text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 #0c4a6e 7.64 · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 outline 8.33 on dark base and 6.83 on dark raised, check 4.42 on primary.900 · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 outline 6.96 · dark text.muted #64748B 3.75 on dark base (disabled).\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 5 rows × 5 columns)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · selected → selected · disabled → disabled · focus → focus · selected + focus → selected-focus (the last shows that selection and focus look different).\nIn R1–R4, the disabled cell shows every chip in the group disabled, with the row's own reason caption under the group. R5 differs (see R5).\n R1 channel → channel (f3-invite-composer): \"Email\" · \"Username\" · \"Share instead\".\n   default: all unselected. selected: \"Email\". disabled: reason \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" focus: focus on \"Username\". selected-focus: \"Email\" selected and focused.\n R2 role → role (f3-invite-composer): \"Member\" · \"Guest\". A capability caption under the group, in caption text.secondary, describes the selected role only. Member: \"Sees and edits the calendar, sees bills and who paid, sees who lives here\". Guest: \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov\".\n   default: both unselected and no capability caption; print the cell note \"caption appears after a role is chosen\".\n   selected: \"Member\", with the Member caption.\n   disabled: both chips disabled, no capability caption, reason \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" (the same surface as R1).\n   focus: focus on \"Guest\", nothing selected, no capability caption.\n   selected-focus: \"Member\" selected and focused, with the Member caption.\n R3 time → time (f4-briefing-optin-card): \"6:30 AM\" · \"7:00 AM\" · \"7:30 AM\" · \"8:00 AM\".\n   default: all unselected. selected: \"7:00 AM\". disabled: reason \"You're offline. Your briefing time will save when you're back online.\" focus: focus on \"7:30 AM\". selected-focus: \"7:00 AM\".\n R4 filter → filter (f10-mail-piece-photo drawer): \"Photographed\", a single toggle chip.\n   default: off. selected: on. disabled: reason \"You're offline. Filters need a connection.\" focus: off and focused. selected-focus: on and focused.\n R5 segment → segment (f3-bills-list): \"Upcoming\" · \"Paid\" · \"All\".\n   default: \"Upcoming\" selected (a segment always has one selection); print \"a segment always has one selected\".\n   selected: \"Upcoming\".\n   disabled: \"Upcoming\" stays enabled and selected (cached bills still show), while \"Paid\" and \"All\" are disabled, with the reason \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\"\n   focus: \"Upcoming\" selected and focus on \"Paid\". selected-focus: \"Upcoming\" selected and focused.\n   Draw the web and Android chip form in the grid; the iOS segmented form is on 01-anatomy (PLATFORMS).\nDark twin: all 25 cells in dark tokens (selected fill primary.900, outline and check primary.400 (dark link), text dark text.primary; unselected outline dark text.secondary; disabled text and outline dark text.muted).\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 and R3 turn into one-column rows. Each option is a full-width row at least 44pt tall, with the label at 44pt, wrapping. The selected row gets the primary.50 fill, the label in primary.700 and a trailing 24pt check stroke in primary.700. Unselected rows show no indicator (native iOS list selection). No ring is drawn on iOS. R2's capability caption sits under the selected row. The iOS segmented control (R5) also becomes these rows at AX sizes.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same rows at 48dp, with Material 3 radio buttons on the leading edge, because they are the Android platform control. Unselected rows show an empty 2px ring in text.secondary; the selected row shows a 2px primary.700 ring with a 12pt filled centre (both are flagged B8 exceptions, recorded on Notes).\n- Web 200% zoom, two frames:\n  390 wide at 200% (195 px effective): this is below the 360 px switch point, so draw the one-column rows in the iOS form (trailing check, no ring), built as role=\"radio\" rows.\n  1440 wide at 200% (720 px effective), cropped to the chip group: the chips wrap onto several lines and stay chips.\n  Print the rule \"switch to rows below 360 px effective width\".\n- GREYSCALE (B10): every cell reads \"yes — selected = check + fill + outline; focus = ring\"; disabled cells read \"yes — reason caption\". Add a WRONG example where the selected chip differs only by hue, with \"fix: add the check\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R3 with the unselected outlines in text.strong, plus the Android unselected radio rings in text.strong. The selected chip is unchanged, and disabled chips stay text.muted (B11).\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Selection is shown by the check, fill and outline, not by colour alone.\n- Each group is one radio group:\n  iOS: buttons with the selected trait, e.g. \"7:00 AM, selected, 2 of 4\".\n  Android: selectable semantics, \"7:00 AM, selected\".\n  Web: role=\"radiogroup\" with role=\"radio\" and aria-checked; arrow keys move between chips.\n- The filter chip is a toggle: \"Photographed, off\" / \"Photographed, on\".\n- Disabled chips stay focusable and read their reason.\n- Target rule: a target (B13) around the 32 visual, with 8pt gaps.\n- The focus ring is distinct from selection.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Sentence case. Exact strings as listed in the grid.\n- Times are written \"7:00 AM\" (a space, AM in capitals).\n- Never \"6:00pm\" or \"7:40 am\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy, and draw all three platforms side by side for R5 and R3)\n- iOS: R5 is a native segmented control (UISegmentedControl look, 32pt, with the selected segment raised). R1–R4 are Pantopus chips.\n- Android: Material 3 filter chips (a leading check when selected, 32dp visual, 48dp target), using Pantopus tokens and the pill radius rather than the M3 default 8dp corner. R5 on Android is a single-select row of the same filter chips.\n- Web: the chips as specified, with a :focus-visible ring and no hover-only affordance.\n- Large text: iOS and web use trailing-check rows; Android uses Material 3 radio buttons.\nPublish the per-platform R5 and R3 forms drawn here with ios, android or web as <size|platform>.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops)\n a) f3-invite-composer, iOS 393, Home A: the channel chips (Email selected) above the field \"priya@example.com\", then the role chips (Member selected) with the capability caption, then the primary button \"Send invite\".\n b) f4-briefing-optin-card, Android 412: \"A morning heads-up?\" with the time chips (7:00 AM selected) and the equal-weight buttons \"Not now\" and \"No thanks\".\n c) f3-bills-list, Home A: \"Upcoming / Paid / All\" as chips in a web 1440 crop (720 wide), and as a segmented control on iOS 393.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of using a ChoiceChip as a status badge, use StatusChip — because a choice chip looks tappable.\n- Instead of a status chip on a person, write the role in plain text — because people are not statuses.\n- Instead of a border.strong outline (1.47:1) as an unselected chip's only edge, use text.secondary — because an input's edge must be visible.\n- Instead of a border.default outline on a disabled chip, use text.muted for its outline — because border tokens are never an input's only edge.\n- Instead of a selected chip whose only boundary is the primary.50 fill (1.07:1), add a 1px primary.700 outline — because the chip's shape must stay visible, as AddressChip's selected edge does.\n- Instead of showing selection with colour alone, add the leading check — because it must read in greyscale.\n- Instead of the focus ring doubling as selection, keep the ring for focus and fill + check + outline for selection — because they are different states.\n- Instead of truncating long labels at large text, switch to one-column rows — because truncated choices cannot be told apart.\n- Instead of an empty-ring radio on iOS or web large-text rows, use a trailing check on the selected row — because iOS has no radio control and an empty ring is the unconfirmed mark's shape.\n- Instead of disabling a segment that still has cached content, keep it enabled and disable only the segments that need a connection — because the reason must match what is disabled.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: channel · role · time · filter · segment. States: default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus. <size|platform> is \"any\" for every 02 grid cell; the R5 and R3 forms drawn per platform on 01-anatomy are published as ios, android and web. Examples: \"ChoiceChip / time / selected / any / dark\" · \"ChoiceChip / segment / selected / ios / light\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"09 ChoiceChip\")\n 09.A1 The unselected outline is text.secondary instead of the source spec's border.strong (1.47:1), following the house-style edge rule.\n 09.A2 The disabled chip has its text and outline in text.muted (2.54:1 light, 3.75:1 dark) instead of a border.default outline (1.24:1), because border tokens are never an input's only edge. Disabled controls are exempt from WCAG contrast; the reason caption under the group carries the meaning.\n 09.A3 The selected chip gets a 1px primary.700 outline (dark: primary.400 (dark link)); the source spec names only the fill. Without it, the selected chip's boundary is the 1.07:1 primary.50 fill.\n 09.A4 The R5 (segment) disabled cell keeps \"Upcoming\" enabled and selected, because cached bills still show; only \"Paid\" and \"All\" are disabled, matching the reason \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\"\n 09.A5 R2 (role) shows a capability caption only for the selected role; with nothing selected (the default, disabled and focus cells) no caption is shown.\n 09.A6 R5's default cell shows \"Upcoming\" selected, because a segment always has one selection.\n 09.A7 Android chips keep the pill radius instead of the M3 default 8dp corner.\n 09.A8 Android 200% rows use Material 3 radio buttons, including an empty ring for unselected options (the same flagged exception as 07.A1 (b)). iOS and web rows use a trailing check and no ring.\n 09.A9 Web zoom has two frames: 390 wide (195 px effective) shows rows, because it is below the 360 px switch point; 1440 wide at 200% (720 px effective) shows the wrapping chips.\n 09.B1 \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" · \"You're offline. Your briefing time will save when you're back online.\" · \"You're offline. Filters need a connection.\" · \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\" · \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Send invite\" · \"caption appears after a role is chosen\" · \"a segment always has one selected\" · \"switch to rows below 360 px effective width\" · \"fix: add the check\".\n 09.B2 Spoken labels: \"7:00 AM, selected, 2 of 4\" · \"7:00 AM, selected\" · \"Photographed, off\" · \"Photographed, on\".\n 09.B3 Sourced, not invented: the Member capability caption (f3-invite-composer research); \"6:30 AM · 7:00 AM · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM\" (f4-briefing-optin-card); \"A morning heads-up?\" (glossary).\n 09.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 09.D Add to 07.D: the same Android radio question applies to ChoiceChip's 200% rows.\n 09.E Every ChoiceChip name, then a closing count of all names in section E.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and Notes has the 09 entries with every earlier entry unchanged and sections A–E complete for all nine components.\n- Both grids have 5 rows × 5 columns with printed keys; every cell is drawn.\n- Every selected chip has the fill, the leading check and the 1px primary.700 outline (dark: primary.400 (dark link)); focus is a ring only.\n- No border token is the only edge of any chip, including disabled chips, and unselected outlines are text.secondary.\n- The R5 disabled cell disables only \"Paid\" and \"All\", and its reason matches.\n- No iOS or web frame draws an empty ring; only the Android 200% frame uses radio rings.\n- The web 390 @200% frame shows rows, and the 1440 @200% frame shows wrapping chips."
          }
        ],
        "resolved": [
          "[major] ProvenanceMark calendar-strip crop (b) had no legend or first-occurrence word. Fixed in 00a-01, crop b: a legend line with drawn S 16pt marks sits above the FourteenDayStrip, labelled \"legend once per surface\". Recorded as 01.A8, and DONE WHEN checks it.",
          "[minor] The default AX5 radio was an empty ring, which is the unconfirmed silhouette, and iOS has no radio control. Setup B8 now says no iOS or web frame ever draws an empty ring. KindGlyph (00a-07) and ChoiceChip (00a-09) draw a trailing check on the selected row and nothing on the others on iOS and web. Ring radios remain only in the Android M3 200% frames, flagged in 07.A1 and 09.A8, with the founder question in 07.D and 09.D. Both components also have an INSTEAD OF line for this.",
          "[minor] The ChoiceChip segment disabled cell contradicted its reason caption. In 00a-09 R5, \"Upcoming\" stays enabled and selected, and only Paid and All are disabled, matching \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\" Recorded as 09.A4, with an INSTEAD OF line and a DONE WHEN check.",
          "[minor + quality] The FreshnessLine 1.2s loop broke the 300ms motion rule. 00a-04 now specifies the platform's own system indeterminate progress indicator (iOS ProgressView, Android M3 LinearProgressIndicator, web progress) with no custom duration, stopped within 5s, in three poses: running, after 5s and Reduce Motion. Setup B15 requires any exemption to be stated and put on Notes, and 04.A1 records it.",
          "[minor] The ChoiceChip web 200% frame was ambiguous. 00a-09 draws two frames. The 390 @200% frame (195 px effective) shows radio rows in the iOS form. A 1440 @200% crop (720 px effective) shows the wrapping chips. The \"switch to rows below 360 px effective width\" rule is printed, setup B9 explains the 195 px viewport, and 09.A9 records it.",
          "[minor] Some rows skipped the relative-count date rule, and \"As of Mon 7:40 AM\" was ambiguous on a Monday. Every date row now leads with the count (\"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\", \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\"). The widget string is now \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\". Setup B16 states the rule, including no weekday for a time today, and 00.A5 says DateRow owns the format. I checked every weekday and count against TODAY (Mon 19 Oct 2026). One more consistency fix: the ProvenanceMark widget crop now reads \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\", matching the same widget in KindGlyph.",
          "[minor] Stale contrast figures did not match. I recomputed every ratio with an unrounded sRGB alpha blend and WCAG 2 luminance, rounded at the end: 3.39 base, 3.36 raised, 3.34 app, 3.32 sunken; dark 4.45, 4.10, 4.48; plus 1.98, 2.24 and 2.36. Setup B7 states the method, 00.A8 records it, and the word \"corrected\" is gone.",
          "[minor + quality] The KindGlyph selected label used weight 700, which is off the type scale. I took the issue's alternative: the label stays label 13/18/600, and selection shows through the primary.50 fill, the corner radio dot and an ink change from text.strong to text.primary. 07.A2 records this, with weight 700 as the fallback if the founder rejects it. The ACCESSIBILITY, greyscale, AX5 and DONE WHEN text no longer says bold.",
          "[minor + major] The disabled ChoiceChip's only edge was border.default. In 00a-09 ⑦, the disabled chip's text and 1px outline are both text.muted (2.54 light, 3.75 dark), and it prints the WCAG disabled-control exemption. border.default is removed from the chip and its dark twin. Recorded as 09.A2, with an INSTEAD OF line and a DONE WHEN check.",
          "[minor] AddressChip R4 and the ChoiceChip R2 default were unclear. 00a-08 ⑧ and R4 say the sender label has no scope sentence, and in-context c puts \"Only you will see this.\" under the recipient's own field (08.A2). ChoiceChip R2 default shows no capability caption and prints \"caption appears after a role is chosen\"; the disabled and focus cells also show none (09.A5). I also gave the R5 segment default a stated rule, \"Upcoming\" selected (09.A6), so no grid cell is left undefined.",
          "[major] Stale age words were appended to every ProvenanceMark row. 00a-01 now gives each row its own stale caption: R1, R3 and R4 are \"Does not apply\" with reasons; R2 reads \"… as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\"; R5 prints \"same as stale variant\"; R6 reuses the R2 caption. Recorded in 01.A2 and 01.B1, with an INSTEAD OF line.",
          "[major] Publish names were unstable. Setup B12 requires a printed \"key: <key>\" on every row and column: lowercase, hyphenated, with no \"/\", spaces, fixture strings or dates. B3 builds cell labels from keys, and PUBLISH builds names only from keys. Each component prompt has a PUBLISH KEYS block with its full key set and matching examples: StatusChip rows are upcoming…deadline-today with the fixture text as specimen only; ProvenanceMark uses tinted-widget; FreshnessLine uses updating…widget-horizon; ChoiceChip uses \"any\" except the per-platform R5 and R3 forms.",
          "[major] \"CalendarStrip\" is not a contract name. Every mention is now FourteenDayStrip: the printed label \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\", 01.A7, 01.B3 and a DONE WHEN check. I scanned all ten prompts: every CamelCase word is a contract component name or a platform or data-source name (AirNow, ProgressView, LinearProgressIndicator, RadioButton, ColorVision).",
          "[major] The R5 × tinted-widget cell was unspecified. 00a-01 adds a rule: no dimming under tinted rendering, full tint (5.93 light, 5.28 dark), with the age words carrying the stale state and the label \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\". This applies to the dark twin too. Recorded as 01.A3, with the failing 2.24 and 2.36 figures in B7 and the table, plus an INSTEAD OF line and a DONE WHEN check.",
          "[minor] Batch-plan artboard names were separated by \" · \". Every BATCH PLAN now puts each artboard on its own numbered line under its batch, and each prompt has its own plan of at most 6 artboards. ProvenanceMark uses 2 batches (6, then 3 including Notes); every other component uses 1 batch of 6 (5 artboards plus the Notes update).",
          "[minor] Lines assumed Claude Design could read the contract. No prompt says \"contract\" any more. DONE WHEN refers to what the prompt lists, borrowed anatomy is written out inline (FourteenDayStrip civic bar, PickupCard contents, DateSheet title \"Add a date\" and button \"Save\"), and founder-facing Notes say \"source spec\". The setup says to rely on nothing outside this project.",
          "[minor] The x-date-sheet primary button label was wrong. In ScopeChip in-context b and KindGlyph in-context a, the primary button is \"Save\" and \"Add a date\" is the sheet title. Checked in ScopeChip DONE WHEN; both strings are listed as sourced in 03.B3 and 07.B3.",
          "[minor] B8 could be read as banning the middle dot. Setup B8 now says: \"the typographic middle dot (·) in text is allowed\"; the rule covers drawn shapes only.",
          "[minor] The B4 size whitelist was incomplete. I took the issue's softer option: setup B5 allows any other dimension only where a component message states it. Each component prompt states its own sizes inline (360 widths, 2px dashes, the 2pt hairline, 1px strikes, 158/338 widget crops, 176/186/175 × 88 picker cells). Setup states the focus gap, end ticks and frame widths.",
          "[minor] OfflineNotice had no used-in list. 00a-05 tells the model to print exactly \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\" instead of ids, recorded as 05.A2, with a DONE WHEN check.",
          "[minor] The KindGlyph grid had ragged extra cells, glyph 2 was never mapped, and one caption rule lacked a default. Part B is now a full 4 × 5 grid with columns default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus for every row, and each non-applicable cell has its reason. The TILE → GLYPH map says glyph 2 is used for a recycling-only pickup row (not the case at Home A or Place B), recorded as 07.A6. The R2 caption default is covered by the ChoiceChip resolution above.",
          "[minor] Some fixture uses were awkward. The AddressChip grid says R1–R3 are specimens only, and 08.A3 records that Jordan already saved Place B. FreshnessLine R6 reads \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (04.A2). The calendar-strip row reads \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\".",
          "[minor] Some content repeated or added noise. ProvenanceMark 03 points to its 02 greyscale column instead of redrawing the grid, and adds only the WRONG example. KindGlyph greyscale is a subset: the 17 row glyphs plus all of Part B. \"corrected\" is gone from the contrast note. The split removed the board-wide manifest, and the artboard list no longer appears in four places: each component lists its own artboards once, and its batch plan gives the order.",
          "Structure: 00a · Notes is now built up across the project. The setup defines sections A–E, the numbering (00 for board-wide, then 01–09 per component) and the board-wide entries 00.A1–00.A9 and 00.B1. ProvenanceMark's last batch creates the artboard, and each later component's last batch redraws it with earlier entries unchanged and its own A/B/C/D/E entries added. Every component-specific note from the old A1–A43 and B lists sits in its component's prompt. Word counts, excluding punctuation-only tokens: setup 2,200; components 2,796 / 1,557 / 1,606 / 1,466 / 1,202 / 1,553 / 2,570 / 1,467 / 2,291. Working copies are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-yingpengwang-skinny-pantopus/52b514da-4f75-4fbb-ab66-72632a65dbcb/scratchpad/00a-00.txt through 00a-09.txt."
        ]
      },
      {
        "setup": {
          "id": "00b-00",
          "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is Foundations board 00b: Data instruments. This message sets up the board; draw nothing yet.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nThis project draws seven components as reference specimens, not screens: ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, SlotMeter, PublicPointMap and FactCount. Later screen prompts ask for them by exact name from separate projects that cannot see this one, so once published, these specimens are their only definition. Draw every number, token and string exactly as the component messages give it.\n\nHOW THIS PROJECT RUNS\n- This message holds the board rules (G1–G8 and R1–R12). They apply to every artboard in this project. Later messages call them \"the board rules from the setup message\".\n- After this, I will send one component message per turn, in this order: ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, SlotMeter, PublicPointMap, FactCount.\n- Each component message ends with its ARTBOARDS list and a BATCH PLAN. Draw only batch 1. Then stop and wait until I type \"continue\" before you draw the next batch. Never start another component's artboards early.\n- The last batch of every component updates 00b · Notes (R12).\n- Everything you need is in the house style, this message and the current component message; do not open other projects.\n\nPUBLISH (my step, after I accept a component)\nWhen I accept a component, I add it to the Pantopus design system under its exact name: ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, SlotMeter, PublicPointMap or FactCount. I include its light and dark specimens and every variant and state. Your job is to make that step mechanical: give every drawn grid cell and every named extra specimen a publish name (R10), and list the names on 00b · Notes. Stand-ins (R11) and anything marked \"do not publish\" never get a publish name.\n\nSHARED GRAMMAR (all seven instruments)\nG1. Each instrument states its fact in words and numbers. The graphic repeats the fact and never replaces it.\nG2. Nothing adds up to a grade, score, percentage or verdict. No progress ring, completion ring, countdown, streak or confetti appears anywhere. The FEMA annual-chance band names (\"0.2% a year\", \"1% a year or more\", \"1% chance each year\") are allowed. \"N of M\" appears only where a component message allows it.\nG3. Nothing depends on colour alone. The EPA AQI hues are the only sanctioned colour scale, and even there the category is printed in words.\nG4. Three shapes mean provenance (00a · ProvenanceMark) and nothing else: a solid disc (Official), a ring (On record, not confirmed) and a solid disc with a knocked-out tick (You added this). No position marker, pointer, bullet, callout end, segment or badge on this board is a plain disc or ring. The component messages that need an exception describe it.\nG5. A mark, cell or segment is never a tap target on its own. The target is the row, the whole instrument or a labelled button.\nG6. Each instrument has a one-sentence summary and a spoken label, both printed on its artboards. The same facts appear nearby as rows or a list.\nG7. Every provenance mark keeps at least 3:1 contrast in every state. Staleness is always stated in words.\nG8. Widgets and the share card are standalone surfaces. They print the provenance word next to each mark or in a legend line inside the block.\n\nBOARD RULES\nR1 · Artboard format and naming.\n- This board overrides the house-style artboard pattern, because one specimen artboard shows several platforms. Name every artboard \"00b · <Component> · <NN-name> · <light|dark>\", exactly as the component's ARTBOARDS list gives it. The last artboard is \"00b · Notes\".\n- Each artboard is 1440 wide and as tall as its content. Use surface.app for light artboards and dark surface.app #020617 for dark ones.\n- Print the exact artboard name above the artboard in label 13/18/600 text.strong.\n- Inside the artboard, at the top: the component name in h1 30/36/700 text.primary, its purpose line in body 16/24 text.secondary, then \"Used in: <surface ids>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary, as the component message gives them.\n- Section headings use overline 11/16/600 caps, for example ANATOMY, VARIANT × STATE, AX5 AND 200%, GREYSCALE, IN CONTEXT, ACCESSIBILITY, INSTEAD OF.\n\nR2 · Frames and cards.\n- Draw specimens at true size (1pt = 1px on the artboard) inside plain frames named as the message names them: iOS 393, Android 412, web-390, web-1440, and the widget outlines 338×158 and 338×354.\n- In the three phone frames, draw the specimen card 358 wide with 16pt padding, which leaves 326pt of content width, and centre the card in the frame. All phone geometry assumes 326pt of content width unless a message says otherwise.\n- Cards use surface.base, radius lg 12, shadow sm and 16pt padding. Dark cards use dark surface.raised #1E293B with a 1px dark border.strong #374151 edge, because dark border.default has no contrast on raised.\n- Each component message gives its own web-1440 card width.\n\nR3 · Units.\n- A size given in pt is the same number in dp (Android) and px (web). Only target minimums differ by platform: 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, and 44px on web.\n- Spacing uses the 4px scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64).\n- A few offsets inside instruments are deliberately off that scale: 6, 3, 2 and 1pt, for cell padding, bar offsets, mark shifts and numeral nudges. Draw them only where a message states them, and never use them for layout spacing.\n- Type uses only the house type scale, plus the R7 sizes, the 11pt widget minimum and the OG sizes that a component message states.\n\nR4 · Callouts.\n- Callouts sit in an annotation gutter outside the UI, in caption 12/16 text.strong.\n- Leader lines are 1px text.secondary and end in a short perpendicular tick, never a dot (G4). Dimension lines are 1px text.secondary with 4pt end ticks.\n- Each callout names the part, its size and its token, for example \"Track · 12pt · fill surface.raised · keyline 1px text.secondary\".\n- Callouts appear on 01-anatomy artboards and wherever a message asks for one.\n- Gutter labels (\"specimen\", \"specimen value\", \"stand-in — …\") use the same style.\n\nR5 · Tokens and dark mode.\n- Label every colour by its token name. Hex values appear on the board only in the contrast tables a message asks for and in the AQI swatch row.\n- On dark artboards, use exactly this mapping:\n  - surface.base → #0F172A · surface.raised → #1E293B · surface.app → #020617 · surface.sunken → #0F172A · surface.muted → #111827\n  - text.primary → #E5E7EB · text.secondary → #94A3B8 · text.strong → #F1F5F9\n  - border.default → #1F2937 · border.strong → #374151 (both decoration only) · border.focus → #38BDF8\n  - primary.700 (links, text buttons, and any edge a message names) → #38BDF8, because primary.700 is 2.47:1 on dark raised.\n- These tokens keep their light values in dark mode, drawn by token name: the primary.600 fill (3.57:1 on dark raised), semantic.error glyphs (3.03:1) and semantic.warning glyphs (4.59:1). Semantic hues go on glyphs only.\n- On dark cards, surface.sunken fills (#0F172A on #1E293B) look darker than the card. That is intended, because keylines and text carry the edges. A sunken-filled pill that sits on dark base uses dark raised #1E293B instead, so it stays visible.\n- Never use the light infoBg wash in dark mode, because dark text.primary on it is 1.16:1. Component messages give the dark highlight.\n- The EPA AQI hues never change in dark mode.\n- This board draws no selection state.\n\nR6 · Contrast numbers (WCAG 2). Opacities are alpha-blended over their surface first. Use these numbers and do not recompute them. Print the rows that a message asks for.\nLight:\n- text.secondary: 4.83 on base · 4.63 on raised · 4.51 on app · 4.39 on sunken (below 4.5, so text on sunken uses text.strong) · 4.65 on a weekend strip cell (sunken at 40% over base)\n- text.strong: 9.37 on sunken · 10.31 on base\n- text.primary: 17.74 on base · 16.12 on sunken\n- primary.700: 5.93 on base · 5.68 on raised · 5.39 on sunken\n- primary.600 fill: 4.10 on base\n- Glyphs: semantic.error 4.83 on base · semantic.warning 3.19 on base\n- Stale mark (the 00a stale variant, text.primary at 50%): 3.39 on base · 3.36 on raised · 3.34 on app · 3.32 on sunken · 3.36 on a weekend cell\n- Never used: text.secondary at 50% (1.98 on base, 1.91 on sunken) · text.muted for readable text (2.54 on base)\nDark:\n- text.secondary #94A3B8: 6.96 on dark base · 5.71 on dark raised · 6.23 on a dark weekend cell\n- text.primary #E5E7EB: 11.82 on dark raised · 14.42 on dark base\n- text.strong #F1F5F9: 16.30 on dark base · 13.35 on dark raised\n- #38BDF8: 6.83 on dark raised · 8.33 on dark base\n- Stale mark (dark text.primary at 50%): 4.45 on dark base · 4.10 on dark raised · 4.48 on dark app · 4.27 on a dark weekend cell\n- Decoration only: dark border.strong 1.42 on dark raised · dark border.default 1.00 on dark raised\n\nR7 · AX5 and 200%.\n- iOS AX5 sizes: h1 58 · h2 58 · h3 55 · body and bodyMedium 53 · bodySmall 49 · label 44 · caption 43 · overline 40.\n- Android 200% sizes (Android 14 non-linear scaling): h1 38 · h2 36 · h3 34 · body 28 · bodySmall 26 · label 25 · caption 24 · overline 22.\n- Web: 200% browser zoom on web-1440, which gives an effective layout 720 CSS px wide.\n- Graphic geometry keeps its size, and text reflows around it. This covers tracks, cells, segments, markers, glyph-only buttons, and marks inside cells, lanes and tracks. Marks inside text lines (captions, rows, legends) scale with their text.\n- Text wraps and never truncates or ellipsises. Side-by-side pairs stack. Widgets fall back to text only, as each message states.\n- Draw iOS AX5 in a 393 frame and Android 200% in a 412 frame, as tall as needed.\n\nR8 · Greyscale. Redraw the listed specimens at 100% desaturation. Under each one, print in caption text.secondary the non-colour cue that still carries the meaning, using the words the component message gives.\n\nR9 · Grids and keys.\n- A variant × state grid has variant rows and state columns, in the order the message gives.\n- Print each row and column label in label 13/18/600 text.strong. Under the label, print its key as \"key: <key>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\n- A key is lowercase and hyphenated, with no spaces, no \"/\", no fixture string and no date. Each component message lists its keys. Use them exactly.\n- Each cell holds one specimen at true size, or the stacked specimens the message asks for. Under the specimen, print the cell's keys, for example \"detail · stale\".\n- A combination with no meaning prints \"n/a — <reason>\" in caption text.secondary and draws nothing else. Use the one reason the message gives. Never leave a cell blank.\n- Specimens outside a grid get the extra key that the message gives.\n\nR10 · Publish names. Give one name to each drawn grid cell and each extra specimen:\n- \"<Component> / <variant key> / <state key> / <light|dark>\"\n- or \"<Component> / extra / <extra key> / <light|dark>\"\nNames use keys only. n/a cells get no name.\n\nR11 · Borrowed parts and stand-ins. These instruments use parts from boards 00a, 00c and 00d. Use the published part when the design system has it. Otherwise draw the stand-in below and label it in the gutter \"stand-in — the 00a/00c/00d specimen replaces it\". Do not design a stand-in any further, and never give it a publish name.\n- 00a · ProvenanceMark: a mark at XS 12pt or S 16pt, in text.secondary at full opacity.\n  - Official is a solid disc.\n  - On record, not confirmed is a ring with a stroke of at least 1.5px.\n  - You added this is a solid disc with a knocked-out tick (a true cut-out).\n  - Stale variant: the same shape in text.primary at 50% opacity, always paired with age words.\n- 00a · SourceCaption: one caption 12/16 line in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken), in the pattern [ProvenanceMark S] authority · scope word · as-of. It wraps and never truncates.\n- 00a · FreshnessLine: one caption line in text.secondary that states age in words, with an optional 16pt leading glyph.\n- 00a · ScopeChip: a 24pt pill on surface.sunken holding a 12pt person or house glyph and the label in label 13/18 text.strong.\n- 00a · KindGlyph: a 24pt line icon with a 2pt stroke, in text.strong.\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow: a row in the component's own slot. It holds a 16pt error glyph (semantic.error on the glyph only), the sentence in body text.primary, and a 44pt \"Retry\" text button in primary.700. It has no tinted background.\n- 00c · DateRow: a row at least 56pt tall. It holds a leading KindGlyph, the title in body text.primary, a trailing ProvenanceMark S, and line 2 in caption text.secondary. Line 2 gives the relative and absolute date (\"Tomorrow\", or \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\") and a short SourceCaption.\n- 00c · FactRow: a 56pt row. The label is in bodySmall text.secondary above the value in body text.primary. The row also holds a ProvenanceMark and a trailing chevron.\n- 00c · TextActionRow (outbound): a row at least 44pt tall with a 1px text.secondary edge, a verb-led label in primary.700 and a trailing \"↗\".\n- 00d · WarmingSkeleton: surface.sunken shapes with the component's final geometry and radius, and no text. It reserves the exact final height. It shimmers by default and is static under Reduce Motion.\n- 00d · QuietDayReceipt: only the one-line forms that a component message describes.\n\nR12 · Fixtures, motion, focus and 00b · Notes.\n- Use the house-style FIXTURES exactly. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific. Draw every quoted string exactly as written.\n- In the gutter, label any value that is not tied to a fixture address \"specimen value\".\n- Show motion as static annotated frames, never as a loop. Annotate Reduce Motion wherever it changes something.\n- Keyboard focus on web is a 2px border.focus outline with a 2px offset around the focusable row, strip or button (#38BDF8 in dark).\n- 00b · Notes is one light artboard, 1440 wide. It has sections A to G, and each section is divided by component, with the component name as an h3 subheading:\n  - A. Invented strings: every quoted string that is not in the house-style fixtures or the component contract. Each component message lists its own.\n  - B. Assumptions.\n  - C. Normalisations.\n  - D. Deviations from the contract. Each one needs my sign-off.\n  - E. Open questions for the founder, numbered across the whole board.\n  - F. n/a cells, each with its reason.\n  - G. Publish names (R10).\n- Create 00b · Notes in the last batch of the first component. Start section B with a \"Board\" subsection that records:\n  - the artboard naming override (R1)\n  - the off-scale micro-geometry (R3)\n  - the 358-wide phone cards (R2)\n  - the dark card edge and dark sunken fills (R5)\n  - stale marks drawn as the 00a stale variant, text.primary at 50%, which passes 3:1 (R6, R11)\n- Each later component appends its entries in its last batch and keeps everything already there.\n\nReply 'ready' and wait for the first component."
        },
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "00b-01",
            "component": "ScaleStrip",
            "artboards": [
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · dark",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · dark",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · dark",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · dark",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light",
              "00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light",
              "00b · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-01: ScaleStrip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The four-layer reading instrument. It draws one row per authority on that authority's own ordered bands, and it never adds up to a grade.\nUSED IN (print it): f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-sheet, f8-og-compare-card.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 640px wide (608px of content).\nSPECIMEN CLOCKS: AirNow readings are hourly, so age decides state. Ready Air rows (including compare \"You\") are drawn at specimen time 7:10 AM on Mon 19 Oct, so \"observed 7:00 AM\" is fresh; print \"specimen time 7:10 AM\" in the gutter wherever one appears. Stale Air rows use TODAY, 6:10 PM (\"— 11 hours ago\").\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Fixed row order, never re-sorted: Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon.\n- Each row, from top to bottom: the layer name (label 13/18/600 text.strong) · the value line \"Word · number\" (bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary) · the track zone · the band names · a 00a · SourceCaption.\n- Padding is 12pt at the top and bottom. Gaps: name → value 4pt, value → track zone 8pt, track zone → band names 4pt, band names → caption 8pt.\n- Each row is at least 48pt tall and is one target (44pt iOS and web, 48dp Android). Markers and pointers are never targets.\n- Layout by container width:\n  - Below 560pt (phones, web-390, compare at 390): stacked, with the track at the full 326pt.\n  - 560pt and wider (web-1440): two columns with a 16pt gap. The left 40% stacks the layer name, value line and SourceCaption. The right 60% holds the track zone with the band names under it, top-aligned with the value line.\n  - AX5 and 200%: stacked. OG: see 05.\n- Track zone: 24pt tall, with a 12pt track centred in it.\n- Track: equal-width bands per layer (no shared axis), filled surface.raised. 1.5px text.secondary separators (4.83:1). A 1px text.secondary keyline, radius xs 4, around the whole track. Least hazard on the left, most on the right.\n- Occupied band: a 2px text.primary outline inside the band's edges.\n- Marker: a vertical capsule 4 × 20pt, radius pill, with a text.primary core and a 2px surface.base halo (8 × 24pt overall; the halo is #0F172A in dark mode). It is centred in the occupied band and extends 4pt above and below the track. It is never a disc (G4).\n- Band names: caption 12/16 text.secondary under the track, up to 2 lines, never truncated.\n  - Flood and Radon print every band name. Wildfire prints only the two end names and the occupied name.\n  - The occupied name is captionMedium 12/16/500 text.primary, directly under the marker. If it comes within 8pt of an end name, it replaces that end name.\n  - Air prints the range labels \"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\", with the occupied range in captionMedium text.primary.\n- Bands:\n  - Flood (3, by annual chance): \"Minimal (X)\" · \"0.2% a year (shaded X)\" · \"1% a year or more (A/V zones)\". The value line prints the actual zone code.\n  - Wildfire (5 USFS classes): \"Very low\" · \"Low\" · \"Moderate\" · \"High\" · \"Very high\".\n  - Radon (3, ordered Zone 3 → Zone 2 → Zone 1): \"Zone 3 · low potential\" · \"Zone 2 · moderate potential\" · \"Zone 1 · highest potential\". Radon never uses \"N of M\".\n  - Air: the AqiBand instrument-row variant, the only coloured track (AqiBand, the next component, defines it in full; draw it exactly like this). Six equal-width 12pt segments in the house-style EPA ColorVision Assist hues, Good to Hazardous, with 2px gaps in the host surface, a 1px text.secondary keyline on each segment and radius xs 4 on the outer corners. The marker is the same capsule at 4 × 20pt, placed by value within its segment. With no reading, the segments are surface.sunken with their keylines and there is no marker. The value line leaves out the pollutant (\"AQI 42 · Good\").\n- Fixture rows (HOME A). All four are Official, and \"●\" stands for the drawn Official mark.\n\n  | Row | Label | Value | Occupied | Caption |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Flood | \"Flood zone\" | \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" | band 1 | \"● FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\" |\n  | Wildfire | \"Wildfire hazard potential\" | \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" | band 3 | \"● USFS · quarter-mile area · 2023\" |\n  | Air | \"Air quality index (AQI)\" | \"AQI 42 · Good\" | marker at 84% of Good | \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\" |\n  | Radon | \"Radon zone\" | \"Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\" | band 3 | \"● EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\" |\n\n- Summary (the web text alternative and the native group label; print it under the 01 fixture instrument): \"Flood Zone X, minimal flood hazard. Wildfire Moderate, 3 of 5. Air AQI 42, Good. Radon Zone 1, county-wide.\"\n- Specimen value (gutter label \"specimen value\"): a Flood row reading \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\", band 3 occupied.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys in brackets)\n- V1 Flood [flood] · V2 Wildfire [wildfire] · V3 Radon [radon] · V4 Air [air], as above.\n- V5 compare [compare]:\n  - Two pointers on one track replace the capsule.\n  - Track zone, top to bottom (60pt): a 16pt line \"Dana\" (captionMedium text.primary) · an 8pt sender pointer · the 12pt track · an 8pt \"You\" pointer · a 16pt line \"You\" (captionMedium text.primary). The band names sit 4pt below the \"You\" line.\n  - The sender pointer is a downward triangle, 12pt wide × 8pt tall, in text.primary with a 2px surface.base halo, its tip touching the top of the track. The \"You\" pointer is the same triangle pointing up, its tip touching the bottom of the track. Both are centred in their band (on Air, placed by value within the segment).\n  - Each occupied band gets the 2px outline. When both readings share a band, only that band is outlined, and the pointers share one x position.\n  - Value lines: differing readings print \"Dana: <value>\" and \"You: <value>\". A shared band prints one line starting \"Both:\".\n  - Chip, right-aligned on the layer-name line: \"Same band\" or \"Different band\". A 24pt pill with a surface.sunken fill and 8pt side padding, in captionMedium text.strong, with no glyph and no hue.\n  - Header: \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\". \"You\" is the recipient's own address, so its readings are specimen values.\n- V6 no data [no-data] (Flood, Wildfire, Radon): bands filled surface.sunken, keyline and separators unchanged, no marker, no outline. Value line \"Not on record\".\n- V7 not studied [not-studied] (Flood only): the same greyed track, with the value \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\".\n- V8 non-burnable [non-burnable] (Wildfire only): the same greyed track, with the value \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\".\n- V6, V7 and V8 must each look different from Wildfire \"Very low\" (a normal track, band 1 occupied).\n- V9 frozen [frozen]: every caption ends \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\". The frozen Air caption is \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\", and its value is \"AQI 42 · Good · on Sat 12 Sep\".\n- V10 collapsed text line [collapsed], for the arrival header below 640px: one wrapping row of body text, at least 44pt tall, with the whole row as the target and no tracks: \"Dana · Camas, WA · Flood X · Wildfire Moderate · Air 42 · Radon Zone 1 ›\".\n\nSTATES (column keys in brackets)\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton showing only the track keyline and separators (no fill, marker or text). The label and value become surface.sunken bars of 60×12 and 140×16. The row height is reserved exactly.\n- ready [ready].\n- partial, loading [partial-loading]: some rows ready, others still loading.\n- partial, failed [partial-failed]: the Air row's own slot shows a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" + Retry. The other rows stay ready.\n- differs tag [differs]: the neutral \"Different band\" chip (V5).\n- stale air row [stale], at TODAY 6:10 PM: the Air row keeps its value and marker. Its caption becomes \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", with the mark in the 00a stale variant (text.primary at 50%, 3.39:1). The age words carry the staleness, and the other rows are unchanged.\n- AX5 [ax5]: text stacked above a full-width track (on 06).\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light and · dark: one detail Wildfire row with every callout; the fixture instrument in an iOS 393 frame with the summary under it; the same instrument in two columns on web-1440, with a callout on the split; and an R6 contrast table (text.secondary on base and raised, text.strong on sunken, the stale mark on base and raised; dark rows on the dark artboard).\n00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light and · dark, a grid:\n- Rows: flood · wildfire · air · radon · wildfire-very-low (label \"Wildfire very low (for contrast)\").\n- Columns: loading · ready · no-data · not-studied-non-burnable · stale · frozen.\n- Cell rules:\n  - flood × ready: the Zone X row, with the Zone AE specimen value under it.\n  - flood × not-studied-non-burnable = V7. wildfire × not-studied-non-burnable = V8.\n  - air × no-data: the AqiBand no-reading instrument row (greyed segments, \"No reading for this address right now\"), not V6.\n  - air × not-studied-non-burnable: \"n/a — AirNow has no such class; see AqiBand no reading\".\n  - radon × not-studied-non-burnable: \"n/a — EPA zones cover every county\".\n  - flood, wildfire and radon × stale: \"n/a — dated datasets carry their effective date, not an age\".\n  - wildfire-very-low × ready: a normal track, band 1 occupied, value \"Very low · 1 of 5\", aligned with the wildfire greyed cells. Its other cells: \"n/a — contrast row; only ready is needed\".\n00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light and · dark:\n- A web-390 compare instrument, \"Dana · Camas, WA\" vs You:\n  - Flood: both in band 1. \"Same band\". \"Both: Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n  - Wildfire: Dana Moderate 3 of 5, You Low 2 of 5. \"Different band\". \"Dana: Moderate · 3 of 5\" and \"You: Low · 2 of 5\".\n  - Air: Dana AQI 42, frozen on Sat 12 Sep; You AQI 42 today, observed 7:00 AM. Both pointers inside Good. \"Same band\". \"Both: AQI 42 · Good\". Two captions, one per line: \"Dana: AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" and \"You: AirNow · observed 7:00 AM\".\n  - Radon: both Zone 1. \"Same band\". \"Both: Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n  - Flood, Wildfire and Radon each print one V9 frozen caption (\"● FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021 · as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\").\n- The compare spoken label, printed under the instrument.\n- Beside it: V10 at 390 wide, and at 320 wide, where it wraps to 3 lines.\n- Below: the compare Wildfire row in two columns on web-1440.\n00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light and · dark: the instrument five times in iOS 393 frames (loading · ready · partial with Air loading · partial with Air failed · stale air row), with all four row labels under ready and only the changed labels under the others.\n00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light (light only, because the share card is light only):\n- A 1200×630 frame, 16px padding top and bottom: a 520px text-and-track column for \"Dana · Camas, WA\" on the left, and \"Yours?\" in the empty right column. Do not design the full card (f8-og-compare-card owns it).\n- Header: \"Dana · Camas, WA\" at 40px on a 48px line, then a 24px gap (72px).\n- Four rows, 112px each: 8px top · one 40px line (48px line height) with the layer word and value · 8px · a 40px track zone holding a 30px track · 8px bottom. No band names or per-row captions; the value line carries the band word. Rows: \"Flood · Zone X — minimal\" · \"Wildfire · Moderate · 3 of 5\" · \"Air · AQI 42 · Good\" · \"Radon · Zone 1 (county)\".\n- OG marker: the capsule at 8 × 40px with a 4px halo, extending 5px beyond each edge of the track.\n- Footer: a 24px gap, then one sources line across the full 1168px at 28px (36px line): a 28px Official ProvenanceMark, then \"Official · FEMA Sep 2021 · USFS 2023 · AirNow Sat 12 Sep · EPA county-wide\". \"Official\" is printed because this is a standalone surface (G8).\n- Print the height budget in the gutter: 16 + 72 + 4 × 112 + 60 + 16 = 612px, within 630.\n- Value lines stay on one line; if one does not fit, the column may widen to 640px while \"Yours?\" narrows. Header and value text stay at 40px or more.\n00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light:\n- the instrument at iOS AX5 and at Android 200%\n- the compare Wildfire row at AX5: \"Dana\" and the chip each take their own line above the track; \"You\" stays below\n- web-1440 at 200% zoom, switched to the stacked layout\n- one Wildfire row under iOS Increase Contrast, with separators, keyline and occupied outline in text.primary.\n00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light: the light 02 and 03 desaturated, with the captions \"Band by position + printed band name + 2px outline\", \"Difference by the words 'Different band' and 'Same band'\" and \"Readings by the pointer labels 'Dana' and 'You'\".\n00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light: three crops of the host card only.\n- (a) f8-scale-strips, web-1440: the two-column instrument in the /start preview card, with the legend line \"● Official\".\n- (b) f6-place-section-details, iOS 393: the instrument in the Place section, with the 00c · TextActionRow \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" under the Radon row.\n- (c) f8-compare-arrival-header, web-390: V10 above the address field; beside it, f8-compare-reveal (web-390) with the Wildfire compare row.\n- Under the crops, in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f8-compare-sheet → V5 compare at 390 (phone sheet width) · f8-og-compare-card → the 05-og-column recipe.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Each row is one element reading its full label. Print these under the ready instrument on 04:\n  - \"Flood zone: Zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, effective September 2021. Official.\"\n  - \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate, 3 of 5, scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023. Official.\"\n  - \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM. Official.\"\n  - \"Radon zone: Zone 1, highest potential, scale Zone 3 to Zone 1. EPA, county-wide. Official.\"\n- Changed labels on 04: loading = \"Loading\", read once for the container · partial with Air loading = \"Loading\" for the Air row · partial with Air failed = \"Air quality: We couldn't reach AirNow just now.\", with the Retry button named \"Retry air quality\" · stale = \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago. Official.\"\n- Compare label on 03: \"Wildfire hazard potential. Dana: Moderate, 3 of 5. You: Low, 2 of 5. Different band. Scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023.\"\n- Meaning comes from position plus a printed name. Every row is text, so the table equivalent is implicit. On web the row is focusable (R12 ring).\n\nCOPY\n- Approved strings, verbatim: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\" · \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate · 3 of 5\" · \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n- Pair a word with a number, except for Radon. Sender rows describe places. Outbound actions start with a verb.\n- Never write \"100-year floodplain\", \"minimal risk\", \"wildfire risk\", \"better\", \"worse\" or \"wins\".\n\nPLATFORMS: Web draws SVG; iOS (SwiftUI) and Android (Compose) draw natively, with identical geometry and platform target minimums. The OG render follows 05.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a grade, score, star, radar chart, cross-layer ramp or shared 0–100 axis, draw four rows on each authority's own equal-width bands, because the layers never add up to a verdict.\n- Instead of re-sorting rows by distance, keep Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon, because people compare rows by position.\n- Instead of arrows, trophies or better/worse words, draw \"Different band\" or \"Same band\", because a difference between places is not a ranking.\n- Instead of a disc marker, draw the capsule, because a disc reads as ● Official.\n- Instead of a filled sender marker and a ringed \"You\", draw two identical labelled triangles, because filled vs hollow means provenance only.\n- Instead of the four-band flood scale \"X · X shaded · AE · VE\", draw three annual-chance bands with the zone code in the value line, because the contract groups A and V zones by annual chance.\n- Instead of drawing \"Not on record\" like \"Very low\", draw a greyed track with no marker plus the words, because no data is not a low reading.\n- Instead of dimming the stale mark with text.secondary at 50% (1.98:1), use the 00a stale variant plus age words, because below 3:1 the shape is lost.\n- Instead of band names and captions on every OG row, print one value line per row and one sources line, because text-heavy OG images fail at thumbnail size.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- 02: each drawn cell, \"ScaleStrip / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- 04: \"ScaleStrip / instrument / <state key> / <light|dark>\", with the state keys loading, ready, partial-loading, partial-failed and stale.\n- 03: \"ScaleStrip / compare / differs / <light|dark>\" (the whole compare instrument) and \"ScaleStrip / collapsed / ready / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: two-column (01), compare-two-column (03), og-column (05, light), ax5 and increase-contrast (06, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: create 00b · Notes with the Board entries from R12, then these)\n- A. Invented strings: every quoted string here that is not a fixture or contract string (row labels, band and range labels, the \"Dana:\", \"You:\" and \"Both:\" lines, chips, summary, spoken labels, \"Yours?\", OG lines, frozen captions, the outbound row, the also-used-in line).\n- B. Assumptions: compare \"You\" is the recipient's own address with specimen values (Wildfire Low, 2 of 5; the other layers in Dana's band). The compare Flood, Wildfire and Radon rows print one frozen caption each. The instrument's Air row leaves out the pollutant. Ready and stale Air differ by specimen clock (7:10 AM vs 6:10 PM), not only by caption.\n- C. Normalisations: \"as of Sep 12, 2026\" → \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\". \"Free test kits · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" → \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" (verb first). The brief's \"Zone 1 — highest potential of EPA's 3 zones\" → the contract's \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n- D. Deviations (need sign-off):\n  - The contract's \"Marker: 12pt two-tone\" is a 4 × 20pt two-tone capsule, because a 12pt round marker reads as a provenance disc.\n  - The contract's compare \"same marker form\" is drawn as identical triangle pointers above and below one track.\n  - The occupied band name sits under the marker, not beside it, so it never collides with other names.\n  - The contract's OG \"text is at least 40px cap\" is read as a 40px font size, as in the brief's \"≥40 px type\"; a true 40px cap height needs about 56px type and does not fit 630px. The sources line is 28px, because at 40px it does not fit on one 1168px line.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 12 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (5 × 6, one reason per n/a).\n- V1–V10, all seven states, the summary and every spoken label are drawn.\n- No text sits on an AQI fill. Discs and rings appear only as provenance marks, and every mark is at least 3:1.\n- The OG budget totals 612px. \"N of M\" appears only in Wildfire readings and \"category 1 of 6\".\n- 00b · Notes holds the Board and ScaleStrip entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (12 artboards plus the Notes artboard, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light\n3. 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light\n4. 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light\n5. 00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light\n6. 00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light\n8. 00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light\n9. 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · dark\n10. 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · dark\n11. 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · dark\n12. 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · dark\nBatch 3:\n13. 00b · Notes (create it)"
