            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-02: AqiBand. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The one officially coloured scale. It shows the EPA AQI with its category name and is drawn the same way everywhere air appears.\nUSED IN (print it): f1-today-air-band, f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, x-provenance-sheet, f8-og-compare-card, f8-compare-reveal.\n\nSPECIMEN CLOCKS. AirNow readings are hourly, so the age of a reading decides its state. Print the specimen time once in the gutter of every artboard that shows one of these specimens.\n- Ready and offline specimens are drawn at specimen time 7:10 AM on Mon 19 Oct, so \"observed 7:00 AM\" is fresh.\n- Alert and still-above specimens are drawn at specimen time 4:10 PM.\n- Stale specimens use TODAY, 6:10 PM, which gives \"— 11 hours ago\".\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Six equal-width category segments in the EPA ColorVision Assist hues. These are the only colours in the product that are not tokens. Name them on the board as swatches, with their RGB values:\n  - aqi.good: Good 158,255,145\n  - aqi.moderate: Moderate 255,201,5\n  - aqi.usg: Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups 255,130,5\n  - aqi.unhealthy: Unhealthy 240,34,0\n  - aqi.veryUnhealthy: Very Unhealthy 137,9,151\n  - aqi.hazardous: Hazardous 100,0,21\n- Segment height: 16pt in the detail variant (Today), 12pt in the instrument row and 8pt in the widget micro variant.\n- Gaps: 2px between segments, in the host surface colour (surface.base on light cards, dark raised #1E293B on dark cards).\n- Keylines: each segment has its own 1px text.secondary keyline (#94A3B8 in dark mode), because some hues nearly vanish against their surface. Good is 1.22:1 and Moderate 1.54:1 on white, and Hazardous is 1.08:1 on dark raised. The outer corners of the first and last segments have radius xs 4.\n- Detail width: (326 − 5 × 2) ÷ 6 = 52.7pt per segment.\n- Range labels: centred under each segment in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\". The occupied segment's label switches to captionMedium text.primary, and that segment gets a 2px text.primary inner outline.\n- Marker: the ScaleStrip capsule. It is 4pt wide, with a text.primary core (#E5E7EB in dark mode) and a 2px halo in surface.base (#0F172A in dark mode, a fixed dark tone). Its height is the segment height + 8pt: 24pt in the detail variant, 20pt in the instrument row and 16pt in the widget micro variant. It passes 3:1 on every hue in both themes, because one of its two tones always contrasts.\n  - Position within the segment = (value − segment low) ÷ (segment high − segment low). AQI 42 sits at 84% of Good, and AQI 118 sits at 35% of Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups.\n  - Values above 500 clamp to the right end of \"301+\", and the number is still printed.\n- Marker contrast table (print it on 01, core / halo against each hue):\n\n  | Hue | Light core | Light halo | Dark core | Dark halo |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Good | 14.50 | 1.22 | 1.01 | 14.59 |\n  | Moderate | 11.50 | 1.54 | 1.25 | 11.57 |\n  | USG | 7.14 | 2.49 | 2.01 | 7.18 |\n  | Unhealthy | 4.17 | 4.26 | 3.44 | 4.19 |\n  | Very Unhealthy | 2.15 | 8.24 | 6.65 | 2.17 |\n  | Hazardous | 1.31 | 13.52 | 10.92 | 1.32 |\n\n- Value line above the band, in bodyMedium text.primary: \"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\" (fixture) or \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · PM2.5\" (alert). The category name and number are always printed on the card in text.primary, never on a fill. The value line is the band's visible one-sentence summary. Inside ScaleStrip, the pollutant is left out (\"AQI 42 · Good\").\n- Health statement below the band, in body 16/24 text.primary, verbatim from EPA:\n  - Good: \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups: \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\" It is followed by the PM2.5 sensitive-groups line \"People with heart or lung disease, older adults, children, and people of lower socioeconomic status are the groups most at risk.\"\n- Pantopus context goes in a separate block below the statement: the overline \"PANTOPUS NOTE\", then a line in bodySmall text.primary. Draw it only on the alert specimen: \"Your alert level is 101. You can change it in Notifications.\"\n- Optional threshold rule at the user's chosen threshold (101, 151 or 201):\n  - a 1.5px dashed vertical rule (3 on, 2 off) in text.primary at the threshold's position, extending 6pt above and below the band\n  - the threshold number above the rule, in caption text.primary (\"101\")\n  - the line \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\" in bodySmallMedium text.primary, with a leading 16pt alert glyph in semantic.warning (the hue goes on the glyph only)\n  - The fixture threshold is 101, the server default. Also draw one specimen at 151, labelled \"threshold 151 (not crossed)\".\n- 00a · SourceCaption: \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\" (alert: \"observed 4:00 PM\"). \"●\" stands for the drawn Official mark.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 detail [detail]: the Today card.\n- V2 instrument row [instrument-row]: inside ScaleStrip, with 12pt segments and no health statement. The ScaleStrip artboards already draw this form; it must match them exactly.\n- V3 widget micro [widget-micro]: the medium widget. No numbers under the segments, and the name and number sit beside the band.\n- V4 no reading: drawn in the no-reading column.\n- V5 alert: the threshold rule plus the 00a · ScopeChip \"Your household\". Drawn in the alert column.\n- V6 still above threshold, no new push. Drawn in the still-above column.\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- ready [ready], at specimen time 7:10 AM.\n- stale [stale], at TODAY 6:10 PM: the hues and marker are unchanged. The caption becomes \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", and the mark is the 00a stale variant (text.primary at 50%, 3.39:1). The age words carry the staleness.\n- no reading [no-reading] (V4):\n  - The segments are filled surface.sunken and keep their keylines. There is no marker and no occupied outline, and the range labels stay.\n  - The value line is replaced by \"No reading for this address right now\", in body text.primary.\n  - When the provider itself failed, a second specimen adds a 00c · InlineErrorRow: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" + Retry.\n- alert [alert] (V5), at specimen time 4:10 PM: the threshold rule, \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the PANTOPUS NOTE.\n- still above threshold [still-above] (V6), at specimen time 4:10 PM: the same band as the alert, plus this line in bodySmall text.primary: \"Still above your alert level (101) since 4:00 PM. No new alert until it drops below 101 and rises again.\"\n- offline [offline], at specimen time 7:10 AM: the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" above the band, with the band drawn from cache.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light and · dark:\n- The V1 detail card at AQI 42 on iOS 393, with every callout.\n- A swatch row showing the six hues with their names and RGB values.\n- The marker contrast table.\n- In the dark version, the hues are unchanged, the gaps use dark raised #1E293B (the card surface), and the marker halo is #0F172A.\n00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: detail · instrument-row · widget-micro.\n- Columns: ready · stale · no-reading · alert · still-above · offline.\n- detail row:\n  - ready: V1 at AQI 42\n  - stale: V1 with the stale caption\n  - no-reading: V4, with the provider-failed specimen under it\n  - alert: V5 at AQI 118\n  - still-above: V6\n  - offline: V1 under the FreshnessLine\n- instrument-row row:\n  - ready: V2 at AQI 42, with the value \"AQI 42 · Good\" and the range labels\n  - stale: V2 with the stale caption\n  - no-reading: V2 greyed, with \"No reading for this address right now\"\n  - alert: V2 at AQI 118 with the threshold rule, and no health statement or PANTOPUS NOTE\n  - still-above: \"n/a — the still-above line belongs to the detail card; the row keeps its alert form\"\n  - offline: \"n/a — the host instrument shows one FreshnessLine for all four rows\"\n- widget-micro row:\n  - ready: V3, \"Air · Good 42\"\n  - stale: \"n/a — widget age is the widget's own 'As of' line (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - no-reading: V3 with greyed segments and \"Air · No reading\"\n  - alert: V3 at AQI 118, \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\", with no threshold rule\n  - still-above: \"n/a — widgets show only the current reading\"\n  - offline: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n- Under the grid, three extra specimens:\n  - the threshold 151 (not crossed) specimen at AQI 118 [extra key threshold-151]\n  - a clamp specimen at AQI 612, labelled \"specimen value\", with the marker at the right end and the value line \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · PM2.5\" [extra key clamp]\n  - six capsule markers, one on each segment, showing that the two-tone capsule passes 3:1 in both themes [extra key marker-on-every-hue]\n00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light and · dark:\n- A medium widget, 338×158pt, with 306pt of content width. The band is 120 × 8pt, with no range labels and no health statement.\n- Beside the band, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"Air · Good 42\". The alert version reads \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\". The short form \"Sensitive groups\" is allowed only in widgets.\n- The caption line, at 11pt or larger, is an XS Official ProvenanceMark followed by \"Official · AirNow · 7:00 AM\". The word \"Official\" is printed because the widget is a standalone surface (G8).\n- Draw the block three times:\n  - iOS in full colour.\n  - iOS tinted (accented) rendering, where every hue flattens to one tint. The gaps and keylines keep the six segments readable, the printed name carries the meaning, and the mark keeps its silhouette.\n  - Android, where the EPA hues stay fixed and never follow dynamic colour, while the rest of the widget follows the house tokens.\n- Widget composition belongs to f7-today-widget. Draw only this block, and label the rest of the outline \"owned by f7-today-widget\".\n00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light:\n- V5 alert at iOS AX5. The range labels leave the band and become a legend list below it, with one row per category. Each row is at least 44pt tall, grows with its text, and holds a 16pt swatch with its keyline, the EPA name and the range.\n- The value line, statement and note wrap, and the band keeps its full width.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- At AX sizes the V3 widget falls back to text only: \"Air · Good 42 · Official · AirNow 7:00 AM\".\n00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light: the light 01 and 02 artboards desaturated. Caption: \"Segments separated by gaps and keylines; category printed in words; marker by two-tone capsule.\"\n00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f1-today-air-band on iOS 393: the alert landing card with the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the header \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" (specimen time 4:10 PM).\n- (b) x-provenance-sheet on Android 412: the sheet header \"Where this fact comes from\" above the V1 band at AQI 42.\n- (c) f6-place-section-details on web-390: the V2 instrument row inside ScaleStrip.\n- Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f8-scale-strips and f8-compare-reveal → V2 inside ScaleStrip · f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet → V3 widget micro · f7-widget-tap-landing → V1 detail · f8-og-compare-card → the ScaleStrip OG Air row.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Summary: the value line (\"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\").\n- The band is one element. Print these spoken labels on 02, under their cells:\n  - Fixture (ready): \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM.\"\n  - Stale: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago.\"\n  - Alert: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n  - No reading: \"Air quality: No reading for this address right now.\"\n- The separators and keylines keep the band readable in greyscale. The printed name carries the meaning in tinted widgets.\n- The band itself is not a target. Retry and any row actions are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- \"Air quality index (AQI)\" is spelled out once per surface.\n\nCOPY\n- EPA category names verbatim: \"Good\", \"Moderate\", \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", \"Unhealthy\", \"Very Unhealthy\", \"Hazardous\".\n- EPA health text verbatim.\n- The short form \"Sensitive groups\" is allowed only in widgets.\n- Never write \"satisfactory for everyone\", \"air score\" or \"pollution level\".\n\nPLATFORMS: The Android widget keeps the EPA hues fixed and never uses dynamic colour. The iOS widget supports tinted rendering, as drawn on 03. Otherwise the geometry is identical on iOS, Android and web.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a proportional 0–500 track, draw six equal-width segments ending in \"301+\", because proportional widths squeeze the everyday 0–100 range and cannot place readings above 500.\n- Instead of brand blue or an invented ramp, draw the six EPA ColorVision Assist hues, because this is the authority's own scale.\n- Instead of printing the category or number on a fill, print them in text.primary on the card, because text on some hues fails contrast (text.primary on Hazardous is 1.31:1).\n- Instead of a disc marker, draw the two-tone vertical capsule, because a disc reads as ● Official.\n- Instead of \"Air quality is satisfactory for everyone\", print EPA's exact sentence, because a paraphrased health statement is an EPA reporting error.\n- Instead of hiding the band on a good day, draw it at AQI 42 with \"Good\", because a quiet reading is still a reading.\n- Instead of a hard-coded 101 mark, draw the rule at the person's chosen threshold, because the band must show the rule that actually fired.\n- Instead of dimming a stale mark with text.secondary at 50%, use the 00a stale variant plus the age words, because the dimmed mark falls below 3:1.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Every drawn 02 cell: \"AqiBand / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\". The detail × no-reading cell also publishes \"AqiBand / detail / no-reading-provider-failed / <light|dark>\".\n- The 02 extras: \"AqiBand / extra / threshold-151 / <light|dark>\", \"AqiBand / extra / clamp / <light|dark>\" and \"AqiBand / extra / marker-on-every-hue / <light|dark>\".\n- From 03: \"AqiBand / widget-micro / ready-tinted / <light|dark>\" and \"AqiBand / widget-micro / ready-android / <light|dark>\".\n- From 04: \"AqiBand / extra / ax5-legend / light\" and \"AqiBand / extra / widget-text-fallback / light\".\n- The six swatches are published only as part of AqiBand.\n\nNOTES (last batch: append an AqiBand part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: \"Air · Good 42\", \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\", \"Air · No reading\", \"Official · AirNow · 7:00 AM\", \"Air · Good 42 · Official · AirNow 7:00 AM\", \"PANTOPUS NOTE\", \"Your alert level is 101. You can change it in Notifications.\", \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", the still-above line, \"threshold 151 (not crossed)\", \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · PM2.5\", the stale and no-reading spoken labels, and the also-used-in line.\n- B. Assumptions: PM2.5 is the pollutant for AQI 42. The specimen clocks are 7:10 AM (ready, offline), 4:10 PM (alert, still above) and 6:10 PM (stale). The swatch names aqi.good … aqi.hazardous are board labels for the six EPA hues.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract example \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\" is drawn as \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", because AQI 118 does not cross 151 and 101 is the default threshold. The contract's contrast reasoning for keylines is restated with computed values (Good 1.22:1 and Moderate 1.54:1 on white, Hazardous 1.08:1 on dark raised).\n- D. Deviations: the stale mark uses the 00a stale variant (text.primary at 50%), not text.secondary at 50%.\n- E. Open question: confirm the PM2.5 sensitive-groups sentence against EPA TAD Table 4.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 9 artboards exist with the exact names below.\n- The 02 grid has 3 rows × 6 columns, with no blank cell and one reason per n/a cell. The three extras are drawn.\n- V1–V6 and all six states appear, and every spoken label above is printed.\n- No text sits on an AQI fill. The hues are identical in light, dark and tinted forms, apart from the tint flattening.\n- The marker is a two-tone capsule at every size, and the contrast table is printed.\n- The widget block prints \"Official\" next to its mark.\n- The only hex or RGB values on these artboards are the six swatches and the contrast tables.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (9 artboards plus the Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light\n4. 00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light\n5. 00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light\n6. 00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · dark\n8. 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n9. 00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · dark\n10. 00b · Notes (append AqiBand)"
