            "promptText": "Component 00b-03: FourteenDayStrip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The next two weeks at this address, drawn as a shape. The strip sits above list rows, and those rows are the real tap targets.\nUSED IN (print it): f5-today-calendar-strip, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, f1-today-tab, x-place-file.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 648px wide (616px of content), so each cell is 44px.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Header line above the strip: the summary label \"Next 14 days: 6 items\", in label 13/18 text.strong. This is the strip's one-sentence summary.\n- Strip: 14 equal cells across the card's content width, with today on the left. At 326pt the pitch is 23.3pt (the contract's phone range is about 23–26pt).\n  - The cells form one track with radius sm 6, a 1px text.secondary keyline and 1px text.secondary separators between cells.\n  - Cell height is 76pt, built from top to bottom:\n    - 6pt top padding\n    - up to 3 XS (12pt) ProvenanceMarks stacked with 4pt gaps (44pt)\n    - a 4pt gap\n    - a 16pt line reserved for \"+N\"\n    - 6pt bottom padding\n  - \"+N\" is in caption 12/16 text.strong (#F1F5F9 in dark mode), because the cell is sunken. It appears when a cell has 4 or more mark items, and the reserved line stays empty otherwise.\n  - All marks use one ink (text.secondary at full opacity) and are centred horizontally in the cell.\n- Cell fill: weekday cells are surface.sunken at 100%. Weekend cells are surface.sunken at 40%. The weekend is shown by lower opacity, not by a hue, and it is also named by the initials (or by the \"Sat–Sun\" labels where there are no initials).\n- Civic, state or county rule: a solid bar 4pt wide spanning the full cell height, in text.strong.\n  - If the cell has no other marks, the bar is centred.\n  - Otherwise the bar sits 2pt from the cell's left edge, and the marks shift 3pt right.\n  - A bar never counts toward the 3-mark limit.\n  - A statewide or county rule is never drawn as a dot. YearBand uses the same bar rule.\n- Holiday move: the mark is drawn on the moved day. The usual day gets a struck ghost: the same mark shape in full text.secondary ink (at least 3:1), crossed by a 1.5px diagonal strike in text.primary (#E5E7EB in dark mode). The strike carries the meaning, and the DateRow names the move in words.\n- Labels under the strip:\n  - Row 1: weekday initials under every cell, in caption text.secondary: \"M T W T F S S M T W T F S S\". Initials appear only where the pitch is 20pt or more, and they are never spoken.\n  - Row 2: anchors in captionMedium text.strong. \"Today\" is left-aligned under cell 1, and the week-start date \"Mon 26 Oct\" is left-aligned under cell 8.\n- Below the strip: one 00c · DateRow per item. The foot is a persistent 48pt row, \"+ Add a date\", with the plus glyph and label in primary.700 (#38BDF8 in dark mode).\n- Fixture window for HOME A, \"Your household\", Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov:\n\n  | Cell | Day | Item (DateRow title) | Mark |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 2 | Tue 20 Oct | Recycling and garbage | hollow (city schedule, not confirmed) |\n  | 5 | Fri 23 Oct | Clark Public Utilities bill | tick |\n  | 8 | Mon 26 Oct | Voter registration, online or mail, must arrive by | state bar |\n  | 9 | Tue 27 Oct | Garbage only | hollow |\n  | 10 | Wed 28 Oct | City of Vancouver water bill | tick |\n  | 14 | Sun 1 Nov | HOA dues | tick, weekend cell |\n\n  That is 6 items, so the summary reads \"Next 14 days: 6 items\". The DateRow line 2 dates follow R11 (\"Tomorrow\"; \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\"; \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\"; \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\").\n- Two extras for 01, each drawn as a separate specimen outside the fixture window and labelled \"specimen\" in the gutter:\n  - Overflow cell [extra key overflow-cell], Mon 2 Nov: the county rule \"Property tax 2nd half\" is the full-height bar, 2pt from the left edge. The cell has four mark items, all ticks: Comcast bill, \"Swap furnace filter\", \"Library books due\" and \"Drop off old paint\". Draw 3 marks shifted 3pt right, then \"+1\" in text.strong on the reserved line. Callout: \"Bar = county rule, not counted in +N; 4 marks → 3 + '+1'; 6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6 = 76pt\".\n  - Holiday-move pair [extra key holiday-move], PLACE B: the Thanksgiving notice for Thursday routes moves the usual Thu 26 Nov pickup to Fri 27 Nov. Draw the hollow mark on Fri 27 Nov and the struck ghost on Thu 26 Nov, with the DateRow \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\" and line 2 \"in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov\".\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 Today card [today-card]: as described above.\n- V2 widget medium [widget-medium], budgeted for the 338×158 widget, which has 306 × 126pt of content:\n  - The strip spans the full 306pt content width, so the pitch is 21.9pt.\n  - Cell height is 60pt: 6pt top · at most 2 XS marks with a 4pt gap (28pt) · 4pt · a 16pt \"+N\" line · 6pt bottom. With 3 or more mark items, the cell shows 1 mark and then \"+N\".\n  - Under the strip: one 16pt line holding only the anchor labels (\"Today\" and \"Mon 26 Oct\", at 11pt or larger, with no initials), plus \"Sat–Sun\" at 11pt text.secondary, centred under cells 6–7 and under cells 13–14.\n  - Then one 16pt legend line at 11pt text.secondary with S-size marks drawn inline: \"● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added\". This line prints the provenance words, because the widget is a standalone surface (G8).\n  - Height used: 60 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16 = 100pt. The remaining 26pt belongs to f7-today-widget's header line. Print this budget in the gutter.\n  - The widget draws no rows and no add row.\n- V3 year-band shaded window (x-place-file): the same 14 days drawn as the shaded window inside YearBand. It is drawn on 03 and 07 only, not in the grid. YearBand (component 00b-04) defines the band in full. For this crop, draw its phone form as follows, and label it \"window crop — YearBand defines the band\":\n  - 326pt wide, with 12 month columns of 27.2pt labelled \"Oct\" to \"Sep\" in caption text.secondary.\n  - Four 24pt lanes, 4pt apart, each with its label above it in captionMedium text.strong: \"You\", \"Your city\", \"Your county\", \"Your state\". Each lane has a surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary keyline with radius xs 4, and 1px text.secondary month separators.\n  - One XS mark per month per lane, centred, with a count numeral 1pt to its right when there are 2 or more. County and state rules are 4pt full-lane-height bars in text.strong.\n  - HOME A content: You has ticks with \"2\" in Oct, \"2\" in Nov, one in Dec and \"2\" in Mar. Your city has 1.5 × 8pt text.secondary ticks every week, with an XS hollow mark and \"Pickup every Tuesday · city schedule\" on its label line. Your county has a bar in Nov. Your state has bars in Oct and Nov.\n  - A 1.5px text.primary today rule at 19 Oct, and a surface.sunken wash from 19 Oct to 1 Nov across all lanes, with a 1px dashed text.secondary edge at 1 Nov. The legend under the band reads \"Shaded: next 14 days\".\n- V4 empty: drawn in the empty column. The cells are drawn with no marks. Under them is the 00d · QuietDayReceipt strip line \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\", then the \"+ Add a date\" row. The summary label reads \"Next 14 days: nothing on file\".\n- QuietDayReceipt line stand-in: one line with a 16pt bare stroked check glyph in text.secondary (a line-drawn check with no disc) and the sentence in bodySmall text.primary. The sentence always starts with \"Checked\", and the check never sits at a mark position. This is the one exception to G4: a bare stroke is not a ticked disc. It is listed as an open question for 00d.\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with 14 cell outlines on surface.sunken, no marks, no text, and a bar in place of the header. It reserves the full height (header + 76pt strip + label rows) and is static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready [ready].\n- empty [empty]: V4.\n- stale [stale]: each mark becomes the 00a stale variant (text.primary at 50%: 3.32:1 on weekday cells and 3.36:1 on weekend cells), and the 00a · FreshnessLine \"Updated 2h ago\" appears under the header. The words carry the staleness.\n- permission-denied [permission-denied]: the viewer may not add dates. The \"+ Add a date\" row is absent, and no ghosted row replaces it. The strip and rows are unchanged.\n- T1 [t1]: PLACE B, with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - One hollow mark on Thu 22 Oct, the next Thursday only, because the pickup frequency is Not set. Its DateRow title is \"Pickup day · frequency not set\", and its source is City of Camas.\n  - The state bar on Mon 26 Oct.\n  - Summary: \"Next 14 days: 2 items\".\n  - The \"+ Add a date\" row is present. Dates added here stay Only you.\n- error [error]: no strip is drawn. The strip's slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't load your dates just now\" + Retry. This is an error row, not an absence.\n- highlighted row [highlighted-row], on push arrival: after the push \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\", the Tue 20 Oct DateRow shows its highlighted state, and accessibility focus moves to that row. The strip itself is unchanged.\n  - Light: an infoBg wash with a 1px semantic.info outline.\n  - Dark: a dark base #0F172A wash with a 1px #38BDF8 outline. Its text is #E5E7EB (14.42:1).\n  - The highlight fades out over 300ms after 4s. Under Reduce Motion it appears and disappears without animation. Draw the start and end frames.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light:\n- V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including one on the 76pt cell-height budget.\n- The overflow cell and the holiday-move pair, each magnified 4× and labelled.\n- A contrast table with these R6 rows: text.secondary on base, on sunken and on a weekend cell; text.strong on sunken; primary.700 on base; and the stale mark on sunken and on a weekend cell.\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: today-card · widget-medium.\n- Columns: loading · ready · empty · stale · permission-denied · t1 · error · highlighted-row.\n- today-card row: every column is drawn as described in STATES. empty is V4, and error is the InlineErrorRow alone in the slot.\n- widget-medium row:\n  - loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n  - ready: V2 with the HOME A marks and the legend line\n  - empty: V2 cells with no marks, and \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" at 11pt in place of the legend line\n  - stale: \"n/a — widget age is the widget's own 'As of' line (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - permission-denied: \"n/a — the widget has no rows or add row\"\n  - t1: V2 with the PLACE B marks (Thu 22 Oct hollow, state bar on Mon 26 Oct) and the legend line\n  - error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - highlighted-row: \"n/a — the widget has no rows\"\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light and · dark:\n- V2 at true size inside a 338×158 outline. Leave the rest of the widget blank, label it \"owned by f7-today-widget\", and print the 100pt budget in the gutter.\n- Beside it, V3: the YearBand phone specimen with the Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov window shaded, and a leader line to the V1 strip showing that they are the same data. The bars match in both (the state bar on 26 Oct).\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light:\n- iOS: the strip as one adjustable element, with a focus outline around the whole strip. Show four consecutive steps (each swipe up or down moves one day), each in a speech bubble:\n  - \"Tuesday 20 October: Recycling and garbage, city schedule, on record, not confirmed\"\n  - \"Wednesday 21 October: nothing on file\"\n  - \"Thursday 22 October: nothing on file\"\n  - \"Friday 23 October: Clark Public Utilities bill, you added this\"\n  - Annotate: \"A tap on the strip scrolls to the rows.\"\n- Android: the same element, with the TalkBack custom actions \"Next day\" and \"Previous day\".\n- Web-390: the strip is hidden from assistive tech because the rows duplicate it. Annotate this, and add \"otherwise a list of full-date labels\".\n- Web-1440 (648px card, 616px content): per-cell tap exists only on desktop web.\n  - Each cell is a 44px-wide button with its own focus ring (R12).\n  - Activating a cell moves focus to that day's first row.\n  - Hover reveals nothing that is not already on screen.\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5. The cells keep their size.\n  - Initials are dropped: the pitch is still 23.3pt, and 43pt initials do not fit.\n  - The anchors become lines above the strip: \"Today · Mon 19 Oct\" and \"Mon 26 Oct\", on separate wrapped lines.\n  - A caption line below the strip keeps the weekend cue: \"Lighter cells are Sat and Sun\".\n  - The summary wraps, and the rows and add row grow.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- At AX sizes the V2 widget falls back to text only: \"Next 14 days: 6 items · Tomorrow: Recycling and garbage\".\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light: the light 02 artboard desaturated. Caption: \"Provenance by shape; rules by bar; weekends by opacity plus initials or 'Sat–Sun'; moves by strike; widget words by legend line; empty by the word 'Checked'.\"\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f5-today-calendar-strip on iOS 393: V1 with its rows and the legend line \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n- (b) f1-today-tab on Android 412: the strip card inside Today, under the ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- (c) x-place-file on web-1440: V1 with per-cell buttons, above the V3 window crop from 03.\n- Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet → V2 widget medium · f7-widget-tap-landing → V1 with the highlighted row.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Summary: the header label. On native, the strip is one adjustable element with the day readouts shown on 04; cells are not targets, and a tap on the strip scrolls to the list. On web-390 the strip is hidden when rows duplicate it, otherwise it is a list of full-date labels. Initials are never spoken.\n- Non-colour encoding: provenance by mark shape, rules by bar, moves by strike, weekends by opacity plus initials (or \"Sat–Sun\").\n- The add row is 48pt. Rows follow DateRow.\n\nCOPY\n- Summary pattern \"Next 14 days: N items\". Dates always show the weekday, and DateRow line 2 adds the relative count beyond tomorrow.\n- Pickup rows name the bins (\"Recycling and garbage\", \"Garbage only\"). Deadlines say \"must arrive by\". The add row reads exactly \"+ Add a date\".\n\nPLATFORMS: Per-cell tap exists only on desktop web. iOS uses an adjustable element, Android uses custom actions, and web-390 has no per-cell targets.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of colouring marks by class (pickup, civic, money, yours), draw one ink and let the DateRow KindGlyph carry the class, because hue alone fails for colour-blind viewers and in tinted views.\n- Instead of 6pt dots with ticks, draw 12pt XS ProvenanceMarks, because below 12pt the three shapes cannot be told apart.\n- Instead of 14 tiny tap targets, make the strip one element and the rows the targets, because 23pt cells fail the 44pt / 48dp rule.\n- Instead of a dot for a statewide or county deadline, draw a full-height bar, because a rule for a whole state or county is not an item at this address.\n- Instead of an even weekly rhythm through a holiday week, draw the moved day and a struck ghost, because holiday moves are the core pickup job.\n- Instead of dimming ghosts or stale marks in text.secondary, keep the ghost at full ink with a strike and use the 00a stale variant, because a dimmed text.secondary mark is 1.91:1 on sunken and its shape is lost.\n- Instead of text.secondary for \"+N\" on a sunken cell, use text.strong, because text.secondary on sunken is 4.39:1.\n- Instead of a ticked disc in the empty receipt, draw a bare stroked check followed by \"Checked\", because the ticked disc means \"You added this\".\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"FourteenDayStrip / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: overflow-cell and holiday-move (01, light), year-band-window (03, light and dark), web-1440-cell-buttons (04, light), widget-text-fallback (05, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a FourteenDayStrip part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: every quoted string here that is not a fixture or contract string (the three extra item names, \"Pickup day · frequency not set\", the other summaries, the error sentence, the widget legend, \"Sat–Sun\", the AX5 lines, the VoiceOver readouts, \"Next day\", \"Previous day\", the DateRow line 2 dates, the also-used-in line).\n- B. Assumptions: the cell is 76pt (6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6); the widget cell is 60pt with at most 2 marks before \"+N\", to fit 100pt of the 158pt widget. PLACE B's frequency is Not set, so only Thu 22 Oct is drawn; the Thanksgiving move is drawn because the City of Camas notice covers every Thursday route. The overflow cell (Mon 2 Nov) is a separate specimen outside the window. The strip counts pickups as items; YearBand does not count its rhythm as dates.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract's \"Next 14 days: 9 items\" → the fixture count \"Next 14 days: 6 items\". The empty line follows QuietDayReceipt (\"next two weeks\"), not the brief's \"next 14 days\".\n- D. Deviations: stale marks use the 00a stale variant, not text.secondary at 50%; the ghost stays at full ink with a strike.\n- E. Open question for 00d: QuietDayReceipt uses a bare stroked check, while G4 reserves the ticked disc for \"You added this\" and legends print \"✓ You added this\". Keep the exemption (bare stroke, no disc, always followed by \"Checked\"), or give the QuietDayReceipt CheckItems a glyph that is not a check?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 9 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (2 × 8, one reason per n/a).\n- V1–V4, all eight states and both extras are drawn. The 76pt cell, 60pt widget cell and 100pt budget add up.\n- Every mark is at least 3:1, rules are bars, and only the web-1440 cells are targets (44px).\n- The widget prints provenance words in its legend line. Notes holds the FourteenDayStrip entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (9 artboards plus the Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light\n4. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light\n5. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light\n6. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light\n8. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n9. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark\n10. 00b · Notes (append FourteenDayStrip)"
