            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-04: YearBand. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): Twelve months of dated rules in four source lanes. It shows the same data as FourteenDayStrip at a longer zoom.\nUSED IN (print it): x-place-file, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 880px wide (848px of content).\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy-phone, with a callout on every part)\n- Summary header in label 13/18 text.strong: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates. Next, in 4 days: Clark Public Utilities bill due Fri 23 Oct.\" The pickup rhythm is not counted as dates.\n- Month columns: 12, starting with the current month, with three-letter labels in caption text.secondary: \"Oct Nov Dec Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep\". The caption \"2027\" sits above \"Jan\".\n- Phone geometry: 326pt wide, so each column is 27.2pt.\n- Four lanes, in this order and with these exact labels: \"You\" · \"Your city\" · \"Your county\" · \"Your state\".\n  - On phones, each label sits above its lane in captionMedium text.strong (a 16pt line). At 768px and wider, the labels sit in a 128px left column.\n  - Each lane track is 24pt tall, with a surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary keyline, radius xs 4, and 1px text.secondary month separators. Lanes are 4pt apart.\n- Marks on phones are grouped per month per lane:\n  - one XS 12pt ProvenanceMark, centred in the month column\n  - a count numeral in captionMedium text.primary, 1pt to the right of the mark, when the month has 2 or more items\n  - if a cluster mixes provenance, the hollow mark (the least certain), with the rows listing each item\n  - Exact-day placement happens only at 768px and wider.\n- Rules: county and state rules are solid bars, 4pt wide and the full lane height, in text.strong, in the \"Your county\" and \"Your state\" lanes. FourteenDayStrip uses the same bar rule. On phones the bar is centred in its month column, with a count numeral when there are 2 or more.\n- Collision rule at 768px and wider: build clusters from left to right within each lane. A mark or bar whose centre is less than 14px from the first item of the current cluster joins that cluster. A cluster is drawn as one item at its earliest day, with a count numeral 1pt to its right. A mixed-provenance cluster shows the hollow mark, as on phones.\n- Today rule: a 1.5px text.primary vertical line through all four lanes at 19 Oct (19/31 of the Oct column), with \"Today\" in caption text.primary above the month labels.\n- Shaded 14-day window: a surface.sunken wash behind the marks from 19 Oct to 1 Nov across all lanes, with a 1px dashed text.secondary edge at 1 Nov. The legend line under the band reads \"Shaded: next 14 days\".\n- Pickup rhythm, in the \"Your city\" lane:\n  - The lane's provenance sits on its label line: after \"Your city\" come an XS hollow ProvenanceMark and the lane caption \"Pickup every Tuesday · city schedule\" in caption text.secondary. At 768px and wider, the mark and caption sit in the label column under \"Your city\".\n  - The rhythm is drawn as 1.5 × 8pt ticks in text.secondary (4.83:1), one per service week, centred vertically in the lane.\n  - After the last published city calendar (Dec 2026), the lane keyline for Jan–Sep turns dashed (3 on, 2 off), with a second lane caption: \"Projected after Dec 2026 (last published city calendar)\".\n  - Holiday moves on phones: that week's tick is drawn 11pt tall with a 1.5px strike. At 768px and wider, when the moved day is at least 14px from the usual day, the tick moves to the real day and a struck ghost sits on the usual day (the same shape at full ink, as in FourteenDayStrip). When the two days are closer than 14px, use the phone form.\n- The band reserves its full height while loading.\n- Caption under the band, in text.secondary: \"The same dates are listed below.\" Then 00c · DateRow and 00c · FactRow rows follow. Those rows are the table.\n- Fixture data for HOME A:\n  - You: an Oct cluster \"2\" (Clark Public Utilities bill Fri 23 Oct; City of Vancouver water bill Wed 28 Oct) · a Nov cluster \"2\" (HOA dues Sun 1 Nov; Comcast bill Mon 2 Nov) · a Dec mark (water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec) · a Mar cluster \"2\" (lease notice deadline Mon 1 Mar; lease ends Wed 31 Mar). All are ticks (You added this).\n  - Your city: the weekly Tuesday pickup rhythm, on record but not confirmed (the hollow mark and caption on the label line). There is no holiday move in the published window.\n  - Your county: a bar in Nov (property tax 2nd half due Mon 2 Nov). The detail row may add \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n  - Your state: bars in Oct (online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct) and Nov (in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov).\n  - Total: 10 dates (7 in You, 1 in Your county, 2 in Your state).\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 place file, HOME A [place-file-home-a]: as described above.\n- V1 place file, PLACE B [place-file-place-b], with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\":\n  - The \"You\" lane is empty.\n  - \"Your city\" has no weekly rhythm, because the frequency is Not set. It shows one tick on the next Thursday (Thu 22 Oct) and the Thanksgiving move in Nov (\"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", from the published 2026 calendar, so not projected). Its label line has the XS hollow mark and the lane caption \"Pickup day Thursday · frequency not set\".\n  - \"Your county\": a bar in Nov. \"Your state\": bars in Oct and Nov.\n  - Summary: \"Next 12 months: 3 dates. Next, in 7 days: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- V2 widget large [widget-large], 338×354pt, with 306pt of content width:\n  - Columns are 25.5pt wide. The lane labels use place names: \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\" (for PLACE B: \"You · Camas · Clark County · Washington\").\n  - The city lane's hollow mark is followed by the printed word \"On record\".\n  - Under the band, one legend line at 11pt text.secondary with S-size marks drawn inline: \"● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added · ▮ Rule\". It prints the words for the filled, ticked and bar items, because the widget is a standalone surface (G8).\n  - Count numerals sit below the mark. All text is at least 11pt.\n  - The widget label is \"Larkspur Loop\".\n  - At AX sizes it drops to text (see 05).\n- V3 gallery sample [gallery-sample]: V2 with the same HOME A data, drawn static inside a gallery preview frame.\n- V4 empty checked [empty-checked]: the lanes, month labels and today rule are drawn with no marks, bars or rhythm. Under them is the 00d · QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\".\n  - QuietDayReceipt line stand-in: one line with a 16pt bare stroked check glyph in text.secondary (a line-drawn check, no disc) and the sentence in bodySmall text.primary. The sentence always starts with \"Checked\", and the check never sits at a mark position. This is the one exception to G4, and it is listed as an open question for 00d (FourteenDayStrip already recorded it).\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with four lane outlines on surface.sunken, reserving the exact final height. It is static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready [ready].\n- empty checked [empty-checked]: V4.\n- error [error]: the band is not drawn. Its slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't load the next 12 months just now\" + Retry. This is an error row, not an absence.\n- offline [offline]: the band is drawn from cache under the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\".\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light:\n- V1 HOME A on iOS 393 with every callout, including one on the county bar: \"county rule = bar, same as FourteenDayStrip\".\n- A contrast table with these R6 rows: text.secondary on base and on sunken, text.strong on sunken, and text.strong on base (the bars).\n00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: place-file-home-a · place-file-place-b · widget-large · gallery-sample · empty-checked.\n- Columns: loading · ready · empty-checked · error · offline.\n- place-file-home-a and place-file-place-b: every column is drawn as described in STATES. empty-checked is V4 under that place's header.\n- widget-large:\n  - loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n  - ready: V2\n  - empty-checked: V2 with no marks, and \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" in place of the legend line\n  - error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - offline: V2 under the widget FreshnessLine form \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (the 00a widget-horizon form; the time is today's, so no weekday)\n- gallery-sample:\n  - ready: V3\n  - loading, empty-checked, error and offline: \"n/a — the gallery shows a static sample\"\n- empty-checked:\n  - empty-checked: V4\n  - loading: the HOME A skeleton\n  - ready: \"n/a — V4 is the empty state\"\n  - error: \"n/a — an error is not a checked result; see the place-file rows\"\n  - offline: V4 under the FreshnessLine\n00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light:\n- V1 on web-1440 in the 880px card (848px content), with the 128px label column and 60px month columns (128 + 12 × 60 = 848px).\n- Every mark and bar sits on its exact day, subject to the collision rule. The state bars are at 26 Oct and 3 Nov, and the county bar is at 2 Nov.\n- In the You lane, 23 Oct and 28 Oct are about 10px apart, so they draw as one mark at 23 Oct with \"2\". 1 Nov and 2 Nov are about 2px apart, so they draw as one mark at 1 Nov with \"2\". 1 Mar and 31 Mar stay separate. Callout on the 1 Nov + 2 Nov pair: \"less than 14px apart → one mark + count numeral\".\n- In the state lane, 26 Oct and 3 Nov are about 16px apart, so they stay separate.\n- The Tuesday ticks sit on exact Tuesdays, about 13.5px apart. Ticks are rhythm, not items, so the collision rule does not merge them.\n- Below it, a PLACE B inset band. Its Thanksgiving move (Thu 26 Nov → Fri 27 Nov) is about 2px apart, so it uses the phone form: an 11pt struck tick. Callout: \"moved day under 14px from usual day → phone form\".\n- Annotate: \"Marks are not targets; the rows below are.\"\n00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light and · dark:\n- V2 at true size, with its legend line, inside a 338×354 outline. Label the rest of the widget \"owned by f7-today-widget\".\n- V3 inside an iOS gallery preview and inside an Android widget-picker preview.\n- V2 under iOS tinted rendering: every mark keeps its silhouette, and the legend words carry the meaning.\n00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5. The lanes keep their geometry. The month labels drop to every third month (\"Oct\", \"Jan\", \"Apr\", \"Jul\") on a line above the band. The lane labels and lane captions wrap above the lanes, and the summary wraps.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- At AX sizes V2 drops to text: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates\", then three lines: \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Clark Public Utilities bill\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Voter registration must arrive by\" · \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct · City of Vancouver water bill\". The widget shows no amounts.\n00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light: the light 02 artboard desaturated. Caption: \"Lanes by label; county and state rules by bar; city lane provenance by hollow mark and caption; projected by dashed keyline and caption; window by wash plus dashed edge; widget words by legend line; empty by the word 'Checked'.\"\n00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) x-place-file on iOS 393: the band under the place file header, with its rows.\n- (b) x-place-file on Android 412: the PLACE B place file with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- (c) f7-widget-gallery on iOS: the V3 sample in the gallery.\n- Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget → V2 widget large.\"\nConsistency check (batch 3): compare the V3 window crops on 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window (light and dark) and the crop (c) on 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context with this anatomy. If any part differs, update those crops to match YearBand exactly, and change nothing else on those artboards.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Summary: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates. Next, in 4 days: Clark Public Utilities bill due Fri 23 Oct.\" The rows below are the table, and the caption under the band says so.\n- On native, the band is one element with adjustable month cells (each swipe up or down moves one month). Print these readouts on 01:\n  - October: \"October: 3 dates. Clark Public Utilities bill due Friday 23 October, you added this. Voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October, Washington, official. City of Vancouver water bill due Wednesday 28 October, you added this. Pickup every Tuesday, city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n  - November: \"November: 4 dates. HOA dues due Sunday 1 November, you added this. Comcast bill due Monday 2 November, you added this. Property tax 2nd half due Monday 2 November, Clark County, official. Voting in person until 8 PM Tuesday 3 November, Washington, official. Pickup every Tuesday, city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- On web, the band is one image with the summary as its text alternative.\n- Marks are never targets. Provenance is carried by shape, and rules by bar.\n\nCOPY\n- Lane labels are exactly \"You · Your city · Your county · Your state\". On widgets they are place names: \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\" for HOME A.\n- Deadlines say \"must arrive by\". Dates show the weekday. Summary sentences and widget lines add the relative count beyond tomorrow.\n\nPLATFORMS: Phones group marks by month. Screens 768px and wider place them on the exact day under the collision rule. Native uses adjustable month cells. Otherwise the geometry is identical.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a heatmap of busy months, draw marks with count numerals in labelled lanes, because colour intensity hides what the dates are and who set them.\n- Instead of collapsing the four lanes into one row, keep You · Your city · Your county · Your state, because the source of a rule matters as much as its date.\n- Instead of day-accurate dots on a phone, draw one cluster per month with a count, because 27pt columns cannot place days legibly.\n- Instead of overlapping marks on desktop, merge marks less than 14px apart into one mark with a count, because overlapping 12pt shapes cannot be read.\n- Instead of a filled dot for a county rule, draw a full-height bar, because the strip and the band show the same data and must encode it the same way.\n- Instead of an unlabelled 1px rhythm, draw 1.5px ticks with a hollow mark and the \"city schedule\" caption, because an unconfirmed schedule must look unconfirmed.\n- Instead of a dimmed ghost, keep the ghost at full ink with a strike, because a dimmed mark falls below 3:1.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"YearBand / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: desktop-exact-day and desktop-place-b-inset (03, light), widget-large-tinted (04, light and dark), gallery-android (04, light and dark), widget-text-fallback (05, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a YearBand part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: both summaries; \"Shaded: next 14 days\"; \"Pickup every Tuesday · city schedule\"; \"Pickup day Thursday · frequency not set\"; \"Projected after Dec 2026 (last published city calendar)\"; \"The same dates are listed below.\"; \"We couldn't load the next 12 months just now\"; \"On record\"; \"● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added · ▮ Rule\"; the widget text lines; the October and November readouts; the specimen item names \"lease notice deadline\" and \"water-heater warranty ends\"; the also-used-in line.\n- B. Assumptions: the pickup rhythm is not counted in \"N dates\" (the strip does count pickups). County rules are bars, as in FourteenDayStrip. The desktop label column is 128px, and the collision threshold is 14px. PLACE B shows only its next Thursday, plus the Thanksgiving move because the City of Camas notice covers every Thursday route.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract's \"Next 12 months: 9 dates. Next: Furnace warranty ends Nov 14.\" is replaced by fixture data. The contract's widget lane names used Camas, which is PLACE B's city; HOME A uses \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\". Summary sentences and widget lines carry the relative count (\"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"), and the widget line was reworded as \"Voter registration must arrive by\". The contract's widget form \"As of Mon 7:40 AM\" is drawn as \"As of 7:40 AM\", matching 00a.\n- D. Deviations: the contract draws only statewide rules as bars; this board draws county rules as bars too, so YearBand matches FourteenDayStrip.\n- E. Open question: the native month readouts give absolute dates only (\"due Friday 23 October\"), although dates beyond tomorrow normally add a relative count. Keep them absolute, or add \"in 4 days\"?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 9 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (5 × 5, one reason per n/a).\n- V1 (HOME A and PLACE B), V2–V4 and all five states are drawn. The 848px desktop grid adds up, and no marks overlap.\n- County and state rules are bars in every lane and size. Every mark is at least 3:1.\n- The widget prints provenance words in its legend line, and all widget text is at least 11pt.\n- The FourteenDayStrip window crops match this band. Notes holds the YearBand entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (9 artboards plus the Notes update and one consistency check, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light\n2. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light\n4. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light\n5. 00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light\n6. 00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light\n8. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n9. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · dark\n10. 00b · Notes (append YearBand)\nBatch 3 (consistency check; update an artboard only if its crop differs):\n11. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light\n12. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark\n13. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light"
          },
          {
            "id": "00b-05",
            "component": "SlotMeter",
            "artboards": [
              "00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light",
              "00b · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-05: SlotMeter. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): An honest, dated Founding Neighbor window. When anything is uncertain, it fails closed.\nUSED IN (print it): f9-founding-meter-preview, f9-block-founders-panel, f9-nearby-cells-map, f9-verification-promise-copy, f9-invite-rewards-card.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Heading \"Founding Neighbor\" in bodyMedium text.primary.\n- Segments: five bounded capsules, each 40 × 12pt, radius pill, with 4pt gaps (216pt in total). Taken segments come first, from the left.\n  - Taken: a solid primary.600 fill with a 1.5px primary.700 edge (#38BDF8 in dark mode, per R5).\n  - Open: a surface.base fill with 45° diagonal hatch lines (1.5px, every 4pt) in text.secondary, and a 1.5px text.secondary edge.\n  - The fixture has 2 taken and 3 open.\n- Numeral label, 8pt to the right of the segments, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"3 of 5 open\". This count of open slots is the one sanctioned \"N of M\" in this component. It counts what is left and never measures progress.\n- Elapsed bar, 8pt below the segments: 4 × 216pt, radius pill.\n  - The elapsed part is a solid text.secondary fill. The remaining part is an unfilled 1px text.secondary outline (never a border token).\n  - The fixture window opened Mon 5 Oct and closes Tue 27 Oct, and TODAY is Mon 19 Oct, so the elapsed part is 138pt wide. Callout: \"elapsed 138pt of 216pt; decorative\".\n  - The bar is decorative and hidden from assistive tech, because the date pill carries the meaning.\n- Date pill, 8pt below the bar: a neutral pill 24pt tall with a surface.sunken fill, holding a 12pt calendar glyph and the label \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" in label 13/18, both in text.strong.\n- RankBadge (part of this specimen, published only with SlotMeter):\n  - It always sits below the meter, at least 24pt away, and never in the same row or sentence as the tier.\n  - A separate squared shape, 120 × 64pt, radius md 8, with a surface.sunken fill, a 1px text.secondary edge, 12pt horizontal padding (96pt of text width) and 8pt vertical padding.\n  - The overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\" in 11/16/600 caps +0.5 text.strong, then the numeral \"#3\" in h2 24/32/600 text.primary.\n  - If the overline is wider than 96pt, it breaks as \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\", and the badge grows to 80pt tall (8 + 16 + 16 + 32 + 8).\n- A contrast table on 01 with these R6 rows: the primary.600 fill on base, primary.700 on base, text.secondary on base, and text.strong on sunken.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 preview card [preview-card] (f9-founding-meter-preview, PLACE B): a card holding the heading, the meter, the date pill and the caption \"A badge — no money or fee change. You can still claim this address.\" in bodySmall text.secondary.\n- V2 Block Founders panel [block-founders-panel] (f9-block-founders-panel, HOME A): the meter and date pill in the panel's tier section, and the RankBadge \"#3\" in a separate rank section below it.\n- V3 wall line replacement [wall-line]: body text.primary only, with no meter: \"3 Founding Neighbor slots are still open on this block.\"\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- open [open].\n- closed [closed]: absent. Zero open slots counts as closed, so an empty meter is never drawn.\n- lookup failed [lookup-failed]: the entire card is absent. For V3, the line is absent.\n- Absence specimens (closed and lookup failed): draw the host context around the gap. In the gutter, add a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation box reading \"Nothing renders here. No space is reserved and no message is shown.\" The box is an annotation, not UI.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light: V1 at true size with every callout, the RankBadge 24pt below it, a taken and an open segment magnified 4×, and the contrast table.\n00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: preview-card · block-founders-panel · wall-line.\n- Columns: open · closed · lookup-failed.\n- Every closed and lookup-failed cell is an absence specimen: preview-card shows the PLACE B preview without the card, block-founders-panel shows the panel without its tier and rank sections, and wall-line shows the cells-map wall without the line.\n- Under the grid, one extra absence specimen [extra key zero-open], with the gutter label \"0 of 5 open → treated as closed\".\n- In dark mode, the taken fill stays primary.600 (3.57:1 on dark raised) with a #38BDF8 edge. The open fill becomes dark base #0F172A, and the hatch, the open edges and the elapsed bar use dark text.secondary (5.71:1 on dark raised).\n00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light: one frame with three encodings side by side, each labelled:\n- the SlotMeter (solid vs hatched, plus \"3 of 5 open\")\n- the PublicPointMap cells-map bucket labels: four small rectangles with a 1px text.secondary outline and a 70% surface.base fill, each printing \"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" or \"16+\" in label 13/18 text.primary\n- the 00a · ProvenanceMark legend \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\", with drawn marks\n- Caption: \"Solid vs hatched means taken vs open. Filled vs hollow means provenance only.\"\n00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5: the segments keep their size, the numeral label moves below the segments, the date pill grows and wraps (it becomes a rounded rectangle, radius lg 12), and the RankBadge grows vertically with \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\" on two lines.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- V1 and V2 desaturated, captioned \"Taken vs open by texture plus numeral.\"\n00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f9-founding-meter-preview on web-390: V1 on the PLACE B preview.\n- (b) f9-block-founders-panel on iOS 393: V2.\n- (c) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 as the wall line. Beside it, f9-verification-promise-copy and f9-invite-rewards-card, each showing one line that names the tier, \"Founding Neighbor · 3 of 5 open · Closes Tue 27 Oct\", and never the rank in the same sentence.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The meter is one element. Its summary and spoken label, printed on 01: \"Founding Neighbor slots: 3 of 5 open, closes Tuesday 27 October.\"\n- The RankBadge reads \"Block Founder number 3\".\n- Taken vs open is carried by solid vs hatched, plus the numeral.\n- The meter is not a target. Any card action is 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- Absent states are silent: nothing is announced.\n\nCOPY\n- Never write \"permanent\" unless the data model guarantees it.\n- Rank (\"Block Founder #3\") and tier (\"Founding Neighbor\") never share a sentence.\n- Closing dates are written as dates, never as \"closes in 6 days\" or hh:mm.\n\nPLATFORMS: identical on iOS, Android and web. Only the target minimums differ.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of hollow segments for open slots, draw hatched segments with an ink edge, because hollow means \"on record, not confirmed\".\n- Instead of a warning-tinted pill, draw a neutral surface.sunken pill, because a deadline for a badge is not an alarm.\n- Instead of an hh:mm or \"closes in 6 days\" countdown, print \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because live countdowns manufacture urgency.\n- Instead of a border-token fill for the remaining time, draw a text.secondary outline, because border tokens are never the only edge of a segment.\n- Instead of a 2px elapsed bar, draw a 4pt bar, because a 1px outline cannot be drawn around a 2px shape.\n- Instead of an empty meter at 0 open, or a meter shown after a failed lookup, render nothing, because the meter must never promise a slot the system cannot honour.\n- Instead of a disc or ring for the rank, draw the squared RankBadge, because discs and rings mean provenance.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each 02 cell: \"SlotMeter / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\". Absence cells are published too, as the rule that nothing renders.\n- Extras: zero-open (02, light and dark), rank-badge (01, light), ax5 (04, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a SlotMeter part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: \"Founding Neighbor\"; \"3 of 5 open\"; \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\"; \"BLOCK FOUNDER\"; \"#3\"; the V1 caption; \"Founding Neighbor · 3 of 5 open · Closes Tue 27 Oct\"; \"Block Founder number 3\"; the absence annotation; \"0 of 5 open → treated as closed\".\n- B. Assumptions: the fixture window opened Mon 5 Oct and closes Tue 27 Oct, with 2 of 5 slots taken. The RankBadge is 120 × 64pt, growing to 80pt when the overline breaks.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract example \"Closes Tue, Sep 22\" became \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because Tue 22 Sep is before TODAY and that window would already be closed. The contract's spoken \"closes Tuesday September 22\" follows it.\n- D. Deviations: the contract's \"2px elapsed bar\" is drawn 4pt tall, with an outlined remaining part, because a 1px outline cannot surround a 2px bar.\n- E. Open question (add it to YearBand's relative-count question): \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" has no relative count, although dates beyond tomorrow normally add one (\"in 8 days\"). This follows the no-countdown rule for the founding window. Keep it?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 6 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (3 × 3).\n- Closed, lookup-failed and 0-open all render nothing and are drawn as absence specimens.\n- Taken vs open is solid vs hatched with an ink edge. No segment is hollow, and nothing is warning-tinted.\n- \"N of M\" appears only as \"3 of 5 open\" and the \"0 of 5 open\" annotation. No countdown appears.\n- The rank and the tier never share a row or sentence. Notes holds the SlotMeter entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (6 artboards plus the Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light\n4. 00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n5. 00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light\nBatch 2:\n6. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n7. 00b · Notes (append SlotMeter)"
