            "promptText": "Component 00b-06: PublicPointMap. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): Shows exactly where neighbours see a post, drawn at true scale from the server's stable public point.\nUSED IN (print it): f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part; the address is HOME A and the viewer is Maya Chen)\n- Map thumb: 16:9, 326 × 183pt inside the card, radius md 8, with a 1px text.secondary edge.\n  - The base map uses neutral tokens only: land is surface.sunken, and streets are 4pt surface.base lines with 1px text.secondary casing. No ramp and no brand tint.\n  - Street labels are in caption 12/16 text.strong with a 2px surface.base halo: \"NE 18th St\", \"NE 138th Ave\", \"NE 23rd St\".\n- The frame is centred on the public pin, never on the home. No home marker appears anywhere.\n- Public pin: a single 24pt teardrop in text.primary with a 2px surface.base halo and a 6pt surface.base centre.\n- Pin label chip, above the pin: a pill in surface.base with a 1px text.secondary edge and shadow md, reading \"What neighbors see\" in label 13/18 text.primary.\n- Scale bar, bottom left, on an 80% surface.base plate: a 1.5px text.primary line with end ticks, in tenths of a mile (\"0\", \"0.1\", \"0.2 mi\"). At this zoom the thumb spans about 0.8 mi, so 0.2 mi = 81pt.\n- Caption under the map, in bodySmall text.primary. It is the map's one-sentence summary: \"Neighbors see your posts at this spot, the same spot every time, about 0.3 mi from your address.\"\n- A row under the caption belongs to f9-privacy-mirror; draw it only in context: \"Hidden from neighbors: your street address, your home on the map\".\n- Controls, 8pt below the caption (or 8pt below the map when there is no caption):\n  - Every button is 44 × 44pt on iOS and web and 48 × 48dp on Android, with radius md 8, a surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary edge and a 20pt text.primary glyph. The accessible names are the words below.\n  - The same two-row cluster is used at every size. On the left edge of the content width is a zoom column: \"Zoom in\" (+) above \"Zoom out\" (−), 8pt apart. On the right edge is a 3 × 2 arrow pad with 8pt gaps. Its top row holds \"Move map up\" (↑) in the middle slot. Its bottom row holds \"Move map left\" (←), \"Move map down\" (↓) and \"Move map right\" (→).\n  - Size: the arrow pad is 148pt wide on iOS and web (3 × 44 + 2 × 8) and 160dp on Android. The whole cluster needs at least 208pt (224dp on Android) with a 16pt minimum gap between the column and the pad, so it fits 326pt. The cluster is 96pt tall on iOS and web and 104dp on Android.\n  - Focus order: Zoom in, Zoom out, Move map up, Move map left, Move map down, Move map right, then List cells when present.\n- Cells-map parts (V3):\n  - Cells are rectangles with a 1px text.secondary outline and a 70% surface.base fill.\n  - Each cell prints its bucket label centred in label 13/18 text.primary: \"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" or \"16+\".\n  - The user's cell gets a 2px primary.600 inner outline, drawn inside its rectangle (the contract calls it a ring; #38BDF8 in dark mode), and the caption \"Your cell\" inside it, in caption text.primary.\n  - \"List cells\" is a text button (primary.700; #38BDF8 in dark mode) on its own third row, 8pt below the controls, left-aligned and 44pt tall (48dp on Android). The V3 controls block is therefore 148pt tall on iOS and web (96 + 8 + 44) and 160dp on Android (104 + 8 + 48).\n- A contrast table on 01 with these R6 rows: text.secondary on base and on sunken, text.strong on sunken, text.primary on sunken, and primary.700 on base.\n\nPENDING DECISION: range box R (not a variant; never published)\n- The ±0.005° box is centred on the home by definition, so drawing it may reveal the home. Until the founder answers the open question, draw R only on 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light, inside a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation frame labelled \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\". Do not draw it on any other artboard.\n- How to draw it: the real box, about 1.11 km tall × 0.78 km wide (about 0.69 × 0.49 mi), as a 1.5px dashed text.secondary rectangle with no fill. Use a zoom where the 326pt thumb spans about 1.6 mi, so the box is about 141 × 99pt and fits inside the 183pt-tall thumb with a margin. The scale bar reads \"0\", \"0.25\", \"0.5 mi\" (0.25 mi = 51pt). The box sits off-centre in the frame.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 privacy mirror [privacy-mirror]: as described above.\n- V2 composer one-liner [composer-one-liner]: a row at least 44pt tall with a 16pt pin glyph in text.secondary, the bodySmall text.primary line \"Neighbors see this post at the same spot as your other posts, about 0.3 mi from your address.\", and a trailing 44pt text button \"See the spot\" (primary.700; #38BDF8 in dark mode) that opens V1. No map is drawn.\n- V3 cells map [cells-map]:\n  - A 326 × 326pt map with 9 cell rectangles in a 3 × 3 grid, with the user's cell in the centre. Names and buckets:\n    - top row: North-west 0 · North 1–5 · North-east 1–5\n    - middle row: West 6–15 · Your cell 6–15 · East 16+\n    - bottom row: South-west 0 · South 0 · South-east 1–5\n  - The summary line \"14 neighbor posts in your cell in 30 days. 3 Pantopus posts not counted.\" in bodySmall text.primary.\n  - The 00a · FreshnessLine \"Updated 12m ago\".\n  - The controls with the \"List cells\" row.\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- ready [ready].\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton panel, a surface.sunken 16:9 block (square for V3), with the controls drawn as outlines at their reserved height (96pt, or 148pt for V3). It is static under Reduce Motion. V2 shows its text immediately.\n- vector fallback [vector-fallback]: when tiles fail, land is surface.base and streets are 1px text.secondary lines. The labels, pin, scale bar and caption stay. The caption \"Simplified map\" sits above the thumb.\n- offline [offline]:\n  - With a cache: the cached map under the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\". The pan and zoom buttons are disabled, with the reason caption \"Moving the map needs a connection.\"\n  - With no cache: the reserved 16:9 slot (square for V3) is a surface.sunken block with the centred line \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\" in body text.strong. The caption stays, and the buttons are disabled.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light: V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including the controls cluster geometry, and the contrast table. Beside it, the pending-decision frame holding R.\n00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: privacy-mirror · composer-one-liner · cells-map.\n- Columns: ready · loading · vector-fallback · offline.\n- privacy-mirror × offline and cells-map × offline: draw the cached form and the no-cache form, stacked in the cell.\n- composer-one-liner:\n  - loading: the line as in ready, because it shows its text immediately.\n  - vector-fallback: \"n/a — no map drawn\".\n  - offline: the line unchanged, because the composer owns the offline notice.\n- Dark base map: land is dark surface.raised, streets are dark surface.base with dark text.secondary casing, the pin core is #E5E7EB with a #0F172A halo, and the user's cell outline is #38BDF8.\n00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light: V3 on Android 412 with its controls. Beside it, the \"List cells\" view: nine 48dp rows, each giving a cell name, its bucket and its lock state.\n- \"Your cell · 6–15 · Detail open\"\n- \"North-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"North of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"North-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"West of your cell · 6–15 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"East of your cell · 16+ · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- The locked tier only states its requirement. Nothing is blurred or fogged.\n00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5. The map keeps its width, and the caption, chip and street labels grow. If the chip would be wider than the map, it moves under the map as a text line: \"What neighbors see: the pin on this map\".\n- The glyph buttons keep their size and the two-row cluster. On V3, \"List cells\" wraps and grows.\n- V1 at Android 200%.\n- V1 and V3 desaturated, captioned \"Pin by shape and label; buckets by printed numbers; your cell by outline width and words.\"\n00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f9-privacy-mirror on iOS 393: V1 with the hidden-from-neighbors row and a neighbour feed-card header.\n- (b) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 with the summary line.\n- (c) the f9-privacy-mirror composer entry on web-390: V2 above a post field.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The map content has a text equivalent. Print both on 02:\n  - V1: \"Map. One pin marks where neighbors see your posts, about 0.3 miles from your address. Your home is not shown. Scale bar 0.2 miles.\"\n  - V3: \"Cells map. Your cell: 6 to 15 posts in 30 days.\" It is followed by the List cells view.\n- Pan and zoom work through buttons, never only by drag or pinch. On web, the focused map also accepts +, − and the arrow keys.\n- Buttons are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8pt / 8dp gaps, and they never auto-hide while assistive tech is on.\n- The pin and cells are not targets.\n\nCOPY\n- Use the caption exactly as given. The pin label is exactly \"What neighbors see\".\n- Never write \"re-rolled every time you post\".\n- Cells-map counts say \"Pantopus posts\", never \"curator\".\n\nPLATFORMS: identical geometry on all three. Only the button minimums differ (44pt iOS · 48dp Android · 44px web), and web adds the keyboard keys.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a 150 m ring around the home, draw the single public pin where neighbours see it, because the real offset area is about 12 times larger and a ring centred on the home reveals the home.\n- Instead of publishing the ±0.005° box now, keep it in the pending-decision frame, because a box centred on the home can reveal the home.\n- Instead of a blurred, fogged or locked map, draw the full map and state the requirement in words, because a hidden map is a carrot, not information.\n- Instead of a lightness-only ramp for post density, print the bucket label in every cell, because adjacent ramp steps are only 1.16 to 1.66:1 apart.\n- Instead of a home marker \"for orientation\", show street labels only, because a screenshot must never locate the home.\n- Instead of one long controls row, draw the zoom column and the arrow pad, because six 48dp buttons do not fit in 326pt.\n- Instead of pinch and drag only, give every movement a labelled button, because gestures alone exclude switch and keyboard users.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"PublicPointMap / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\". The offline cells also publish \"PublicPointMap / <row key> / offline-no-cache / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: list-cells (03, light), ax5 (04, light).\n- Never publish the range box R.\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a PublicPointMap part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: the street labels; \"0.1\", \"0.2 mi\", \"0.25\", \"0.5 mi\"; the V2 line; \"See the spot\"; \"Your cell\"; \"List cells\"; all six control names; the summary line; the nine List cells rows; \"Simplified map\"; \"Moving the map needs a connection.\"; \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\"; \"What neighbors see: the pin on this map\"; both map text equivalents; \"Hidden from neighbors: your street address, your home on the map\"; \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\".\n- B. Assumptions: the nine cell names and buckets; the two-row controls cluster with an arrow pad (the contract names only zoom buttons; pan buttons follow the brief's rule that pan and zoom work by buttons); the no-cache offline line; the summary counts only the user's cell.\n- D. Deviations: none beyond the added pan buttons listed under B.\n- E. Open question: the optional ±0.005° range box has the home at its geometric centre, even when the frame is off-centre. Should it exist at all? Until this is answered, it appears only in the pending-decision frame on 01 and is not published.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 6 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (3 × 4, one reason per n/a, both offline forms).\n- No home marker, ring around the home, blur, fog or density ramp appears.\n- R appears only inside the \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\" frame on 01.\n- The controls cluster fits 326pt, and the reserved heights are 96pt / 104dp (148pt / 160dp with List cells).\n- The List cells view has nine rows matching the nine cells. Notes holds the PublicPointMap entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (6 artboards plus the Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light\n4. 00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n5. 00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light\nBatch 2:\n6. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n7. 00b · Notes (append PublicPointMap)"
