            "promptText": "Component 00b-07: FactCount. Follow the board rules from the setup message. This is the last component on the board.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): States how much is on file for the address, without implying that anything is missing.\nUSED IN (print it): x-place-file, f11-keeper-strip, f1-claim-receipt.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- A vertical block, at most 160pt wide.\n- Line 1: the integer in h3 20/28/600 (label weight) text.primary, a 4pt gap, then \"on file\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary, sharing one baseline.\n- Line 2, 6pt below line 1: category pips, one labelled pip for each category that has anything known, in this fixed order: Place · Dates · Money · People · Proof.\n  - Pip: 20pt tall, radius pill, surface.sunken fill, captionMedium 12/16/500 text.strong (9.37:1), 8pt horizontal padding, 4pt gaps.\n  - Pips wrap to a further line when needed.\n  - A pip is always a word, never a bare dot.\n- Unknown categories draw nothing: no outline, no placeholder, no \"0\". The host screen (x-place-file) owns any \"You can also add\" list. This component never draws one.\n- Target: the whole block is one target of at least 44pt (48dp on Android), extended beyond the visible block if needed. Tapping it opens the place file. Inside x-place-file, it scrolls to the list.\n- The place file header and the keeper strip use the same geometry.\n- Fixture: HOME A shows \"14 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates · Money · People. The same home at the same moment shows the same number on every surface.\n- A contrast table on 01 with these R6 rows: text.primary on base, text.secondary on base, and text.strong on sunken. In dark mode, pips on a dark raised card use dark sunken #0F172A; pips on dark base use dark raised #1E293B (R5).\n\nVARIANTS (row keys are in brackets)\n- V1 place file header [place-file-header]: \"14 on file\" with Place · Dates · Money · People, left-aligned.\n- V2 keeper strip [keeper-strip]: \"14 on file\" with Place · Dates · Money · People, right-aligned within 160pt.\n- V3 T1 [t1] (PLACE B, \"Saved place · Only you\"): \"7 on file\" with Place · Dates only. Only Place and Dates can exist at T1.\n- Claim-time count (extra, only in the f1-claim-receipt crop): \"11 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates, because the facts carried into a claim come from T1.\n\nSTATES (column keys are in brackets)\n- default [default].\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with a surface.sunken 24 × 20pt bar for the integer and two 48 × 20pt pill shapes. No ring outline and no count-up. It is static under Reduce Motion.\n- offline [offline]: the count stays, with the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" under the block.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy · light: V1 with every callout, one pip magnified 4×, and the contrast table.\n00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: place-file-header · keeper-strip · t1.\n- Columns: default · loading · offline.\n- Every cell is drawn. The t1 row shows the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\" beside the block.\n- Print the spoken label under each default cell.\n00b · FactCount · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n- V1 and V2 at iOS AX5: the integer and \"on file\" stack, the pips wrap one per line if needed, the 160pt maximum width is lifted to the full row, and in the keeper strip the block moves below the name and mood line.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- All three variants desaturated, captioned \"Categories by printed words, not colour.\"\n00b · FactCount · 04-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) x-place-file on iOS 393: the header \"Your place file\" with V1 \"14 on file\" and the ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- (b) f11-keeper-strip on Android 412: Ollie (otter) with the mood word \"On it\", the mood line \"Recycling and garbage go out tomorrow by 6:30 AM\", and V2 \"14 on file\".\n- (c) f1-claim-receipt on web-390: \"11 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates in the claim receipt, at claim time.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The block is one element. Its spoken label starts with the visible text (WCAG 2.5.3, label in name):\n  - V1 and V2: \"14 on file: place, dates, money, people.\"\n  - T1: \"7 on file: place, dates.\"\n  - Claim receipt: \"11 on file: place, dates.\"\n- Categories are carried by words, not colour.\n- The target is 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY\n- Never \"X of Y\", never \"knows\" (no \"Ollie knows\"), never a percentage.\n- Use \"on file\" exactly as written.\n\nPLATFORMS: identical on iOS, Android and web. Only the target minimums differ.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a closed five-segment ring with outlined empty segments, draw the integer and word pips for known categories only, because an empty slot reads as a task left undone.\n- Instead of a progress bar, level or XP, draw the plain count \"14 on file\", because the count states what is held, not how far someone has come.\n- Instead of a count-up animation, show the final number at once, because motion here implies an achievement.\n- Instead of \"3 of 6 things on file\", write \"14 on file\", because fractions imply incompleteness.\n- Instead of different counts for the same home on different surfaces, show \"14 on file\" everywhere at the same moment, because drift between surfaces reads as an error.\n- Instead of the spoken \"14 things on file\", say \"14 on file\", because the spoken name must contain the visible text.\n- Instead of greyed placeholder pips for unknown categories, draw nothing, because the host owns the \"You can also add\" list.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each 02 cell: \"FactCount / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: claim-time (04, light), ax5 (03, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a FactCount part to each section, then finish the board)\n- A. Invented strings: \"7 on file\"; \"Your place file\"; the three spoken labels; \"On it\"; \"Recycling and garbage go out tomorrow by 6:30 AM\".\n- B. Assumptions: the claim-time receipt shows Place · Dates only, because claimed facts come from T1. The brief's \"You can also add\" list belongs to the host x-place-file, not to this component. PLACE B has 7 facts on file.\n- D. Deviations:\n  - The pips sit below the integer, not beside it (as the contract says), so the block fits its 160pt maximum width.\n  - The contract gives the keeper strip \"11 on file\". The keeper strip shows \"14 on file\" to match the place file for the same home, and \"11 on file\" is used only as the claim-time count.\n  - The contract's spoken label \"11 things on file: …\" is drawn as \"14 on file: …\", so the spoken name contains the visible text (WCAG 2.5.3).\n- F. Finish the board: check that section F lists every n/a cell on the board with its reason, that section G lists every publish name, and that section E numbers the questions 1 to 4 across the board (PM2.5 sentence, QuietDayReceipt check, relative counts, range box).\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 FactCount artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (3 × 3).\n- No progress or completion ring, fraction, percentage or count-up appears. Unknown categories draw nothing.\n- The spoken labels start with the visible text.\n- 00b · Notes is complete for the whole board: sections A–G, with every component's entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (5 artboards plus the final Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; this is one batch)\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n4. 00b · FactCount · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n5. 00b · FactCount · 04-in-context · light\n6. 00b · Notes (append FactCount and finish the board)"
          }
        ],
        "resolved": [
          "1 [major] Stale marks below 3:1: stale marks now use the published 00a stale variant (text.primary at 50%). It measures 3.39 on base, 3.32 on sunken and 3.36 on weekend cells, and 4.10–4.48 in dark. It is defined in setup R6/R11 and used in the ScaleStrip, AqiBand and FourteenDayStrip stale states. The holiday ghost stays at full text.secondary ink, and the strike carries the move. This removes the contract conflict, so the old open question for 00a is dropped. Each prompt records the change on Notes D.",
          "2 [major] Widget provenance words: setup G8 states the rule. FourteenDayStrip V2 prints an 11pt legend line with inline S marks ('● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added'). YearBand V2 prints the word 'On record' plus a legend line that includes '▮ Rule'. AqiBand V3 prints 'Official'. The ScaleStrip OG sources line prints 'Official'. Every widget's DONE WHEN checks this.",
          "3 [major] County rule drawn two ways: YearBand now draws county and state rules as full-lane-height bars, with a numeral when there are 2 or more. This covers the 01 callout, the desktop bar at 2 Nov, the 06 greyscale caption and the November readout. The change is recorded as a YearBand contract deviation (the contract names statewide bars only). FourteenDayStrip keeps the same rule and cross-references it.",
          "4 [major] 68pt strip cell does not add up: the cell is now 76pt (6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6), with a callout on 01, the same figure in the skeleton's reserved height, and a check in DONE WHEN. The widget uses a 60pt cell with at most 2 marks before '+N', inside a 100pt budget (60 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16) of the 126pt content height.",
          "5 [major] Closed dark palette missing tokens: setup R5 now gives the full dark mapping. primary.600 fill, semantic.error glyphs and semantic.warning glyphs keep their light values (3.57, 3.03 and 4.59 on dark raised). primary.700 maps to #38BDF8. The light infoBg wash is banned in dark (1.16:1). FourteenDayStrip defines the dark highlighted DateRow as a dark base wash with a 1px #38BDF8 outline (14.42:1).",
          "6 [major] Empty-receipt tick vs provenance grammar: the QuietDayReceipt stand-in is a bare stroked check with no disc. The sentence always starts with 'Checked', and the check never sits at a mark position. FourteenDayStrip and YearBand both state it as the single G4 exception, and both greyscale captions add 'empty by the word Checked'. The 00d question is on Notes E and names the contract's CheckItems.",
          "7 [major] OG 40px cap: the ScaleStrip Notes D records reading '40px cap' as a 40px font size (a true cap height needs about 56px type and does not fit 630px), and it records the 28px sources line as a deviation. Header and value text stay at 40px or more, and the budget prints 612px.",
          "8 [minor] ScaleStrip spoken-label placement: all four row labels are printed under the ready instrument on 04. The compare label is printed on 03. The stale-Air, failed-Air ('Retry air quality') and loading labels are written out in full.",
          "9 [minor] FactCount label-in-name: the spoken labels are '14 on file: place, dates, money, people.', '7 on file: place, dates.' and '11 on file: place, dates.', citing WCAG 2.5.3. The change is recorded as a contract deviation.",
          "10 [minor] RankBadge overline width: the badge is 120×64pt with 96pt of text width. If 'BLOCK FOUNDER' is wider, it breaks as 'BLOCK / FOUNDER', and the badge grows to 80pt (8 + 16 + 16 + 32 + 8).",
          "11 [minor] Cells-map summary: the line now reads '14 neighbor posts in your cell in 30 days. 3 Pantopus posts not counted.' It is listed in PublicPointMap Notes A, and Notes B records that it counts only the user's cell.",
          "12 [minor] PLACE B weekly rhythm with frequency Not set: FourteenDayStrip T1 draws only Thu 22 Oct ('Pickup day · frequency not set'). YearBand PLACE B has no rhythm, only one tick plus the Thanksgiving move. Both prompts add a Notes B assumption explaining that the Camas notice covers every Thursday route.",
          "13 [minor] Invented strings and brief reconciliation: each component's Notes A lists its own invented strings, including the row labels, control names, readouts and fallback lines. ScaleStrip Notes C records the brief's radon wording. FactCount records that the host (x-place-file) owns the 'You can also add' list.",
          "14 [minor] Ready and stale air share one age: ScaleStrip and AqiBand add SPECIMEN CLOCKS. Ready and offline specimens are drawn at 7:10 AM, alert and still-above at 4:10 PM, and stale at TODAY 6:10 PM. Artboards print the specimen time in the gutter, and Notes B records the clocks.",
          "15 [major, quality] Strip cell overflow geometry: see item 4 (76pt cell, 60pt widget cell, skeleton and budget updated).",
          "16 [major, quality] PublicPointMap controls too wide: every size uses a two-row cluster, with a zoom column at the left edge and a 3×2 arrow pad at the right edge (at least 208pt, or 224dp). It is 96pt tall (104dp), and 148pt (160dp) with the 'List cells' third row. The prompt gives the focus order, the skeleton reserves these heights, and an INSTEAD OF line explains the choice.",
          "17 [major, quality] YearBand desktop overlaps: a collision rule applies at 768px and wider. Items less than 14px from the first item of a cluster merge into one item at the earliest day, with a count numeral, and a mixed cluster shows the hollow mark. The prompt works through 23+28 Oct, 1+2 Nov (with a callout), the state bars 26 Oct and 3 Nov (16px, kept separate), the Tuesday ticks as rhythm (not merged) and the PLACE B Thanksgiving move in its phone form.",
          "18 [major, quality] Ready and stale Air timestamps: see item 14.",
          "19 [minor, quality] ScaleStrip 04 label conflict: see item 8. Partial with Air loading reads 'Loading' for the Air row, and the container reads 'Loading' once.",
          "20 [minor, quality] Two-column ScaleStrip layout: the left 40% stacks the layer name, value line and SourceCaption. The right 60% holds the track zone with the band names under it, top-aligned with the value line, with a 16pt gap. The 640px web-1440 card width is stated.",
          "21 [minor, quality] Compare geometry: the compare track zone is 16 + 8 + 12 + 8 + 16 = 60pt, with band names 4pt below 'You'. Each occupied band is outlined, a shared band is outlined once, and a shared band prints one 'Both:' value line. All four compare rows have explicit value lines and captions. The triangle pointers are recorded as a contract deviation.",
          "22 [minor, quality] Stand-ins: setup R11 labels each stand-in 'stand-in — the 00a/00c/00d specimen replaces it' and gives one-line anatomies for ProvenanceMark (including its stale variant), SourceCaption, FreshnessLine, ScopeChip, KindGlyph, InlineErrorRow, DateRow, FactRow, TextActionRow, WarmingSkeleton and QuietDayReceipt. KindGlyph ink is corrected to text.strong, as in the contract.",
          "23 [minor, quality] Missing strings and values: 'Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar' now has its line 2 'in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov'. The PLACE B summary is 'Next 12 months: 3 dates. Next, in 7 days: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.' The October and November readouts are written out in full. The triangle-pointer change is on ScaleStrip Notes D.",
          "24 [minor, quality] Claim-receipt pips vs T1: the f1-claim-receipt crop shows '11 on file' with Place · Dates and reads '11 on file: place, dates.', and Notes B explains why.",
          "25 [minor, quality] 9 cells vs 4 list rows: all nine cells have names and buckets, and the List cells view has nine matching 48dp rows.",
          "26 [minor, quality] Air no-data wording: the ScaleStrip 02 cell rule sets air × no-data to the AqiBand no-reading instrument row ('No reading for this address right now'), not V6. V6 is limited to Flood, Wildfire and Radon.",
          "27 [minor, quality] Missing relative counts: the summaries and widget lines now carry 'in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct' and similar, the widget line reads 'Voter registration must arrive by', and the FourteenDayStrip DateRow line 2 dates are listed. The remaining absolute-only cases (the native month readouts and 'Closes Tue 27 Oct') form one open question: YearBand raises it, and SlotMeter adds to it.",
          "28 [minor, quality] Ring ban vs required rings: setup G2 now bans 'progress ring, completion ring' only. FactCount DONE WHEN matches. The PublicPointMap user cell is described as a rectangular inner outline ('the contract calls it a ring').",
          "29 [minor, quality] Stale style fails 3:1: see item 1. The 00a stale variant passes, and the R6 table lists the failing text.secondary-at-50% values (1.98 and 1.91) under 'Never used'.",
          "30 [minor, quality] Small layout rules: (a) AqiBand AX5 legend rows are 'at least 44pt' and grow with their text. (b) The RankBadge sits below the meter, at least 24pt away. (c) The widget micro variant always draws the XS Official mark plus 'Official'. (d) Web-1440 card widths are set per component: ScaleStrip 640, FourteenDayStrip 648 (44px cells), YearBand 880; FactCount keeps its 160pt maximum. (e) The YearBand desktop grid is 128 + 12 × 60 = 848. (f) Offline with no cache shows 'You're offline. The map needs a connection.' in the reserved slot.",
          "31 [minor, quality] Batch separators and repetition: each component ends with one numbered 'ARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN' list, one artboard per line and at most 6 per batch. The single 11k-word prompt is split into a setup message (about 2,200 words) and seven component messages (about 1,150–2,950 words each). Board rules are stated once, and the Notes guidance is per component.",
          "Also fixed while splitting: the AqiBand keyline rationale used wrong numbers ('yellow 1.07:1 on white', 'maroon 1.62:1 on dark base'). The computed values are Good 1.22, Moderate 1.54 and Hazardous 1.08 on dark raised, and a full marker core/halo contrast table was added. Order dependencies are removed: ScaleStrip, which is sent before AqiBand, now carries the full instrument-row geometry for Air, and FourteenDayStrip's V3 window crop carries a compact YearBand phone spec, with a YearBand batch 3 consistency check. The YearBand widget freshness line follows 00a ('As of 7:40 AM', with no weekday for today). New contract deviations are recorded for the ScaleStrip 4×20 capsule (the contract says '12pt marker'), the SlotMeter 4pt elapsed bar (the contract says 2px), the FactCount pips sitting below the integer, and the PublicPointMap pan buttons. Setup R6 contrast numbers were recomputed with the WCAG formula. Cross-board flag, not changed here: 00a's B9 AX5/200% sizes (caption 40, bodySmall 46; Android body 32) differ from this board's Apple/Android-14 table (caption 43, bodySmall 49; Android body 28)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "setup": {
          "id": "00c-00",
          "promptText": "Setup 00c-00: Foundations board 00c, Rows and lists.\n\nUse the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is Foundations board 00c, \"Rows and lists\". Read this message, then reply. Draw nothing yet.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nThis is a component specimen board with no screens. I will send one component per message, in this order: DateRow, FactRow, FirstWeekRow, BillRow, MemberRow, InviteRow, NotificationRow, TextActionRow, LockedActionRow, GrantLimitList, InlineErrorRow, ThumbnailRail. Each component message is that component's complete specification. This message holds only the rules for all twelve, R1 to R14 (\"the board rules\").\nLater screen projects will use these components by exact name and key, with no other reference, so every specimen must be complete, exact and labelled. ATTACH: none.\n\nPUBLISH\nWhen I accept a component, I add it to the published Pantopus design system under its exact name above. Its variants and states are published under the printed keys from its grid (R7), e.g. DateRow variant \"deadline-voter\", state \"highlighted-arrival\". Never publish a drawing labelled \"stand-in\" (R11); those components come from their own Foundations boards.\n\nHOW EACH COMPONENT TURN WORKS\n- Each component message ends with ARTBOARDS, a BATCH PLAN and DONE WHEN. Draw only what the BATCH PLAN lists for the current turn, then stop and wait for \"continue\". Never start a component before its message arrives.\n- Before stopping, check the batch against DONE WHEN and name anything missing.\n- If a component message and these rules disagree, the component message wins; note it on Notes.\n- Ask a question only if two readings would produce materially different components.\n\nR1. ARTBOARDS\n- Name each artboard \"00c · <ComponentName> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\", exactly as the component's ARTBOARDS list gives it (this replaces the house style's surface naming). Show the name as a visible label above the frame in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\n- Each component gets exactly five artboards, in this order:\n  01-anatomy · light: one specimen at 2x with numbered callouts (R3), then five labelled text panels: ACCESSIBILITY, COPY RULES, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF, USED IN.\n  02-grid · light: the variant × state grid at 1x (R7).\n  03-ax5-200-greyscale · light: at the top, two large-text columns labelled \"iOS · AX5 (body 53pt)\" and \"Android · 200%\" (Android 14 nonlinear scaling), per R9. Below, full width at 1x, a greyscale (0% saturation) copy of the whole 02 grid, per R10.\n  04-in-context · light: the crops the component names (R13).\n  05-grid · dark: the 02 grid in the same layout in dark tokens (R5), plus the 1x anatomy specimen in dark at top left.\n- The last artboard in the project is \"00c · Notes\" (R14).\n\nR2. CANVAS AND UNITS\n- Artboards are at least 1440 wide, on surface.app (dark: dark app). Grow them to fit cells at 1x; never scale a cell down.\n- 1pt = 1dp = 1px. Callouts give iOS pt, or all three where they differ (\"44pt / 48dp / 44px\").\n- Row frames unless a cell says otherwise: iOS 393pt with 16pt side margins (361pt content); Android 412dp (380dp content); web-390 390px (358px content); web-1440 a 720px list column.\n- Spacing and radii by name (spacing.2 = 8, spacing.3 = 12, spacing.4 = 16; md 8, lg 12).\n\nR3. CALLOUTS\n- Outside the component: a numbered circle (1px text.secondary outline), a 1px text.secondary leader, and a caption with size and token, e.g. \"② title · body 16/24/400 · text.primary\". Numbers match the component's ANATOMY list.\n- Callouts never overlap the component. Spacing uses 1px dimension lines (\"16pt · spacing.4\").\n- Draw every target as a dashed 1px text.secondary rectangle labelled \"target 44pt / 48dp / 44px\".\n- Every 01-anatomy has a \"web menu\" callout (R12), worded as the component message says.\n\nR4. TYPE AND LIGHT TOKENS\n- Type scale only: body 16/24/400 · bodyMedium 16/24/500 · bodySmall 14/20/400 · bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 · label 13/18/600 · caption 12/16/400 · captionMedium 12/16/500 · overline 11/16/600 caps +0.5. SF Pro on iOS, Roboto on Android, system-ui on web. Amounts use tabular figures.\n- Token names only, never hex on a component. Light values are in the house style; this board also uses primary.50, primary.700, errorBg, infoBg and identity.home.\n- text.muted appears nowhere on this board.\n- Secondary-role text (captions, \"Not set\", disabled labels, reason captions) is text.secondary on base, raised and app, and text.strong on surface.sunken and errorBg, where text.secondary fails (R6).\n- Text buttons and links are bodySmallMedium primary.700 unless a component says otherwise.\n- Semantic hues and identity.home go on glyphs and rules only, never on text.\n- Border tokens are decoration. Row separators are 1px border.default hairlines inset 16pt from the leading edge, and no row relies on a hairline as its only edge. Any edge that carries meaning uses text.secondary ink.\n\nR5. DARK MODE (every 05)\nDark tokens: surface.base #0F172A, raised #1E293B, sunken #0F172A (same as base), app #020617; text.primary #E5E7EB, text.strong #F1F5F9, text.secondary #94A3B8; border.default #1F2937, strong #374151, subtle #1E293B, focus #38BDF8. Links and text buttons use dark border.focus.\nDark has no infoBg, errorBg, primary.50, primary.700 or semantic tokens, and dark sunken equals base. Use exactly these substitutes, and record each use on Notes:\n- D1 Highlight: dark raised wash plus the 4pt leading bar in dark border.focus. On a row already on raised (D3), the bar alone.\n- D2 Write-failure fill: dark raised plus a 1.5px error border.\n- D3 A row on sunken in light sits on dark raised, with dark text.strong.\n- D4 Any sunken fill (skeleton bars, avatars, chip fills, thumbnail slots, a disabled filled button) becomes dark raised on a base row and dark border.strong on a raised row; text inside is dark text.strong.\n- D5 Selection: dark raised plus a 1.5px dark border.focus edge plus a leading check in dark border.focus. Never primary.50.\n- D6 Non-link primary.700 graphics (progress rings, spinners, unread dot) use dark border.focus; ring tracks use dark border.strong.\n- D7 Semantic glyph hues and the identity.home rule keep their light values, on glyphs and rules only. Caption the R6 ratio beside the first occurrence on each 05.\n- D8 Any card gets a 1px dark text.secondary keyline, because dark border.default on raised is 1.00:1. Caption its ratio beside the first occurrence.\nIncrease Contrast: no separate artboard. Every R6 check must also hold under Increase Contrast; the only change is that light cards get the same text.secondary keyline as D8. Write this once as a caption on each 05.\n\nR6. CONTRAST TABLE (use these numbers in captions; never place a pair marked FAIL)\nLight text, 4.5:1:\n- text.primary: 16 or more on every light surface · text.strong: 9.37 or more on every light surface\n- text.secondary: base 4.83 · raised 4.63 · app 4.51 · infoBg 4.54 · sunken 4.39 FAIL · errorBg 4.42 FAIL\n- primary.700: base 5.93 · sunken 5.39 · primary.50/infoBg 5.57 · errorBg 5.42\nLight graphics, 3:1:\n- border.focus: base 4.10 · infoBg 3.84 · sunken 3.72\n- success: base 3.77 · sunken 3.42\n- warning: base 3.19 · sunken 2.89 FAIL\n- error: base 4.83 · sunken 4.39\n- identity.home: base 3.30 · infoBg 3.09 · sunken 2.99 FAIL\n- text.secondary glyph or keyline: base 4.83 · raised 4.63 · app 4.51 · sunken 4.39\n- primary.700 ring on border.strong track: 4.03\nDark text, 4.5:1:\n- text.primary: base 14.42 · raised 11.82 · text.strong: 9.41 or more everywhere\n- text.secondary: base 6.96 · raised 5.71 · on border.strong 4.02 FAIL\n- border.focus links: base 8.33 · raised 6.83\nDark graphics, 3:1:\n- border.focus: base 8.33 · raised 6.83 · on border.strong 4.81\n- success: base 4.74 · raised 3.88 · on border.strong 2.74 FAIL\n- warning: base 5.60 · raised 4.59\n- error: base 3.70 · raised 3.03 · on border.strong 2.13 FAIL\n- identity.home: base 5.42 · raised 4.44\n- text.secondary keyline (D8): raised 5.71 · app 7.87\n\nR7. GRID LABELS AND KEYS\n- Variants are rows, labelled at the left in label 13/18 text.strong. States are columns, labelled at the top in overline 11/16/600.\n- Each label reads exactly \"<code> · <key>\" with the codes and keys from the component message (e.g. \"V3a · deadline-voter\", \"S2a · highlighted-arrival\"). Under it, print \"key: <key>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\n- Keys are lowercase and hyphenated, with no spaces, no \"/\", no fixture string and no date. Publish names use keys only.\n- Under every cell, in caption 12/16 text.secondary, print exactly \"<ComponentName> · <variant key> · <state key>\" (e.g. \"DateRow · deadline-voter · done\").\n- Draw only the cells in GRID CELLS. Every other position stays empty canvas: no frame, no label, no \"n/a\".\n- An n/a cell appears only where a component writes \"n/a\": a plain cell reading \"n/a — <reason>\" in caption text.secondary, with the normal cell caption. Never draw a ghost component there.\n\nR8. TARGETS, FOCUS, HIGHLIGHT, SELECTION, DISABLED\n- Targets: 44pt iOS, 48dp Android with 8dp gaps, 44px web. A ProvenanceMark, glyph or dot is never a target by itself.\n- Focus: a 2px border.focus ring 2px outside the whole row. When a row holds a separate target (link, overflow, Retry, Resend, Add, dismiss), focus on it rings that target only.\n- Highlight (arrival from a notification): an infoBg wash across the row plus a 4pt border.focus bar on the leading edge, full height. No outline, never a check. If the row has a 2px identity.home rule, the bar sits directly inside it. In an \"on arrival\" frame the focus ring is also drawn 2px outside the row, so bar and ring never touch. Dark: D1.\n- Selection: primary.50 fill plus a leading check glyph. Dark: D5.\n- Focus, highlight and selection must look different. Wherever a grid has a highlighted or selected cell, a focused cell sits directly beside it.\n- Disabled text actions look the same everywhere: label in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken, per R4), never primary.700 or text.muted, still focusable, with a reason caption directly under it in caption 12/16 (same colour rule). Disabled filled buttons: surface.sunken fill, text.strong label (dark: D4).\n- Disabled controls stay in the accessibility tree with their reason as a hint.\n\nR9. AX5 / 200% (every 03)\n- Text wraps and never truncates, except a field the component names as truncating at default sizes only.\n- Side-by-side pairs stack. Trailing elements (amount, mark, chevron, text action) move below the text block, aligned to its leading edge, and keep their targets.\n- Leading glyphs and marks scale with the text; ProvenanceMark keeps its shape. Row heights grow; stated heights are minimums.\n\nR10. GREYSCALE (every 03)\nDraw the whole 02 grid desaturated, same labels and captions. Beside it, caption each variant or state with its non-colour cue, e.g. \"done = tick glyph + 'You marked this done'\". A cell that reads only through colour is a defect: fix the component.\n\nR11. SHARED STAND-INS\nIf the published design system has one of these, use it; otherwise draw this stand-in, labelled \"stand-in\". Components may add their own.\n- ProvenanceMark: OFFICIAL = solid disc; ON RECORD, NOT CONFIRMED = ring, stroke at least 1.5px; YOU ADDED = solid disc with a knocked-out tick (a cut-out, never a second colour). Ink text.secondary (dark: dark text.secondary). S = 16pt in rows; XS = 12pt minimum. Spoken \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\", \"you added this\". Filled vs hollow means provenance only. Every other check on this board is a bare stroke, never a disc.\n- Legend line: \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\" in caption text.secondary, or the word beside the first mark.\n- ScopeChip: pill, 24pt, surface.sunken fill (dark: D4), 12pt glyph plus label 13/18 text.strong. Exactly \"Saved place · Only you\" (person glyph) or \"Your household\" (house glyph), spoken \"Visible to only you\" / \"Visible to your household\". Sentences exactly \"Only you will see this.\" / \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"; where finance access differs, name the people (\"You and Sam can see these\"), never \"Everyone\". When the chip opens the scope control, draw its 44pt / 48dp target.\n- StatusChip: pill, 24pt, captionMedium, surface.sunken fill (dark: D4), text.strong; any semantic hue on a leading glyph only; one per row.\n- InlineUndo: the row collapses in place to \"<what happened> · Undo\", announced with role=status. Undo is focusable, 44pt, and stays until the user leaves the screen. No countdown.\n- WarmingSkeleton: surface.sunken bars (dark: D4) in the final geometry and height, no text, announced once as \"Loading\" (aria-busy on web); static under Reduce Motion.\n- FreshnessLine / OfflineNotice: caption text.secondary, e.g. \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" (invented). No banner colour.\n\nR12. PLATFORMS AND THE WEB MENU\n- Unless a component's PLATFORMS says otherwise, write \"No platform differences\" in its panel.\n- Custom actions are VoiceOver custom actions on iOS and TalkBack custom actions on Android.\n- On web, custom actions that are not already visible buttons get a row menu button: a 20px ellipsis in a 44px target at the row's trailing edge. An existing overflow button or visible buttons already are the web menu; never add a second. Draw it in every web crop where it applies.\n\nR13. IN-CONTEXT CROPS (every 04)\n- Label each crop \"<surface id> · <ios|android|web-390|web-1440>\". Show only enough host to place the component: outlines, section titles, neighbouring rows.\n- Every crop that shows a ProvenanceMark also shows the legend line and the place's ScopeChip: \"Your household\" for Home A, \"Saved place · Only you\" for Place B.\n\nR14. FIXTURES, MOTION, NOTES\n- Use the house-style FIXTURES. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific; relative counts come from it. Dates always show the weekday (\"Fri 23 Oct\"), never numeric formats, never \"midnight\". Emails use @example.com. No percentage or completion fraction is drawn on any specimen, callout or crop; an INSTEAD OF panel may name one only as the pattern to avoid.\n- Motion: highlights fade within 300ms. Under Reduce Motion they cross-fade, spinners are removed and in-progress labels stay as static text. Idle loops stop within 5s.\n- \"00c · Notes\" is the last artboard. Create it when a BATCH PLAN first says so; update it whenever a BATCH PLAN says so. One line per item.\n  Board section first: each D1–D8 with the components that used it and the D7/D8 ratios; the Increase Contrast note; the R11 stand-ins you drew; any string you added that no message lists; any state you could not draw, and why.\n  Then one section per component, in delivery order, under its exact name, with the lists its message gives: Invented strings · Fixture deltas · Contract conflicts (each \"drawn as X instead of contract Y\") · Assumptions.\n\nReply 'ready' and wait for the first component."
        },
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "00c-01",
            "component": "DateRow",
            "artboards": [
              "00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light",
              "00c · DateRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00c · DateRow · 04-in-context · light",
              "00c · DateRow · 05-grid · dark",
              "00c · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-01: DateRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: DateRow. This message is the complete DateRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). One dated fact in a list. Its row grammar is shared by the 14-day strip list, the calendar agenda, the place file Dates section and reminder rows.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f5-today-calendar-strip · f3-household-calendar · x-place-file · x-date-sheet · f3-household-notifications · f7-today-widget.\n\nEXTRA STAND-INS FOR THIS COMPONENT (label each \"stand-in\", per R11)\n- KindGlyph: a 24pt line icon with a 2pt stroke in text.strong, with one distinct drawing per kind: garbage, recycling, garbage+recycling, notice deadline, warranty ends, HOA dues, property-tax due, property-tax appeal, voter registration. Never one generic calendar icon.\n- SourceCaption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"authority · scope · as-of\". It wraps and never ellipsises the authority.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V3a at 2x for callouts ①–⑦ and ⑩. Beside it, draw V3c in S3 (done) at 2x for callouts ⑧ and ⑨.\n① Row: minimum height 56pt, padding 16pt horizontal and 12pt vertical, on surface.base. The whole row is the target: draw the dashed target rectangle around it.\n② Leading KindGlyph, 24pt, text.strong, top-aligned with the title, with a 12pt (spacing.3) gap after it.\n③ Title: body 16/24/400, text.primary. It wraps and is never truncated.\n④ Line 2: caption 12/16 text.secondary, the relative date then the absolute date, e.g. \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" stand alone, with no absolute date after them. An approximate date reads \"about Dec 2026\".\n⑤ SourceCaption short form (authority · scope). It continues line 2 after a middot, or wraps to line 3.\n⑥ Trailing ProvenanceMark S (16pt), vertically centred, with 8pt (spacing.2) between it and the text. It is not a target.\n⑦ Optional chip after the title reading \"Statewide — WA\", in ScopeChip geometry (24pt pill, surface.sunken fill, label 13/18 text.strong) with a 12pt state-outline glyph. It states coverage, not visibility.\n⑧ Annual rows and self-entered rows: a 2px identity.home rule on the leading edge, full row height, plus a recurrence caption on the last line in caption text.secondary (\"Every year\", \"Every month\" or \"Does not repeat\").\n⑨ Done tick: a 16pt stroke check before the title. It is a bare stroke, not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark.\n⑩ Web menu callout: \"web menu: a row menu button (20px ellipsis, 44px target) after the mark, holding Edit · Remind me · Where this comes from · Mark done\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\nV1 pickup. Home A as of TODAY, before Maya confirmed her pickup day. The title names the bins.\n- V1a · pickup-both: garbage+recycling glyph · title \"Recycling and garbage\" · line 2 \"Tomorrow · Waste Connections · city schedule\" · hollow mark.\n- V1b · pickup-garbage: garbage glyph · \"Garbage only\" · \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct · Waste Connections · city schedule\" · hollow mark.\n- V2 · holiday-moved (Place B, Camas): garbage glyph · \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\" · \"in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\" · hollow mark.\nV3 deadline. The weekday is always shown, and received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n- V3a · deadline-voter: voter registration glyph · \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · chip \"Statewide — WA\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Washington Secretary of State · statewide\" · filled mark.\n- V3b · deadline-notice: notice deadline glyph · \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · last line \"Does not repeat · Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V3c · deadline-tax: property-tax due glyph · \"Property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov · Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\" · last line \"Every year\" · filled mark · identity.home rule.\n- V4 · conditional-rule: property-tax appeal glyph · \"Property-tax appeal window\" · \"Closes Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Clark County Board of Equalization · county-wide\" · last line \"Every year\" · filled mark · identity.home rule.\n- V5 · reminder: warranty glyph · \"Reminder: Water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec\" · \"in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec · You added this\" · last line \"Does not repeat\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V5x · reminder-approx (fixture delta: the warranty date was entered as approximate): warranty glyph · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"about Dec 2026\" · last line \"Does not repeat\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V6 · money: HOA dues glyph · \"HOA dues\" · amount \"$285.00\" in bodyMedium with tabular figures, right-aligned and placed before the mark · \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov · You added this\" · last line \"Every month\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2a, S2b, SF, S3, S4)\n- S1 · default.\n- S2 · highlighted: arrival from a notification, per R8 (dark: D1), with accessibility focus moved onto the row. Drawn as two columns:\n  - S2a · highlighted-arrival: infoBg wash, 4pt leading bar, and the focus ring 2px outside the row.\n  - S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; the focus ring remains.\n- SF · focused: the R8 focus ring on the whole row.\n- S3 · done: the ⑨ tick before the title; title and line 2 in text.secondary; line 2 prefixed \"You marked this done ·\". Done is personal. On every row, including the civic V3a row, it stays Only you and is never shown to the household.\n- S4 · permission-hidden: the row is not rendered at all.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 26 cells)\n- S1 and S3: V1a, V1b, V2, V3a, V3b, V3c, V4, V5, V5x and V6 (20 cells).\n- S2a and S2b: V1a and V3a (4 cells).\n- SF: V3a, so it sits directly beside V3a S2a and V3a S2b (1 cell).\n- S4: one cell, in the V6 row: a three-row list of V1a, [absent V6], V3a. The rows above and below close the gap, with no placeholder and no ghost row. An annotation arrow outside the list reads \"row absent: viewer lacks permission\" (1 cell).\n- Outside the V3a S3 cell, annotate: \"done stays Only you\".\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. Highlight uses D1. The \"Statewide — WA\" chip fill uses D4. Marks and the done tick use dark text.secondary; each KindGlyph uses dark text.strong.\n- The identity.home rule keeps its hue (D7). Beside the first one, caption \"identity.home on dark base 5.42:1\".\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V3a and V6 in both columns.\n- The title wraps to as many lines as it needs.\n- The \"Statewide — WA\" chip drops below the title.\n- Line 2 wraps at middots.\n- The amount and the mark move below the text block: the amount first, then the mark, scaled to about 28pt.\n- The KindGlyph scales to 32pt and stays top-aligned.\n- The identity.home rule stays full height.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- provenance = disc vs ring vs disc with knocked-out tick.\n- done = stroke tick + \"You marked this done\".\n- highlighted = 4pt leading bar.\n- annual = 2px rule + \"Every year\".\n- kind = KindGlyph shape.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The whole row is one element and one target (minimum 56pt), read in visual order. The mark and the glyph are not targets.\n- Spoken pattern: \"<title>, <line 2 as shown>, <authority, scope>, <mark name>\". The label speaks only the dates the row shows, so \"Tomorrow\" is spoken as \"tomorrow\" with no absolute date. Example: \"Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Waste Connections city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- Done rows start with \"You marked this done\". Done stays Only you.\n- Custom actions: Edit · Remind me · Where this comes from · Mark done. On web they sit in the ⑩ row menu button.\n- Non-colour encoding: the glyph shape carries the kind, the mark shape carries provenance, the leading bar carries highlight, and the words carry done.\n- Contrast: text at least 4.5:1; mark at least 3:1 (text.secondary on base, 4.83:1).\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- For deadlines, the title names the action: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\n- Received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n- Dates are spelled out with the weekday (\"Mon 26 Oct\"), never 10/26/2026.\n- Beyond tomorrow, the relative count comes first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Conditional rules (V4) are exempt from the relative count.\n- Source captions carry a scope word: \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\".\n- Pickup titles use exactly \"Recycling and garbage\" or \"Garbage only\".\n- Holiday moves read \"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", never \"delayed\" or \"cancelled\".\n- \"I did this\" reads \"You marked this done\" and stays Only you.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences, except that web adds the ⑩ row menu button (R12).\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of red text or an overdue chip on an annual date that has passed, draw the next occurrence with its \"Every year\" caption. Annual dates never inherit overdue red.\n- Instead of one generic calendar icon for every row, draw the specific KindGlyph. The glyph is what tells kinds apart without colour.\n- Instead of a greyed placeholder row for a date the viewer may not see, draw nothing. A ghost row leaks that something exists.\n- Instead of a numeric date like 10/26/2026, draw \"Mon 26 Oct\". The weekday is what people plan by.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops, each with the legend line and the ScopeChip (R13).\n1. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; a card (radius lg) holding a 14-cell strip drawn only as a plain outline (the strip is specified on another board), above rows V1a, V3a and V6; a foot row \"+ Add a date\"; the legend line. Annotate the strip: \"strip cells are not targets; the rows below are\".\n2. x-place-file · web-1440, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; section overline \"DATES\"; rows V3b, V4 and V5, each with its ⑩ row menu button; the legend line.\n3. f3-household-calendar · android, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; an agenda with the day header \"Tue 20 Oct\" and row V1a in S2a; the legend line.\n\nNOTES (add a \"DateRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"city schedule\" · \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide\" · \"Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" as a caption · the \"Reminder:\" title prefix · \"Every year\" · \"Every month\" · \"Does not repeat\".\n- Fixture deltas: V1a and V1b show Home A as of TODAY, before Maya confirmed Tuesday (hollow) · V5x: the warranty date was entered as approximate (\"about Dec 2026\") instead of Sat 12 Dec 2026 · V6: HOA dues appears both as a household bill (BillRow) and as a self-added monthly date.\n- Contract conflicts: \"Statewide — WA\" drawn in ScopeChip geometry as a coverage chip, instead of one of ScopeChip's two exact strings · highlighted drawn as a wash plus a leading bar, instead of contract \"wash + outline\", so it never looks like focus.\n- Assumptions: V2 has a hollow mark on an official city holiday move, because Place B's schedule is unconfirmed · V5x carries the identity.home rule and \"Does not repeat\", like every other self-entered row.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (created in this component's Turn 2)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then create 00c · Notes with its board section (R14) and the DateRow section above. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five DateRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label, and 00c · Notes exists as the last artboard.\n- 01 shows callouts ①–⑩ with size and token, the dashed row target, and the five panels with the text above.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 26 listed cells, with every row and column labelled \"<code> · <key>\" plus its printed key, and every cell captioned \"DateRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- V3a SF sits beside V3a S2a and S2b, and bar, ring and wash are each distinct. S2a shows bar and ring without touching.\n- The done tick is a bare stroke check; the YOU ADDED mark is a disc with a knocked-out tick; every mark is at least 12pt with a 1.5px ring stroke.\n- Every row has its own KindGlyph, and no row is red or carries an overdue chip.\n- The S4 cell shows no ghost row and carries its annotation arrow; the V3a S3 cell carries \"done stays Only you\".\n- 03 shows V3a and V6 in both columns, following the AX5 rules above, and the greyscale grid with its five captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops, each with the legend line and ScopeChip; the web crop shows the row menu button on every row.\n- 05 uses D1, D4 and D7 (with its 5.42:1 caption) and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string on the board is in this message or listed on Notes."
          },
