            "promptText": "Component 00c-04: BillRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: BillRow. This message is the complete BillRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). A household bill with payer attribution, so two people don't pay the same bill.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-bills-list · f3-member-home-dashboard · f3-bill-detail-web · f10-mail-piece-photo.\n\nFIXTURE ROWS (Home A, viewer Maya unless stated)\n- Clark Public Utilities · Upcoming · $142.18 · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n- City of Vancouver water · Upcoming · $84.00 · \"Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\".\n- HOA dues · Upcoming · $285.00 · \"Due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\".\n- Comcast · Upcoming · $79.99 · \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n- Paid example: Comcast · Paid · $79.99 · \"Due Fri 2 Oct\" · \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\".\n- Overdue example: Waste Connections · Overdue, with an error glyph in the chip · $38.75 · \"Due Thu 15 Oct\".\n- Due-today example (fixture delta: shown on Fri 23 Oct): Clark Public Utilities · Due today · $142.18 · \"Due today · Fri 23 Oct\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw the list header ⑧ above two rows at 2x: the Clark Public Utilities upcoming row and the paid Comcast row.\n① Row: minimum 64pt, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal, on surface.base. The whole row opens bill detail: draw its dashed target.\n② Line 1, left: the provider in bodyMedium 16/24, text.primary. This is the ONLY field that truncates, and it truncates first (default sizes only).\n③ Line 1: one StatusChip after the provider.\n④ Line 1, right: the amount in bodyMedium with tabular figures, right-aligned in the same optical column on every row.\n⑤ Line 2, left: the due date in bodySmall 14/20, text.secondary, e.g. \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n⑥ Line 2, right: the attribution in bodySmall text.secondary, e.g. \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\". It is never truncated.\n⑦ Overflow button: a 20pt ellipsis in a 44pt / 48dp target, 8dp from the row target. Its menu holds Mark paid · I paid this · Paid a different amount · Skip this month. Draw its dashed target.\n⑧ List header in bodySmall text.strong. Viewer Maya: \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Sam can see these\". Viewer Sam: \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Maya can see these\". Finance access differs between members, so the header names the people instead of saying \"Everyone\".\n⑨ Callout on S3: \"the household notification is held until the user leaves the screen without undoing\".\n⑩ Web menu callout: \"the ⑦ overflow is the web row menu button; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · manage (viewer Maya): the Clark Public Utilities upcoming row. In S1 its overflow menu is drawn open, showing its four items.\n- V2a · member-overflow (viewer Sam): the same row; the overflow holds \"I paid this\" only.\n- V2b · member-no-overflow (viewer Sam): the same row with no overflow; the caption \"Maya can mark this paid\" replaces the right side of line 2.\n- V3 · only-me: the same row; line 2 adds a 12pt person glyph and ScopeChip's sentence \"Only you will see this.\" after the due date, wrapping to line 3.\n- V4 · former-member: the paid Comcast row with the attribution \"Paid by Sam (no longer here) · Thu 1 Oct\".\nChip strip rows (the fixture examples above):\n- C1 · chip-upcoming: Clark Public Utilities, Upcoming.\n- C2 · chip-due-today: Clark Public Utilities, Due today.\n- C3 · chip-overdue: Waste Connections, Overdue, with the error glyph inside the chip (hue on the glyph only).\n- C4 · chip-paid: Comcast, Paid, with \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2a, S2b, SF, S3, S4, S5)\n- S1 · default.\n- S2 · highlighted from a notification, per R8 (dark: D1), with focus moved to the row. Two columns:\n  - S2a · highlighted-arrival: infoBg wash, 4pt leading bar, and the focus ring 2px outside the row.\n  - S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; the focus ring remains.\n- SF · focused: the R8 ring on the whole row.\n- S3 · marked-paid: the row collapses in place to the InlineUndo \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\", announced with role=status. Beside it, draw the same row after the user has left the screen: \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\". Add the ⑨ callout.\n- S4 · permission-denied (viewer Sam before Maya shared bills; fixture delta): the header shows only the list title \"Bills\", with no count, total or scope sentence. The list body is replaced by one locked row: a 16pt lock glyph in text.secondary, then \"Maya can give you access to bills\" in bodySmall text.secondary on surface.base, no link, 44pt minimum, with a 1px border.subtle hairline above. (This is the names-who-can-act form of LockedActionRow, which a later message on this board specifies.)\n- S5 · offline: the FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" sits above the rows. Rows stay readable and still open cached detail. The overflow opens, but its items are disabled per R8, with the reason \"You're offline. You can mark bills paid when you're back.\"\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 15 cells)\n- V1: S1 (menu open), S2a, S2b, SF, S3 and S5 (6 cells). SF sits directly beside S2a and S2b.\n- V2a: S1 and S4 (2 cells). V2b: S1 (1 cell).\n- V3: S1. V4: S1 (2 cells).\n- C1, C2, C3 and C4: S1 (4 cells).\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. Highlight uses D1. StatusChip fills use D4. The overdue error glyph keeps its hue (D7): caption \"error on dark raised 3.03:1\" beside it, since the chip fill is dark raised.\n- The open overflow menu is a card: give it the D8 keyline and its \"5.71:1\" caption.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw the C1 row (Clark Public Utilities) and the C4 row (paid Comcast) in both columns.\n- The provider wraps; it no longer truncates at AX sizes.\n- The chip drops below the provider, then the amount below the chip.\n- The due date and the attribution stack, attribution last.\n- The overflow button stays top-trailing and keeps its target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- status = chip words.\n- overdue = error glyph + \"Overdue\".\n- payer = the name in \"Paid by Sam\".\n- highlighted = 4pt leading bar.\n- marked paid = \"marked paid · Undo\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The label is merged: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday 23 October, upcoming.\"\n- Paid: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99 cents, paid by Sam, Thursday 1 October.\"\n- S3 is a live region: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid. Undo.\" Undo is focusable.\n- Overflow items are also custom actions.\n- The row target is the full row; the overflow is a separate 44pt / 48dp target, 8dp away.\n- Disabled offline items stay in the tree with their reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Notifications say \"marked paid\", not \"paid\".\n- The attribution form is \"Paid by <first name> · <weekday day month>\".\n- A former member reads \"Sam (no longer here)\".\n- The list header names who can see the bills. Never \"Everyone\" when finance access differs.\n- Never write monitoring language such as \"still hasn't paid\".\n\nPLATFORMS (panel; added by this board, not in the contract): the overflow uses the native menu: an iOS pull-down menu, an Android M3 DropdownMenu, and a web menu button with keyboard support. Draw all three in 04.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a one-tap \"Mark paid\" on the row face or the dashboard, draw it inside the overflow menu. A mis-tap must not notify the whole household.\n- Instead of an avatar without a name, draw \"Paid by Sam\". The name is the point.\n- Instead of a budget meter or spend bar, draw the header sentence with the total.\n- Instead of truncating the attribution, truncate the provider.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops plus a platform strip (R13).\n1. f3-bills-list · ios, viewer Maya: the ⑧ header (\"… You and Sam can see these\") and the four upcoming fixture rows, each with its overflow.\n2. f3-member-home-dashboard · android, viewer Sam: a Bills card (radius lg) with the header \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Maya can see these\" and two V2b rows (Clark Public Utilities and City of Vancouver water), each with \"Maya can mark this paid\".\n3. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440: the V1 row as the page's header summary, reached from a notification (S2a), with its overflow as the web menu button.\nPlatform strip: the V1 overflow menu drawn three times, as an iOS pull-down menu, an Android M3 DropdownMenu and a web menu with a visible keyboard focus on its first item.\n\nNOTES (add a \"BillRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: the paid Comcast example · the overdue Waste Connections example with $38.75 · the due-today example · \"Maya can mark this paid\" · \"Maya can give you access to bills\" · \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" · \"You're offline. You can mark bills paid when you're back.\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\".\n- Fixture deltas: C2 shown on Fri 23 Oct · S4 shows Sam before Maya shared bills · HOA dues appears both as a household bill and as a self-added monthly date (DateRow V6).\n- Contract conflicts: header drawn as \"… You and Sam can see these\" instead of contract \"… Everyone at Maple St can see these\", because finance access differs and ScopeChip's doNot requires naming the people · V3 drawn with ScopeChip's sentence \"Only you will see this.\" · platform notes (native overflow menus) added by this board; the contract has none · V2a \"I paid this\" drawn because the contract lists it, but the research brief did not adopt member-recorded payments (a finance.view product decision), so the crops use V2b.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · BillRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · BillRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · BillRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the BillRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five BillRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the header and two rows with callouts ①–⑩, both dashed targets, and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 15 listed cells, labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"BillRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- The V1 SF cell sits beside S2a and S2b, and bar, ring and wash are each distinct.\n- Amounts line up in one column; only the provider ever truncates; the attribution never does.\n- No header says \"Everyone\"; the S4 header has no count, total or scope sentence.\n- \"Mark paid\" appears only inside overflow menus.\n- S3 shows the InlineUndo, the \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" row and the ⑨ callout, with no countdown.\n- 03 shows C1 and C4 in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops and the three native menus.\n- 05 uses D1, D4, D7 and D8 with their captions and the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
