            "promptText": "Component 00c-05: MemberRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: MemberRow. This message is the complete MemberRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). A person in the household. It carries no trust badge and no status badge.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-members-roster · f3-member-home-dashboard · f3-household-block · f3b-owner-attestation · x-place-file · f3b-invitation-decision.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw a MEMBERS group at 2x: the ⑥ heading, the V3 row and the ⑦ disclosure. Beside it, draw V1 at 2x to show ⑧.\n① Row: minimum 56pt, padding 16pt, on surface.base. The row is one element: draw its dashed target.\n② A 40pt initials avatar: a surface.sunken circle (dark: D4) with initials in label 13/18 text.strong. It is neutral, with no identity hue.\n③ Name: body 16/24, text.primary.\n④ Caption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" or \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\".\n⑤ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) holding Change role · Confirm lives here · Remove. On the viewer's own row, the only item is \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". Draw its dashed target.\n⑥ Group heading in overline 11/16, text.secondary: OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS.\n⑦ Group disclosure: a 44pt row under its heading, with a chevron. MEMBERS \"What can members do?\", ADMINS \"What can admins do?\", GUESTS \"What can guests do?\". OWNER has no disclosure.\n⑧ Optional second caption naming method and date: \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 15 Oct 2026\", in caption text.secondary with no badge shape. It appears only on the viewer's own row, never on another person's row, so household members never look different from one another.\n⑨ Web menu callout: \"the ⑤ overflow is the web row menu button; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Home A, viewer Maya. Role variants reuse Sam Ortega, so no new people are invented.\n- V1 · owner: under OWNER · \"Maya Chen (you)\" · \"joined Mon 21 Sep 2026\" · ⑧ caption (Maya's own row) · overflow.\n- V2 · admin: under ADMINS · \"Sam Ortega\" · \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" · no ⑧ · overflow.\n- V3 · member: under MEMBERS · \"Sam Ortega\" · \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" · no ⑧ · overflow.\n- V4 · guest: under GUESTS · \"Sam Ortega\" · \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" · no ⑧ · overflow.\n- V5 · you: Maya's own row, with the overflow open, showing only \"Leave Larkspur Loop\".\n- V6a · roster-line: a 44pt row \"Maya and Sam live here · View\", where \"View\" is a text button.\n- V6b · roster-count (Priya's view before she accepts; count only): a 44pt row \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\", with no action.\n- V7 · empty (Home A before Sam joined; fixture delta): a 44pt row \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\", where \"Invite someone\" is a text button in primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus).\nDraw V1–V4 with their group heading above the row inside the cell.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · default.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the whole row.\n- S2 · loading: a WarmingSkeleton at 56pt with a 40pt circle and two bars, no text, announced once as \"Loading\".\n- S3 · offline: the overflow button opens, but its items are disabled per R8, with the reason \"You're offline. You can change roles when you're back.\" On V5, \"Leave Larkspur Loop\" is disabled with \"You're offline. You can leave when you're back.\"\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 13 cells)\n- S1: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6a, V6b and V7 (8 cells).\n- SF: V3 (1 cell).\n- S2: V3 and V6a (2 cells).\n- S3: V3 and V5 (2 cells), each with its menu open to show the disabled items.\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. Avatar circles and skeleton shapes use D4. Open menus are cards with the D8 keyline and its \"5.71:1\" caption.\n- \"View\" and \"Invite someone\" use dark border.focus.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V3 and V6a in both columns.\n- The avatar stays 40pt, or scales to 48pt at most, top-aligned.\n- The name and caption wrap.\n- V6a moves \"View\" onto its own line, keeping its target.\n- The overflow button stays top-trailing.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- role = the group heading words, never colour.\n- own row = \"(you)\" and the ⑧ caption words.\n- loading = skeleton shapes in the row's geometry.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The avatar is decorative; the name is read.\n- Pattern: \"Sam Ortega, member, joined Tuesday 22 September 2026. Actions available.\"\n- The loading state is announced once as \"Loading\".\n- The overflow items are also custom actions.\n- Row and overflow targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- V6b is read as text, with no action.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Verification is shown on actions, through LockedActionRow, and never on names.\n- The only exception is ⑧ on the viewer's own row, which names the method and the date.\n- Roles are Owner, Admin, Member, Guest. Never \"resident\".\n- Before someone accepts, show only a count: \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\".\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a \"Verified\" or \"Household member\" chip, draw the plain ⑧ caption on the viewer's own row only. A badge on a person reads as a trust score.\n- Instead of a check-badge shape on the avatar, draw the plain initials circle.\n- Instead of listing names to someone who has not accepted, draw the count line \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3-members-roster · ios, viewer Maya: OWNER with V1 (no disclosure), MEMBERS with V3 and its disclosure, then a PENDING group drawn as an outline: the overline \"PENDING\" and one quiet row with a 16pt mail glyph, \"priya@example.com\", the caption \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires Mon 26 Oct\" and a \"Resend\" text button. (That row is InviteRow, which a later message on this board specifies.)\n2. f3-household-block · android: V7 (Home A before Sam joined).\n3. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440, viewer Priya: V6b. No row menu button (no actions).\n\nNOTES (add a \"MemberRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"(you)\" suffix · \"joined Mon 21 Sep 2026\" · \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" · \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" · \"Thu 15 Oct 2026\" in the ⑧ caption · \"What can admins do?\" · \"What can guests do?\" · \"You're offline. You can change roles when you're back.\" · \"You're offline. You can leave when you're back.\"\n- Fixture deltas: V7 shows Home A before Sam joined · V6b shows Priya's view before she accepts · V2 and V4 reuse Sam Ortega in other roles · join dates set in September so that \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\" (BillRow) falls after Sam joined.\n- Contract conflicts: ⑧ verification caption drawn on the viewer's own row only, instead of never (contract \"never on names\") · \"What can members do?\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary lists \"members (in user copy)\" under Not for \"Your household\".\n- Assumptions: the neutral avatar colour (surface.sunken with text.strong initials).\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · MemberRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · MemberRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · MemberRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the MemberRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five MemberRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the MEMBERS group and V1 with callouts ①–⑨, both dashed targets and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 13 listed cells, labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"MemberRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- No row carries a badge, chip, check shape or identity hue; ⑧ appears only on Maya's own row.\n- OWNER has no disclosure; the other three groups each have theirs.\n- The S3 cells show disabled menu items, each with its reason.\n- 03 shows V3 and V6a in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops, with the PENDING outline in crop 1.\n- 05 uses D4 and D8 with their captions and the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
