            "promptText": "Component 00c-06: InviteRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: InviteRow. This message is the complete InviteRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). A pending invitation or invite link, with its expiry and a one-tap fix.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-members-roster · x-place-file · f3-invite-composer · f3-invite-banner.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 at 2x under its \"PENDING\" overline.\n① Row: minimum 56pt, inside a \"PENDING\" group (overline 11/16 text.secondary) that only managers see. It is drawn quieter than people: no avatar.\n② Leading mail glyph, 16pt, text.secondary.\n③ Recipient: bodySmall 14/20, text.primary: \"priya@example.com\", or a username in the form \"@priya\".\n④ Caption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires Mon 26 Oct\".\n⑤ Inline \"Resend\" text button, bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), 44pt target. Draw its dashed target.\n⑥ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) holding Cancel · Extend, 8dp from Resend. Draw its dashed target.\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"the ⑥ overflow is the web row menu button; rows without an overflow use their visible buttons; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · pending-email: as in the anatomy (Resend and overflow).\n- V1u · pending-username: the same row with the recipient \"@priya\".\n- V2 · expiring (fixture delta: shown on Sun 25 Oct): caption \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires tomorrow\". The expiry is words in text.secondary, not tinted. Resend and overflow as V1.\n- V3 · needs-reissue: a 16pt warning glyph (hue on the glyph only; dark: D7) and, in bodySmall text.primary, \"Needs reissue — your household's invite rules changed · Reissue\", where \"Reissue\" is a text button. The row keeps the ⑥ overflow.\n- V4 · declined (fixture delta: Priya declined): the recipient, then a StatusChip \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\". The overflow holds only \"Remove\". There is no Resend.\n- V5 · link-active: a 16pt link glyph, then \"Invite link · Works once · Expires Mon 26 Oct · Turn off link\". \"Turn off link\" is a text button. No overflow.\n- V6 · awaiting-approval (Priya joined by link, so the link is used and no expiry applies): \"priya@example.com · Waiting for your OK\", with two equal-weight text buttons, \"Approve\" and \"Remove\", 8dp apart. No overflow.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · default (the variants as above).\n- SF · focused: the ring on the Resend button only.\n- S2 · sending: \"Resend\" becomes \"Sending…\" and \"Reissue\" becomes \"Reissuing…\", each with a 12pt spinner before it (dark: D6; static text under Reduce Motion). The button is not re-tappable. Beside the cell, draw the follow-on frame: the caption gains \"Sent\" as a role=status caption and the button returns to \"Resend\".\n- S3 · offline: each action is disabled per R8, with its own reason caption under it:\n  - Resend (V1): \"You're offline. You can resend when you're back.\"\n  - Reissue (V3): \"You're offline. You can reissue when you're back.\"\n  - Turn off link (V5): \"You're offline. You can turn off the link when you're back.\"\n  - Approve (V6): \"You're offline. You can approve when you're back.\"\n  - Remove (V4, V6): \"You're offline. You can remove this when you're back.\"\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 14 cells)\n- S1: V1, V1u, V2, V3, V4, V5 and V6 (7 cells).\n- SF: V1, ring on Resend only (1 cell).\n- S2: V1 and V3 (2 cells). V4 in S2: \"n/a — declined invites cannot be resent\" (1 cell).\n- S3: V1, V5 and V6 (3 cells). The V6 cell shows both Approve and Remove disabled, each with its own reason.\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. The V3 warning glyph keeps its hue (D7): caption \"warning on dark base 5.60:1\" beside it. The StatusChip fill uses D4. Spinners use D6.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V6 in both columns.\n- The recipient wraps at the \"@\".\n- The caption wraps at middots.\n- Resend drops below the caption and keeps its target; the overflow stays top-trailing.\n- Approve and Remove stack, each at full width with its own target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- expiring = \"Expires tomorrow\" words.\n- needs reissue = warning glyph shape + \"Needs reissue\".\n- declined = chip words \"Declined\".\n- link = link glyph + \"Works once\".\n- sending = \"Sending…\" words.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Pattern: \"Invitation to priya@example.com, member, expires Monday 26 October. Resend. Button.\"\n- A successful resend is announced as \"Invitation resent\".\n- Expiry is always in words.\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps.\n- Overflow items are also custom actions.\n- Disabled offline actions stay in the tree with their reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The expiry is shown on every pending invite (email or username) and on every active link. An awaiting-approval row shows none, because its link has already been used.\n- The link warning (\"Works once\") appears at the point of choice.\n- Every email uses @example.com.\n- Each offline reason names the action it blocks.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a \"Remind them\" action on a declined invite, draw only \"Remove\". A decline is an answer.\n- Instead of a real email domain, draw @example.com.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted expiring row, draw \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.secondary words. Urgency comes from the date, not from colour.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3-members-roster · ios, viewer Maya: the PENDING group with V1 and V5, below the MEMBERS group outline.\n2. f3-invite-banner · android: V3 as the banner's single slot.\n3. f3-invite-composer · web-1440: V5 under the link choice. \"Turn off link\" is visible, so there is no row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add an \"InviteRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"@priya\" · \"sent Mon 12 Oct\" · \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"Expires Mon 26 Oct\" on the link row · \"Sending…\" · \"Reissuing…\" · \"Sent\" · \"Invitation resent\" · the five offline reasons.\n- Fixture deltas: V2 on Sun 25 Oct · V4: Priya declined · V6: Priya joined by link and awaits approval.\n- Contract conflicts: \"Approve\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary lists \"approve member\" under Not for confirming a person · expiry drawn on pending invites and the active link and omitted on the awaiting-approval row, narrowing \"the expiry is always shown\".\n- Assumptions: V3 keeps the Cancel · Extend overflow.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · InviteRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · InviteRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · InviteRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the InviteRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five InviteRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the V1 row with callouts ①–⑦, both dashed targets and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 14 listed cells (including the one n/a cell with its reason), labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"InviteRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- No row has an avatar or a tint; the expiring row uses words only.\n- Every S3 action carries the reason that names it.\n- Every email ends in @example.com.\n- 03 shows V1 and V6 in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops.\n- 05 uses D4, D6 and D7 with its caption, and the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
