            "promptText": "Component 00c-07: NotificationRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: NotificationRow. This message is the complete NotificationRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). The in-app twin of every push. Tapping it lands on the exact object.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-household-notifications · f4-notification-settings.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 (unread) and V4 (unread, system) at 2x, stacked, and V7 expanded beside them.\n① Row: minimum 64pt, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt trailing, on surface.base. The whole row is the target: draw its dashed target.\n② A fixed 12pt leading column holding a 6pt unread dot in primary.700 (dark: D6), with the accessibility label \"Unread\". Read rows keep the empty column, so the text never shifts. The dot is not a provenance mark and not a target.\n③ A 28pt initials avatar (surface.sunken circle, text.strong initials; dark: D4). System rows have no avatar, and their text keeps the same leading alignment.\n④ Line 1: body 16/24, text.primary, a sentence with the actor first.\n⑤ Line 2: caption 12/16 text.secondary, joined by middots: the date and time · the home label (only for readers with more than one home) · for reminders, a trailing ProvenanceMark S.\n⑥ Grouped row: a chevron disclosure that expands to the individual rows.\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Home A, viewer Maya. Times are invented except 7:00 AM, the morning briefing time. Each variant is an independent specimen.\n- V1 · bill-paid: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid · $142.18\" · \"Today · 5:40 PM\".\n- V2 · task-completed: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked \"Carts out\" done\" · \"Today · 5:55 PM\".\n- V3 · event-created: Sam avatar · \"Sam added a date: Gutter cleaning, Sat 7 Nov\" · \"Yesterday · 8:12 PM\".\n- V4 · date-reminder (system): \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · filled mark.\n- V5 · bill-reminder (system): \"Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · $142.18\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · YOU ADDED mark.\n- V6j · member-joined (fixture delta: Priya has accepted): Priya avatar · \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\" · \"Today · 4:20 PM\".\n- V6l · member-left (fixture delta: Sam has left): Sam avatar · \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\" · \"Today · 4:25 PM\".\n- V7 · grouped: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" · \"Today · 5:40 PM\" · chevron. Draw it expanded below into three V1-style rows (Clark Public Utilities $142.18, City of Vancouver water $84.00, Comcast $79.99).\n- V8 · gone-target: the landing after tapping a removed bill: the bill screen's header outline with a visible Back, and a plain body line \"That bill was removed.\" in the bill's slot. The notifications list stays reachable through Back.\n- V9 · multi-home (fixture delta: Maya has a second home): V1 with line 2 \"Today · 5:40 PM · Larkspur Loop\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2, SF, S3, S4)\n- S1 · unread: dot present.\n- S2 · read: no dot; identical text weight and fill.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the whole row.\n- S3 · push-off: a 44pt banner row at the top of the list: \"Push is off. You'll still see these here. · Turn on\", in bodySmall text.strong on surface.sunken (dark: D3), with \"Turn on\" as a text button (primary.700, 5.39:1 on sunken).\n- S4 · offline: the FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" above the list. Rows stay readable. Tapping a row whose object is not cached shows the reason \"You're offline. This opens when you're back.\" under that row.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 21 cells)\n- S1 and S2: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6j, V6l and V7 (16 cells).\n- S1: V9, and V8 as one cell (2 cells).\n- SF: V1 (1 cell).\n- S3: one cell in the V1 row: the banner above a V1 row.\n- S4: one cell in the V1 row: the FreshnessLine above V1 and V4, with the reason under V4.\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. The unread dot uses D6. Avatars use D4. The S3 banner uses D3. Marks use dark text.secondary.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V7 in both columns.\n- The sentence wraps fully.\n- Line 2 wraps at middots.\n- The dot column stays 12pt, top-aligned with line 1.\n- The avatar stays 28pt.\n- The V7 chevron moves below the text and keeps its target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03)\n- Captions: unread = dot presence + \"Unread\" spoken first · reminder provenance = mark shape · grouped = chevron + \"3 bills\".\n- Draw one extra greyscale cell showing an unread V1 above a read V1, differing only by the dot, with the caption \"unread is also spoken first\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The label is merged, with \"Unread\" first: \"Unread. Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid, 142 dollars 18 cents. Today, 5:40 PM.\"\n- Reminder rows end with the mark name: \"…Today, 7:00 AM, official.\"\n- The row is the target and lands on the exact object.\n- The grouped row reads \"Sam marked 3 bills paid, collapsed, button\".\n- The S3 banner is read as text, then \"Turn on. Button.\"\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Amounts appear in-app only, never in pushes.\n- Use \"marked paid\", not \"paid\"; the grouped row reads \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\".\n- The actor comes first.\n- A landing whose object no longer exists says \"That bill was removed.\"\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of bold text or a tinted background for unread rows, draw the 6pt dot plus the spoken \"Unread\". Weight and tint changes make read rows look disabled.\n- Instead of landing on a generic list when the object exists, land on the object: the bill row highlighted (BillRow highlighted-arrival).\n- Instead of an avatar on system rows, leave the avatar slot empty and keep the text aligned.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): two crops (R13).\n1. f3-household-notifications · ios, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; the S3 banner; then V1 (unread), V4 (unread) and V3 (read); the legend line.\n2. f4-notification-settings · web-1440: the \"Household activity\" settings group with a sample V1 row. No row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add a \"NotificationRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"5:40 PM\", \"5:55 PM\", \"8:12 PM\", \"4:20 PM\", \"4:25 PM\" · \"Carts out\" · \"Gutter cleaning, Sat 7 Nov\" · \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\" · \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\" · \"You're offline. This opens when you're back.\"\n- Fixture deltas: V1 shows Clark Public Utilities marked paid, while BillRow shows it upcoming · V6j: Priya joined, although the fixture has her pending · V6l: Sam left · V7: three bills marked paid · V9: Maya with a second home.\n- Contract conflicts: grouped row drawn as \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" instead of contract \"Sam paid 3 bills\" · \"Push is off…\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary limits \"push\" to technical settings copy.\n- Assumptions: V5 carries a YOU ADDED mark (household bills are entered by the household); the contract requires a mark but does not say which.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · NotificationRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · NotificationRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the NotificationRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five NotificationRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1, V4 and expanded V7 with callouts ①–⑦, the dashed row target and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 21 listed cells, labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"NotificationRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- Unread and read rows differ only by the dot: same weight, same fill, no text shift.\n- System rows (V4, V5) have no avatar and keep their text aligned; reminder rows end with a mark.\n- The home label appears only on V9.\n- 03 shows V1 and V7 in both columns, the greyscale grid, its captions and the extra unread/read cell.\n- 04 shows both crops; the iOS crop has the legend line and \"Your household\".\n- 05 uses D3, D4 and D6 and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
