            "promptText": "Component 00c-09: LockedActionRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: LockedActionRow. This message is the complete LockedActionRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). Replaces or accompanies an unavailable control. It states the reason and the path forward.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3b-locked-action-row · f3-members-roster · f3-member-home-dashboard · f3b-invitation-decision · f3-bills-list · f3-bill-detail-web · f3-household-calendar · f10-bill-provenance · f10-extraction-confirm · x-place-file · x-date-sheet · f6-home-basics-rows · f9-block-founders-panel · f11-keeper-strip.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 at 2x: the disabled button with the row under it.\n① One row, minimum 44pt, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal.\n② Leading lock glyph, 16pt, text.secondary.\n③ Reason in bodySmall 14/20: text.strong on surface.sunken, or text.secondary on surface.base.\n④ Trailing link \"Verify address\" in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), with a 44pt target. Draw its dashed target.\n⑤ A 1px border.subtle hairline above the row (decoration only).\n⑥ The reason wraps to 2 lines before anything truncates.\n⑦ When the row sits under a disabled button, tapping the disabled button opens the same reason. Draw a callout arrow from the button to the row.\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · under-cta: a disabled filled button \"Message your neighbors\" (per R8: surface.sunken fill, text.strong label, kept focusable; dark: D4), with the row directly below it on surface.base: \"Address verification needed to message your neighbors · Verify address\".\n- V2 · list-row: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter · Verify address\", drawn as two rows:\n  - V2s · list-row-sunken: on surface.sunken, reason in text.strong.\n  - V2b · list-row-base: on surface.base, reason in text.secondary.\n- V3 · card-header: a card (radius lg, shadow sm; dark: D8 edge) titled \"Residency Pass\", with the row inside the header on surface.base: \"Address verification needed to show your Residency Pass · Verify address\".\n- V4 · pending (viewer Sam, whose postcard is still in transit; Maya's address is already confirmed): \"We're checking your postcard code — expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\", with no link.\n- V5 · server-refused, shown after a tap the server refused: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter. We checked again. · Verify address\".\n- V6 · names-who-can-act (viewer Sam, who can see bills but not add them): \"Maya can add bills here\", with no link.\n- V7 · not-at-tier (Place B): \"Claim this address first\" in text.secondary, with no link and no button.\nAll rows sit on surface.base unless stated.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · locked.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the \"Verify address\" link only (R8).\n- S2 · pending: V4's form.\n- S3 · offline: the link is disabled per R8 (text.secondary, focusable), with the reason caption \"You're offline. You can verify when you're back.\" under it. On V1, the disabled button keeps its own reason.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 17 cells)\n- S1: V1, V2s, V2b, V3, V5, V6 and V7 (7 cells). V4 in S1: \"n/a — pending is its own variant\" (1 cell).\n- SF: V2b (1 cell).\n- S2: V4 (1 cell).\n- S3: V1, V2b, V3 and V5 (4 cells). V4, V6 and V7 in S3: \"n/a — this variant has no link to disable\" (3 cells).\n\nDARK (05)\n- V2s uses D3 (dark raised, dark text.strong). The V1 disabled button uses D4. The V3 card uses D8: caption \"keyline 5.71:1\" beside it. Other rows sit on dark base with dark text.secondary reasons (6.96:1).\n- The lock glyph uses dark text.secondary. Links use dark border.focus.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V2b in both columns.\n- The reason wraps fully.\n- \"Verify address\" drops to its own line below the reason, left-aligned, keeping its target.\n- The lock glyph scales to 24pt and stays top-aligned.\n- The V1 button grows in height and its label wraps.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- locked = lock glyph + the words; nothing is coloured except the link.\n- link = its position and its verb.\n- offline = the reason caption under the dimmed link.\n- pending = \"We're checking\" words, no lock-state colour.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The reason is at 4.5:1 or better (text.strong on sunken 9.37:1; text.secondary on base 4.83:1).\n- The link names its destination: \"Verify address, opens Verify this address\".\n- The disabled button is exposed with its reason as a hint: \"Message your neighbors, dimmed. Address verification needed to message your neighbors.\"\n- The offline link is exposed as dimmed, with its reason as a hint.\n- Row and link targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The pattern is \"Address verification needed to <specific action>\". Any extra context (V5) follows as a second sentence.\n- Never write a generic \"Verification required\".\n- When someone else can act, name them (\"Maya can add bills here\").\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of red or amber colouring, draw the neutral lock glyph in text.secondary. Nothing is wrong; something is not yet available.\n- Instead of text.muted for the reason or the disabled link, draw text.strong on sunken or text.secondary on base, because both must be read.\n- Instead of a present but inert control with no explanation, draw the control with this row under it.\n- Instead of showing a saved-place user a verification lock on a home-only feature, draw V7 \"Claim this address first\". Verification means nothing before a claim.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios, viewer Sam: V1.\n2. f3-bills-list · android, viewer Sam after Maya shared bills (Sam can see them but not add them): the header \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Maya can see these\", two bill rows drawn as outlines (Clark Public Utilities $142.18, City of Vancouver water $84.00), and V6 at the foot of the list.\n3. f9-block-founders-panel · web-1440: V3's card-header form on a card titled \"Block Founders\", with the row \"Address verification needed to earn a Block Founder rank · Verify address\".\n\nNOTES (add a \"LockedActionRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"We're checking your postcard code — expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\" · \"We checked again.\" · \"You're offline. You can verify when you're back.\" · \"Address verification needed to earn a Block Founder rank\" · the other reasons, built from the contract pattern and the grant/limit string set.\n- Fixture deltas: V4: Sam's postcard is still pending, while Maya's address is already confirmed · V6 and crop 2: Sam can see bills after Maya shared them but cannot add them.\n- Contract conflicts: \"Verify address\" drawn instead of the glossary's \"Verify this address\" · V7 \"Claim this address first\" (a contract string) drawn on a Place B row, although ScopeChip's copy rule says a saved place never uses the word \"claim\" · V5 drawn as \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter. We checked again.\" instead of a generic server-refusal notice, to keep the contract pattern.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · LockedActionRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · LockedActionRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · LockedActionRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · LockedActionRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · LockedActionRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · LockedActionRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · LockedActionRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the LockedActionRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five LockedActionRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1 with callouts ①–⑧, the link target, the button-to-row arrow and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 17 listed cells (including four n/a cells with their reasons), labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"LockedActionRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- No red, amber or text.muted appears; reasons use text.strong on sunken and text.secondary on base.\n- Every reason with a link follows \"Address verification needed to <specific action>\".\n- The V2b SF cell rings the link only.\n- 03 shows V1 and V2b in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops; the bills crop never says \"Everyone\".\n- 05 uses D3, D4 and D8 with its caption, and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
          },
