            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-10: GrantLimitList. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: GrantLimitList. This message is the complete GrantLimitList specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). Two scannable lists: what you get now (ticked) and what needs address verification (locked). One component serves invite, attestation and verify.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3b-invitation-decision · f3-invite-composer · f3b-owner-attestation · f3b-verify-address-sheet · f9-verification-promise-copy · f3-members-roster.\n\nEXTRA STAND-IN FOR THIS COMPONENT (label it \"stand-in\", per R11)\n- ChoiceChip: pill, 32pt visual height inside a 44pt / 48dp target, label 13/18. Selected: primary.50 fill, primary.700 label and a leading check glyph (dark: D5). Unselected: a 1px text.secondary edge and a text.strong label. The focus ring is distinct from selection. At AX sizes the chips become radio rows. Platform notes: an iOS segmented control where native; M3 filter chips on Android.\n\nSTRING SET (exact; every variant draws from it)\n- Grants: \"Sees and edits the calendar\" · \"Sees bills and who paid\" · \"Sees who lives here\".\n- Limits: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw the specimen twice: the stacked iOS form of V1 at 2x, and the two-column web-1440 form of V1 beside or below it at 1x (never shrunk; R2).\n① Grant list heading \"What you get now\": label 13/18 text.strong. The grant list always comes first.\n② Grant rows, 44pt each: a 16pt bare stroke check in success hue (a stroke, not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark; dark: D7), a 12pt gap, and the verb phrase in body 16/24 text.primary.\n③ Limit list heading \"What needs address verification\": label 13/18 text.strong.\n④ Limit rows, 44pt each: a 16pt lock glyph in text.secondary, a 12pt gap, and the verb phrase in body 16/24 text.primary.\n⑤ Callout: \"both lists use identical type and row height\".\n⑥ Callout: \"two columns 24pt apart on web 1440; stacked on mobile (iOS, Android, web 390)\".\n⑦ Callout: \"one shared string set; every variant draws from it\".\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · invitation-decision: both headings, all 3 grants and all 5 limits. The grid cell draws the stacked iOS form.\n- V2 · role-offered: under a 44pt disclosure row \"Role offered: Member\" (expanded), the heading \"What you get now\" and the 3 grants only.\n- V3 · attestation: the heading \"What you get once Maya confirms you live here\", then 3 rows with stroke checks: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show your Residency Pass\".\n- V4 · verify-unlock: the heading \"What needs address verification\", then \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" with lock glyphs, then a 44pt row \"and 3 more\" with a chevron that expands the remaining three limits.\n- V5 · role-caption-member: a ChoiceChip pair, \"Member\" (selected) and \"Guest\". Under them, a caption in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"Sees and edits the calendar · Sees bills and who paid · Sees who lives here\". It has no visible heading and is exposed as a list with the accessible name \"What members can do\".\n- V5g · role-caption-guest: the same chips with \"Guest\" selected. The caption reads \"Sees and edits the calendar\", exposed as a list named \"What guests can do\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2, SF, SX)\n- S1 · default.\n- S2 · accepted: the limit list gains the caption \"Verify your address to unlock these\", in caption text.secondary, directly under its heading.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the \"and 3 more\" row only.\n- SX · selected: the V5 \"Member\" chip in its selected form, placed so it sits directly beside the SF cell for comparison.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 14 cells)\n- S1: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5 and V5g (6 cells).\n- S2: V1 (1 cell). V2, V3, V4, V5 and V5g in S2: \"n/a — accepted applies after an invitation is accepted\" (5 cells).\n- SF: V4 (1 cell).\n- SX: V5 (1 cell).\n\nDARK (05)\n- Lists sit on dark surface.base. The success check keeps its hue (D7): caption \"success on dark base 4.74:1\" beside the first one. Lock glyphs use dark text.secondary.\n- Selected chips use D5. Unselected chip edges use dark text.secondary (6.96:1).\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V5 in both columns.\n- The two lists stack, grants first.\n- Phrases wrap; glyphs stay top-aligned and scale to 24pt.\n- In V5, the chips become radio rows, each with a 44pt / 48dp target, and the caption wraps under them.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- grant vs limit = stroke check vs lock (shape) + the headings.\n- selected chip = its check glyph.\n- accepted = the \"Verify your address to unlock these\" caption.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Each list has a heading, exposed as a heading. Where there is no visible heading (V5, V5g), the list has an accessible name.\n- The check and lock glyphs are decorative; the heading carries the meaning.\n- Rows are read as list items: \"What you get now, list, 3 items. Sees and edits the calendar.\"\n- \"and 3 more\" is a 44pt / 48dp button, spoken \"Show 3 more\".\n- Chips are spoken with their selected state: \"Member, selected\".\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Every row is a verb phrase.\n- Use the string set exactly.\n- Never write a bare product name.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): stacked on mobile (iOS, Android, web 390) and two columns on web 1440. The V5 chips follow the ChoiceChip platform notes (an iOS segmented control where native; M3 filter chips on Android).\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a warning box around the limits, draw the plain lock rows. Limits are information, not danger.\n- Instead of bare product names (\"Real Rent\", \"Residency Pass\"), draw verb phrases (\"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\"). People decide on what they can do.\n- Instead of text.muted on sunken for locked rows, draw body text.primary with a text.secondary lock, because these rows must be read.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440: V1 in two columns, with \"Accept\" and \"Not now\" as equal-weight buttons below.\n2. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios: a medium-detent sheet with a visible Close, holding V4.\n3. f3-invite-composer · android: V5 with M3 filter chips.\n\nNOTES (add a \"GrantLimitList\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"What you get now\" · \"What needs address verification\" · \"What you get once Maya confirms you live here\" · \"What members can do\" · \"What guests can do\" · \"Role offered: Member\" · \"Show 3 more\".\n- Contract conflicts: unselected ChoiceChip drawn with a text.secondary edge instead of the contract's border.strong, because the house style forbids a border token as an input's only edge.\n- Assumptions: the three attestation grant rows (V3) and the Guest capability caption (V5g); the contract does not give them.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · GrantLimitList · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · GrantLimitList · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · GrantLimitList · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · GrantLimitList · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · GrantLimitList · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · GrantLimitList · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · GrantLimitList · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the GrantLimitList section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five GrantLimitList artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the stacked 2x form and the two-column 1x form with callouts ①–⑧ and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 14 listed cells (including five n/a cells with their reason), labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"GrantLimitList · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- Every row uses a string from the set, exactly; grants come first; both lists share type and row height.\n- Grant glyphs are bare stroke checks; no warning box appears.\n- SF (V4) and SX (V5) sit side by side and look different.\n- 03 shows V1 and V5 in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops; the sheet has a visible Close.\n- 05 uses D5 and D7 with its caption, and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
          },
          {
