        "resolved": [
          "[major] BillRow header broke ScopeChip's exact-string and doNot rules. Resolved in 00c-04: header ⑧ reads '… You and Sam can see these' for Maya and '… You and Maya can see these' for Sam. The S4 header is just 'Bills', with no count, total or scope claim. The BillRow Notes carry the contract-conflict line ('Everyone at Maple St' replaced, and why). The name-the-people rule is also in the R11 ScopeChip stand-in in 00c-00.",
          "[major] Home A pickup provenance was contradictory. Resolved with one timeline: as of TODAY the pickup is hollow (DateRow V1a/V1b in 00c-01, FactRow V1b in 00c-02). FactRow V1d (a filled twin of V1b, key known-pickup-confirmed) and V4 show the state after Maya confirmed Tuesday. They sit in adjacent rows and are listed as a fixture delta in both components' Notes.",
          "[major] LockedActionRow V5 was a generic notice. Resolved in 00c-09: V5 reads 'Address verification needed to get a residency letter. We checked again. · Verify address'. 'We checked again.' is listed as invented, and the conflict is recorded.",
          "[minor] InviteRow offline reason was wrong for Turn off link and Reissue. Resolved in 00c-06 S3: one reason per action (Resend, Reissue, Turn off link, Approve, Remove). The V6 cell shows both Approve and Remove with their own reasons, and a copy rule requires each reason to name its action.",
          "[minor] InviteRow 'expiry always shown' contradicted V5/V6. Resolved in 00c-06: V5 shows 'Expires Mon 26 Oct'. The copy rule is narrowed to pending invites and active links, with none on awaiting-approval because the link is used. The narrowing is on Notes.",
          "[minor] Glossary conflicts (Approve; Upload failed / Uploading) were missing from Notes. Resolved as Notes contract-conflict lines in 00c-06 (Approve), 00c-11 (Upload failed) and 00c-12 (Uploading / Upload failed).",
          "[minor] BillRow platform notes contradicted the platforms default. Resolved: the 00c-04 PLATFORMS panel is labelled 'added by this board, not in the contract', R12 in 00c-00 says the default applies 'unless a component's PLATFORMS says otherwise', and the addition is on Notes.",
          "[minor] Disabled text actions were inconsistent (text.muted vs text.secondary). Resolved in R8 of 00c-00 with one treatment everywhere: label in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken, per R4), focusable, reason caption underneath, never text.muted. R4 says text.muted appears nowhere on the board, and every component's offline state points to R8.",
          "[minor] Highlight looked like selected plus focused. Resolved in R8: highlight is an infoBg wash plus a 4pt leading bar inside the row, with no outline and never a check. Focus is a ring 2px outside. Selection is a fill plus a check. Focused cells sit beside highlighted or selected cells (DateRow V3a SF, BillRow V1 SF, GrantLimitList SF/SX, ThumbnailRail SX/SF).",
          "[minor] Crops were missing the provenance legend and ScopeChip. Resolved in R13: every crop that shows a mark carries the legend line and the place's ScopeChip. Each such crop names both explicitly (DateRow 1–3, FactRow 1, FirstWeekRow 1, NotificationRow 1, TextActionRow 2, InlineErrorRow 1). The DateRow strip crop is annotated 'strip cells are not targets; the rows below are'.",
          "[minor] DateRow approximate sub-cell was not recorded as a delta. Resolved: V5x (key reminder-approx) is labelled a fixture delta and listed in the DateRow Notes. It also gets the identity.home rule and 'Does not repeat', like other self-entered rows (recorded as an assumption).",
          "[minor] DateRow spoken example included an unseen absolute date. Resolved in the 00c-01 ACCESSIBILITY panel: the label speaks only the dates the row shows, and the example is now 'Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Waste Connections city schedule, on record, not confirmed.'",
          "[minor] ScopeChip stand-in lacked spoken names. Resolved in R11 of 00c-00: 'Visible to only you' and 'Visible to your household'.",
          "[minor] The web row menu button was never drawn. Resolved: R3 requires a 'web menu' callout on every 01-anatomy, and each component gives its exact wording (a row menu button for DateRow; overflow-as-menu for BillRow, MemberRow and InviteRow; 'no row menu button' elsewhere). R12 requires the button in web crops, and every web crop says whether it draws one.",
          "[minor] 'Claim this address first' on Place B conflicts with ScopeChip's no-'claim' rule. Resolved as a contract-internal conflict line in the FactRow (00c-02) and LockedActionRow (00c-09) Notes.",
          "[minor] Fixture drift (V4 viewer; HOA dues). Resolved: LockedActionRow V4 names viewer Sam, with Maya already confirmed (00c-09 delta). The DateRow and BillRow Notes both record that HOA dues appears as a household bill and as a self-added monthly date.",
          "[minor] GrantLimitList tick could read as the YOU ADDED mark. Resolved: 00c-10 ② is a 'bare stroke check … not a disc', FactRow V4 says the same, and R11 states that every non-provenance check on the board is a bare stroke.",
          "[minor] Increase Contrast and a dark card edge were missing. Resolved in R5: D8 gives a 1px dark text.secondary keyline with ratio captions (5.71:1 on raised), and an Increase Contrast note is required on every 05. D8 is applied to the LockedActionRow V3 card, the InlineErrorRow V5 card and the open BillRow/MemberRow menus.",
          "[major] Fraction row, percentage string and 'founder decision' were drawn. Resolved: there is no 06-fraction artboard, each component has exactly five artboards (61 in total, including Notes), and PUBLISH has no 'unless I accept' clauses. ThumbnailRail draws only 'Uploading 2 of 3'. The FirstWeekRow and ThumbnailRail Notes record the contract strings as 'contract lists …; not drawn, because house invariant 6 and the research brief rejected it', without printing the fraction or percentage and without 'founder decision needed'. R14 bans both from specimens, callouts and crops. The FactRow skeleton widths are now given in pt, not percentages.",
          "[major] Grid cells had no exact labels. Resolved in R7 with the B18-style key grammar: labels read '<code> · <key>' with a printed 'key: <key>' line underneath. Keys are lowercase and hyphenated, with no '/', fixture string or date. Every cell is captioned '<ComponentName> · <variant key> · <state key>', and PUBLISH uses keys only. Every variant and state in all twelve prompts has a key. Three keys that contained fixture words were renamed: FactRow V1c known-pickup-saved-place, TextActionRow V2a outbound-source-named, and V2b outbound-verb-first.",
          "[minor] Highlight and focus used the same stroke, and dark D1 matched D3 rows. Resolved in R8 (bar inside, ring 2px outside, never touching) and in R5 D1 ('on a row already on raised (D3), the bar alone').",
          "[minor] One offline reason was reused for the wrong actions (quality duplicate of the InviteRow item). Resolved by the same per-action reasons in 00c-06, each marked invented on Notes.",
          "[minor] FactRow 'Add' target was ambiguous. Resolved in 00c-02 ⑧: chevron rows are one target. On text-action rows, the action is a separate 44pt/48dp/44px button and the row is not a target. V3 and V8 are not targets. The SF cell rings 'Add' only, and the contract narrowing is on Notes.",
          "[minor] InlineErrorRow V5 host card was undefined. Resolved in 00c-11: an f9-block-founders-panel card titled 'Block Founders', with a card-header LockedActionRow directly under the title, no gap and no error row, dashed brackets labelled founding meter / invite banner / Earn row, and the fail-closed annotation.",
          "[minor] BillRow header said everyone could see bills (quality duplicate). Resolved with the named, viewer-relative header in 00c-04 ('You and Sam' / 'You and Maya', matching ScopeChip's doNot example). The same header is used in the BillRow crops and the LockedActionRow bills crop.",
          "[minor] Open layout details. Resolved: in BillRow, the V2b caption 'replaces the right side of line 2'. In MemberRow, 'OWNER has no disclosure'. In TextActionRow, the 12pt spinner replaces the start of the 'Compare with a friend' label, which reads 'Making a link…'; the contract's 'URL row' wording is noted as a conflict.",
          "[minor] DateRow strings broke the section's own rules. Resolved in 00c-01 COPY RULES ('Conditional rules (V4) are exempt from the relative count') and with the corrected spoken example.",
          "[minor] Some invented strings were unmarked. Resolved: each component prompt now has its own NOTES 'Invented strings' list naming them, including Sending…, Reissuing…, Retrying…, Sent, Making a link…, the 'Reminder:' prefix, city schedule, 'Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027' and 'Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills'.",
          "[minor] Source asides and a duplicated reasons list. Resolved: no prompt cites v1 prompts, the brief or the contract's inconsistency list as a source. Notes lines use 'drawn as X instead of contract Y', one per line, and the non-conflict item was dropped.",
          "[minor] BillRow platform notes (quality duplicate). Resolved by the same label in 00c-04 and the Notes line 'platform notes (native overflow menus) added by this board; the contract has none'.",
          "[minor] Delivery order reversed the house-style priority. Resolved: R1 orders the artboards 01-anatomy, 02-grid, 03-ax5-200-greyscale, 04-in-context, 05-grid · dark. Every BATCH PLAN draws 01+02 in Turn 1 and 03–05 plus the Notes update in Turn 2. The fallback order note is gone.",
          "EXTRA (contrast): computed ratios showed text.secondary failing on sunken (4.39) and errorBg (4.42), warning and identity.home failing on sunken, and dark text.secondary failing on dark border.strong (4.02). R4, R6 and R8 now require text.strong on sunken and errorBg (including disabled labels and reasons) and mark those pairs FAIL. InlineErrorRow's 'Retrying…' follows that rule.",
          "EXTRA (FactRow V6 offline): 'Open Settings' opens the system settings and needs no network. V6 S3 now keeps it enabled, with the annotation 'Open Settings works offline', recorded on Notes.",
          "EXTRA (fixture drift): the LockedActionRow bills crop showed V6 'Maya can add bills here' for Sam before bills were shared, which contradicted BillRow S4 ('Maya can give you access to bills'). The crop now shows Sam after sharing (view-only), with the named header. NotificationRow V3 had Sam adding HOA dues, which DateRow marks YOU ADDED for Maya; it now reads 'Sam added a date: Gutter cleaning, Sat 7 Nov' (invented). MemberRow join dates (12/13 Oct) fell after 'Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct', so they moved to Mon 21 / Tue 22 Sep 2026.",
          "EXTRA (research brief): the brief did not adopt member-recorded 'I paid this'. BillRow V2a is still drawn because the contract lists it, but it is flagged on Notes as a finance.view product decision, and the member dashboard crop now uses V2b ('Maya can mark this paid').",
          "EXTRA (turn order): BillRow S4 and the MemberRow roster crop need LockedActionRow and InviteRow, which arrive later in the requested order, so both are described inline as outlines. InlineErrorRow V5 (after LockedActionRow) and ThumbnailRail ⑤ (after InlineErrorRow) reference components already drawn. The DateRow 01 adds a V3c done specimen so callouts ⑧ and ⑨ have something to point at.",
          "Word counts (words containing letters or digits; the contrast table adds numeric tokens): setup ≈2,250; components 1,107 to 2,034. Artboard names and contract names were checked by script: every component name matches the contract, and no non-contract component name is introduced."
        ]
