      {
        "setup": {
          "id": "00d-00",
          "promptText": "Foundations board 00d: States, feedback and asks. BOARD SETUP.\n\nUse the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is one Foundations board. This message sets the board rules and draws nothing. Eight component prompts follow, one per turn, in this order: 1 QuietDayReceipt, 2 WarmingSkeleton, 3 InlineUndo, 4 DestructiveConfirm, 5 LandingBannerSlot, 6 NotificationAsk, 7 PushCopy, 8 ReminderLeadControl. Each one opens with \"Component 00d-NN: <Name>. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\" and carries that component's complete specification.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nType: NEW, a component specimen board, with no screens. The eight components cover the moments when the product must be honest about time and consent: nothing is wrong, something is loading, something can or can't be taken back, something is waiting, and the product wants to interrupt now or on dates you chose. Each has a quiet default; none nags.\nLater, 59 surfaces are designed in separate projects with no memory of this one, and they use these components by exact name from the published Pantopus design system. So every size, token, string and state in a component prompt is literal. Draw each component once, precisely, with every variant and state its prompt lists.\n\nHOW THIS PROJECT RUNS\n1. Each component prompt has an ARTBOARDS list and a BATCH PLAN of at most 6 artboards per turn. Draw batch 1 and stop; the founder types \"continue\" before each later batch. After a component's last batch, wait for the next component prompt.\n2. Before every batch, re-read these rules (R1–R19) and the whole current component prompt. Don't carry details from one component to another unless a prompt says so.\n3. Component order replaces the house-style priority order, so each component is finished, dark twin included, before the next starts. A named attachment arrives with its component prompt.\n4. Ask a question only if two readings would give materially different specimens. Otherwise decide, and record it on Notes (R19).\n\nPUBLISH (a founder step)\nWhen the founder accepts a component by name, the founder adds it to the Pantopus design system under that exact name (QuietDayReceipt, WarmingSkeleton, InlineUndo, DestructiveConfirm, LandingBannerSlot, NotificationAsk, PushCopy, ReminderLeadControl), with each specimen under the name printed beneath it (R7). Make that step mechanical: every specimen carries its name, and Notes section F lists them all. Rules:\n- Every drawn specimen is published in light. Every specimen on a component's dark artboards is published in dark; every variant × state cell has a dark twin there.\n- Light-only frames (platform strips, large-text frames, web-1440 crops, and anything a prompt marks light only) are published in light only and listed on Notes section E. A later dark surface takes their geometry from the light frame and their colours from the dark artboard and R9.\n- Greyscale copies, \"Not applicable\" cells, \"Not this\" thumbnails and IN CONTEXT crops are review aids, never published.\n\nBOARD RULES\n\nR1. Artboard names. \"00d · <Component> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\", exactly as each ARTBOARDS list gives it. This replaces the house-style format \"<surface-id> · <platform> · <NN-state> · <light|dark>\" on this board, because one artboard can hold several platforms; the platform goes in each specimen's name (R7). The Notes artboard is named exactly \"00d · Notes\", with no light/dark suffix. Print it above the frame in label 13/18/600 text.strong.\n\nR2. Artboard format. 1600px wide, as tall as needed, on surface.app (dark: dark app). Top left: the component name in h2 24/32/600 text.primary, then the artboard's subject in body text.secondary. Each 01 artboard also prints the PURPOSE line (body text.secondary) and \"Used in:\" line (caption 12/16 text.secondary) as given. Section headings are overline 11/16/600 caps text.strong.\n\nR3. Platforms and widths. Specimens are 1x at real width: iOS 393pt, Android 412dp, web-390 390px, web-1440 1440px (cropped to the relevant column and labelled \"web-1440 crop\"). Content width inside 16 margins: 361pt iOS, 380dp Android, 358px web-390. Print the platform key (ios / android / web-390 / web-1440) under each specimen in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\n\nR4. Units and type. pt, dp and px have equal values (16pt = 16dp = 16px), except targets (R11). Spacing uses only the 4px scale. Type uses only the house-style scale, plus bodyMedium 16/24/500 and bodySmallMedium 14/20/500, plus the R17 large-text sizes. Other dimensions appear only where a component prompt states them.\n\nR5. Callouts. An anatomy callout is a numbered SQUARE marker (16×16, radius xs 4, surface.sunken fill, 1px text.strong outline, numeral in label 13/18/600 text.strong), joined to its part by a 1px text.secondary leader line. The key sits beside the specimen in caption 12/16 text.strong as number · size · token, for example \"1 · 16pt tick glyph · text.secondary\". Markers are squares, never circles (circles mean provenance). Dimension rulers are 1px text.secondary with 4px end ticks and the number in caption text.secondary.\n\nR6. Grids. A \"variants-by-states\" artboard is a table: rows are variants, columns are states, in the order given. Headers are label 13/18/600 text.strong in sentence case (\"V1 · Removed row\", \"S1 · Pending undo\"). Each cell holds one specimen unless the prompt lists more. Draw every cell. A combination that doesn't apply is a surface.sunken cell with \"Not applicable: <reason in one clause>\" in caption text.strong, using the prompt's reason. Never a blank cell or a bare \"Not applicable\".\n\nR7. Keys and specimen names. Every grid row and column carries a key, printed under its label in caption 12/16 text.secondary as \"key: <key>\": lowercase, hyphenated, no spaces, no \"/\", and never a fixture string, name, amount or date. Use the keys each prompt lists, exactly. Under every specimen, inside grids and outside them, print its published name in caption 12/16 text.strong:\n  <Component> / <variant-key> / <state-key> / <platform> / <light|dark>\nFor example: \"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo / ios / light\". Specimens outside grids (anatomy insets, platform strips, sub-specimens) use the keys their component prompt gives. An anatomy specimen that repeats a grid cell carries that cell's name. Large-text frames use these platform keys: ios-ax5, ios-ax2, android-200, android-150. A specimen that a component prompt calls platform-neutral uses the platform key \"any\".\n\nR8. Tokens by name. Label every colour by token name; hex values appear only with the R10 figures. Semantic hues go on glyphs and borders, never text. text.muted is for disabled labels only. Readable secondary text is text.secondary on base, raised or app, and text.strong on sunken. Border tokens are decoration, never the only edge of a control, segment or card.\n\nR9. Dark mapping. Every dark artboard redraws its light twin with this mapping:\n  surface.base → dark base #0F172A · surface.raised → dark raised #1E293B · surface.app → dark app #020617 · surface.sunken → dark base (the same colour as dark base, so it separates nothing)\n  text.primary → dark text primary #E5E7EB · text.strong → dark text.strong #F1F5F9 · text.secondary → dark text.secondary #94A3B8 · text.muted → dark text.muted #64748B (disabled labels only) · text.inverse → dark text.inverse #111827\n  border.default → dark border #1F2937 (decoration only, never an edge) · border.strong → dark border.strong #374151 · border.focus → #38BDF8\n  primary.700 (text buttons, links, filled buttons, selected borders and checks) → dark link #38BDF8\n  primary.50 (selected fill) → primary.900 #0c4a6e, with dark text primary on it\n  semantic.error #DC2626 and semantic.warning #D97706 keep their hue, on glyphs and borders only.\n  A dark card's edge is the fill step (dark raised on dark app), never border.default, and it has no shadow. Dialogs and sheets are dark base. Print the container surface each prompt names in the dark frame's subject line.\n\nR10. Contrast table. The only contrast figures on the board. Prompts cite them as \"(R10)\"; print the figure beside the part and never compute a new one.\n  Light, on surface.base: text.secondary 4.83:1 · text.strong 10.31:1 · primary.700 5.93:1 · text.inverse on a primary.700 fill 5.93:1 · semantic.error 4.83:1 (glyphs and borders only) · semantic.warning 3.19:1 (glyphs only) · text.muted 2.54:1 (disabled labels only, never readable text) · border.default 1.24:1 and border.strong 1.47:1 (decoration only).\n  Light, other surfaces: text.strong on sunken 9.37:1 · text.secondary on sunken 4.39:1 (below 4.5:1, which is why text on sunken is text.strong) · primary.700 on sunken 5.39:1 · primary.700 border against a primary.50 fill 5.57:1.\n  Dark, on dark raised #1E293B: #94A3B8 5.71:1 · #38BDF8 6.83:1 · #F1F5F9 13.35:1 · #D97706 4.59:1 (glyphs only) · #DC2626 3.03:1 (glyphs only) · #64748B 3.07:1 (disabled only) · #1F2937 1.00:1 (never an edge).\n  Dark, on dark base #0F172A: #94A3B8 6.96:1 · #38BDF8 8.33:1 · #F1F5F9 16.30:1 · #DC2626 3.70:1 (glyphs and borders only) · #64748B 3.75:1 (disabled only) · #111827 on a #38BDF8 fill 8.28:1.\n  Dark selection: #E5E7EB on primary.900 #0c4a6e 7.64:1 · #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42:1 (checks and borders only, never text) · primary.900 against dark base 1.89:1 (a fill, never an edge; the #38BDF8 border is the edge).\n\nR11. Targets. Minimum hit areas: 44×44pt iOS, 48×48dp Android with 8dp gaps, 44×44px web. Draw each control's hit area as a dashed 1px text.secondary rectangle labelled with its size. A glyph is never a target on its own.\n\nR12. Focus and selection. Focus is a 2px border.focus ring (dark #38BDF8) with a 2px gap. Selection is always a primary.50 fill, a 1.5px primary.700 border, a 16pt primary.700 check and a 600-weight text.primary label (dark: primary.900 fill, 1.5px #38BDF8 border, #38BDF8 check, dark text primary label). They never look alike. A component prompt may define one further treatment, in full.\n\nR13. Glyphs and circles. Use only the Pantopus icon set, 16pt unless stated, 1.5px stroke. Filled vs hollow circles mean provenance only, so no glyph, tick, bullet, marker or control is a plain disc or ring. The one exception is an avatar circle (a MemberRow avatar, or its skeleton shape), which holds initials and is never a mark. A tick is a bare check stroke. No control uses a radio circle, on any platform or at any text size.\n\nR14. Strings and fixtures. Use the house-style FIXTURES exactly (TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific). Every string comes from the house style or the current component prompt; any string you add goes on Notes section D. Print character counts where given. No string ends in an ellipsis unless a prompt says so. Dates always show the weekday.\n\nR15. Components from other Foundations boards. FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, KindGlyph, AqiBand, ScaleStrip, PickupCard, MemberRow and the Pantopus app icon come from the published design system. If one isn't published yet, draw a surface.sunken box at the size below with its name in caption text.strong, and list it on Notes section C. Fallback sizes: FourteenDayStrip 361×40pt · YearBand 361×120pt with four 24pt lanes · AqiBand 361×48pt · ScaleStrip row 361×48pt · PickupCard 361×196pt · MemberRow 361×56pt · KindGlyph a 16pt or 42pt square, as stated · Pantopus app icon a 20pt square labelled \"Pantopus app icon\". Never draw a fallback box where the published component exists.\n\nR16. Disabled controls. A disabled control stays focusable and reads \"<label>, unavailable, <reason>\". Its label is text.muted (dark #64748B), and the reason is also written nearby in readable text (R8). No button is silently dead.\n\nR17. Standard artboards. Component prompts use four artboard types:\n  - \"01-anatomy\" (light): the default specimen with callouts (R5), sizes, tokens and R10 figures.\n  - \"variants-by-states\" (light and dark): the R6 grid.\n  - \"ax5-200-greyscale\" (light), with three required columns. (a) iOS at AX5: caption 12 → 40pt, label 13 → 44pt, bodySmall 14 → 46pt, body 16 → 53pt, h3 20 → 55pt. (b) Android at 200% font scale with Android 14 non-linear scaling: caption 12 → 24sp, label 13 → 25sp, bodySmall 14 → 26sp, body 16 → about 28sp, h3 20 → about 34sp. (c) Greyscale (100% desaturated) copies of the light default and of the most state-heavy light cell, each captioned \"Reads without colour: <the cue: a word, a glyph shape, a weight>\". Extra frames a prompt lists go in a labelled row below the columns. At these sizes, pairs stack, text wraps instead of truncating, sheets may scroll (sticky buttons reserve scroll padding), glyphs scale with text up to 2×, and hit areas grow.\n  - \"in-context-and-rules\" (light), five panels in order. IN CONTEXT: two or three crops (393pt iOS or 390px web-390 wide, about 300pt tall), each labelled with its surface id and captioned \"host illustrative, not a spec\", then \"Also consumed by: <ids>\"; draw undesigned hosts only as far as the crop needs. ACCESSIBILITY. COPY. PLATFORMS. INSTEAD OF: \"Instead of X, draw Y — because Z\", with a struck-through thumbnail of X labelled \"Not this\" (caption text.strong) beside a thumbnail of Y.\n\nR18. Motion. Motion has a purpose and lasts 300ms or less; idle loops stop within 5 s. Wherever something moves, draw its Reduce Motion form (cross-fade or static). Nothing is gesture-only or hover-only.\n\nR19. The Notes artboard. \"00d · Notes\" is shared by all eight components. Create it in QuietDayReceipt's last batch, extend it in each later component's last batch, and never drop entries. Body 16/24 text.primary on surface.base, overline headings. Six sections, grouped by component in board order:\n  A. Decisions and contract conflicts, numbered by component (1.1 … 8.n), for the founder to confirm or override: every item the prompt lists, plus anything you decided. Section A opens with a board item: \"0.1 Dark selection uses a primary.900 fill with a #38BDF8 border and check, so selection reads the same everywhere in the Pantopus design system. Confirm.\"\n  B. Assumptions.\n  C. Missing dependencies: every R15 fallback box you drew, and any named attachment that didn't arrive.\n  D. Invented strings (not in the house style or contract): each prompt's list plus any you added. Board chrome for all components: \"host illustrative, not a spec\" · \"Not this\" · every \"Not applicable: <reason>\" caption · \"key: <key>\" · \"Reads without colour: <cue>\" · \"web-1440 crop\" · \"Also consumed by:\" · the callout key texts · the \"Platforms\" and \"Reduce Motion\" row labels.\n  E. Omitted, with reason, including each component's light-only list.\n  F. Publish index: every specimen name for each component, light first, then dark.\n\nReply 'ready' and wait for the first component."
        },
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "00d-01",
            "component": "QuietDayReceipt",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · QuietDayReceipt · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00d · QuietDayReceipt · 02-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · QuietDayReceipt · 03-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · QuietDayReceipt · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · QuietDayReceipt · 05-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-01: QuietDayReceipt. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Makes silence readable: a finished \"nothing needs you\" state that lists the checks that were run.\nUsed in (print on 01): f1-today-tab, f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file, f7-today-widget, f4-briefing-optin-card, f4-notification-settings, f11-keeper-strip\nATTACH: none. This component hasn't shipped yet.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then create Notes)\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (create it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Today full = today-full · V2 Widget one-liner = widget-one-liner · V3 Briefing settings row = briefing-settings-row · V4 Strip empty = strip-empty · V5 Year band empty = year-band-empty.\nStates: S1 All ticked = all-ticked · S2 One pending = one-pending · S3 One failed = one-failed.\nExample: \"QuietDayReceipt / today-full / all-ticked / ios / light\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: the V1 S1 specimen on iOS 393 with callouts)\n1. Card: surface.base, radius lg 12, padding 16, shadow sm, full content width (361pt on iOS, 380dp on Android, 358px on web-390, 560px max in the web-1440 Today column).\n2. Heading: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, \"Nothing needs your attention today\". It appears only in the all-ticked state.\n3. Receipt line, 8pt below the heading: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Checked 6:00 PM\" (R10: 4.83:1).\n4. CheckItem row, 12pt below the receipt line: one row of four CheckItems with 16pt gaps, wrapping to a second row if the width runs out. The items are \"weather\", \"air\", \"alerts\" and \"your calendar\", in that order.\n5. CheckItem: a 16pt tick glyph (a bare check stroke, R13) in text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1), a 4pt gap, then the label in caption 12/16 text.secondary. An optional source time follows in the same style after \" · \", for example \"air · 6:00 PM\". Draw one CheckItem with a source time as a small inset beside the card, named \"QuietDayReceipt / checkitem-with-time / all-ticked / ios / light\".\n6. No illustration, no keeper, no colour fill and no semantic tint.\nCallout on the card: \"The whole receipt reads as one line: Checked 6:00 PM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\".\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 Today full: the card above (f1-today-tab).\nV2 Widget one-liner: a single caption line with no card, \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\", drawn inside a 338×158pt medium widget with text no smaller than 11pt (f7-today-widget).\nV3 Briefing settings row: a settings row under the Briefings group, in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary, \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\" (f4-notification-settings, f4-briefing-optin-card).\nV4 Strip empty: a FourteenDayStrip (R15) with 14 empty day cells in one ink colour, then the caption \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" (f5-today-calendar-strip).\nV5 Year band empty: a YearBand (R15) with 12 month columns and the four lanes You / City / County / State left empty, then the caption \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" (x-place-file).\nV4 and V5 are fixture-free specimens: no address, place label or scope appears on them. The provider named in their failed state is the City of Vancouver calendar.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 All ticked: the only state that shows the heading (V1) or the all-clear phrase (V2 to V5).\nS2 One pending: no heading. The \"air\" CheckItem shows a spinner-free pending mark instead of a tick: three 3pt dots in a row inside the 16pt glyph box, in text.secondary. Draw them as three small rounded squares, never as a single dot or a circle, so they can't be read as a filled provenance mark. The label reads \"air · not back yet\". The receipt line still reads \"Checked 6:00 PM\". Nothing animates.\nS3 One failed: no heading. The \"air\" CheckItem becomes a line: a 16pt error glyph (semantic.error on the glyph only, R10: 4.83:1), then \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, then a \"Retry\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44×44pt hit area. The other three items keep their ticks.\n\nFill every cell of the 5 × 3 grid like this:\n- V1: S1, S2 and S3 as described above.\n- V2 widget. S1: \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\". S2: \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\". S3: \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\", with no Retry inside the widget, because tapping the widget opens Today, where Retry lives.\n- V3 settings row. S1: \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\". S2: \"Not applicable: the row appears only after tonight's check has finished\". S3: \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\", with the error glyph before it and Retry as a 44pt text button.\n- V4 strip. S1: the empty strip plus its caption. S2: \"Not applicable: the strip shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\". S3: no strip is drawn; the slot shows the error glyph, then \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\" with Retry as a 44pt text button.\n- V5 year band. S1: the empty band plus its caption. S2: \"Not applicable: the year band shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\". S3: no band is drawn; the slot shows the error glyph, then \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\".\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: the 5 × 3 grid above, with iOS specimens.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9). Container: the V1 card and the V3 settings group are dark raised on dark app; the V2 widget is dark raised; the V4 strip and V5 band sit on dark raised. Ticks and pending dots are dark text.secondary (R10: 5.71:1), the error glyph is #DC2626 (R10: 3.03:1, glyph only), and Retry is #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1). Print these figures beside the parts.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 at S1, S2 and S3: the heading wraps to three lines. The CheckItems become a vertical list, one item per line (tick plus word). Retry drops under \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" onto its own line and stays at least 44pt tall. Names: \"QuietDayReceipt / today-full / <state-key> / ios-ax5 / light\".\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 at S1, S2 and S3: the same vertical list, with 48dp rows. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of S1, S2 and S3 of V1. Caption: \"Reads without colour: glyph shape (check / three dots / error glyph) and words ('not back yet', 'Couldn't reach')\".\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Widget at AX sizes\": the V2 widget at AX sizes, text only with no glyphs, in S1, S2 and S3. The line wraps to at most three lines inside the 338×158pt medium widget. Names: \"QuietDayReceipt / widget-one-liner / <state-key> / ios-ax5 / light\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The card is read as a list. S1: \"Nothing needs your attention today. Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" S2: \"Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, alerts, your calendar. Air: not back yet.\" S3: \"Couldn't reach AirNow.\" followed by the button \"Retry air quality\". The contract's spoken label is \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\"; the S1 label adds the heading and the time (Notes 1.3).\n- Non-colour encoding: every tick is paired with a word, and state is carried by glyph shape plus words.\n- Targets: Retry is 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. CheckItems are not targets.\n- The change from S2 to S1 is announced politely, once, without moving focus.\n\nCOPY. The heading appears only when every check succeeded. Never \"All caught up\", \"Inbox zero\" or \"You're all set\". Strings: \"Nothing needs your attention today\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM\" · \"weather\" · \"air\" · \"alerts\" · \"your calendar\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\" · \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\" · \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" · \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" · \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" · \"Retry\" · \"air · not back yet\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\" · \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\" · \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" · \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\".\n\nPLATFORMS. The same on iOS, Android and web. The only differences are target size (44pt / 48dp / 44px) and the text-only widget fallback at AX sizes.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17). All three crops show PLACE B, viewer Jordan Lee, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. Pickup there is on Thursday, so nothing is due tonight and the quiet state is true.\n- f1-today-tab: the Today tab for PLACE B with the scope string \"Saved place · Only you\", the air band (AqiBand, R15) and the V1 card under it.\n- f7-today-widget: the medium widget labelled \"Birchfield Ct\", with the V2 line.\n- f4-notification-settings: Jordan's Briefings group, showing the line \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" (the reminder before last Thursday's pickup) with the V3 row under it.\nAlso consumed by: f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file, f4-briefing-optin-card, f11-keeper-strip\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"All caught up\", \"Inbox zero\" or \"You're all set\", draw \"Nothing needs your attention today\" with the four checks — because the person needs to see what was checked, not a mood.\n- Instead of showing the heading while one provider is still loading, draw S2 with no heading — because an early all-clear teaches people to stop trusting the product.\n- Instead of a cheerful illustration or keeper pose, draw the plain card — because silence here is a fact, not a celebration.\n- Instead of ticks inside filled or hollow circles, draw bare check strokes — because filled vs hollow is reserved for provenance.\n- Instead of a generic \"Something went wrong\", draw \"Couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" — because a failed check names its provider.\n\nNOTES (create 00d · Notes per R19 and add these)\nA. 1.1 V4 caption: the contract says \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\", and research brief section 4 says \"…next 14 days\". This board uses the contract. Confirm.\n   1.2 Pending mark: the contract says one pending dot. This board draws three 3pt rounded squares so the mark can't be read as a filled provenance mark. Confirm.\n   1.3 Spoken label: the contract says \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" This board's S1 label adds the heading and the time (\"Nothing needs your attention today. Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\"). Confirm.\n   1.4 IN CONTEXT uses PLACE B (Jordan Lee, pickup on Thursday, \"Saved place · Only you\", widget label \"Birchfield Ct\"), because HOME A has pickup on Tue 20 Oct, so Monday evening at HOME A is not a quiet day.\nB. Jordan's last briefing was sent Wed 14 Oct at 6:00 PM, the night before his Thursday pickup.\nC. List AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip or YearBand here if you drew any of them as a fallback box.\nD. \"air · not back yet\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\" · \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\" · \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" · \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\" · \"Retry air quality\" (spoken) · the S1–S3 spoken labels · \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" · \"Birchfield Ct\" (widget label taken from the fixture street) · chrome: the \"Widget at AX sizes\" row label and the one-line receipt callout.\nE. Light only: every frame on 04 (the ios-ax5 and android-200 V1 frames and the ios-ax5 widget row) and the checkitem-with-time inset. Omitted: none.\nF. Light: 12 grid cells (every cell except the three Not applicable cells), the checkitem-with-time inset, and the 04 frames. Dark: the same 12 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and 00d · Notes exists with sections A–F and this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have 5 rows and 3 columns with V/S labels and keys. Every cell is drawn, and the three Not applicable cells carry their reasons.\n- The heading appears only in V1 S1. S2 and S3 never show the heading or an all-clear phrase.\n- The pending mark is three small squares; no tick sits in a circle anywhere.\n- Every S3 cell names its provider (AirNow, or the City of Vancouver calendar). Retry has a dashed 44pt hit area everywhere except the widget, which has no Retry.\n- Every specimen carries its R7 name. The dark grid prints its container and the R10 figures for the tick, error glyph and Retry.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) plus the widget row; no string ends in an ellipsis.\n- 05 has three labelled crops with PLACE B fixtures, the \"Also consumed by\" line, and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (create it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-02",
            "component": "WarmingSkeleton",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · WarmingSkeleton · 01-anatomy · light",
