            "promptText": "Component 00d-02: WarmingSkeleton. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Content-shaped placeholders that sit in their final slots during cold loads of 1–10 s, so nothing jumps when the data arrives.\nUsed in (print on 01): f1-today-tab, x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f1-your-places, f3-members-roster, f3-household-block, f3-member-home-dashboard, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map, f10-bill-trend, f11-keeper-strip, f7-widget-tap-landing\nATTACH (optional, reference only): docs/screenshots/hub-v2-skeleton-ios.png, hub-v2-skeleton-android.png and hub-v2-skeleton-web.png, which show the existing shimmer tone. Use them for tone only. Their layout is not a spec.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Section skeleton = section-skeleton · V2 Row skeleton = row-skeleton · V3 Instrument skeleton = instrument-skeleton · V4 Panel skeleton = panel-skeleton.\nV3 holds four sub-specimens, each with its own variant key: a = instrument-skeleton-strip · b = instrument-skeleton-year-band · c = instrument-skeleton-scale-strip · d = instrument-skeleton-bill-trend.\nStates: S1 Shimmer = shimmer · S2 Static = static · S3 Replaced progressively = replaced-progressively.\nExamples: \"WarmingSkeleton / section-skeleton / shimmer / ios / light\" · \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument-skeleton-bill-trend / static / ios / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 at S1 on iOS 393 with callouts, plus V3d beside it)\n1. Shapes are filled with surface.sunken on surface.base cards. They match the final geometry: strip cells, track shapes, row bars and avatar circles. For a count of facts, draw a number bar plus pill-shaped chip bars, because the count is an integer plus chips and has no ring, so there is no ring skeleton. Each shape uses the same radius as the part it stands in for. Shapes are filled, not outlined, because an outline-only skeleton reads as an empty state. (The avatar circle is the one circle R13 allows. It is a placeholder shape and carries no meaning.)\n2. The skeleton reserves the exact final height. Draw a height ruler beside the skeleton and a second ruler beside the loaded version, and caption both \"same height\".\n3. No text, no glyphs and no \"checking…\" anywhere inside a skeleton.\n4. Shimmer: a soft band 30% of the shape's width, surface.base at 60% opacity, sweeping left to right across the shapes. One pass takes 1.2 s. The shimmer stops after 4 passes (under 5 s, R18) and then holds static. Draw the band mid-sweep with a callout \"1.2 s per pass · stops after 4 passes\".\n5. Container: one accessibility element labelled \"Loading\" (callout).\n6. Dark: on a dark raised card, shapes are dark border.strong #374151. On dark base, shapes are dark raised #1E293B. (Dark surface.sunken equals dark base, so it would vanish.) Print on the board: \"Skeleton shapes are decorative and have no contrast requirement.\"\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 Section skeleton (f1-today-tab), iOS 393, three blocks in one column:\n  - Air band: a 48pt-tall row with a 12pt-tall filled track shape (radius pill) and a 96×12pt label bar.\n  - Pickup card: a card with a 42×42pt square (radius md) in the KindGlyph slot, two bars (200×20pt and 240×14pt, radius xs) and two 44pt-tall button shapes of equal width (radius md).\n  - Fourteen-day strip: 14 cells, each 22×40pt with radius xs and 4pt gaps.\nV2 Row skeleton (lists), iOS 393: three rows. Each row is as tall as the final row it stands in for; draw it at 56pt, the MemberRow height, and caption it \"height = the consuming row's final height\". Each row has 16pt padding, a 40pt avatar circle, and two bars (60% width × 14pt and 40% width × 12pt).\nV3 Instrument skeleton, iOS 393, four sub-specimens stacked in the cell, each labelled a–d:\n  a. 14-day strip: 14 cells, 361×40pt overall.\n  b. Year band: 361×120pt, 12 month columns × 4 lanes of 24pt, with lane-label bars.\n  c. Scale strip: 4 rows, each 48pt tall, with a 12pt filled track shape and a 72×14pt reading bar beside it.\n  d. Bill trend: a 160×14pt summary bar above 12 columns, each 16pt wide with 8pt gaps and radius xs, bottom-aligned, at heights of 40, 56, 48, 64, 52, 44, 60, 72, 56, 48, 64 and 52pt (varied, never equal).\nV4 Panel skeleton (f9-nearby-cells-map): a 361×240pt panel with radius lg in surface.sunken, a 6×4 grid of 1px border.default lines (decoration), and a 120×14pt caption bar below it.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Shimmer (the default): draw the band mid-sweep.\nS2 Static (Reduce Motion): the same shapes with no band. Loaded content replaces the skeleton with a 200 ms cross-fade.\nS3 Replaced progressively: each replacement is a 200 ms cross-fade in place, and the height ruler shows no change. Loaded content per variant:\n  - V1: the air band is loaded (AqiBand, R15: AQI 42 Good, AirNow, observed 7:00 AM). The pickup card and the strip are still skeletons.\n  - V2: row 1 is loaded as MemberRow (R15, owner variant) \"Maya Chen\" with the caption \"Owner\". Rows 2 and 3 are still skeletons.\n  - V3: sub-specimen a is loaded as FourteenDayStrip (R15) for HOME A, starting Mon 19 Oct 2026, with pickup marks on Tue 20 Oct and Tue 27 Oct and date marks on Fri 23 Oct (Clark Public Utilities), Mon 26 Oct (voter registration must arrive by), Wed 28 Oct (City of Vancouver water) and Sun 1 Nov (HOA dues). Sub-specimens b, c and d are still skeletons, and each keeps its own name.\n  - V4: \"Not applicable: the panel lands as one piece\".\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 4 rows × 3 columns, iOS. The V3 row has four sub-specimens per cell, each named.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9). Container: the V1–V3 cards are dark raised on dark app, so their shapes are dark border.strong; the V4 panel sits on dark base, so its shapes are dark raised. The shimmer band is dark raised at 60% opacity over border.strong shapes, and dark base at 60% over the V4 shapes. Loaded content uses its own dark tokens.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE / REDUCE MOTION (04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V2 at S1: bar heights follow the line heights of the text they stand in for at AX5, so V1 grows to its AX5 final height and the two pickup button shapes stack. V2 rows grow to their AX5 heights. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 and V2 at S1: the same, with 48dp minimum rows. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V3 S3. Caption: \"Reads without colour: yes — no text, and the shapes are content-shaped, so it still reads as a placeholder.\"\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Reduce Motion\": V1 and V3 drawn static, with the caption \"no shimmer; replacements cross-fade\". These frames repeat the S2 cells and are not published a second time.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Loading\", once, on the container. VoiceOver reads the container label. On Android the container's contentDescription is \"Loading\". On web the section has aria-busy=\"true\" plus a visually hidden \"Loading\". Individual shapes are hidden from assistive tech.\n- Non-colour encoding: none needed, because skeletons carry no data.\n- Targets: skeletons are not interactive. Controls can't be tapped until their content lands.\n- Under Reduce Motion there is no shimmer.\n\nCOPY. No text inside skeletons and no \"checking…\" claims. The only string is the spoken \"Loading\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- All platforms skip skeletons for loads under about 1 s. Draw a callout: \"under 1 s: show nothing new; keep the old content\".\n- Warm screens (the widget path, f7-widget-tap-landing) never show a skeleton. They refresh in place with no hairline.\n- Android uses the app's existing shimmer component with these shapes and the shimmer spec in anatomy item 4. iOS and web match it.\n- Components that fail closed never get a skeleton: the founding meter (f9-founding-meter-preview), the Earn row (f9-earn-removal) and LandingBannerSlot render nothing until their data is confirmed. Print this fail-closed list in the PLATFORMS panel.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f1-today-tab: a cold load showing V1 under the header \"Larkspur Loop\" with the scope string \"Your household\".\n- f3-members-roster: V2 with three rows.\n- f10-bill-trend: V3d inside the bill trend card.\nAlso consumed by: x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f1-your-places, f3-household-block, f3-member-home-dashboard, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map, f11-keeper-strip, f7-widget-tap-landing (as the warm path with no skeleton)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a full-page spinner, draw content-shaped skeletons in their final slots — because a spinner hides how long the wait is and the page jumps when data lands.\n- Instead of an empty card frame with nothing inside, draw the filled shapes of the final content — because a frame-only skeleton looks like an empty state.\n- Instead of skeleton text such as \"Checking air…\", draw text-free shapes — because a skeleton must not claim a check is under way.\n- Instead of a ring-shaped placeholder for a count of facts, draw a number bar and chip bars — because the count is an integer plus chips, never a ring.\n- Instead of a skeleton for the founding meter or the invite banner, draw nothing — because those fail closed and must never suggest something is coming.\n- Instead of a shimmer that loops forever, stop it after 4 passes — because idle loops stop within 5 s.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 2.1 Dark shapes: dark surface.sunken equals dark base, so shapes use dark raised on dark base, and dark border.strong on dark raised cards.\n   2.2 Shapes: the contract says \"track outlines\" and \"ring outline\". This board draws filled shapes (an outline-only skeleton reads as empty, per the contract's own \"no frame-only skeletons\") and drops the ring, because research brief section 4 replaced the count ring with an integer plus chips. Confirm.\n   2.3 Threshold: the contract says cold loads of 1–10 s, and research brief P11 says about 2–10 s. This board follows the contract (nothing under 1 s). Question: skeleton or nothing between 1 and 2 s?\nB. The V3a loaded strip includes HOA dues (Sun 1 Nov) and the voter registration deadline (Mon 26 Oct) as HOME A date marks. Comcast (Mon 2 Nov) and property tax (Mon 2 Nov) fall outside the 14 days.\nC. List AqiBand, MemberRow or FourteenDayStrip here if you drew any of them as a fallback box. List the three skeleton screenshots if they didn't arrive (they are optional).\nD. \"Loading\" (spoken) · \"Owner\" (MemberRow caption) · the skeleton bar sizes and the bill-trend column heights · chrome: \"same height\" · \"height = the consuming row's final height\" · \"1.2 s per pass · stops after 4 passes\" · \"under 1 s: show nothing new; keep the old content\" · \"no shimmer; replacements cross-fade\" · \"Skeleton shapes are decorative and have no contrast requirement.\"\nE. Light only: the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames on 04. The Reduce Motion row repeats S2 and isn't published again. Omitted: skeletons for fail-closed components (by rule).\nF. Light: V1, V2 and V4 at every applicable state, plus the four V3 sub-specimens at every state (V4 S3 is Not applicable), plus the 04 large-text frames. Dark: the same grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have 4 rows × 3 columns with keys. The V3 cells show sub-specimens a–d, each with its own name. V4 S3 carries its reason.\n- No skeleton contains text, a glyph or a ring. Every shape is filled, with the radius of its final part.\n- Every skeleton has a \"same height\" ruler pair, and S3 shows no height change.\n- S3 uses only the fixture content listed above; nothing else is invented.\n- The dark grid prints its container and uses border.strong shapes on raised and raised shapes on base.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) and the Reduce Motion row.\n- 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line, the five panels and the fail-closed list.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
          },
