            "promptText": "Component 00d-03: InlineUndo. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Reversible removals and declines, with no timers and no dialogs.\nUsed in (print on 01): x-date-sheet, f1-your-places, f3-household-block, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f6-home-basics-rows, x-place-file, f3-bills-list, f10-snap-capture-tray\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · InlineUndo · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · InlineUndo · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Removed row = removed-row · V2 Declined ask = declined-ask · V3 Triage decision = triage-decision · V4 Undo all = undo-all · V5 Bill + photo deleted = bill-and-photo-deleted · V6 Fan-out hold = fan-out-hold.\nStates: S1 Pending undo = pending-undo · S2 Undone = undone · S3 Committed = committed.\nSpecimens outside the grid: \"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo-with-echo / android / light\" (in-row line plus snackbar) and \"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo-with-echo / web-390 / light\" (in-row line plus toast).\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393 with callouts, plus one Android inset)\n1. The removed row collapses in place into a line on surface.base: its height animates to 56pt over 200 ms (Reduce Motion: no animation, the line simply replaces the row). The line reads 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\"' in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, then \" · \", then an \"Undo\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44×44pt hit area.\n2. The line stays until the person leaves the screen. There is no countdown, no progress bar and no auto-dismiss. Callout: \"stays until you leave this screen\".\n3. Optional echo, Android only. Draw it as a separate Android 412 inset beside the iOS anatomy, labelled \"android only\": a Material 3 snackbar with the same text and Undo, above the bottom tab bar. It stays for as long as a screen reader is running (indefinite duration). It is never the only record: the in-row line is always there too. iOS never draws an echo. The web toast appears only in the Platforms row on 04.\n4. Fan-out hold: a write that notifies the household (Mark paid) holds its household notification until the undo line closes. Draw it on a V6 line with a callout, and the caption line \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary under the undo line.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; the viewer is Maya Chen at HOME A, except V1, which is Maya's own list of places)\nV1 Removed row: 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\" · Undo' (f1-your-places).\nV2 Declined ask: \"Just you, then. · Undo\", in the household block slot (f3-household-block). This is the contract string (Notes 3.1).\nV3 Triage decision: \"Comcast · Recycled · Undo\", kept until the person taps \"Finish day\" (f10-mail-day-triage). Draw the \"Finish day\" button beneath it: outlined, surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border, bodyMedium text.primary label, 44pt tall, radius md 8.\nV4 Undo all: a line at the top of the triage list, \"6 pieces sorted · Undo all 6\" (f10-mail-day-triage). The action is \"Undo all 6\".\nV5 Bill + photo deleted: \"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\" (f10-bill-provenance, f3-bills-list).\nV6 Fan-out hold: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\", with the caption \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" (f3-bills-list). This variant comes from the contract's fan-out rule (Notes 3.2).\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Pending undo: the collapsed line with Undo.\nS2 Undone: the original row returns at full height with a primary.50 fill that fades to surface.base over 300 ms (Reduce Motion: shown static with no fade). It is announced as \"Restored\". Per variant: V1 the place row \"The Blairmont rental\" returns; V2 the household block ask returns; V3 the Comcast piece returns to its untriaged row; V4 all six rows return; V5 the bill row returns with its photo thumbnail slot; V6 the bill row returns unpaid and no household notification is sent (caption \"No notification sent\").\nS3 Committed: the person has left and come back. The row is gone, the list has closed the gap, and there is no trace or banner. Draw the neighbouring rows touching where the removed row was. For V3 and V4, the triage list after \"Finish day\" shows the remaining pieces only. For V6, the household notification has been sent: beside the cell, draw a small labelled thumbnail (title only, \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\", captioned \"sent to Sam\") for reference. The thumbnail is board chrome, not a PushCopy specimen.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 6 rows × 3 columns, iOS. Every cell applies.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9). Container: the rows sit in a dark raised card on dark app. Undo is #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1 on dark raised). The S2 flash is a primary.900 fill fading to dark raised. The \"Finish day\" border is #94A3B8 (R10: 5.71:1).\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V4 at S1: the message wraps, and the action (\"Undo\" or \"Undo all 6\") moves to its own line below, left-aligned and still at least 44pt tall. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 and V4 at S1: the same, with a 48dp action. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V6 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: Undo is a word with a heavier weight (500 vs 400); Restored is announced and written.\"\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Platforms\": V1 S1 on each platform. iOS: the in-row line only (\"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo / ios / light\", the grid cell repeated). Android: the in-row line plus the snackbar echo (\"… / pending-undo-with-echo / android / light\"). web-390: the in-row line plus the toast above the tab bar (\"… / pending-undo-with-echo / web-390 / light\").\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: when a line appears, role=status announces 'Removed The Blairmont rental. Undo, button.' Undo is focusable. Focus stays where it was; it doesn't jump to Undo. After Undo, the status reads \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\"\n- Non-colour encoding: Undo is a word with a weight change, not only a link colour.\n- Targets: Undo is 44×44pt on iOS, 48×48dp on Android and 44×44px on web. \"Finish day\" is 44pt tall.\n\nCOPY. The pattern is \"<what happened> · Undo\". Never \"(4s)\" countdowns and never \"Undo in 5…\". Strings: 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\"' · \"Undo\" · \"Just you, then.\" · \"Comcast · Recycled\" · \"Finish day\" · \"6 pieces sorted\" · \"Undo all 6\" · \"Bill and photo deleted\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid\" · \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" · \"Restored\" · \"No notification sent\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: the in-row line only. iOS has no native snackbar, so no echo is drawn.\n- Android: the in-row line, plus an optional Material 3 snackbar echo with indefinite duration and a 48dp action, drawn above the bottom tab bar with scroll padding reserved.\n- Web: the in-row line, plus an optional toast in a polite live region: bottom left on web-1440, above the tab bar on web-390. The toast doesn't auto-hide while focus is inside it.\n- The specimens are in the \"Platforms\" row on 04.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f1-your-places: Maya's list of places, with V1 in place of the removed row.\n- f10-mail-day-triage: V3 and V4 together, with \"Finish day\" at the bottom.\n- f3-household-block: V2 in the block's slot on Today for HOME A.\nAlso consumed by: x-date-sheet, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f6-home-basics-rows, x-place-file, f3-bills-list, f10-snap-capture-tray\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a \"Remove this place?\" dialog for a cheap delete, draw the in-row V1 line — because routine actions are reversible and dialogs teach people to click through.\n- Instead of \"Undo (4s)\" with a countdown, draw \"Undo\" with no timer — because undo stays until the person leaves the screen.\n- Instead of a toast as the only trace, draw the in-row line, with the toast only as an echo — because toasts vanish before some people can reach them.\n- Instead of sending \"marked paid\" to the household at once, hold it until the undo line closes — because a notification can't be taken back.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 3.1 V2 \"Just you, then.\": the glossary forbids \"just you\" as a stand-in for \"Only you\", and names \"Just me\" as the household decline. Kept as the contract string. Question: switch to \"Just me, then.\"?\n   3.2 V6 Fan-out hold is a sixth variant that the contract's variant list doesn't have (it lists five: removed row · declined ask · triage decision · 'Undo all 6' · bill + photo deleted). It comes from the contract's anatomy rule \"Household-notifying writes (Mark paid) hold their fan-out until undo closes\". Confirm it as a published variant.\nB. The Blairmont rental is one of Maya's saved places.\nC. None expected.\nD. \"Restored\" · \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\" (spoken) · \"6 pieces sorted\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid\" · \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" · \"No notification sent\" · \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" and \"sent to Sam\" (reference thumbnail) · chrome: \"stays until you leave this screen\" · \"android only\".\nE. Light only: the Android snackbar echo (01 and 04), the web-390 toast (04), and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Omitted: an iOS echo (no native snackbar).\nF. Light: all 18 grid cells, the two pending-undo-with-echo specimens, and the 04 large-text frames. Dark: all 18 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have 6 rows × 3 columns with keys, and every cell is drawn.\n- No specimen shows a countdown, timer, progress bar or dialog.\n- Every Undo (and \"Undo all 6\") shows its dashed 44pt hit area.\n- The iOS anatomy has no echo; the Android echo is a separate inset labelled \"android only\".\n- V6 shows the hold caption in S1, \"No notification sent\" in S2, and the sent-to-Sam thumbnail in S3.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) and the Platforms row with three named specimens.\n- 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line, and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
