            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-04: DestructiveConfirm. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The confirm for real losses. It names what goes and what stays.\nUsed in (print on 01): f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-mail-snap-privacy, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f3-members-roster\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (6, then extend Notes)\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 03-platforms · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 04-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 06-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 One photo = one-photo · V2 All photos = all-photos · V3 Keeper = keeper · V4 Leave home sheet = leave-home-sheet.\nStates: S1 Open = open · S2 Deleting = deleting · S3 Done = done.\nSpecimens outside the grid: \"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open-keep-focused / ios / light\" (the focus specimen on 01) · \"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open / android / light\" · \"… / one-photo / open / web-390 / light\" · \"… / one-photo / open / web-1440 / light\" · \"DestructiveConfirm / leave-home-sheet / open / android / light\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393, plus a web-1440 crop of the same dialog, with callouts)\n1. Container. V1, V2 and V3 are dialogs: surface.base, radius xl 16, padding 24, shadow lg, over the platform's standard scrim. Width is 320pt on iOS, 312dp on Android (a Material 3 basic dialog) and 400px on web. V4 is a sheet: surface.base, radius xl 16 on the top corners, large detent, with a visible \"Close\" text button in the top bar (44pt hit area).\n2. Title: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, a question that names the object (\"Delete this photo?\").\n3. Body: one sentence in body 16/24 text.primary, naming what survives.\n4. Buttons: two buttons of equal size, 44pt tall (48dp on Android), radius md 8, whose labels describe outcomes.\n   - Destructive button: surface.base fill, a 1.5px semantic.error border (R10: 4.83:1), a leading 16pt trash glyph in semantic.error, and the label in body 16/24 at weight 600 in text.primary. Red goes on the border and the glyph only, as the house style requires. Callouts: \"no red fill\" and \"no red text\".\n   - Keep button: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border (R10: 4.83:1), label in bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary, no glyph.\n   - Order: side by side, Keep leads and Delete trails. Stacked (iOS at every size, and every platform at AX5 and 200%), Delete is on top and Keep below.\n   - Gap between buttons: 8.\n5. Initial focus: screen readers start on the title. Keyboard focus lands on the Keep button, never on the destructive one. Draw the R12 focus ring on \"Keep it\" in a second iOS specimen beside the first, named \"… / open-keep-focused / ios / light\".\n6. Dark (for 04): dialogs and sheets are dark base, never dark raised. The destructive border and trash glyph stay semantic.error #DC2626 (R10: 3.70:1 on dark base, which passes for a non-text edge and a glyph). The label is dark text primary at weight 600. The Keep border is #94A3B8 (R10: 6.96:1). No red text and no red fill in either theme. The contract's red label is an alternative for the founder (Notes 4.1); it is not drawn.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; the viewer for V1–V3 is Maya Chen, for V4 Sam Ortega)\nV1 One photo. Title \"Delete this photo?\" Body \"The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed.\" Buttons \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\". (f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-bill-provenance)\nV2 All photos. Title \"Delete all 17 photos?\" Body \"The bills and their amounts stay; only the photos are removed.\" Buttons \"Delete 17 photos\" / \"Keep them\". (f10-mail-snap-privacy)\nV3 Keeper. Title \"Remove Ollie?\" Body \"Today goes back to no keeper. You can add one again any time.\" Buttons \"Remove Ollie\" / \"Keep Ollie\". (f11-keeper-naming)\nV4 Leave home sheet. Title \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" Two labelled lists with a label 13/18/600 text.primary heading each; every item is a 16pt glyph in text.secondary plus words in bodySmall text.primary:\n  \"What goes\" (glyph: a minus stroke): \"The household calendar and bills\" · \"Household activity notifications\" · \"Your access to this home's place file\".\n  \"What stays\" (glyph: a check stroke): \"Dates you added that are Only you\" · \"Your saved places\" · \"Bills you marked paid still show 'Sam (no longer here)'\".\n  Buttons \"Leave this home\" (destructive, with the trash glyph replaced by a leave glyph from the icon set, still in semantic.error) / \"Stay in this home\". (f3-members-roster)\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Open: as above.\nS2 Deleting: the title stays. The body is replaced by a progress line in body 16/24 text.primary with a 4pt linear bar under it (primary.700 on surface.sunken, R10: 5.39:1). V1 \"Deleting the photo…\" · V2 \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" with the bar at 5/17 · V3 \"Removing Ollie…\" · V4 \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\". These progress lines are the only strings on this component that end in an ellipsis. Both outcome buttons are hidden until the action finishes. During S2, Escape (web), Back (Android) and swipe-to-dismiss do nothing, and the live region keeps reading progress. On the V4 sheet, \"Close\" stays visible but disabled per R16: label in text.muted, still focusable, read as \"Close, unavailable, Close is available when this finishes.\" The progress line above it is the readable reason. Dialogs (V1–V3) have no Close, so nothing else is added to them.\nS3 Done: the dialog or sheet has closed. Draw the host screen's status line that replaces it, in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary with a 16pt check glyph in text.secondary: V1 \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · V2 \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · V3 \"Ollie removed.\" · V4 the Place tab with the line \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" There is no Undo on any of these, because the loss is real.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 4 rows × 3 columns, iOS. Every cell applies.\n04-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9) with the dark rule from anatomy item 6. Container: every dialog and sheet is dark base over the scrim; S3 status lines sit on a dark raised host card. The S2 bar is #38BDF8 on a dark raised track (dark sunken would vanish on the dark base dialog). The disabled Close is #64748B (R10: 3.75:1).\n\nPLATFORMS (03-platforms · light; light only). V1 S1 drawn four ways:\n- iOS 393: the custom in-app dialog with stacked buttons, Delete on top. It is not the system alert, so the outlined destructive treatment can show (the grid cell, repeated).\n- Android 412: a Material 3 basic dialog with the same title and body and outlined buttons side by side, right-aligned: \"Keep it\" then \"Delete photo\". Back cancels in S1.\n- web-390: a bottom-anchored dialog at full width minus 16px on each side, buttons side by side.\n- web-1440 crop: a 400px centred modal with buttons side by side, right-aligned. Escape cancels in S1. Focus is trapped inside the dialog and returns to the control that opened it on close.\nAlso V4 S1 on Android: a bottom sheet with a drag handle and a visible \"Close\". (V4 on iOS is the grid cell.)\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (05-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V4 at S1: both become scrollable sheets. Buttons stack full width and stay pinned at the bottom, with scroll padding reserved so the last body line is never hidden under them. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 at S1: the dialog content scrolls and the buttons stack, Delete on top. Name uses android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V4 S1. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the destructive button has its outcome label, its trash glyph and its heavier 1.5px border; the V4 lists differ by glyph shape and heading word.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Delete this photo?, dialog. The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed. Delete photo, button. Keep it, button.\" While deleting, a polite live region reads progress at most every 5 items: \"Deleting 5 of 17\", \"Deleting 10 of 17\", \"Deleting 15 of 17\", then \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\"\n- Each variant's title is unique. In S1, Escape (web), Back (Android) and the Close control (sheets) all cancel. In S2 they do nothing, as stated above.\n- Non-colour encoding: the destructive action is named by its label and marked by its glyph, never by red alone. The glyph is decorative for screen readers.\n- Targets: buttons are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8pt gaps. Close is 44pt.\n\nCOPY. Titles are questions that name the object, bodies name what survives, and buttons name outcomes. Never just \"Are you sure?\" or \"This can't be undone\". Strings: every title, body and button under VARIANTS · \"What goes\" · \"What stays\" and the six list items · the four progress lines under S2 · the four status lines under S3 · \"Close\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (06-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f10-mail-piece-photo: the photo viewer with V1 open over it.\n- f10-mail-snap-privacy: the \"Mail snaps\" card with V2 open.\n- f3-members-roster: Sam's member view with the V4 sheet.\nAlso consumed by: f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Are you sure?\" / \"OK\" / \"Cancel\", draw \"Delete this photo?\" / \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\" — because people decide faster when the buttons say what happens.\n- Instead of \"This can't be undone\", draw the sentence naming what stays — because people fear losing more than they will.\n- Instead of a filled red button, a red slab above the content, or red label text, draw the outlined button with a semantic.error border, the trash glyph and a text.primary label — because a red fill shouts, semantic hues go on glyphs and borders only, and red text drops below readable contrast in dark mode.\n- Instead of default focus on the destructive button, put keyboard focus on Keep — because Enter must never destroy something.\n- Instead of this dialog for a cheap removal, use InlineUndo — because dialogs are only for losses that can't be undone.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 4.1 Label treatment: the contract asks for a red label (\"text.error\", which is not a token), but the house style says semantic hues go on glyphs and borders only. This board follows the house style: a text.primary label at body 16/24 weight 600 (a weight step on an existing size, not a new type style), a 1.5px semantic.error border and a 16pt semantic.error glyph. The founder may instead choose the contract's red label in semantic.error (4.83:1 on base); that would need a dark error text token, because #DC2626 is 3.70:1 on dark base, below 4.5:1. Question for the founder.\n   4.2 Dark: there is no dark error token. Red appears only on the border and glyph, where #DC2626 at 3.70:1 on dark base passes for a non-text edge and glyph. No accent token is used. Dialogs and sheets stay on dark base, where the figure is higher than on dark raised (3.03:1).\n   4.3 S2: Escape, Back and swipe-to-dismiss are ignored while deleting, and the V4 Close stays visible, disabled and focusable. The contract only says \"Escape / Back cancels\". Confirm.\n   4.4 S2 progress is announced every 5 items, so the drawn example is \"Deleting 5 of 17…\".\n   4.5 V4 uses a leave glyph instead of the trash glyph, because nothing is deleted. Confirm.\nB. Sam Ortega is the member who leaves in V4. Ollie is HOME A's keeper. HOME A has 17 mail photos.\nC. None expected.\nD. \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" · \"What goes\" · \"What stays\" and all six list items · \"Leave this home\" · \"Stay in this home\" · \"Remove Ollie\" · \"Keep Ollie\" · \"Deleting the photo…\" · \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" · \"Removing Ollie…\" · \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\" · \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · \"Ollie removed.\" · \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Close\" · \"Close is available when this finishes.\" (spoken) · \"Deleting 10 of 17\" and \"Deleting 15 of 17\" (spoken) · chrome: \"no red fill\" · \"no red text\".\nE. Light only: 03-platforms (Android, web-390 and web-1440 dialogs, and the Android Leave home sheet), the open-keep-focused specimen, and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. A later dark surface takes their colours from 04 and anatomy item 6. Omitted: the red-label alternative (Notes 4.1).\nF. Light: all 12 grid cells, the open-keep-focused specimen, the four 03 platform specimens that aren't grid repeats, and the 05 large-text frames. Dark: all 12 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 6 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have 4 rows × 3 columns with keys, and every cell is drawn.\n- No specimen has a red fill or red text. Red appears only on the destructive border and its glyph.\n- Keyboard focus is drawn on Keep. Keep leads when side by side; Delete is on top when stacked.\n- S2 shows \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" on V2, hides both buttons, and draws the V4 Close as disabled with its reason.\n- S3 shows the host status line with no Undo.\n- 03 shows V1 on four platforms and V4 on Android, each named.\n- 05 has columns (a), (b) and (c); 06 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n- Every button and Close shows its dashed hit area.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-platforms. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-variants-by-states dark, 05-ax5-200-greyscale, 06-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-05",
            "component": "LandingBannerSlot",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-05: LandingBannerSlot. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The single arrival slot at the top of Place and /start. It shows exactly one banner at a time.\nUsed in (print on 01): f3-invite-banner, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-founding-meter-preview, x-place-file, f1-claim-receipt\nATTACH: a screenshot of the shipped mailbox-arrival pill at the top of the Place tab (iOS, Android and web-390). LandingBannerSlot copies its geometry exactly. If the screenshot is missing, use the fallback geometry in anatomy item 1, and write \"mailbox-arrival pill screenshot missing; fallback geometry used\" on Notes section C.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 One invite = one-invite · V2 Count = count · V3 Expiring = expiring · V4 Sender reissue = sender-reissue · V5 Expired compare link = expired-compare-link · V6 Sync merge = sync-merge · V7 Claim receipt = claim-receipt.\nSecondary specimens drawn inside rows: V1 degraded = one-invite-degraded · V3 seven days out = expiring-early.\nStates: S1 Hidden = hidden · S2 Shown = shown · S3 Offline = offline.\nExamples: \"LandingBannerSlot / expiring / shown / ios / light\" · \"LandingBannerSlot / expiring-early / offline / ios / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy-and-precedence: V1 S2 on iOS 393 with callouts, then the ladder and the failure frames)\n1. Geometry: copy the attached mailbox-arrival pill exactly (height, radius, padding, fill, edge). Fallback if the screenshot isn't attached: minimum height 44pt, radius pill, horizontal padding 16, vertical padding 12, surface.base on surface.app, shadow sm, and a 1px border.default as decoration.\n2. Leading 16pt glyph in text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1). Glyph per variant: an envelope for V1, V1 degraded, V2, V4 and the V3 seven-days-out specimen · a warning glyph in semantic.warning for V3 \"Expires tomorrow\" (R10: 3.19:1, glyph only) · a link glyph for V5 · a sync glyph for V6 · a home glyph for V7. The glyph is not a target.\n3. A one-line sentence in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, with the actor's name first.\n4. One trailing action: a text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44×44pt hit area.\n5. Placement: 16pt below the navigation title and 16pt above the first section, at full content width (361pt on iOS, 380dp on Android, 358px on web-390, 640px max in the web-1440 Place column).\n6. Two-line content (the expiring variant, a wrapping sentence, or any wrap at large text) changes the shape from pill to radius 2xl 20, so the corners never clip text. Callout: \"two lines → radius 2xl\".\n7. Precedence ladder. Draw a vertical list of eight labelled steps joined by \"wins over\" connectors: invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify. Beside it, draw a scenario: an invite and a compare arrival are both pending, and only the invite banner shows. Caption: \"Never two banners.\" (The places of claim receipt and sync merge are this board's proposal; Notes 5.3.)\n8. Fetch failure: the slot renders nothing and the layout doesn't move. Draw two stacked frames of the Place top (banner shown, then fetch failed) with identical section positions below the slot height, captioned \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\". No error banner.\nThe ladder, scenario and failure frames are documentation, not published specimens.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 One invite (viewer: Priya): \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\". In the same S2 and S3 cells, draw the degraded form as a small secondary specimen: \"Someone invited you to a home in Vancouver · Review\" (used when the name or address can't be shown).\nV2 Count: \"You have 3 invitations · Review\". Callout: \"→ Invitations list\".\nV3 Expiring (viewer: Priya, drawn as if viewed on Sun 25 Oct 2026, the day before the Mon 26 Oct expiry): line 1 \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\". Line 2 is \"Expires tomorrow\" in caption 12/16 text.primary. Leading glyph: the warning glyph. In the same S2 and S3 cells, draw the seven-days-out secondary specimen as viewed on TODAY (Mon 19 Oct): line 2 reads \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", with the envelope glyph and no warning glyph. Both use the radius 2xl shape.\nV4 Sender reissue (viewer: Maya): \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\".\nV5 Expired compare link: \"That comparison link has expired. Type an address to see your own place.\" with the trailing action \"Close\". The sentence wraps to two lines, so this uses the radius 2xl shape.\nV6 Sync merge: \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\".\nV7 One-time claim receipt (viewer: Maya): \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\". Callout: \"→ the persistent receipt in the place file, 'What moved when you claimed'\".\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Hidden: an empty 0pt slot, shown with a dashed annotation outline and the caption \"hidden = 0pt\" (board chrome only). The same drawing is used for every row, including the secondary specimens, which have no separate hidden cell.\nS2 Shown: as above.\nS3 Offline: the action is disabled per R16. Its label is text.muted, it stays focusable, and it reads its reason aloud. A caption line under the banner, in caption 12/16 text.secondary, is the readable reason:\n  - V1, V1 degraded, V2, V3, V3 seven-days-out and V6: caption \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" Spoken: \"Review, unavailable, You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\"\n  - V4: caption \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" Spoken: \"Fix, unavailable, You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\"\n  - V5 and V7 keep their action live, because Close and the local receipt both work offline. Their S3 cells show the S2 banner with the chrome caption \"action works offline\".\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 7 rows × 3 columns on iOS, with the secondary specimens in the V1 and V3 rows. Every cell applies.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid, secondary specimens included, in dark tokens (R9). Container: the banner is dark raised on dark app, with no shadow and no border edge. Actions are #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1), glyphs #94A3B8 (R10: 5.71:1), the warning glyph #D97706 (R10: 4.59:1, glyph only), and disabled actions #64748B (R10: 3.07:1). The offline caption sits on dark app in #94A3B8.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V3 at S2 and V4 at S3: the radius 2xl shape. The sentence wraps across as many lines as it needs, and the action moves below it, left-aligned, at least 44pt tall. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, the same three: a 48dp action. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S2 and V3 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: V3 still reads as expiring from the words 'Expires tomorrow' and the warning glyph shape.\"\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Platforms\": V1 S2 on Android and on a web-1440 crop, named \"LandingBannerSlot / one-invite / shown / android / light\" and \"LandingBannerSlot / one-invite / shown / web-1440 / light\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: role=status once, when the banner appears: \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop. Review, button.\" Expiry is spoken in words: \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\" The seven-days-out form: \"Expires in 7 days, Monday 26 October.\"\n- Non-colour encoding: expiry is carried by words plus the warning glyph, never by a tinted pill.\n- Targets: the action is 44pt / 48dp / 44px. The glyph is not a target.\n- The slot never takes focus when it appears.\n\nCOPY. Actor name first. Degrade to \"Someone invited you…\" or \"…a home in <city>\" (for HOME A the city is Vancouver). Expiry in words. Offline captions start with \"You're offline.\" and then say what happens next. Strings: every banner sentence and action under VARIANTS · \"Expires tomorrow\" · \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · the two offline captions.\n\nPLATFORMS. The same geometry on iOS, Android and web. On web, /start (anonymous) can show only V5 and compare arrivals; Place shows all of them.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f3-invite-banner: the Place tab for Priya with V1 at the top (iOS, 393pt crop).\n- f8-compare-arrival-header: /start on web-390 (390px crop) with V5 above the address field.\n- f1-claim-receipt: the Place tab for Maya with V7 at the top.\nAlso consumed by: x-place-file, f9-founding-meter-preview (shares the slot and fails closed the same way)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of stacking an invite banner over a compare banner, draw only the winner of the precedence ladder — because two banners split attention and push content down.\n- Instead of a red \"Couldn't load invitations\" banner on a fetch failure, render nothing — because a failed optional fetch must not look like an alert.\n- Instead of an amber-tinted pill for expiry, draw \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.primary with the warning hue only on the glyph — because tinted text fails contrast and colour alone doesn't carry meaning.\n- Instead of \"You've been invited!\", draw \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" — because the actor comes first.\n- Instead of a dead action while offline, keep it focusable with its reason read out and written — because silent dead buttons leave people guessing.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 5.1 V1: the contract example \"Sam Ortega invited you to the Payne St house\" uses a street that isn't in the fixtures and the word \"house\", which the glossary forbids. This board uses \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\", and the degraded form \"…a home in Vancouver\" (the contract's example city is Camas).\n   5.2 V6: \"Synced 3 items from your other device\" uses \"synced\", which the glossary lists as a forbidden freshness word. It is kept as the contract string, and its \"· Review\" action is this board's addition. Question for the founder.\n   5.3 Precedence: the contract ladder (invite > reissue > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > setup > verify) leaves out sync merge (V6) and the claim receipt (V7). This board proposes invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify. Confirm the order.\n   5.4 Glyphs: the contract names no glyphs. This board uses the envelope for every invitation banner except \"Expires tomorrow\" (warning glyph), a link glyph for V5, a sync glyph for V6 and a home glyph for V7. Confirm.\n   5.5 Offline: V5 (Close) and V7 (a local receipt) keep their actions live, because both work offline.\nB. Priya is the invitee viewing V1–V3 (priya@example.com, invite expires Mon 26 Oct). V3 \"Expires tomorrow\" is drawn as if viewed on Sun 25 Oct; everything else is viewed on TODAY.\nC. The mailbox-arrival pill screenshot, if it didn't arrive.\nD. \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\" and \"Expires in 7 days, Monday 26 October.\" (spoken) · \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" · \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" · the \"· Review\" action on V6 · \"Close\" on V5 · \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\" · \"What moved when you claimed\" · chrome: \"Never two banners.\" · \"wins over\" · \"hidden = 0pt\" · \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\" · \"two lines → radius 2xl\" · \"→ Invitations list\" · \"action works offline\".\nE. Light only: the Platforms row (Android and web-1440) and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Not published: the precedence ladder, scenario and fetch-failure frames (documentation). Omitted: the compare-arrival, mailbox-arrival, setup and verify banners, which appear in the ladder only because their strings belong to their own surface prompts.\nF. Light: 7 × 3 grid cells, plus one-invite-degraded and expiring-early at shown and offline, plus the Platforms row and the large-text frames. Dark: the same grid cells and secondary specimens.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have 7 rows × 3 columns with keys, including the degraded and seven-days-out specimens in S2 and S3.\n- 01 shows the eight-step ladder with claim receipt and sync merge, the one-banner scenario, and the zero-shift failure frames.\n- Every banner has exactly one action with a dashed 44pt hit area, and its actor name comes first.\n- The only warning glyph is on V3 \"Expires tomorrow\". No pill is tinted.\n- Every S3 cell either shows a disabled, focusable action with its written reason, or the \"action works offline\" caption.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) and the Platforms row; 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy-and-precedence, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
