              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-06: NotificationAsk. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The in-context notification permission ask and its denial states. It is never a second \"Yes\".\nUsed in (print on 01): f4-notification-primer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f4-today-pickup-card, f4-notification-settings, f3-household-notifications\nATTACH: none. The OS permission dialog is never drawn.\n\nARTBOARDS (7, then extend Notes)\n00d · NotificationAsk · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 02-card-row-states · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 04-card-row-states · dark\n00d · NotificationAsk · 05-primer-and-denial-by-platform · dark\n00d · NotificationAsk · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 07-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nGrid variants (02 and 04): V1 Card row = card-row · V7 Time chips = time-chips.\nGrid states: S1 Never asked = never-asked · S2 Granted = granted · S3 Declined = declined · S4 OS blocked = os-blocked · S5 Save status = save-status. The S5 cell holds three specimens with the state keys saving, saved and save-failed.\nSheet variants (03 and 05): V2 Primer iOS = primer-ios · V3 Primer Android = primer-android · primer-ios-household · primer-android-household · V4 iOS denied = ios-denied · V5 Android denied once = android-denied-once · V6 Android blocked = android-blocked.\nSheet states: never-asked (the four primers) · denied (V4) · denied-once (V5) · blocked (V6).\nThe seven sheet names are exactly:\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-ios / never-asked / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-android / never-asked / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-ios-household / never-asked / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-android-household / never-asked / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / ios-denied / denied / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / android-denied-once / denied-once / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / android-blocked / blocked / android / <theme>\"\nwhere <theme> is light on 03 and dark on 05.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: the card row and the pickup primer on iOS 393, with callouts)\nA. Card row form (lives on f4-briefing-optin-card):\n  1. Question in body 16/24 text.primary: \"The night before pickup?\"\n  2. Two buttons of equal weight, side by side: \"Yes\" and \"Not now\". Both are outlined: 1px text.secondary border (R10: 4.83:1), surface.base fill, bodyMedium text.primary label, radius md 8, 44pt tall, equal widths, 8pt gap. Callout: \"Yes fires the OS prompt directly. The OS prompt is not drawn.\"\n  3. Granted collapse: the row becomes \"6:00 PM · Change\", where \"Change\" is a primary.700 text button (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44pt hit area.\n  4. Time chips, shown after Change: four chips, \"5:00 PM\", \"6:00 PM\", \"7:00 PM\" and \"8:00 PM\", each 44pt tall with radius pill and 8pt gaps. Unselected: surface.base, 1px text.secondary border, text.primary label. Selected: the R12 selection treatment (fill + check + 600 weight). Wrap to a second line if the width runs out.\n  5. Status slot at the trailing edge of the row, in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"Saving…\" / \"Saved\" / \"Couldn't save · Retry\" (Retry is a primary.700 text button with a 44pt hit area).\n  Callout on the card row: \"Appears only after an action that shows the purpose\".\nB. Primer sheet form, used only for the two indirect entries the contract names: the first confirmed pickup, and household activity from Mail. Draw the anatomy with the pickup entry. The household entry differs only in items 2, 3 and 4.\n  1. iOS sheet at medium detent, surface.base, radius xl 16 on the top corners, with a visible \"Close\" text button at top right (44pt hit area).\n  2. Unique title in h3 20/28/600 text.primary. Pickup entry: \"Pickup reminders on this phone\". Household entry: \"Household updates on this phone\".\n  3. The PushCopy tray preview (PushCopy comes later on this board; draw it exactly as described here), with the caption \"This is the whole thing.\" under it. It is an in-app illustration: a surface.raised inset card (radius lg 12, padding 12) on a surface.sunken panel (radius lg, padding 16), holding the Pantopus app icon at 20pt (R15), \"Pantopus\" and \"now\" in caption text.strong, the title in bodySmallMedium text.primary and the body in bodySmall text.primary. The caption is caption text.strong on the panel. It never looks like a system alert. Pickup entry: title \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\", body \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\". Household entry: title \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\", body \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\".\n  4. Body in body 16/24 text.primary. Pickup entry: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Nothing else unless you turn it on.\" Household entry: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\"\n  5. Silence contract in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\"\n  6. iOS only: one forward button, \"Continue\": primary.700 fill, text.inverse label (R10: 5.93:1), full width, 44pt tall, radius md.\n  7. Caption under it in caption text.secondary: \"Your phone will ask next.\"\n  8. Android only (shown on 03): a Material 3 bottom sheet with a drag handle and a visible \"Close\". Two buttons, \"Continue\" and \"Not now\", both outlined: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border, bodyMedium text.primary label, 48dp tall, equal widths, 8dp gap, radius md. Neither is filled, so neither dominates. The filled button is iOS-only.\n\nGRID (02-card-row-states · light, iOS): rows V1 and V7 × columns S1–S5. Not every variant has every state; fill the cells exactly like this:\n- V1 Card row. S1: the row as drawn in A1–A2. S2: the collapsed row \"6:00 PM · Change\". S3 Declined: the card slot collapses (200 ms; static under Reduce Motion) and is replaced, once, by a row \"Put Today on your home screen\" with an \"Add the widget\" text button (primary.700, 44pt). That row never appears again after this visit. S4: \"Not applicable: shown in settings, not on the card\". S5: \"Not applicable: the card row saves only through the chips\".\n- V7 Time chips. S1: \"Not applicable: chips appear only after granted\". S2: the four chips with 6:00 PM selected. S3: \"Not applicable: chips are hidden after a decline\". S4 OS blocked, drawn as the f4-notification-settings Briefings group row: the Briefings switch shows on; beneath it, a 16pt warning glyph (semantic.warning, glyph only, R10: 3.19:1), then \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" in bodySmall text.primary, then an \"Open Settings\" text button (primary.700, 44pt). S5: three small specimens of the chip row with the status slot reading \"Saving…\", \"Saved\", and \"Couldn't save · Retry\". In \"Couldn't save\", the chip the person picked (7:00 PM) stays selected.\n\nSHEETS (03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light): seven full sheets at their platform widths, each with its exact name (see KEYS) and, under it, a caption naming its entry:\n- primer-ios: anatomy B, pickup entry. Caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\".\n- primer-android: B with item 8 in place of 6, pickup entry. Caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\".\n- primer-ios-household: B, household entry. Caption \"after household activity from Mail\".\n- primer-android-household: B with item 8, household entry. Caption \"after household activity from Mail\".\n- ios-denied (V4): the pickup primer with the same title and tray, but items 4, 5 and 7 are replaced by \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" in body text.primary, an \"Open Settings\" button in the iOS filled style from B6, and the caption \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" Close stays. Caption \"after the iOS prompt was declined\".\n- android-denied-once (V5): the pickup Android primer again, with outlined \"Continue\" (which asks again) and \"Not now\", and the caption \"Your phone will ask next.\" Caption \"after the Android prompt was declined once\".\n- android-blocked (V6): the pickup Android sheet with the same title and tray, but items 4 and 5 are replaced by \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\", with \"Open Settings\" and \"Not now\" as equal outlined buttons (B8). Close stays. Caption \"after the Android prompt was declined twice\".\n\nDARK (04 and 05, in dark tokens per R9)\n04-card-row-states · dark: the full 02 grid (both rows, all five columns, the same Not applicable cells). Container: the briefing card and the settings group are dark raised on dark app. Outlined buttons and chips have a #94A3B8 border (R10: 5.71:1). The selected chip uses the R12 dark selection. Change, Add the widget, Retry and Open Settings are #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1). The S4 warning glyph is #D97706 (R10: 4.59:1, glyph only).\n05-primer-and-denial-by-platform · dark: all seven 03 sheets. Container: sheets are dark base. The tray inset is dark raised on a dark base panel. On iOS sheets, Continue and Open Settings are a #38BDF8 fill with a dark text.inverse label (R10: 8.28:1). On Android sheets, every button is outlined: dark base fill, 1px #94A3B8 border (R10: 6.96:1), dark text primary label.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (06-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: V1 S1, where \"Yes\" and \"Not now\" stack full width in that order, both at least 44pt tall; V7 S2, where the chips wrap one per line; and primer-ios, where the sheet scrolls and Continue stays pinned with scroll padding. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android: V1 S1, V7 S2 and primer-android, with 48dp buttons and chips and 8dp gaps. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V7 S2 and V7 S4. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the selected chip has its check glyph and weight; S4 reads as a problem from its words and glyph shape.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken, card row: \"The night before pickup? Yes, button. Not now, button.\" Chips: \"6:00 PM, selected, 2 of 4.\" Status is announced in a polite live region (\"Saved\") without moving focus. Each primer's title is unique (\"Pickup reminders on this phone\", \"Household updates on this phone\") and is read first when the sheet opens. Sheets trap focus, and Close, Back and Escape dismiss them.\n- Non-colour encoding: a selected chip has fill + check + weight. The blocked state has a glyph + words.\n- Targets: buttons and chips are 44pt on iOS, 48dp with 8dp gaps on Android, and 44px on web.\n\nCOPY. The body lists the real defaults (B4). Silence contract: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\" Other strings: \"The night before pickup?\" · \"Yes\" · \"Not now\" · \"6:00 PM · Change\" · \"5:00 PM\" · \"6:00 PM\" · \"7:00 PM\" · \"8:00 PM\" · \"Pickup reminders on this phone\" · \"Household updates on this phone\" · the two body sentences · \"Continue\" · \"Your phone will ask next.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" · \"Open Settings\" · \"Put Today on your home screen\" · \"Add the widget\" · \"Saving…\" · \"Saved\" · \"Couldn't save · Retry\" · \"Close\" · \"This is the whole thing.\" · the two tray title/body pairs. \"Saving…\" is the only string on this component that ends in an ellipsis.\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: the primer has a filled Continue only (plus Close). When denied, \"Open Settings\" opens the app's Notifications page.\n- Android: the primer has outlined Continue + Not now. Denied once → Continue asks again. Blocked → outlined \"Open Settings\" + \"Not now\".\n- Web: not drawn on this board (no web push is in scope; Notes 6.7).\n- All platforms: never at cold launch, sign-up or save.\n\nIN CONTEXT (07-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f4-briefing-optin-card: the briefing card on Today for HOME A, with V1 at S1.\n- f4-notification-primer: primer-ios over f4-today-pickup-card (PickupCard, R15), just after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\".\n- f4-notification-settings: the Briefings group at S4.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card, f3-household-notifications (the household-entry primer, drawn on 03)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a primer button labelled \"Yes\" or \"Allow\", draw \"Continue\" with \"Your phone will ask next.\" — because the decision already happened on the card, and a second Yes is a trick.\n- Instead of imitating the iOS or Android system dialog, draw the in-app sheet with the tray illustration — because a fake system dialog is deceptive and App Review rejects it.\n- Instead of a permanent amber banner for someone who tapped Not now, close the slot and offer the widget row once — because \"Not now\" never asks again on its own.\n- Instead of a filled \"Yes\" beside a grey \"Not now\", draw two equal outlined buttons — because declines are equal weight.\n- Instead of a filled Continue beside an outlined Not now on Android, draw both outlined — because Android keeps Not now as an equal choice.\n- Instead of the ask at launch or sign-up, draw it only after the first confirmed pickup, household activity from Mail, or a card tap — because people grant a request whose purpose they can see.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 6.1 \"Open Settings\" vs \"Open settings\": the contract uses both (its variants say \"Open Settings\", its S4 state says \"Open settings\"). This board uses \"Open Settings\" everywhere. It is title case, which conflicts with the house-style sentence-case rule (see 7.4). Question for the founder.\n   6.2 V1: the glossary says \"Not now\" is always paired with a lasting decline, but the contract's card row has only \"Yes / Not now\". This board draws the contract. Question: add \"No thanks\"?\n   6.3 Entry points: the contract uses the primer for indirect entries (the first confirmed pickup, household activity from Mail), and this board draws the pickup primer after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\". Research brief section 2 item 8 instead has the push ask follow the first \"That's my day\" inline (\"Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM\") and go straight to the OS dialog. This board follows the contract. Question: primer sheet, or an inline row after the first pickup confirm?\n   6.4 Household primer: the title \"Household updates on this phone\" and the body \"…Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" are invented. \"Arrive quietly\" is this board's plain wording for iOS Passive / Android LOW. Confirm the wording, and whether this entry should switch household activity on after the grant.\n   6.5 S3 widget row: \"Put Today on your home screen\" capitalises Today to match the tab name. The glossary names the widget \"Today at your address\". Question: should the row read \"Add Today at your address to your home screen\"?\n   6.6 Denial sheets (V4, V6) keep the pickup title and tray and replace only the body. The contract doesn't say. Confirm.\n   6.7 Web: no web push in scope, so no web NotificationAsk is drawn. Question for the founder.\nB. The primers are for HOME A (Maya), so the tray shows \"Larkspur Loop\". \"Couldn't save\" is drawn after Maya picked 7:00 PM.\nC. The Pantopus app icon or PickupCard, if drawn as a fallback box.\nD. \"Pickup reminders on this phone\" · \"Household updates on this phone\" · \"Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" · \"Put Today on your home screen\" · \"Add the widget\" · \"Saving…\" · \"Saved\" · \"Couldn't save · Retry\" · \"Close\" · \"now\" · \"6:00 PM, selected, 2 of 4.\" (spoken) · chrome: \"Yes fires the OS prompt directly. The OS prompt is not drawn.\" · \"Appears only after an action that shows the purpose\" · the seven entry captions (\"after the first confirmed pickup\", \"after household activity from Mail\", \"after the iOS prompt was declined\", \"after the Android prompt was declined once\", \"after the Android prompt was declined twice\").\nE. Light only: the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Omitted: NotificationAsk on web (Notes 6.7), and the OS permission dialog (never drawn).\nF. Light: the 5 applicable grid cells (V1 S1–S3; V7 S2 and S4) plus the three S5 status specimens, the seven sheets, and the 06 large-text frames. Dark: the same grid specimens and the seven sheets.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 7 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- The light and dark grids have rows V1 and V7 × columns S1–S5 with keys, and the five Not applicable cells carry their reasons.\n- 03 and 05 each show all seven sheets with their exact names and entry captions, including both household primers with their own title, tray and body.\n- No primer button says \"Yes\" or \"Allow\". On Android no button is filled. On iOS only Continue / Open Settings is filled.\n- Yes and Not now are equal outlined buttons; the selected chip has fill, check and weight.\n- No system dialog is drawn or imitated.\n- Every button, chip and text button shows its dashed hit area.\n- 06 has columns (a), (b) and (c); 07 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-card-row-states light, 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform light, 04-card-row-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 05-primer-and-denial-by-platform dark, 06-ax5-200-greyscale, 07-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-07",
            "component": "PushCopy",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · PushCopy · 05-android-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · PushCopy · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 07-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-07: PushCopy. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The canonical push strings and tray-preview artwork, so every surface draws the same notification.\nUsed in (print on 01): f4-notification-primer, f4-today-pickup-card, f1-today-air-band, f3-household-notifications, f4-notification-settings\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (7, then extend Notes)\n00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light\n00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light\n00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light\n00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · PushCopy · 05-android-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · PushCopy · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · PushCopy · 07-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Unconfirmed pickup = unconfirmed-pickup · V2 Confirmed pickup = confirmed-pickup · V3 Air, Time Sensitive = air-time-sensitive · V4 Air, below 151 = air-below-threshold · V5 Bill marked paid = bill-marked-paid · V6 Household roll-up = household-roll-up · V7 Date reminder = date-reminder · V8 Hidden-preview placeholders = hidden-preview.\nStates: S1 Collapsed = collapsed · S2 Expanded = expanded · S3 Lock screen public = lock-screen-public.\nV8 cells hold four specimens each, one per placeholder group, with these state keys: collapsed-pickup, collapsed-air, collapsed-household, collapsed-date (S1) and lock-screen-public-pickup, lock-screen-public-air, lock-screen-public-household, lock-screen-public-date (S3).\nLevels table rows (platform-neutral, light only): \"PushCopy / levels / pickup-briefings-dates-bills / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / household / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / air-151-and-above-and-noaa / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / air-below-151 / any / light\".\nExample: \"PushCopy / air-time-sensitive / expanded / android / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy-and-levels: V1 S2 on iOS 393 with callouts, then the levels table)\n1. The tray preview is an in-app illustration: a surface.raised inset card (radius lg 12, padding 12) on a surface.sunken panel (radius lg, padding 16). It is never drawn as a system alert, over a wallpaper, or with system chrome. In the grids, the panel spans the full device width (393pt on iOS, 412dp on Android), so the inset is the real notification width: 361pt on iOS and 380dp on Android. Inside a host sheet (IN CONTEXT, and the NotificationAsk primers) the panel fits the sheet's content width and the inset shrinks with it.\n2. Inside the inset, the top row: the Pantopus app icon from the design system at 20pt (R15; if it isn't published, use the R15 fallback box and log it on Notes C), then \"Pantopus\" in caption 12/16 text.strong, then \"now\" in caption text.strong, right-aligned. (Secondary words on the raised inset inside a sunken frame use text.strong.) On Android, the row uses the Android small-icon form of the same app icon, in the same illustrated style.\n3. Title: bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 text.primary, 30 characters or fewer, caveat first. Draw a character ruler under it with a tick at 30.\n4. Body: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, 40 characters or fewer on its first line, carrying the source. Draw a ruler with a tick at 40.\n5. Place label: the street name only (\"Larkspur Loop\"), and only when the person has more than one place. Callout: \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\".\n6. Caption under the panel: \"This is the whole thing.\" in caption text.strong (it sits on the sunken panel, R10: 9.37:1).\n7. Actions (expanded only): title-case text buttons inside the inset in bodySmallMedium primary.700, separated from the body by a 1px border.default rule (decoration). They are drawn for illustration; real tray actions belong to the system.\n8. Levels table, on the same artboard: four rows, each printed with its name from KEYS.\n   - pickup, briefings, dates, bills: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   - household: iOS Passive / Android LOW, one thread per home.\n   - air at AQI 151 or above, and NOAA warnings: iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH.\n   - air below AQI 151: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   Under the table, print: \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" and \"Android: the air group holds two channels, one HIGH (AQI 151 or above, and NOAA warnings) and one DEFAULT (below 151). Every other group has one channel.\"\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; the viewer is Maya, HOME A, who also has a saved place, so street labels show). Print each string's character count beside it.\nV1 Unconfirmed pickup. Title \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35). Action \"That's My Day\". Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV2 Confirmed pickup. Title \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\" (32). No action. Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV3 Air, Time Sensitive. Title \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" (22). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). Level: iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH (176 is 151 or above). On this row only, draw the words \"Time Sensitive\" as a caption word inside the inset beside \"now\" (caption text.strong), not as copied system chrome.\nV4 Air, below 151 (the fixture alert). Title \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" (25). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT (the air group's below-151 channel).\nV5 Bill marked paid (the actor is Sam). Title \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" (25). Body \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\" (30). No amount. Level: iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV6 Household roll-up. Title \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" (23). Body \"Larkspur Loop\" (13). One notification that updates in place. Level: iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV7 Date reminder. Title \"Lease notice due in 14 days\" (27). Body \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\" (31). Action \"Done\". Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV8 Hidden-preview placeholders: \"Pickup reminder\" (15) · \"Air quality alert\" (17) · \"Household update\" (16) · \"Date reminder\" (13). Android public versions: \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\" (26) · \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\" (28) · \"Pantopus · Household update\" (27) · \"Pantopus · Date reminder\" (24).\nPrint each row's level in words at the start of the row, under the row label.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Collapsed tray at true truncation. On iOS, drawn at 393pt device width (inset 361pt); on Android, at 412dp (inset 380dp). The title is on one line, and the body is on one line, truncated with an ellipsis at the real width if it doesn't fit. This is the only truncation ellipsis on the whole board. Mark the visible part with the ruler. V8 S1: four collapsed trays with previews hidden, each showing \"Pantopus\" plus its placeholder.\nS2 Expanded: the full body. V1 and V7 add their action row (\"That's My Day\", \"Done\"). V2–V6 are drawn expanded with the full body and the board caption \"No action\" under the inset. V8 S2: \"Not applicable: a hidden preview does not expand until the device is unlocked\".\nS3 Lock screen public version, still drawn as the inset illustration, never on a wallpaper. On iOS with previews hidden: \"Pantopus\" plus the placeholder for the variant's group (V1, V2 → \"Pickup reminder\"; V3, V4 → \"Air quality alert\"; V5, V6 → \"Household update\"; V7 → \"Date reminder\"). On Android: the public version \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\" for the same group. V8 S3: the four public forms for that grid's platform. Addresses, names and amounts never appear in S3.\n\nGRIDS\n02-ios-variants-by-states · light: 8 rows × 3 columns, iOS.\n03-android-variants-by-states · light: the same 8 × 3 grid on Android.\n04-ios-variants-by-states · dark: the full 02 grid in dark tokens (R9).\n05-android-variants-by-states · dark: the full 03 grid in dark tokens (R9).\nDark container: the inset is dark raised on a dark base panel. Inset top-row words are #F1F5F9 (R10: 13.35:1 on dark raised). Title and body are dark text primary. Action buttons are #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1). The caption \"This is the whole thing.\" is #F1F5F9 on the dark base panel (R10: 16.30:1). Rulers and counts stay board chrome in dark text.secondary.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (06-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 S2 and V3 S2: in the in-app illustration, the title and body wrap fully and never truncate; the caption \"This is the whole thing.\" wraps; the illustration grows taller and never scales down. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 S2 and V3 S2: the same. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V3 S2 and V4 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the Time Sensitive marker on V3 reads by its words; levels are labelled in words, never by colour.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The in-app illustration is read as one element: \"Example notification. Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow. Recycling + garbage · city schedule. This is the whole thing.\" (each variant reads its own title and body).\n- No house numbers and no full addresses in any string. Actions are title case (\"That's My Day\", \"Done\").\n- Non-colour encoding: levels are labelled in words on the board.\n- Targets: the illustration is not interactive. Real tray actions belong to the system.\n\nCOPY. Titles are 30 characters or fewer, with the caveat first. Bodies are 40 or fewer, with no house number and no amounts. Never \"Open Pantopus to…\". No keeper name or voice. No marketing, Founding or referral pushes. No pickup reminder alongside the briefing for the same pickup. Strings: every title, body, action and placeholder under VARIANTS · \"Pantopus\" · \"now\" · \"Time Sensitive\" · \"This is the whole thing.\" · \"No action\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: Active / Passive / Time Sensitive, as in the levels table. Hidden previews show the placeholder. Provisional authorization is never used for pickup.\n- Android: DEFAULT / LOW / HIGH channels, one channel per group, except the air group, which holds a HIGH and a DEFAULT channel (levels table). The public version is \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\".\n- Web: no push on this board.\n- Actions: no tray \"Mark paid\" action on any platform, because it notifies the household and can't show an Undo.\n\nIN CONTEXT (07-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f4-notification-primer: V2's tray illustration inside the pickup primer sheet (a NotificationAsk sheet, drawn only as far as the crop needs).\n- f4-notification-settings: the \"Air & weather alerts\" group row with V3 as its example and the level spelled out (\"Time Sensitive at AQI 151 or above\").\n- f3-household-notifications: the notification list row that V5 opens.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card (where V1 and V2 land), f1-today-air-band (where V3 and V4 land)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow — not yet confirmed\", draw \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" — because at 30 characters a caveat at the end is the part that gets cut.\n- Instead of \"Bins out tonight. 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\", draw \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\" — because a house number doesn't belong on a lock screen.\n- Instead of \"Sam paid Clark PUD $142.18\", draw \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" — because amounts stay inside the app, and \"marked paid\" is the product's word.\n- Instead of the notification over a phone wallpaper, as a system alert, or with a copied Time Sensitive badge, draw the inset illustration captioned \"This is the whole thing.\" — because an imitation of system UI misleads.\n- Instead of \"Open Pantopus to see today's pickup\", draw the fact itself — because the notification is the whole message.\n- Instead of Time Sensitive for a pickup reminder, draw Active — because pickup is never Time Sensitive.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 7.1 The contract's example strings use \"Lacamas Dr\", \"Maple St\", \"Due Sep 20\" and \"Sun 31 Jan\". This board uses the fixture-aligned strings from research brief section 3 (\"Larkspur Loop\", \"Due Fri 23 Oct\", \"Mon 1 Mar\").\n   7.2 V1: the contract body \"Recycling + garbage · City of Camas schedule. Bins out tonight.\" is 63 characters, over the 40 limit. This board uses \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35).\n   7.3 V6: the contract's \"Sam paid 3 bills\" conflicts with the glossary rule \"marked … paid\". This board uses \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\", with the body \"Larkspur Loop\".\n   7.4 Title case: the contract says push actions are title case (\"That's My Day\"), while research brief section 3 writes \"That's my day\" and the house style requires sentence case everywhere. \"Open Settings\" (6.1) is also title case. This board follows the contract for both. Question: keep title case for these, or switch to sentence case (\"That's my day\", \"Open settings\")?\n   7.5 V4 \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" is an invented title for the fixture's AQI 118 alert, which is below the Time Sensitive threshold.\n   7.6 V1 body: the glossary allows \"Recycling + garbage\" only in 30-character push titles. It is kept in the body to fit 40 characters. Question for the founder.\n   7.7 Levels: the contract has no row for air below AQI 151. This board adds \"air below 151: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT\" (research brief section 3, \"HIGH / DEFAULT\"), so the Android air group has two channels and \"one channel per group\" has that one exception. Confirm.\n   7.8 V5 level: research brief section 3 makes bill_paid Active for members who still see the bill as unpaid and due within 3 days. Clark Public Utilities is due Fri 23 Oct, 4 days after TODAY, so V5 is drawn Passive.\n   7.9 V8 adds a \"Date reminder\" placeholder; the contract lists only three placeholders.\nB. Maya also has a saved place (The Blairmont rental), so street labels show. V3's AQI 176 reading at 4:00 PM is the contract's example, not the fixture reading.\nC. The Pantopus app icon, if it isn't published yet (the R15 fallback box).\nD. \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" · \"now\" · \"Time Sensitive\" (as a word inside the illustration) · \"Date reminder\" · \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\" · \"Pantopus · Household update\" · \"Pantopus · Date reminder\" · \"Larkspur Loop\" as the V6 body · \"Time Sensitive at AQI 151 or above\" · the spoken \"Example notification…\" labels · \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" · the Android air-channel line under the levels table · chrome: \"No action\" · \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\" · the character counts and ruler ticks.\nE. Light only: the levels table (documentation, platform-neutral) and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Omitted: web push (none in scope).\nF. Light: 23 iOS cells and 23 Android cells (every cell except V8 S2), with V8's four specimens per cell, plus the four levels rows and the 06 large-text frames. Dark: the same 46 cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 7 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Four grids (iOS light, Android light, iOS dark, Android dark) each have 8 rows × 3 columns with keys. V8 S2 carries its reason, and V8 S1 and S3 each hold four named specimens.\n- Every title is 30 characters or fewer and every body 40 or fewer, each with its count printed. No string has a house number or an amount.\n- S3 cells show only \"Pantopus\" and a placeholder, never an address, name or amount.\n- Nothing is drawn over a wallpaper, as a system alert, or with copied system chrome. \"Time Sensitive\" appears only on V3, as a caption word.\n- The levels table has four named rows and the two lines under it.\n- Only S1 collapsed trays are truncated with an ellipsis.\n- 06 has columns (a), (b) and (c); 07 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy-and-levels, 02-ios-variants-by-states light, 03-android-variants-by-states light, 04-ios-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 05-android-variants-by-states dark, 06-ax5-200-greyscale, 07-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
