            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-08: ReminderLeadControl. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Shows every reminder that will actually fire, on a small timeline running back from the date the person must act.\nUsed in (print on 01): x-date-sheet, f10-extraction-confirm\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then finish Notes)\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend and finish it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Date sheet = date-sheet · V2 Extraction confirm = extraction-confirm · V3 Lease = lease-notice.\nStates: S1 Default = default · S2 Lead already passed = lead-passed · S3 Disabled = disabled.\nSpecimens outside the grid: \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default-one-day / ios / <theme>\" (the one-day specimen, light on 02 and dark on 03) · \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default-focused / ios / light\" (the focus specimen on 01) · \"ReminderLeadControl / segment / chosen-then-passed / ios / light\" (the inset on 01) · \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / ios-ax2 / light\" · \"… / date-sheet / default / android-150 / light\" · \"… / date-sheet / default / web-1440 / light\".\n\nPASSED-LEAD RULE (one rule for every variant)\nTODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026. A lead whose date is before TODAY has passed. A passed lead gets exactly one of two treatments:\n- Passed (never chosen): disabled per R16. Label in text.muted (R10: 2.54:1, disabled only), no check, still focusable, read as \"<N> days, unavailable, <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" Activating it shows the explanation line and suggestion instead of selecting it.\n- Chosen-then-passed (the lead was selected, then the date was edited so it has now passed): a primary.50 fill, a 1.5px primary.700 border, NO check, the label in bodySmall 14/20 at weight 400 in text.primary, and the word \"passed\" under the label in caption 12/16 text.primary. Both lines fit inside the 44pt segment. Dark: a primary.900 fill, a 1.5px #38BDF8 border, no check, with the label and the word in dark text primary. It is read as \"<N> days, selected, passed. <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" It keeps this treatment, with the explanation line and suggestion under the control, until the person picks another lead. This is the one extra treatment R12 allows; it differs from selection by no check, 400 weight and the word \"passed\".\nThe suggestion is always the longest lead that is still ahead. Nothing is saved until the person taps the suggestion or picks a live segment. The timeline never draws a tick for a passed lead.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393 with callouts; the example date is the water-heater warranty ending Sat 12 Dec 2026)\nLead dates for this example: 60 days = Tue 13 Oct 2026 (passed) · 30 days = Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 7 days = Sat 5 Dec 2026 · 1 day = Fri 11 Dec 2026.\n1. Label above the control: label 13/18/600 text.primary, \"Remind me\".\n2. Segmented control, 361pt wide × 44pt tall (Android 380 × 48dp), with four equal segments: \"60 days\", \"30 days\", \"7 days\", \"1 day\". The container has a 1px text.secondary outline (R10: 4.83:1), radius md 8, and 1px text.secondary dividers.\n   - Unselected segment: surface.base, label in bodySmall text.primary.\n   - Selected segment: the R12 selection treatment (fill + check + 600 weight).\n   - Passed segment: \"60 days\" is drawn disabled per the PASSED-LEAD RULE. Callout: \"passed: Tue 13 Oct; focusable, reason read out\".\n   - Chosen-then-passed segment: drawn once as a small inset beside the control (named in KEYS), per the PASSED-LEAD RULE. Callout: \"chosen before a date edit; no check; 'passed' written\".\n   - Focus: the R12 ring, drawn on the unselected live segment \"7 days\" in a second full specimen beside the first (named \"default-focused\").\n3. Mini timeline, 12pt below the control: a 2px text.secondary horizontal line with three ticks (12pt tall, 2px wide), evenly spaced and not to scale. A two-slash break mark sits between the first and second ticks, captioned \"not to scale\". Each tick carries two labels:\n   - The date in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary: \"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" · \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\" · \"Sat 12 Dec 2026\".\n   - The role in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"30 days before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\".\n   A leader line runs from the \"Day of\" tick to an event label at the right end: KindGlyph (16pt, R15) plus \"Water-heater warranty ends\" in caption text.primary.\n4. Caption, 8pt below the timeline: \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\" in caption text.secondary.\n5. When \"1 day\" is selected, the lead and the day before are the same day, so only two ticks are drawn (\"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\"), and the caption reads \"We'll also remind you on the day.\" This is the one-day specimen, drawn beside the grid on 02 and 03.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 Date sheet (x-date-sheet): the anatomy example: 30 days selected, 60 days disabled (passed).\nV2 Extraction confirm (f10-extraction-confirm): 7 days is the default. The date is the City of Vancouver water bill, due Wed 28 Oct 2026. Passed leads: 60 days (Sat 29 Aug 2026) and 30 days (Mon 28 Sep 2026), both disabled. 1 day = Tue 27 Oct 2026. Ticks: \"Wed 21 Oct 2026 · 7 days before\", \"Tue 27 Oct 2026 · Day before\", \"Wed 28 Oct 2026 · Day of\". Event label: \"Water bill due\".\nV3 Lease, anchored to the notice deadline (x-date-sheet, lease kind). The event is \"Notice deadline · Mon 1 Mar 2027\", never the lease end date. Past the event, draw the lease end \"Wed 31 Mar 2027\" as a label in caption text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1, readable, never text.muted), with the caption \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\". 30 days is selected. No lead has passed (60 days = Thu 31 Dec 2026, 7 days = Mon 22 Feb 2027, 1 day = Sun 28 Feb 2027). Ticks: \"Sat 30 Jan 2027 · 30 days before\", \"Sun 28 Feb 2027 · Day before\", \"Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Day of\".\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Default: as drawn per variant, with passed segments disabled (V1: 60 days; V2: 60 and 30 days; V3: none).\nS2 Lead already passed (suggested alternative), per the PASSED-LEAD RULE. Print the scenario label above each cell in caption text.secondary.\n  - V1. Scenario label: \"date first entered as Sat 16 Jan 2027 with 60 days chosen (Tue 17 Nov 2026), then edited to Sat 12 Dec 2026\". \"60 days\" uses the chosen-then-passed treatment; 30, 7 and 1 days are live and unselected. Under the control: a 16pt info glyph (primary.700), then \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" in bodySmall text.primary, then a suggestion button \"Use 30 days instead\" (outlined: surface.base, 1px text.secondary border, bodySmallMedium text.primary, 44pt tall, radius md). The timeline shows the suggested series \"Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 30 days before\", \"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\", captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V2. Scenario label: \"the extraction first read Sun 22 Nov 2026 and 30 days was chosen (Fri 23 Oct 2026); the date was then corrected to Wed 28 Oct 2026\". The event label stays \"Water bill due\". \"30 days\" uses the chosen-then-passed treatment, \"60 days\" is disabled (passed), and 7 and 1 days are live and unselected. The explanation line reads \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\", then the button \"Use 7 days instead\". The timeline shows \"Wed 21 Oct 2026 · 7 days before\", \"Tue 27 Oct 2026 · Day before\", \"Wed 28 Oct 2026 · Day of\", captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V3: \"Not applicable: no lead has passed for Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\nS3 Disabled (the date field is empty): the segment container is on surface.sunken, all four segment labels are text.muted, there is no selection, and no timeline is drawn. The segments stay focusable and read \"<N> days, unavailable, Add the date first to set reminders.\" The line \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" sits under the control in bodySmall text.strong (on sunken, R10: 9.37:1). This state applies to all three variants.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 3 rows × 3 columns on iOS, plus the one-day specimen beside the V1 row.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid, one-day specimen included, in dark tokens (R9). Container: the control sits in a dark base sheet. The selected segment uses the R12 dark selection, and the chosen-then-passed segment uses its dark form from the PASSED-LEAD RULE. The container outline, dividers and ticks are #94A3B8 (R10: 6.96:1). Disabled labels are #64748B (R10: 3.75:1). The info glyph is #38BDF8. In S3, the container is dark raised (dark sunken would vanish on the dark base sheet), and the reason line is #F1F5F9.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) iOS AX5, V1 S1: the segments become four selectable rows, each at least 44pt tall. The selected row has the R12 selection treatment (primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, 16pt check glyph, 600-weight label). Unselected rows have no glyph, and there are no circles. Line one is the role and line two is the date. For a passed row, only line one is text.muted; line two carries the date and the word \"passed\" in text.secondary, so the reason is always readable. The rows read:\n  \"60 days before\" (text.muted) / \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" (text.secondary) · \"30 days before\" / \"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" (selected) · \"7 days before\" / \"Sat 5 Dec 2026\" · \"1 day before\" / \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\".\n  The timeline becomes a vertical list of three rows: \"Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 30 days before\", \"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\". Name uses ios-ax5.\n- (b) Android 200%, V1 S1: the same selectable rows at 48dp. Name uses android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V1 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the selected segment has its check and weight; a passed lead has its lighter label, no check, and the word 'passed' in the AX rows; the chosen-then-passed segment has the word 'passed' and no check; S2 has its explanation line.\"\n- Extra row below: iOS AX1–AX2 (the segments become a 2×2 grid of 44pt cells; ios-ax2) · Android 150% (a 2×2 grid of 48dp cells; android-150) · a web-1440 crop of V1 S1 inside the date sheet's 480px side panel (web-1440, 44px segments).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Remind me, 30 days before, selected, 2 of 4.\" A passed segment: \"60 days, unavailable, 60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" A chosen-then-passed segment: \"60 days, selected, passed. 60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" The timeline is one element with a summary: V1 \"Reminders on Thu 12 Nov, Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec.\" · V2 \"Reminders on Wed 21 Oct, Tue 27 Oct and Wed 28 Oct.\" · V3 \"Reminders on Sat 30 Jan, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar.\" The same facts appear as a list at AX sizes. The S2 explanation line is announced politely when it appears.\n- Non-colour encoding: selection is a text label plus a fill change plus a check, never colour alone.\n- Targets: segments (disabled ones included) are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. The suggestion button is 44pt. The ticks are not targets.\n\nCOPY. The caption is \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\" Dates always show the weekday. Other strings: \"Remind me\" · \"60 days\" · \"30 days\" · \"7 days\" · \"1 day\" · \"60 days before\" · \"30 days before\" · \"7 days before\" · \"1 day before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\" · \"passed\" · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"Water bill due\" · \"Notice deadline\" · \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\" · \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" · \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\" · \"Use 30 days instead\" · \"Use 7 days instead\" · \"Suggested\" · \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" · \"We'll also remind you on the day.\"\n\nPLATFORMS. The same on all platforms apart from target sizes and the large-text layouts above. On web-1440, the control sits in the date sheet's 480px side panel (drawn in the extra row on 04).\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- x-date-sheet: the Date sheet for \"Water-heater warranty\", with V1 below the date field.\n- x-date-sheet (lease): the Date sheet for the lease, with V3 anchored to the notice deadline.\n- f10-extraction-confirm: \"Confirm what we read\" for the water bill, with V2.\nAlso consumed by: none beyond these two surfaces.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a single \"Remind me 30 days before\" row, draw all three reminders with their real dates — because three will fire, and the person should see each one.\n- Instead of anchoring the lease reminder to Wed 31 Mar 2027, anchor it to the notice deadline Mon 1 Mar 2027 — because the notice is what the person must act on.\n- Instead of silently accepting a lead that has already passed, draw the explanation and \"Use 30 days instead\" — because a reminder dated in the past never fires.\n- Instead of hiding or silently greying a passed lead, keep it focusable with its reason read and written — because silent dead controls leave people guessing.\n- Instead of keeping the check on a lead that passed after a date edit, draw the chosen-then-passed segment with the word \"passed\" — because a check says a reminder will fire.\n- Instead of radio circles at large text, draw selectable rows with a check — because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance.\n- Instead of showing selection by colour alone, draw fill + check + weight — because colour alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind people.\n- Instead of a timeline drawn to scale, draw evenly spaced ticks with a \"not to scale\" break — because a to-scale 60-day line squashes the last two ticks together.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes, then finish it)\nA. 8.1 V3: the fixture's lease reminder is Mon 15 Feb 2027 (14 days before the notice deadline, and PushCopy V7 says \"due in 14 days\"), but the contract's leads are 60 / 30 / 7 / 1. This board draws 30 days (Sat 30 Jan 2027). Question: add a 14-day option, or change the fixture?\n   8.2 Passed leads: the contract gives no rule. This board uses the PASSED-LEAD RULE: a passed lead is disabled but focusable with its reason read out (following OfflineNotice's \"Disabled controls stay focusable\"), except a lead chosen before a date edit, which gets a third, chosen-then-passed treatment (selection fill and border, no check, 400 weight, the word \"passed\") until it is replaced. The suggestion is the longest lead still ahead. Confirm.\n   8.3 Large text: the contract says \"radio rows\". This board draws selectable rows with a check and no circles, because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance only.\n   8.4 Selection: segments use the R12 treatment, the same as NotificationAsk chips (an earlier primary.700 segment fill was dropped).\n   8.5 S3 dark: the disabled container uses dark raised, because dark sunken equals the dark base sheet.\nB. The S2 starting dates (Sat 16 Jan 2027 for the warranty; the misread Sun 22 Nov 2026 for the water bill) are invented so the chosen leads were still ahead before the edit.\nC. KindGlyph, if drawn as a fallback box.\nD. Every COPY string except the contract caption and the four segment labels · the chosen-then-passed and passed spoken labels · \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" · the V2 and V3 timeline summaries · chrome: \"not to scale\" · the two S2 scenario labels · \"passed: Tue 13 Oct; focusable, reason read out\" · \"chosen before a date edit; no check; 'passed' written\".\nE. Light only: the default-focused and chosen-then-passed insets on 01 (their dark forms are defined in R9, R12 and the PASSED-LEAD RULE, and appear inside the dark grid), and every frame on 04 (ios-ax5, android-200, ios-ax2, android-150, web-1440). Omitted: a 14-day lead (Notes 8.1).\nF. Light: 8 grid cells (V3 S2 is Not applicable), the one-day specimen, the two 01 insets, and the 04 frames. Dark: the same 8 grid cells and the one-day specimen.\nThen check that Notes A–F cover all eight components in order, 0.1 first, and that F lists every printed name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and 00d · Notes is complete for all eight components.\n- The light and dark grids have 3 rows × 3 columns with keys, plus the one-day specimen. V3 S2 carries its reason.\n- Every passed lead is disabled but focusable (V1: 60 days; V2: 60 and 30 days), except a lead chosen before a date edit, which uses the chosen-then-passed treatment (V1 S2: 60 days; V2 S2: 30 days). The V1 and V2 S2 cells are real specimens with scenario labels, explanation lines, suggestion buttons and \"Suggested\" timelines.\n- No tick for a passed lead; every tick shows a weekday date and a role. V3 is anchored to Mon 1 Mar 2027, with the lease end in text.secondary.\n- No radio circles. At AX sizes, a passed row's date and \"passed\" are in text.secondary.\n- Every segment (disabled ones included) and the suggestion button show their dashed hit area.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) and the extra row; 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend and finish it). Then stop: the board is complete.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message."
          }
