        "resolved": [
          "[major] NotificationAsk household primer missing (00d-06): added primer-ios-household and primer-android-household sheets on 03 (light) and 05 (dark), each with the unique title \"Household updates on this phone\", the PushCopy V5 tray (\"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" / \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\") with \"This is the whole thing.\", a body saying household updates stay off until switched on and then arrive quietly (Passive/LOW), and the caption \"after household activity from Mail\". Anatomy B names both entries; Notes 6.4 records the invented wording, and the strings are in Notes D.",
          "[major] Dark set incomplete vs PUBLISH: took fix (a) for every variant×state grid and (b) for platform/large-text frames. NotificationAsk now has 04-card-row-states dark (the full 2×5 grid) and 05-primer-and-denial-by-platform dark (all seven sheets). PushCopy now has full 8×3 dark grids for iOS (04) and Android (05). Every other component's dark grid is the full grid. The setup PUBLISH rules say every variant×state cell has a dark twin, and that platform strips, large-text frames and web-1440 crops are light only. Each component's Notes E lists its light-only frames, including DestructiveConfirm 03-platforms and the InlineUndo and LandingBannerSlot Platforms rows, with the rule for deriving dark (geometry from light, colours from the dark artboard plus R9).",
          "[minor] Invented strings missing from Notes: each component prompt now has its own Notes D list. NotificationAsk D includes \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\", the longer settings line, \"Put Today on your home screen\" and \"Add the widget\". Setup R19 D lists the shared board chrome (every \"Not applicable: <reason>\", \"key:\", \"Reads without colour:\" and others). Component chrome such as \"same height\" (WarmingSkeleton) and \"Never two banners.\" (LandingBannerSlot) is in each component's D list. The \"Put Today\" capitalisation question is Notes 6.5.",
          "[minor] InlineUndo V6 not logged: Notes 3.2 records V6 Fan-out hold as an added sixth variant from the contract's fan-out anatomy rule, listing the contract's five variants, for the founder to confirm.",
          "[minor] QuietDayReceipt spoken label change not logged: Notes 1.3 records that the S1 label adds the heading and time to the contract's \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\", and the ACCESSIBILITY section cites it.",
          "[minor] DestructiveConfirm progress vs cadence: the S2 visual is now \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" with the bar at 5/17. The live region reads 5, 10 and 15, then the done line. Notes 4.4 records this.",
          "[minor] PushCopy levels table: added a fourth row, \"PushCopy / levels / air-below-151 / any / light\" (iOS Active / Android DEFAULT). Under the table, the prompt now says the Android air group holds two channels (HIGH at 151 or above and NOAA; DEFAULT below 151). V4 states Android DEFAULT on the below-151 channel, and PLATFORMS names the one exception to \"one channel per group\". Notes 7.7 records it.",
          "[minor] ReminderLeadControl V2 S2 scenario: the scenario is now \"the extraction first read Sun 22 Nov 2026 and 30 days was chosen (Fri 23 Oct 2026); the date was then corrected to Wed 28 Oct 2026\". The event label stays \"Water bill due\" throughout V2. All weekdays were checked. Notes B records the invented start dates.",
          "[minor] ReminderLeadControl AX5 passed row readable: at AX5 only line one (the role) is text.muted. Line two \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" is text.secondary, and DONE WHEN checks this.",
          "[minor] LandingBannerSlot glyphs and V4 caption: anatomy item 2 now names a glyph for every variant, with the envelope for V1, V1 degraded, V2, V4 and the seven-days-out specimen. V4's offline caption is spelled out in full: \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\", with its spoken form. Notes 5.4 asks the founder to confirm the glyphs.",
          "[major] PASSED-LEAD RULE contradiction: the rule now defines two exclusive treatments. Passed (disabled per R16) and chosen-then-passed: primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, NO check, 400-weight label, the word \"passed\" under it, with a dark form and the spoken label \"<N> days, selected, passed. …\". S2 (V1: 60 days; V2: 30 days), anatomy, greyscale, DONE WHEN, setup R12 (\"one further treatment\") and Notes 8.2 all use it.",
          "[major] DestructiveConfirm label vs house style: the default is now a text.primary 600 label, a 1.5px semantic.error border and a semantic.error glyph. Dark keeps #DC2626 on the border and glyph only (3.70:1 on dark base), and no accent.red is used. Anatomy item 6, the dark grid note, INSTEAD OF and DONE WHEN match. Notes 4.1 presents the contract's red label as an alternative for the founder, and no longer calls it 'approved'.",
          "[major] LandingBannerSlot precedence ladder: anatomy item 7 draws eight steps (invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify) with the one-banner scenario. DONE WHEN checks the ladder, and Notes 5.3 asks the founder to confirm the order.",
          "[major] WarmingSkeleton S3 content unspecified: S3 now spells out the content for each variant. V2 row 1 is MemberRow (owner) \"Maya Chen\" with the caption \"Owner\". V3 sub-specimen a is FourteenDayStrip for HOME A from Mon 19 Oct, with pickup marks Tue 20 and Tue 27 Oct and date marks Fri 23 Oct, Mon 26 Oct, Wed 28 Oct and Sun 1 Nov. b, c and d stay skeleton, each with its own key. All content is fixture content, with R15 fallback boxes if needed, and Notes B explains which dates fall inside the 14 days.",
          "[major] InlineUndo iOS anatomy vs no-echo rule: anatomy item 3 now draws the snackbar echo as a separate Android 412 inset labelled \"android only\", and says iOS never draws an echo. The web toast appears only in the 04 Platforms row, whose specimens have exact names.",
          "[minor] Android 200% sizes: setup R17(b) now gives Android 14 non-linear values: caption 12→24sp, label 13→25sp, bodySmall 14→26sp, body 16→about 28sp, h3 20→about 34sp.",
          "[minor] AX artboards with extra frames: setup R17 says the three columns (a)(b)(c) are required and any extra frames go in a labelled row below them. InlineUndo PLATFORMS now points to \"the Platforms row on 04\" instead of \"under the grid\".",
          "[minor] Specimens without exact names: setup R7 adds a B18-style key grammar, \"<Component> / <variant-key> / <state-key> / <platform> / <light|dark>\", with keys that are lowercase and hyphenated and never contain fixture strings or dates. It also adds large-text platform keys (ios-ax5, ios-ax2, android-200, android-150) and \"any\". Every component prompt lists its keys and names every specimen outside the grid. Examples: the four WarmingSkeleton V3 sub-keys (…-bill-trend and the others), LandingBannerSlot expiring-early and one-invite-degraded, the four \"PushCopy / levels / …\" rows, the seven NotificationAsk sheet names (ios-denied / denied, android-blocked / blocked and the rest), and the ReminderLeadControl insets. Notes F is a publish index.",
          "[minor] NotificationAsk dark ambiguity: resolved by the full dark grid (04) and the full dark sheet set (05). The old partial list, with its inconsistent 'S4' wording, is gone.",
          "[minor] Incomplete or unlogged strings: QuietDayReceipt IN CONTEXT gives \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" (Jordan's Thursday pickup). \"Birchfield Ct\" is in QuietDayReceipt Notes D. PushCopy Notes B records the assumption that Maya also has a saved place (The Blairmont rental), so street labels show.",
          "[minor] App icon placeholder box: PushCopy anatomy item 2, the NotificationAsk tray, and setup R15 now use the Pantopus app icon from the design system at 20pt. The labelled box is only the R15 fallback, and it is logged under Notes C (missing dependencies).",
          "[minor] Artboard naming vs house style: setup R1 says this board's format \"00d · <Component> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\" replaces the house-style format, that the platform goes in each specimen name (R7), and that Notes is named exactly \"00d · Notes\".",
          "[minor] Primer entry conflict and title case: Notes 6.3 records the conflict between the contract's primer entry points and research brief section 2 item 8 (inline ask straight to the OS dialog) as a founder question. Notes 7.4 (and 6.1 for \"Open Settings\") say title case also conflicts with the house-style sentence-case rule, and ask the founder to decide.",
          "[minor] Length and repetition: the board is now one setup prompt plus eight component prompts, each under about 2,800 words (the old single prompt was about 103 KB). Contrast figures are stated once, in setup R10, and cited as \"(R10)\". The disabled pattern is stated once, in R16. Each BATCH PLAN ends with \"re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message\", and each component has at most 2 batches of at most 4 artboards plus Notes.",
          "Additional board-level decision (not from the issue list, recorded as Notes 0.1): the dark selected fill is primary.900 with a #38BDF8 border and check, so it matches the other Foundations boards' dark mapping; R9 and R10 carry the figures (7.64:1 for the label, 4.42:1 for the check, used on glyphs only). R13 also names the avatar circle as the one allowed circle (MemberRow and its skeleton)."
        ]
      }
