    "groups": [
      {
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "00a-00",
            "promptText": "SETUP 00a-00. Foundations board 00a: Marks, captions and chips. Draw nothing yet.\n\nUse the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is the Foundations board 00a.\nTYPE: NEW (a component specimen board).\nATTACH: none. Nothing here has shipped. Tokens, type scale and base icons come from the published Pantopus design system.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nThe first design work for Pantopus, before any screen. It draws nine components once, precisely, with every variant and state: ProvenanceMark · SourceCaption · ScopeChip · FreshnessLine · OfflineNotice · StatusChip · KindGlyph · AddressChip · ChoiceChip. Every later screen is designed in a separate project with no memory of this one and uses these exact names, so label everything with its name, keys (B12) and tokens.\n\nHOW THIS PROJECT RUNS\n- The board rules (B1–B17) and the Notes rules below apply to every artboard in this project.\n- Next, I send one component message per turn, in order. Each one opens with \"Component 00a-NN: <Name>.\" and carries that component's specification, its ARTBOARDS list and its BATCH PLAN.\n- A long component arrives in parts (for example 00a-NNa, then 00a-NNb). A part message takes the place of \"continue\" and carries the specification for the next batch. Specifications from earlier parts of the same component still apply.\n- Draw only the current batch (at most 6 artboards), in the listed order. Then stop and wait for \"continue\", the next part or the next component message. If a batch will not fit, finish the artboards in order and say which ones moved to the next turn.\n- Everything you need is in this message and the current component message (with its earlier parts). Components already drawn here are final; reuse them exactly when embedded. Never rely on any other project, file or link.\n- Where a component message differs from a board rule, it wins for that component only, and the difference goes on Notes.\n\nPUBLISH (a founder step; you only prepare the index)\nWhen the founder accepts a component, the founder adds it to the published Pantopus design system under its exact name, so it comes out identical on all 59 later surfaces. Make this mechanical: list every specimen name on 00a · Notes, section E. Give one name per drawn grid cell, plus one for each anatomy size or platform form the component message lists under PUBLISH KEYS. \"Does not apply\" cells get no name.\n  <Component> / <variant> / <state> / <size|platform> / <light|dark>\n<variant> and <state> are exactly the printed keys (B12), never the labels. The <size|platform> slot takes exactly one of these strings: size codes in uppercase (XS, S, M, L, OG); platform codes in lowercase (ios, android, web); otherwise \"any\". It is \"any\" unless the component message says otherwise. Example: \"StatusChip / overdue / default / any / light\".\n\n======================================================================\nBOARD RULES\n======================================================================\n\nB1. Artboards. Every artboard is 1440 px wide and as tall as its content needs, on surface.app (light) or dark surface.app (dark). A component message may set a wider artboard for a grid (for example 2000 or 2400 px); that message gives the margins, label column and gutters, and records the width on Notes, section A. Name each artboard \"00a · <Component> · <NN-state> · <light|dark>\". The component name takes the house style's platform slot, because one specimen artboard shows all three platforms. The only other artboard is \"00a · Notes\". Print each exact name above its frame in label 13/18/600 text.strong. The standard kinds are:\n  01-anatomy: callouts, TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF.\n  02-variants-states (light and dark): the variant × state grid.\n  03-scaling-greyscale: AX5, 200% and web zoom frames, GREYSCALE and INCREASE CONTRAST.\n  04-in-context: crops of real surfaces. Label each crop with its surface id, platform, width and fixture (Home A, Place B or Friend C).\nThe component message lists its exact artboards and any extra dark twins.\n\nB2. Top block. Inside each component artboard, print the component name in h1 30/36/700 text.primary, its one-line purpose in body 16/24 text.secondary, then \"Used in:\" plus the line the message gives, in caption 12/16 text.secondary, exactly. Each section below gets an overline 11/16/600 caps heading (ANATOMY, GREYSCALE and so on).\n\nB3. Specimen cells. Draw each specimen on a surface.base card (radius lg 12, shadow sm, 16 px padding) unless the cell names another surface. Under the card, print its cell label in caption 12/16 text.secondary: its keys, size and surface, joined by \" · \". Example: \"official · default · S 16pt · on surface.base\".\n\nB4. Callouts. Draw 1 px text.secondary leader lines that end in a numbered SQUARE badge (16×16, radius xs 4, surface.sunken fill, label 13/18/600 text.strong numeral). Beside each number, give the measurement and token in caption 12/16 text.strong, for example \"[1] 12pt disc · ink text.secondary\". Badges are square because circles are reserved (B8). Callout numbers written [1]–[7] or ①–⑦ in a component message are these square badges; never draw them as circles. Dimension lines are 1 px text.secondary with 4 px end ticks and the number centred.\n\nB5. Units and sizes. The first time a size appears in a section, give it three ways: \"16pt / 16dp / 16px\" (iOS / Android / web; the values are equal). Spacing uses only 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48 and 64. Type uses only the type scale, the large-text sizes in B9, and any deviation a message records on Notes. Any other dimension is allowed only where this setup or a component message states it.\n\nB6. Tokens by name, and dark mode. Label every colour by its token name. Hex values appear only in each TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE; the values below are for you. Dark artboards use:\n  surface.base #FFFFFF → dark surface.base #0F172A\n  surface.raised #F9FAFB → dark surface.raised #1E293B\n  surface.sunken #F3F4F6 → dark surface.sunken #0F172A (same as dark base)\n  surface.app #F6F7F9 → dark surface.app #020617\n  surface.muted #F8FAFC → dark surface.muted #111827\n  text.primary #111827 → dark text.primary #E5E7EB\n  text.strong #374151 → dark text.strong #F1F5F9\n  text.secondary #6B7280 → dark text.secondary #94A3B8\n  text.muted #9CA3AF → dark text.muted #64748B (disabled controls and placeholders only)\n  border.default #E5E7EB → dark border.default #1F2937 (decoration only)\n  border.strong #D1D5DB → dark border.strong #374151 (decoration only)\n  border.focus #0284c7 → dark border.focus #38BDF8\n  primary.700 #0369a1 (links, selected text, selected edges) → \"primary.400 (dark link)\" #38BDF8, the same value as dark border.focus. Use that exact name on the board.\n  primary.50 #f0f9ff (selected fill) → primary.900 #0c4a6e with dark text.primary on it. primary.400 (dark link) on primary.900 is for glyphs and edges only.\n  primary.500 #0ea5e9 appears only where a component message names it.\n  semantic.success #059669, semantic.warning #D97706 and semantic.error #DC2626 keep their hue in dark mode and go on glyphs only. primary.700 stands in for semantic.info where a message says so.\n  Sunken fills: dark surface.sunken equals dark surface.base, so a sunken fill vanishes on a dark base card. Use dark surface.sunken on dark surface.raised, and dark surface.raised on dark surface.base or dark surface.app. These fills need no border.\n\nB7. Contrast numbers. Ratios are WCAG 2 ratios computed from the real tokens. A colour at an opacity is alpha-blended over its surface in sRGB with unrounded channels, and every ratio is rounded to 2 decimals at the end. Each component message's TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE gives the figures that component needs. Print them exactly as given, and do not recompute them.\n\nB8. Circles are reserved. Only ProvenanceMark may draw a solid disc, a ring, or a disc with a knocked-out tick. This covers any glyph silhouette and any drawn dot, bullet or badge. The typographic middle dot (·) in text is allowed. Round sub-parts inside a larger glyph are fine (a head, cart wheels, a pin's hole). Draw dot groups inside a glyph as short dashes or small rounded squares. The only other exceptions are the platform radio indicators that a component message names and flags on Notes. No iOS or web frame draws an unselected radio ring; the only ring in those frames is ProvenanceMark's unconfirmed mark.\n\nB9. Large text. AX5 frames (iOS, 393 wide): caption 40pt, label 44pt, bodySmall 46pt, body 53pt. Android 200% frames (412 wide): caption 24sp, label 26sp, bodySmall 28sp, body 32sp. Crop both frames to the component and its row. Pairs stack, text wraps and never ends in an ellipsis, pills that must wrap become rounded rectangles (radius lg 12), and hit areas grow. Glyphs and marks scale with their text, capped at 2× their default size; a component message states any size that does not scale. Web 200% zoom frames are 390 px wide, a 195 px effective viewport, so they show the narrowest layout. A message that needs the wide zoomed form asks for a 1440 frame at 200% (720 px effective).\n\nB10. Greyscale. Each light 03 artboard repeats the light grid at 50% scale, fully desaturated, unless the message sets a different scope. Next to each cell, print \"Reads without colour: yes — <cue>\", or the failure and its fix where the message names one.\n\nB11. Increase Contrast. Each light 03 artboard shows what changes, or prints \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — <why>\". By default, text.secondary becomes text.strong (dark: dark text.strong). Disabled text.muted stays, because the reason caption carries the meaning. Each message states its result.\n\nB12. Grids, keys and cell labels. Rows are the message's variants and columns are its states, in the given order. Draw every cell. Under each row and column label, print \"key: <key>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary. Keys are lowercase and hyphenated, with no \"/\", spaces, fixture strings or dates. Labels may be longer and may quote fixtures. Each message lists its keys, and cell labels and publish names use only those keys. A cell that \"does not apply\" is an empty surface.base card reading \"Does not apply — <reason>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary; a shared reason is printed in each cell. Never leave a cell blank or skip a row or column.\n\nB13. Targets. The minimum hit area is 44pt on iOS, 48dp with 8dp gaps on Android, and 44px on web: \"target (B13)\". Draw it as a 1 px dashed text.secondary outline labelled \"target 44pt / 48dp / 44px\". Point a small \"not a target\" label at any mark or glyph inside a row.\n\nB14. Focus vs selection. Focus is a 2 px border.focus ring (dark: dark border.focus) with a 2 px gap outside the shape. Selection is a fill plus a glyph, plus the edge or ink change the message states. Never show selection with a ring alone, or focus with a fill.\n\nB15. Motion. Nothing animates unless a message says so. Where motion exists, draw its Reduce Motion pose and its end pose beside it. Any exemption from the house style's 300ms limit is stated in the message and recorded on Notes.\n\nB16. Fixtures and dates. Use only the house-style FIXTURES and the strings quoted in the messages. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific. Compute every relative time from it: \"observed 7:00 AM\" is \"11 hours ago\", Mon 26 Oct is \"in 7 days\", and Sat 10 Oct is \"9 days ago\". Date rows put the relative count first (\"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"). \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" stand alone, with no date. A time today shows no weekday (\"As of 7:40 AM\"). Any other string goes on Notes, section B.\n\nB17. Air readings. The AQI track belongs to AqiBand, which is not on this board. Air rows show the value line and caption only. No EPA ColorVision Assist hue appears, and no text sits on an AQI fill.\n\n======================================================================\n00a · NOTES (one artboard, built up across the project)\n======================================================================\nProvenanceMark's last part creates 00a · Notes, and each later component's last batch updates it. On each update, redraw the whole artboard, keep every earlier entry word for word, and add the new entries under the component's subheading. Print numbered lists in body 16/24 text.primary on surface.base, in five sections:\n  A. Deviations and decisions (each needs a founder yes or no).\n  B. Invented strings.\n  C. Omitted or merged states (\"none\" if every cell was drawn).\n  D. Open questions (only where two readings would give materially different components).\n  E. Publish index (every PUBLISH name, one per line, grouped by component).\nEntry numbers start with the component number: 00 for board-wide entries, then 01 ProvenanceMark through 09 ChoiceChip (for example \"01.A3\"). Print these entries first, under \"Board\":\n  00.A1 Artboard names put the component in the platform slot, because each artboard covers all three platforms.\n  00.A2 Marks and glyphs at AX5 / 200% are capped at 2× their default size.\n  00.A3 No dark primary.50 exists, so the dark selected fill is primary.900. The dark link colour is named \"primary.400 (dark link)\" (= dark border.focus).\n  00.A4 Dark surface.sunken equals dark surface.base, so sunken fills on a dark base or app surface use dark surface.raised.\n  00.A5 Dated rows follow DateRow's format (B16). DateRow owns the format, and later surfaces copy it from there.\n  00.A6 Web 200% zoom frames are 390 px (195 px effective), so they show the narrowest layout.\n  00.A7 Every grid row and column carries a key, and publish names use only keys.\n  00.A8 Contrast figures use the B7 method (sRGB alpha blend, unrounded channels, rounded at the end). Each component's figures are printed in its own TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE.\n  00.A9 No AQI track or EPA hue appears on this board.\n  00.A10 The dark text.strong, text.muted, border.strong and surface.muted values come from the published design system, not the house style. Dark text.strong is intentionally brighter than dark text.primary, for Increase Contrast.\n  00.A11 Artboards are 1440 px wide unless a component message sets a wider grid artboard; each such width is recorded under that component.\n  00.A12 Publish-name size and platform slot casing: size codes uppercase (XS, S, M, L, OG), platform codes lowercase (ios, android, web), otherwise \"any\".\n  00.B1 Board annotations: \"Does not apply — …\" reasons, \"not a target\", \"target 44pt / 48dp / 44px\", \"Reads without colour: yes — …\", \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — …\".\n\nReply 'ready' and wait for the first component.",
            "component": null
          },
          {
            "id": "00a-01",
            "component": "ProvenanceMark",
            "artboards": [
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark",
              "00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark",
              "00a · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00a-01: ProvenanceMark. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nIt comes first because every other component embeds its marks, and it gets a full light and dark set.\n\nARTBOARDS (8, exact names; the batch plan gives the order)\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark\nPlus 00a · Notes, created in batch 2.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark\n 6. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark\nThen stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2:\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark\n 3. 00a · Notes (create it with the \"Board\" entries from the setup message and the 01 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): The only way the product says how sure it is about a fact: three shapes, one meaning each, used everywhere.\nUSED IN (print): x-provenance-sheet, x-date-sheet, x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, f1-today-tab, f3-household-calendar, f3-household-notifications, f8-scale-strips, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-sheet, f8-og-compare-card, f8-seasonal-aha, f6-place-section-details, f10-extraction-confirm, f10-bill-provenance, f10-bill-trend, f10-mail-day-triage, f11-keeper-strip, f1-claim-receipt.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: each silhouette at L 56pt with callouts, then all sizes in a row)\n- OFFICIAL: a solid disc. The diameter equals the size.\n- UNCONFIRMED: a ring with the same outer diameter and a transparent centre. Stroke width: XS 12 → 1.5px, S 16 → 2px, M 24 → 3px, L 56 → 7px. Never thinner than 1.5px.\n- YOU ADDED: a solid disc with a tick KNOCKED OUT of it. The tick is a true cut-out that shows the surface behind, not a second colour painted on top. The tick spans the middle 56% of the diameter. Its stroke width equals the ring stroke for that size (XS 1.5, S 2, M 3, L 7), with round caps and joins. This drawing survives one-colour tinting.\n- Ink: text.secondary (4.83:1 on base) or darker in light mode; dark text.secondary in dark mode. Add a crossed-out swatch row labelled \"never border.* · never text.muted\" (border.default is 1.24:1, text.muted is 2.54:1).\n- Sizes, each with its use printed:\n  XS 12pt / 12dp / 12px: the smallest size at which the three shapes can still be told apart (strip cells, widget, tray previews).\n  S 16pt: list rows and captions.\n  M 24pt: the sheet legend.\n  L 56pt: the provenance sheet header.\n  OG 28px at 1200 wide: the share-card minimum.\n- Below 12pt, no mark is drawn. Show a row labelled \"10pt → no mark\" that prints the words instead: \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\".\n- Spacing: 8pt (spacing.2) between the mark and its text, shown with a dimension line.\n- LEGEND specimen (at M 24pt, stacked): [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\". Where a legend is written \"● Official · ○ … · ✓ …\", those characters stand for the drawn marks: always render the vector mark, never a font character.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy, light and dark)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83:1 on base · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96:1 on dark base, 5.71:1 on dark raised · stale: text.primary #111827 at 50% (the B7 50% figures) · dark stale: dark text.primary #E5E7EB at 50% (B7) · tinted widget: primary.700 #0369a1 on surface.base 5.93:1 (light) and primary.500 #0ea5e9 on dark surface.raised 5.28:1 (dark), never dimmed (at 50% they drop to 2.24:1 and 2.36:1) · never: primary.500 on surface.base 2.77:1, border.default 1.24:1, text.muted 2.54:1, text.secondary at 50% 1.98:1.\n01-anatomy · dark carries the three silhouettes, the size row, the legend and this table in dark tokens only. It has no text blocks.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 6 rows × 5 columns; each cell is a 358-wide row at S 16pt on surface.base unless a column rule says otherwise)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (dimmed + age words) → stale · inside tap target → in-target · tinted/accented widget rendering (silhouette only) → tinted-widget · greyscale → greyscale.\nRows (label → key), used in every column unless a column rule says otherwise:\n R1 official (filled) → official: \"Flood zone\" / \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\", caption \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n R2 unconfirmed (hollow) → unconfirmed: \"Pickup day\" / \"Thursday\", caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" (Place B).\n R3 you-added (filled + knocked-out tick) → you-added: \"Warranty ends\" / \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\", caption \"You added this\" (Home A).\n R4 read-from-your-photo → read-from-photo: a machine read before the user commits it, drawn with the UNCONFIRMED ring. Row \"Clark Public Utilities\" / \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". Under the uncertain value only (the due date), add the flag line \"We weren't sure — check this\" in caption 12/16 text.strong with a 12pt text.strong pencil glyph (not a circle). Beside the cell, draw a small arrow to a copy of the row after commit, where the mark becomes YOU ADDED, labelled \"on commit → you-added\".\n R5 stale → stale: the fact's own provenance shape (the official disc for air) in text.primary at 50% (3.39:1). Row \"Air quality\" / \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17), with the words \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\" in caption text.secondary.\n R6 reported → reported: shape unchanged (the unconfirmed ring for the Place B pickup row), plus a status line under the row, \"You reported this · checking\", in caption 12/16 text.secondary with no glyph.\nColumn rules:\n - default: as above.\n - stale: dim the mark to text.primary at 50% and replace the caption with that row's own stale caption. The dimming is never the only cue: the age words always appear. Per row:\n   R1: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   R2: dimmed ring, caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\".\n   R3: Does not apply — your own entry does not age.\n   R4: Does not apply — a pre-commit read is not refreshed.\n   R5: print \"same as stale variant\" (R5 is already stale) and draw the R5 row.\n   R6: dimmed ring, the R2 stale caption, and the \"You reported this · checking\" line under it.\n - in-target: draw the whole row at a 44pt minimum height (iOS), with the dashed target (B13) around the row and a \"not a target\" label on the mark. Add \"48dp on Android · 44px on web\".\n - tinted-widget: draw the row at XS 12pt inside a 158×158 widget crop rendered in one accent hue. Light cell: widget background surface.base, tint primary.700, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.93:1\" (never primary.500: 2.77:1). All silhouettes are one colour; the YOU ADDED tick stays a cut-out showing the widget background. Print the word next to every mark (a widget is a standalone surface).\n   R5 tinted-widget: no dimming under tinted rendering. Draw the full-strength tint (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and let the age words \"— 11 hours ago\" carry the stale state. Label it \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\".\n - greyscale: the default cell at 0% saturation, labelled \"shape carries the meaning\".\nDark twin: the same 30 cells in dark tokens. The tinted column uses widget background dark surface.raised with tint primary.500, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.28:1\". Its R5 cell follows the same no-dimming rule.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1, R2 and R3 stacked. The mark scales with Dynamic Type relative to the caption style, capped at 32pt. The row text wraps, and the mark top-aligns to the first line. The legend becomes one entry per line.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same three rows with sp scaling, mark capped at 32dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same, with the SVG sized in em.\n- XS legibility strip: the three marks at XS 12pt on surface.base, surface.sunken, dark surface.base and dark surface.raised, plus both tinted-widget backgrounds from the grid, labelled \"must be told apart at 12pt\".\n- GREYSCALE (this component overrides B10): do not redraw the grid. Print \"Greyscale: see the greyscale column on 02-variants-states — every cell reads yes — shape\". Draw one deliberate FAIL example labelled \"WRONG\": two discs that differ only in hue, with the fix label \"fix: shape, not colour\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: the three marks in text.strong, labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\".\nDark twin (03 · dark): the AX5 and 200% frames in dark tokens, the XS strip, and the three marks in dark text.strong labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\". It leaves out the web zoom frame and the greyscale pointer, because greyscale does not depend on theme.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Spoken names are fixed: \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\", \"you added this\". The name is appended to the row's merged label:\n  \"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, FEMA, official\"\n  \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\"\n  \"Warranty ends, water heater, in 54 days, Saturday 12 December, you added this\"\n- Non-colour encoding: the shape; colour never tells the marks apart.\n- Target rule: the mark is never a tap target on its own. The enclosing row or cell is the target (B13).\n- Contrast: at least 3:1 in both themes, including the tinted widget. Scales with Dynamic Type or sp up to AX5 / 200%.\n- Each surface shows a legend or a first-occurrence word once.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Legend strings, exactly: \"Official\" · \"On record, not confirmed\" · \"You added this\".\n- Print the word next to the mark once per surface. On standalone surfaces (widget, OG card, push landing), print it next to every mark.\n- In a push, the caveat goes at the front of the title: \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\".\n- Glossary: never \"verified\", \"confirmed\" or \"trusted\" for official data; never \"unverified\", \"estimated\", \"guessed\", \"pending\" or \"probable\" for the hollow mark; never \"user-entered\", \"self-reported\" or \"manual\" for the tick.\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- iOS widgets: the mark is widgetAccentable, and the tick stays knocked out under accented rendering.\n- Android widgets: fixed ink (text.secondary / dark text.secondary), not a Material dynamic colour role.\n- Web: inline SVG with role=\"img\" and an aria-label holding the spoken name.\n- OG card: at least 28px at 1200 wide.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three 390-wide crops; the dark twin has the same three crops)\n a) x-place-file, Place B. A legend strip at the top (\"Official · On record, not confirmed · You added this\" with drawn M-size marks), then these rows: \"Flood zone · Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" (official); \"Radon zone · Zone 1 — highest potential\" (official, caption \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"); \"Pickup day · Thursday\" (unconfirmed); \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" (no mark, because nothing is on record).\n b) f5-today-calendar-strip, Home A. At the top of the crop, above the strip, a legend line: [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\", with the marks at S 16pt, labelled \"legend once per surface\". Then a 14-cell FourteenDayStrip from Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov, with marks at XS 12pt in one ink colour. Draw every fixture date in the window:\n   Tue 20 Oct: unconfirmed ring (recycling and garbage, city schedule).\n   Fri 23 Oct: you-added mark (Clark Public Utilities bill).\n   Mon 26 Oct: voter registration, a statewide rule, drawn as a full-height bar spanning the cell with no mark. Label it \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\".\n   Tue 27 Oct: unconfirmed ring (garbage only).\n   Wed 28 Oct: you-added mark (City of Vancouver water bill).\n   Sun 1 Nov: you-added mark (HOA dues).\n   All other cells are empty. Beside the strip print \"at most 3 marks per cell, then +N\".\n  Under the strip, draw the matching rows at S 16pt, each with its mark:\n   \"Recycling and garbage\" / \"Tomorrow\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\" / \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" / \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (official)\n   \"Garbage only\" / \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00\" / \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"HOA dues · $285\" / \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" (you added)\n  Label: \"the strip is one element; rows are the targets\".\n c) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\". Marks at XS 12pt, each with its word printed beside it, for example \"On record, not confirmed\" next to \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Instead of filled vs hollow for any other meaning (sender vs you in compare, taken vs open founding slots, density), draw labelled pointers, or solid vs hatched segments plus a numeral — because filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage, bar or star, draw one of the three marks plus its word — because the product never grades certainty.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on an official public dataset (EPA radon zone, USFS wildfire hazard), draw the filled mark and put the limit in the caption's scope word (\"county-wide estimate\") — because hollow means \"not confirmed\", not \"coarse\".\n- Instead of a tick painted in a second colour on top of the disc, knock the tick out — because a second colour disappears under one-colour widget tinting.\n- Instead of a light tinted widget in primary.500, use primary.700 on surface.base — because primary.500 is 2.77:1 on white and marks need 3:1.\n- Instead of dimming a tinted widget mark for stale, keep the full tint and add the age words — because a dimmed tint drops below 3:1.\n- Instead of making an 8px dot the tap target, make the enclosing row or cell the target — because a small mark cannot be hit reliably.\n- Instead of a bare \"Unverified\" suffix on every row, show the word once per surface in a legend — because repetition is noise and \"unverified\" is forbidden.\n- Instead of text.secondary at 50% for stale, use text.primary at 50% — because the first drops to 1.98:1.\n- Instead of one age suffix on every row, give each fact its own stale caption — because an effective date or your own entry does not age.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: official · unconfirmed · you-added · read-from-photo · stale · reported. States: default · stale · in-target · tinted-widget · greyscale.\n<size|platform> is the size the cell is drawn at (XS, S, M, L, OG); tinted-widget cells are XS. Examples: \"ProvenanceMark / official / default / S / light\" · \"ProvenanceMark / you-added / tinted-widget / XS / dark\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"01 ProvenanceMark\")\n 01.A1 Stale ink is text.primary at 50% (3.39:1 on base), not a plain \"50% opacity\", because text.secondary at 50% is 1.98:1 and marks need 3:1.\n 01.A2 Stale captions are per row, not one shared suffix. The pickup schedule reads \"as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\". The official effective-date row, your own entry and a pre-commit photo read \"does not apply\", because they do not age.\n 01.A3 The tinted widget is never dimmed for stale. The full tint stays (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and the age words carry the state, because a 50% tint drops to 2.24:1 (light) and 2.36:1 (dark).\n 01.A4 Tinted-widget stand-in: primary.700 on surface.base in light (5.93:1) and primary.500 on dark surface.raised in dark (5.28:1). primary.500 on white is 2.77:1, so it is not used in light mode.\n 01.A5 The ring and tick stroke widths per size (1.5 / 2 / 3 / 7) and the 56% tick span are this board's geometry. The source spec sets only the 1.5px minimum.\n 01.A6 The spoken example \"Trash day Tuesday, City of Camas, …\" became \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\", following the glossary (\"Pickup day\") and the Place B fixture.\n 01.A7 In the calendar-strip crop, Mon 26 Oct voter registration is FourteenDayStrip's full-height civic bar (a civic, state or county rule is a full-height bar spanning the cell), not a mark. Its row uses the \"must arrive by\" wording.\n 01.A8 The calendar-strip crop prints the legend once above the strip, so that surface shows each mark's word once (invariant 1).\n 01.B1 \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" · \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\" · \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" · \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\" · \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\".\n 01.B2 The six calendar-strip rows under crop b, each quoted exactly as written there.\n 01.B3 Annotations: \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\" · \"legend once per surface\" · \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\" · \"on commit → you-added\".\n 01.B4 The flood-zone and warranty spoken labels from ACCESSIBILITY.\n 01.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 01.E Every ProvenanceMark name, by the grammar and keys above.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 8 artboards and 00a · Notes (Board and 01 entries) exist with exact names.\n- Both 02 grids have 6 × 5 cells with printed keys; \"Does not apply\" cells print their reasons; the stale column uses each row's own caption; both R5 tinted cells are at full tint.\n- No mark is under 12pt, no ring stroke under 1.5px, and the tick is a cut-out everywhere, including both tinted cells (each printing its background, tint and ratio).\n- Crops a and b print the legend once; the widget crop prints the word beside every mark.\n- The strip is named \"FourteenDayStrip\" and nothing else. No mark is a target on its own."
          },
          {
            "id": "00a-02",
            "component": "SourceCaption",
            "artboards": [
              "00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light",
              "00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light",
              "00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light",
              "00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark",
              "00a · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00a-02: SourceCaption. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nSourceCaption embeds the ProvenanceMark you drew in 00a-01. Reuse those marks exactly, including the stale ink and stroke rule.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light: the caption pattern with callouts, base vs sunken ink, the wrap example, link vs no link, the OG strip, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light: the 7 × 3 grid\n3. 00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light: f8-scale-strips, f1-today-air-band (default and alert, no track), and the f8-compare-arrival-header frozen row\n4. 00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light: AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark: the same 21 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\nWIDTH: both 02-variants-states artboards are 1600 px wide (an exception to B1; Notes 02.A4). All other artboards are 1440.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 02 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): Puts the minimum provenance on the value itself: who says it, what it covers, and when.\nUnder the purpose, print this rationale line in body 16/24 text.secondary (a top-block addition, Notes 02.A3): \"Almost nobody opens the provenance sheet, so the caption carries the caveat.\"\nUSED IN (print): f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f1-today-air-band, f8-seasonal-aha, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-og-compare-card, f8-compare-sheet, x-provenance-sheet, x-place-file, f4-today-pickup-card, f5-today-calendar-strip, f3-household-calendar, f10-bill-trend.\n\nLINK RULE (applies to every cell, crop and frame)\nA caption is a link only when its source has a URL. A link caption shows all three of these: the authority word in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)) with an underline; the trailing external-link glyph in the same colour; and the dashed target (B13) around the caption line. A caption with no URL is all text.secondary (text.strong on sunken), with no underline, no glyph and no target.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: callouts on a 358-wide specimen, \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\", with a URL, so it shows the link form. Callout numbers are the square badges from B4.)\n- [1] ProvenanceMark at S 16pt, leading, top-aligned to the first line, with an 8pt gap.\n- [2] Authority, [3] \" · \" separator, [4] scope word, [5] \" · \", [6] as-of. All in caption 12/16/400.\n- Ink: text.secondary on base, raised or app surfaces; text.strong on sunken. Draw two copies side by side, one on base and one on sunken, each labelled with its tokens and ratios.\n- The caption wraps to two lines at default size and never cuts the authority short with an ellipsis. Draw a 240-wide wrap example: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\n- [7] The optional trailing external-link glyph (12pt, an arrow out of a square, not a circle), shown only when a source URL exists (LINK RULE).\n- Beside the specimen, draw the same caption without a URL, labelled \"no URL: flat, not a target\", so link and no-link sit side by side.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.secondary #6B7280: 4.83 on base / 4.63 raised / 4.51 app / 4.39 sunken (below 4.5, so text on sunken is text.strong) · text.strong #374151: 9.37 on sunken, 10.31 on base · primary.700 #0369a1: 5.93 on base / 5.68 raised / 5.54 app / 5.39 sunken · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8: 8.33 on dark base / 6.83 dark raised · dark text.secondary #94A3B8: 6.96 on dark base / 5.71 dark raised · dark text.strong #F1F5F9: 16.30 on dark base · mark ink: as in the ProvenanceMark table (at least 3:1; stale text.primary at 50%: 3.39 on base, dark 4.45 on dark base).\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 7 rows × 3 columns)\nLayout: 48 px side margins, a 238 px row-label column, 32 px gutters, and three 390-wide columns (48 + 238 + 3 × (32 + 390) + 48 = 1600). Each cell is a 390-wide surface.base card (358 content + 16 px padding each side) showing the value line in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary above the caption. R5 content is 320 wide (a 352-wide card), left-aligned in its column.\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (the as-of age appended) → stale · offline (\"as of\" date) → offline.\nEach row states its mark and whether it has a URL. Apply the LINK RULE in every cell of the row. Offline rule (Notes 02.A7): captions with an effective date, a frozen date or a stated as-of do not change offline; only live captions switch to \"as of <time>\".\n R1 dated static → dated-static. Mark: official. URL: none. Value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n   default: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n   stale: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   offline: unchanged. Draw the default caption and label it \"static captions do not change offline\".\n R2 live → live. Mark: official. URL: yes (AirNow). Value \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17).\n   default: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today\".\n   stale: dimmed mark, \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\" (the same string as ProvenanceMark R5).\n   offline: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\". The link form stays, because the URL still exists.\n R3 frozen token (a compare card's saved reading) → frozen. Mark: official. URL: none. Value \"AQI 42 · Good\".\n   default: \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n   stale: Does not apply — a frozen reading is dated, never \"ago\".\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\n R4 county scope → county. Mark: official (the limit goes in the scope word, never a hollow mark). URL: yes (EPA). Value \"Zone 1 — highest potential\". This caption has no as-of (Notes 02.A9).\n   default: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\n   stale: Does not apply — a county zone does not age.\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\n R5 collapsed sources line, only at 320–360 wide → collapsed. URL: none on the sources line. Draw it in the 320-wide content under these four value rows, each with the official mark at S 16pt:\n   \"Flood · Zone X — minimal flood hazard\"\n   \"Wildfire · Moderate · 3 of 5\"\n   \"Air · AQI 42 · Good\" (with its own time on the row: \"observed 7:00 AM today\")\n   \"Radon · Zone 1 — highest potential\"\n  The sources line itself has no mark.\n   default: \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\".\n   stale: the sources line is unchanged; only the air row dims its mark and appends \"— 11 hours ago\".\n   offline: the sources line is unchanged; the air row reads \"as of 7:00 AM\".\n R6 no URL, a flat caption that is not tappable → no-url. Mark: unconfirmed (the Place B pickup schedule, as in ProvenanceMark R2). URL: none. Value \"Thursday\".\n   default: \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\", with no glyph and no underline, labelled \"not a target\".\n   stale: the dimmed ring (text.primary at 50%, as in ProvenanceMark) and \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\", flat, no link, labelled \"not a target\". This matches ProvenanceMark R2 stale.\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\n R7 dated static, with URL → dated-static-link. Mark: official. URL: yes (FEMA). Value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\". It exists so the difference between R1 and R6 is visible.\n   default: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\" in the link form.\n   stale: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   offline: unchanged; label it as in R1.\nThat leaves 4 \"Does not apply\" cells per grid (R1, R3, R4 and R7 stale) and 17 drawn cells.\nDark twin: all 21 cells in dark tokens, same 1600 px layout. Stale ink is dark text.primary at 50%.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R2 and R4 at caption 40pt with the mark at 32pt (stroke 4px), wrapping to as many lines as needed and never ending in an ellipsis. Both are links, so both keep the underline, the glyph (scaled to 24pt) and a target that grows with the text.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same at 24sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): all 21 cells; the 4 \"Does not apply\" cells repeat their reasons. Drawn link cells (R2 and R4 default and offline, R7 default and offline, R2 stale): \"Reads without colour: yes — underline + glyph\". All other drawn cells, including R6 stale: \"Reads without colour: yes — words; the mark's shape\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R2 default with the non-link caption text in text.strong. The authority link stays primary.700 with its underline and glyph.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Contrast is at least 4.5:1 (see the table).\n- The caption is read after the value in the row's merged label: \"Air quality, AQI 42, Good, AirNow, nearest monitors, observed 7:00 AM today, official\".\n- When a URL exists, the row exposes the link as a custom action named \"Open <authority>\" (for example \"Open AirNow\"). On web, the link is a separate focusable link after the row.\n- The non-colour cue for a link is the underline plus the external-link glyph.\n- Target rule: a caption is a target (B13) only when a URL exists. A caption with no URL is never a target.\n- There is no hover-only content.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Always authority · scope · as-of (as-of where the source has one).\n- Use the authority's own word, \"hazard\" or \"potential\"; never \"risk\" unless the source says risk.\n- Deadlines received by a date say \"must arrive by\" (\"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\").\n- Never write \"Sources:\" at widths above 360 (except the OG image).\n- Never write \"provider\", \"feed\" or \"partner\" for the source.\n- Never label a frozen reading \"today\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Same on iOS, Android and web.\n- On the OG image, the caption is at least 28px and may be merged into one sources line; the full captions go in og:description. Draw a 1200-wide strip crop showing \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" at 28px on surface.base in text.secondary, with no mark and no link, labelled \"OG sources strip · 28px\". This strip is a published specimen.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three 390-wide crops)\n a) f8-scale-strips, Place B: the flood row. Draw the value line \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" and the R1 caption (official mark, no URL) only. Where the strip would sit, between the value and the caption, draw a 1 px text.secondary placeholder box labelled \"track omitted: ScaleStrip\".\n b) f1-today-air-band, Place B: \"AQI 42 · Good\" with the R2 caption (official, link form). Beside it, draw an alert-variant copy: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" with \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM today\" (official, link form). Both show the value line and caption only; label them \"track omitted: AqiBand\" (B17).\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, Friend C: a \"Dana · Camas, WA\" card with the row \"Air on Sat 12 Sep · AQI 42 · Good\" and the R3 caption \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" (official, no URL).\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of hiding the source behind a tooltip or \"learn more\", print authority · scope · as-of on the value — because almost nobody opens the sheet.\n- Instead of labelling a frozen reading \"today\", write \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" — because a shared card is read days later.\n- Instead of making a caption with no URL tappable, draw it flat — because a target that goes nowhere breaks trust.\n- Instead of \"Sources:\" on wide layouts, give every row its own caption — because the collapsed line exists only for 320–360 widths (except the OG image).\n- Instead of cutting a long authority short with an ellipsis, wrap to a second line — because the authority is the caveat.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on a county-wide official estimate, use the filled mark and the scope word — because hollow means \"not confirmed\".\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: dated-static · dated-static-link · live · frozen · county · collapsed · no-url. States: default · stale · offline. <size|platform> is \"any\" for grid cells. Example: \"SourceCaption / live / stale / any / light\".\nAlso publish the OG strip: \"SourceCaption / collapsed / default / OG / light\".\nTotal: 35 names (17 drawn cells per theme, plus the OG strip).\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"02 SourceCaption\")\n 02.A1 Source example strings were re-dated to the house-style fixtures (TODAY Mon 19 Oct 2026) and the weekday date format: \"effective Sep 24, 2021\" → \"effective Sep 2021\"; \"observed 3:10 PM today\" → \"observed 7:00 AM today\"; \"on Sep 12, 2026\" → \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\"; \"— 9 hours ago\" → \"— 11 hours ago\"; \"as of Sep 15\" → \"as of 7:00 AM\".\n 02.A2 SourceCaption adds a dated-static-link key (row R7) for the with-URL form, so the link form can be published separately from the no-URL form.\n 02.A3 The top block carries a second line, a rationale, under the purpose.\n 02.A4 Both 02-variants-states artboards are 1600 px wide (an exception to B1): 48 px side margins, a 238 px row-label column, 32 px gutters and three 390-wide cards (358 content + 16 px padding). R5 content is 320 wide (a 352-wide card), left-aligned in its column.\n 02.A5 URL and mark per row: R2 live (AirNow), R4 county (EPA) and R7 dated-static-link (FEMA) have URLs; R1, R3, R5 and R6 do not. R1–R5 and R7 carry the official mark; R6 carries the unconfirmed mark. R5's marks sit on its four value rows, and the sources line has none.\n 02.A6 The OG sources strip is published as \"SourceCaption / collapsed / default / OG / light\", using the board's uppercase size code.\n 02.A7 Captions with an effective date, a frozen date or a stated as-of do not change offline; only live captions switch to \"as of <time>\". The contract's offline state (\"as of <date>\") therefore applies to live captions only.\n 02.A8 When a URL exists, the row exposes the link to assistive tech as a custom action \"Open <authority>\"; on web it is a separate focusable link after the row.\n 02.A9 The county caption has no as-of: a county zone map is undated, so the contract string is used as-is. The printed copy rule reads \"as-of where the source has one\".\n 02.A10 The Place B pickup caption has a stale form (\"— 9 days ago\"), matching ProvenanceMark R2 and 01.A2, so later surfaces get one answer.\n 02.B1 \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\" · \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM today\" · \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" · \"Air on Sat 12 Sep · AQI 42 · Good\" · \"Flood · Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · \"Wildfire · Moderate · 3 of 5\" · \"Air · AQI 42 · Good\" · \"Radon · Zone 1 — highest potential\" · \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" · \"Open AirNow\" · \"track omitted: AqiBand\" · \"track omitted: ScaleStrip\" · \"static captions do not change offline\" · \"dated static, with URL\" · \"no URL: flat, not a target\" · \"OG sources strip · 28px\" · \"Reads without colour: yes — underline + glyph\" · \"Reads without colour: yes — words; the mark's shape\". \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\", its \"— 9 days ago\" form and \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\" are already listed under 01; \"not a target\" is listed under 00.\n 02.B2 Spoken label: \"Air quality, AQI 42, Good, AirNow, nearest monitors, observed 7:00 AM today, official\".\n 02.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 02.E All 35 SourceCaption names: one per drawn grid cell (17 light, 17 dark), plus the OG strip.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names, and both 02 artboards are 1600 px wide with the stated margins, label column and gutters. Notes has the 02 entries, with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have 7 rows × 3 columns with printed keys; exactly 4 cells per grid (R1, R3, R4, R7 stale) are \"Does not apply\" and print their reasons.\n- Every cell carries the mark its row names. R6 uses the unconfirmed ring, and its stale cell shows the dimmed ring with \"— 9 days ago\", flat. No R5 sources line has a mark.\n- R2, R4 and R7 cells show the underline, the glyph and the dashed target. No other cell or crop without a URL shows any of the three.\n- Text on sunken is text.strong. No authority is cut short with an ellipsis. \"Sources:\" appears only in the 320-wide R5 cells and on the OG strip.\n- No frozen reading says \"today\". No air or scale crop draws a track or an EPA hue; each shows its \"track omitted\" label instead.\n- 02.E lists exactly 35 names."
