            "promptText": "Component 00a-04: FreshnessLine. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · FreshnessLine · 01-anatomy · light (1440 wide): placement, glyphs, the system hairline (running, stopped at 5s, Reduce Motion), the Retry target, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · light (2400 wide): the 6 × 5 grid, then the no-reflow strip below it\n3. 00a · FreshnessLine · 04-in-context · light (1440 wide): f1-today-tab, f7-today-widget past horizon, f3-bills-list header\n4. 00a · FreshnessLine · 03-scaling-greyscale · light (2400 wide): AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · dark (2400 wide): the same 30 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · FreshnessLine · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · FreshnessLine · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · FreshnessLine · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 04 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One persistent line that states how old the content is: refresh, stale and offline all go here instead of a toast.\nUSED IN (print): f1-today-tab, f7-widget-tap-landing, f7-today-widget, f1-today-air-band, x-place-file, f9-invite-rewards-card, f9-nearby-cells-map, f11-keeper-strip, f10-bill-trend, f3-bills-list, f3-members-roster, f1-your-places.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on a 358-wide card header, \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with the \"Saved place · Only you\" ScopeChip, and the line under it)\n- ① Placement: directly under the location row or card header, 4pt / 4dp / 4px (spacing.1) below it.\n- ② Caption 12/16/400 in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken).\n- ③ Optional leading 16pt / 16dp / 16px glyph, in text.secondary with an 8 gap: offline (a cloud with a slash) or retry (a circular arrow drawn as an open arc with an arrowhead, not a closed ring).\n- ④ Optional 2pt / 2dp / 2px indeterminate hairline under the header, full card width, in primary.700 (5.93:1 on base; at least 3:1 on its surface). It is each platform's own system indeterminate progress indicator (iOS linear ProgressView, Android Material 3 LinearProgressIndicator, web an indeterminate progress bar), tinted primary.700, with no custom duration or easing. It runs only if the refresh takes 1s or longer. This is the only motion on the board (the B15 exemption; see 04.A1). Draw three poses side by side:\n   running: a short segment partway along the track, with the note \"system indeterminate progress indicator · no custom duration · exempt from the 300ms rule, stopped within 5s (see Notes)\".\n   after 5s (the end pose): the hairline stops and is removed. \"Updating…\" stays in the line until the result arrives; then the line becomes \"Updated just now\" or the failed line (R3). Label it \"idle loops stop within 5s\".\n   Reduce Motion: no hairline at all; the word \"Updating…\" carries the state.\n- ⑤ \"Retry\" is an inline text button in label 13/18/600 primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), with its target (B13) drawn dashed.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83 on base · text.strong #374151 9.37 on sunken · primary.700 #0369a1 5.93 on base · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 6.83 on dark raised.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 6 rows × 5 columns)\nGeometry: a 160-wide row-label column and a 12 gutter, then five 390-wide columns with 12 gutters: 160 + 12 + 5 × 390 + 4 × 12 = 2170 wide, on the 2400-wide artboard. Each drawn cell is the full 390-wide B3 card (the 358-wide header plus line, with 16 padding) at 100% scale; nothing is scaled. Does-not-apply cells are 390 wide too. Cells grow in height to fit.\nColumns (label → key): fresh → fresh · refreshing → refreshing · stale → stale · failed → failed · offline → offline.\nEach variant exists in exactly one state (see 04.A6). Draw that one cell as described, and fill the row's other four cells with the reason given for that row (B12).\n R1 \"Updating…\" → updating → refreshing. Stack two sub-cells vertically in the one cell: \"under 1s: no hairline\" above \"1s or longer: hairline\". The other four cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only while refreshing\".\n R2 \"Updated just now\" / \"Updated 12m ago\" / \"Updated 2h ago\" (the system relative date) → updated → fresh. Stack all three strings as specimen text in the one cell. The refreshing, failed and offline cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only while fresh\". The stale cell: \"Does not apply — stale is stated per fact (R5)\".\n R3 \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\" → failed → failed, with the retry glyph and the Retry target. The other four cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only after a refresh fails\".\n R4 \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" → offline → offline, with the offline glyph. The other four cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only while offline\".\n R5 per-fact stale → fact-stale → stale: the card shows the header (\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with its ScopeChip) with no freshness line under it, then the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" with the R5 line \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\" under it. Show the air row's value line only: no AQI track and no EPA hue (B17); label the cell \"track omitted: AqiBand\". The rest of the card stays undimmed. The other four cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only while one fact is stale\".\n R6 widget past horizon → widget-horizon → stale: \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\", in a 338×158 widget crop (its card is 370 wide, inside the 390 column). The widget shows the label \"Larkspur Loop\", then two rows, \"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" and \"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\", with no provenance marks, then the R6 line. The time is today's, so no weekday is shown. The other four cells: \"Does not apply — this line appears only while the widget is past its refresh horizon\".\nBELOW the grid, draw a \"what does not change\" strip: the same 358-wide card at 100% in the fresh and refreshing states, side by side, with identical layout, labelled \"no dim, no skeleton, no reflow while refreshing\".\nDark twin: all 30 cells in dark tokens, same geometry, on its 2400-wide artboard.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale, 2400 wide)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R3 and R4 at caption 40pt. The line wraps, and \"Retry\" moves to its own line as a full-width text button with its label at 44pt and a hit area at least 44pt tall that grows with the text. The glyph scales to 32pt.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same at 24sp, with the label at 26sp and a hit area at least 48dp tall that grows with the text.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10, scope changed): the light grid again at 100% scale, not 50%, fully desaturated, in the same 2170-wide geometry, so the 12/16 lines stay legible. Every drawn cell reads \"yes — words state the state\"; Does-not-apply cells get no verdict.\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R3 and R4 with the line and glyph in text.strong; Retry stays primary.700.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Changes are announced in a polite live region, never an assertive one (iOS: an accessibility announcement queued behind current speech (default or low priority); Android: accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"; web: aria-live=\"polite\").\n- Non-colour: stale is stated in words.\n- Target rule: Retry is a target (B13).\n- Ageing text is announced once, not every minute.\n- Spoken example: \"You're offline, as of 7:04 AM\".\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Relative time for recency (\"Updated 12m ago\"). \"As of\" plus an absolute time for offline or frozen data (\"as of 7:04 AM\"); add the weekday only when the time is not today.\n- Never \"Last synced\", \"refreshed at\" or \"last seen\".\n- Never a disappearing toast as the only proof.\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy)\n- iOS widgets use the system Text(date, style: .relative).\n- Android widgets use the equivalent system relative-time text.\n- The hairline is each platform's system indeterminate progress indicator.\n- Web: a polite live region.\n- Same wording everywhere.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops at 100%, each labelled with surface id, platform, width and fixture)\n a) f1-today-tab, Place B, web 390: the location row, the ScopeChip, \"Updated 12m ago\", then the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only; label it \"track omitted: AqiBand\") with R5 beneath it. Label R5 \"shown only when the air reading is stale\".\n b) f7-today-widget, Home A, iOS 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\", with the same two rows as R6 and the R6 line. The rest of the widget stays at full ink; only the stated line changes.\n c) f3-bills-list, Home A, web 390: the header \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" with the \"Your household\" ScopeChip beside it (wrapping under it if narrow), and \"Updated just now\" under the header.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of dimming, skeletoning or reflowing a warm screen while refreshing, keep it and show \"Updating…\" (and the hairline after 1s) — because stale content is still useful.\n- Instead of a hairline that loops until the request ends, stop it at 5s and leave \"Updating…\" — because idle loops stop within 5s.\n- Instead of a custom animated hairline, use the platform's system indeterminate indicator — because a custom loop is a motion spec nobody needs to maintain.\n- Instead of greying a whole widget when only AQI is old, put the age words on the air line — because the other facts are still current.\n- Instead of a toast, use this line — because toasts vanish before people read them.\n- Instead of \"Last synced\", write \"Updated\" or \"As of\" — because \"synced\" is jargon.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: updating · updated · failed · offline · fact-stale · widget-horizon. States: fresh · refreshing · stale · failed · offline. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"FreshnessLine / updating / refreshing / any / light\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"04 FreshnessLine\")\n 04.A1 The hairline is the platform's system indeterminate progress indicator, with no custom duration. It is exempt from the house style's 300ms motion limit because it is a progress indicator, not a transition. Instead it is capped at 5s, per \"idle loops stop within 5s\", after which \"Updating…\" carries the state.\n 04.A2 Source example strings were re-dated to the fixtures: \"Observed 6:00 AM · AirNow — 9 hours ago\" → \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\"; \"As of Mon 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" → \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (the time is today, so the weekday is dropped).\n 04.A3 The f3-bills-list research header \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills · 3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" is not drawn: its scope sentence is a third scope wording, against house-style invariant 2 and the ScopeChip copy rules. The crop shows \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" with the \"Your household\" ScopeChip instead ($306.17 = $142.18 + $84.00 + $79.99).\n 04.A4 Date-rule exception (B16): \"through Mon 2 Nov\" is a range end, not a date row, so it has no relative count (\"through in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" reads badly).\n 04.A5 Both 02 grids and the 03 greyscale grid are drawn at 100% on 2400-wide artboards (160 + 12 + 5 × 390 + 4 × 12 = 2170 wide), not at 1440 and not at the B10 50%, so the 12/16 lines stay at type-scale size and the greyscale verdicts can be checked. The 01 and 04 artboards stay 1440; the no-reflow strip and in-context crops are at 100%.\n 04.A6 Each FreshnessLine variant is the line for exactly one state (updating → refreshing, updated → fresh, failed → failed, offline → offline, fact-stale and widget-horizon → stale); the other cells do not apply. The source lists variants and states independently, so this mapping is a reading of it.\n 04.B1 \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (re-dated source string) · \"idle loops stop within 5s\" · \"system indeterminate progress indicator · no custom duration · exempt from the 300ms rule, stopped within 5s (see Notes)\" · \"what does not change\" · \"no dim, no skeleton, no reflow while refreshing\" · \"under 1s: no hairline\" · \"1s or longer: hairline\" · \"track omitted: AqiBand\" · \"shown only when the air reading is stale\" · \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" · the widget rows \"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" and \"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · the six row reasons (\"Does not apply — this line appears only while refreshing\" · \"… only while fresh\" · \"Does not apply — stale is stated per fact (R5)\" · \"… only after a refresh fails\" · \"… only while offline\" · \"… only while one fact is stale\" · \"… only while the widget is past its refresh horizon\").\n 04.B2 Sourced, adapted: \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" (f3-bills-list research, scope sentence replaced by the chip; see 04.A3).\n 04.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 04.D Keep the sourced sentence \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\" on f3-bills-list, or replace it with the \"Your household\" chip as drawn? (04.A3)\n 04.E Every FreshnessLine name (one per variant, in its one state).\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names and stated widths, and Notes has the 04 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have 6 rows × 5 columns with printed keys, are drawn at 100% (no \"shown at\" scale label anywhere), fit the 2400 artboard, and each row has one drawn cell and four \"Does not apply\" cells, each with its row's reason.\n- The greyscale grid on 03 is at 100% with a verdict beside every drawn cell.\n- The \"what does not change\" strip sits below the grid.\n- The R5 cell shows the header with no freshness line, then the air row with the R5 line under it.\n- The hairline is drawn as the system indicator in three poses (running, stopped after 5s, Reduce Motion), with no custom duration anywhere.\n- No refreshing frame dims, skeletons or reflows the card, and no widget is greyed as a whole.\n- Retry has a dashed target; no string says \"Last synced\", \"refreshed at\" or \"last seen\".\n- Each in-context crop is labelled with its surface id, platform, width and fixture.\n- Scope is stated only by the ScopeChip; no crop prints \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\"."
          },
