            "promptText": "Component 00a-05: OfflineNotice. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nOfflineNotice embeds the FreshnessLine you drew in 00a-04. Reuse its offline line exactly.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, exact names)\n1. 00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light (1440 wide): the offline line and what-still-works sentence, a disabled control with its reason, plain vs sunken, the focusable disabled control, ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF\n2. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light (2000 wide): the 3 × 3 grid\n3. 00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light (1440 wide): f8-native-share-compare, f1-add-place-sheet, f10-snap-capture-tray\n4. 00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light (2000 wide): AX5, 200%, web zoom, the greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n5. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark (2000 wide): the same 9 cells in dark tokens\nAlso: update 00a · Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nBatch 1 (this turn):\n 1. 00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · Notes (update it with the 05 entries below)\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One pattern for no connection: cached content stays readable, and actions are disabled with a stated reason.\nUSED IN (print exactly this sentence; do not list ids): every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy: callouts on a 390-wide Today crop for Place B)\n- ① FreshnessLine in its offline variant at the top: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", with the offline glyph. It is the \"You're offline.\" opener. Directly under it, 4 below, the what-still-works sentence \"You can still see everything saved here.\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary (4.83:1 on base); it does not repeat \"You're offline\".\n- ② Cached content at full ink, not dimmed: the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only: no AQI track and no EPA hue).\n- ③ A disabled control, the secondary button \"Compare with a friend\", 44pt / 48dp / 44px tall: a surface.sunken fill with a 1px text.muted outline, and its label in text.muted. The outline gives the button an edge on the base card (sunken alone is about 1.1:1). Disabled is the one allowed use of text.muted, and the label and outline are exempt from the contrast minimum.\n- ④ A reason caption directly under that control, 4 below: \"Compare needs a connection.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary (4.83:1 on base).\n- ⑤ Background: no banner colour. Either plain (on base or app) or a surface.sunken strip with text.strong. Draw both and label them \"plain\" and \"sunken strip\".\n- ⑥ The disabled control keeps a focus ring when focused (B14), which shows that it stays focusable.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE (01-anatomy)\ntext.secondary #6B7280 4.83 on base · text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37 · text.muted #9CA3AF: disabled label on sunken and disabled outline on base (disabled; exempt, no ratio) · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96 on dark base.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (02-variants-states: 3 rows × 3 columns; all 9 cells apply)\nGeometry: a 160-wide row-label column, then three columns with 24 gutters. Each cell is a B3 card holding a 390-wide crop (422 wide with padding), at 100% scale; nothing is scaled. Content width: 160 + 24 + 3 × 422 + 2 × 24 = 1498, on the 2000-wide artboard. Cells grow in height to fit.\nColumns (label → key): offline → offline · reconnecting → reconnecting · back online (the line reverts to FreshnessLine) → back-online.\n R1 read-only cached screen → cached-screen: f1-today-tab, Place B, with the air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only) and the \"Compare with a friend\" button.\n   offline: as in the anatomy, including \"You can still see everything saved here.\"\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the what-still-works sentence stays; the button is still disabled with its reason.\n   back-online: two sub-cells stacked vertically, joined by a down arrow. First (above) the line reads \"Updating…\", then (below) \"Updated just now\". The what-still-works sentence is gone, the button is enabled and the reason caption is gone.\n R2 queued writes → queued-writes: f10-snap-capture-tray, Home A, with three mail-snap thumbnails.\n   offline: the line \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", and under it the what-still-works sentence \"You can keep taking photos.\" (it does not repeat \"You're offline\"); each thumbnail has the caption \"Will upload when you're back online\".\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the sentence stays; the thumbnails keep their captions.\n   back-online: the FreshnessLine reads \"Updated just now\"; under it the live status \"Uploading 2 of 3\" replaces the sentence; the first thumbnail has lost its caption and the other two keep theirs.\n R3 form offline → form: f1-add-place-sheet, signed in. The form uses a message strip in place of the FreshnessLine: \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.strong on a surface.sunken strip directly above the address field. The disabled field has a text.muted outline and text.muted placeholder (the disabled exemption), not a border token. The sheet keeps a visible \"Close\".\n   offline: as described.\n   reconnecting: the same message, with \"Reconnecting\" as a caption under it.\n   back-online: the field is enabled and the message is gone. No FreshnessLine appears, because a form has no content age; print that note on the cell.\nDark twin: all 9 cells in dark tokens, same geometry, on its 2000-wide artboard. Disabled labels, the disabled button outline and the field outline use dark text.muted (exempt; print no ratio). The disabled button fill and the sunken strips follow B6.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale, 2000 wide)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 offline. The line and the what-still-works sentence wrap, the button goes full width, and the reason caption wraps under it at 40pt.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same, with the button at least 48dp tall.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10, scope changed): the light grid again at 100% scale, not 50%, fully desaturated, in the same 1498-wide geometry, so the captions stay legible. Every cell reads \"yes — words; disabled is stated, not only greyed\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 offline with the reason caption and the what-still-works sentence in text.strong. The disabled label and outline stay text.muted, because the reason caption carries the meaning (B11).\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Disabled controls stay focusable and read their reason:\n  iOS: \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Android: \"Compare with a friend, disabled, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Web: aria-disabled=\"true\" (not the disabled attribute), with aria-describedby pointing at the reason caption.\n- Status changes are announced politely.\n- Target rule: the disabled control keeps its target size (B13).\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Start with \"You're offline.\" and then say what still works. On a screen with content, the offline FreshnessLine is the opener and the sentence under it says what still works; a form with no FreshnessLine opens its message strip with \"You're offline.\"\n- Exact strings: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"You can still see everything saved here.\" · \"You can keep taking photos.\" · \"Compare needs a connection.\" · \"Will upload when you're back online\" · \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\"\n- Never \"No internet\", \"Connection lost\" or \"Network error\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy): the same on iOS, Android and web.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops at 100%, each labelled with surface id, platform, width and fixture)\n a) f8-native-share-compare, Place B, iOS 393: the offline line at the top with \"You can still see everything saved here.\" under it, then the Place B location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with its \"Saved place · Only you\" ScopeChip, then \"Compare with a friend\" disabled with \"Compare needs a connection.\" under it. Crop out everything else.\n b) f1-add-place-sheet, signed in, Android 412: R3 offline, with the sheet's visible \"Close\".\n c) f10-snap-capture-tray, Home A, iOS 393: R2 offline.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy)\n- Instead of a full-page offline illustration, keep the cached screen readable with the offline line on top — because people still need what they already had.\n- Instead of silent dead buttons, disable the control and put the reason under it — because a button that does nothing looks broken.\n- Instead of a red or amber banner, use plain or surface.sunken with text.strong — because being offline is a condition, not an error.\n- Instead of blanking stale data, keep it with \"as of 7:04 AM\" — because a blank throws away true information.\n- Instead of \"You're offline\" twice in a row, let the offline line open and the next sentence say what still works — because the repeat adds nothing.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\nVariants: cached-screen · queued-writes · form. States: offline · reconnecting · back-online. <size|platform> is \"any\". Example: \"OfflineNotice / form / reconnecting / any / dark\".\n\nNOTES ENTRIES (subheading \"05 OfflineNotice\")\n 05.A1 The form variant uses a message strip above the field in place of the FreshnessLine in all three states (the contract's anatomy puts the FreshnessLine at the top), and shows neither when back online, because a form has no content age. Its reason sits above the field, not under it.\n 05.A2 The used-in line is the sentence \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\", not a list of ids.\n 05.A3 Both 02 grids and the 03 greyscale grid are drawn at 100% on 2000-wide artboards (160 + 24 + 3 × 422 + 2 × 24 = 1498 content width), not at 1440 and not at the B10 50%, so captions and bodySmall stay at type-scale size. The 01 and 04 artboards stay 1440; in-context crops are at 100%.\n 05.A4 The copy rule \"Start with 'You're offline.' and then say what still works\" is met on content screens by the offline FreshnessLine as the opener plus a what-still-works sentence under it (bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary) that does not repeat \"You're offline\". The per-control reason captions carry what does not work.\n 05.A5 The disabled button has a 1px text.muted outline on its sunken fill (matching the disabled field in R3), because sunken on a base card is about 1.1:1 and border tokens are never the only edge. Disabled label and outline are exempt from contrast; no ratio is printed.\n 05.B1 \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Reconnecting\" · \"You can still see everything saved here.\" · \"You can keep taking photos.\" · \"plain\" · \"sunken strip\".\n 05.B2 Spoken labels: \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\" · \"Compare with a friend, disabled, Compare needs a connection.\"\n 05.B3 Sourced, not invented: \"Uploading 2 of 3\" (the live-status pattern from the research brief, section 5).\n 05.C List any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 05.D none\n 05.E Every OfflineNotice name.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 5 artboards exist with their exact names and stated widths, and Notes has the 05 entries with the earlier entries unchanged.\n- Both grids have all 9 cells with printed keys, are drawn at 100% (no \"shown at\" scale label anywhere), fit the 2000 artboard, and R1 back-online shows both sub-cells stacked.\n- The greyscale grid on 03 is at 100% with a verdict beside every cell.\n- R1 and R2 back-online both show a FreshnessLine; R2 back-online reads \"Uploading 2 of 3\".\n- R1 and R2 offline and reconnecting show a what-still-works sentence under the line, and no cell prints \"You're offline\" twice.\n- Cached content is never dimmed or blanked; no frame uses a red, amber or other semantic banner.\n- Every disabled control has its reason caption under it (the form's field: the message strip above it), stays focusable (a focus ring is drawn once), and keeps its 44pt / 48dp / 44px target; the disabled button has a text.muted outline.\n- text.muted appears only on disabled labels, the disabled button outline and the disabled field; text on sunken strips is text.strong.\n- The used-in line reads exactly \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\"."
          }
