            "promptText": "########## SEND 1 OF 2 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-06: StatusChip, send 1 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · StatusChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · Notes: add the subheading \"06 StatusChip\" with 06.A1–06.A6, 06.B2 and 06.D below. Leave earlier entries unchanged.\nThen stop and wait for send 2.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One status per object (bills and invites), stated in words.\nUSED IN (print): f3-bills-list, f3-bill-detail-web, f3-members-roster, f8-seasonal-aha, f10-bill-provenance, f9-block-founders-panel.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on \"Overdue\")\n① Pill, radius pill, height 24pt / 24dp / 24px.\n② Padding 8 horizontal; 4 gap between glyph and text.\n③ Leading 12pt glyph, the only place a semantic hue may appear. No glyph is a plain circle or ring (B8).\n④ Text captionMedium 12/16/500, text.strong. captionMedium is a published design-system style (design-tokens.md) and is the source spec's \"caption medium\"; it is recorded on Notes (06.A6).\n⑤ Fill surface.sunken (dark: B6). No border.\n⑥ The chip is not a target; its row is (B13). Print \"not a target\".\n\nGLYPHS (a labelled row; draw exactly)\n- Upcoming and deadline chip: calendar outline, text.strong.\n- Deadline \"Today\": calendar outline; light text.strong, dark semantic.warning.\n- Due today: clock face drawn as a rounded square with hands, not a circle; light text.strong (warning fails on sunken), dark semantic.warning.\n- Overdue: exclamation mark in a triangle outline, semantic.error.\n- Paid: plain check stroke, no enclosing shape, semantic.success.\n- Expires: hourglass, text.strong.\n- Declined: × stroke, text.strong.\n- Waiting for your OK: speech-bubble outline with three short dashes inside (not dots; B8), primary.700 standing in for semantic.info (dark: primary.400 (dark link)).\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE\nLight, on sunken: text.strong #374151 9.37 · semantic.error #DC2626 4.39 · semantic.success #059669 3.42 · semantic.warning #D97706 2.89 (FAILS, so light warning glyphs use text.strong) · primary.700 #0369a1 5.39.\nDark, on dark raised (chips on dark base and dark app): semantic.warning 4.59 · semantic.success 3.88 · semantic.error 3.03 · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 6.83 · dark text.strong #F1F5F9 13.35.\nDark, on dark sunken #0F172A (= dark base; chips on a dark raised card): semantic.warning 5.60 · semantic.success 4.74 · semantic.error 3.70 · primary.400 (dark link) 8.33 · dark text.strong 16.30.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print)\n- The word carries the state and is read at the end of the row label: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99, due in 14 days, Monday 2 November, Upcoming\". The glyph is decorative (hidden from assistive tech).\n- Non-colour cue: the word. Target: never the chip; the row is (B13).\n\nCOPY (print)\n- Exactly one chip per row. Sentence case. Dates show the weekday.\n- Beyond tomorrow, deadlines, due dates and expiries lead with the relative count: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". Tonight, today and tomorrow stand alone (\"Today\"), and a date or time today shows no weekday (write \"today\").\n- Past dates on chips show the date only, with no \"x days ago\": \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\". This is an exception to B16 (06.A5).\n- Never \"Paid\" as a verb in notifications; write \"marked paid\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print): no platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print)\n- Warning-hue text on a warning tint → text.strong on surface.sunken with the hue on the glyph only, because warning text on its tint is about 3:1.\n- Two chips on one row → the one status that matters, because two chips compete and get misread.\n- A status chip on a person (\"Verified\", \"Active\") → the role in plain text, because people are not statuses.\n- A warning-tinted countdown pill (founding window) → a neutral date chip, because countdowns pressure people.\n- The date before the count (\"Mon 26 Oct · in 7 days\") → \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", because the house style and DateRow lead with the count and every consuming surface copies this chip.\n- A disc-shaped status dot → the listed glyphs, because circles belong to ProvenanceMark.\n\nNOTES (subheading \"06 StatusChip\")\n 06.A1 Warning glyphs (Due today, deadline Today) are text.strong in light mode (semantic.warning is 2.89 on sunken) and semantic.warning in dark mode (4.59 on dark raised, 5.60 on dark sunken). \"Waiting for your OK\" uses primary.700 in place of semantic.info.\n 06.A2 Deadline chip ORDER CHANGED: the source spec writes the date first (\"Oct 26 · 18 days\"). This board leads with the count, matching the house style, the research brief (section 6) and DateRow (\"in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct\"). All 6 consuming surfaces (and every DateRow-style chip) copy this chip, so any date-first decision must come before publishing.\n 06.A3 The invite expiry chip also leads with the count. Alternative if rejected: \"Expires Mon 26 Oct\".\n 06.A4 Re-dated to the fixtures: \"Expires Sep 23\" → \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Declined · Sep 15\" → \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\"; \"Oct 26 · 18 days\" → \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n 06.A5 Past dates on chips show the date only (no \"x days ago\"), for example \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\". This is an exception to B16.\n 06.A6 Type: the chip text uses captionMedium 12/16/500, a published design-system style (design-tokens.md) and the source spec's \"caption medium\". It is not in the house-style type list (caption is 12/16/400), so it is recorded here as a type-scale deviation (B5).\n 06.B2 Spoken label: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99, due in 14 days, Monday 2 November, Upcoming\".\n 06.D Deadline chip: count first (as drawn) or date first? (06.A2)\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 01-anatomy has every block above; no glyph is a plain disc or ring, and semantic hues appear only on glyphs.\n- Notes has 06.A1–06.A6, 06.B2 and 06.D, with earlier entries unchanged.\n\n########## SEND 2 OF 2 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-06: StatusChip, send 2 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message. Keep 01-anatomy as drawn and reuse its glyphs.\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 2. 00a · StatusChip · 04-in-context · light\n 3. 00a · StatusChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 4. 00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 5. 00a · Notes: append 06.B1, 06.C and 06.E under \"06 StatusChip\".\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nGRID (02-variants-states: 9 rows × 1 state)\nDraw each chip three times side by side: in a surface.base row, on a surface.raised card and in a surface.app list. Print \"on surface.base\", \"on surface.raised\" or \"on surface.app\" in each cell label. They are one chip in three contexts, not variants.\nColumn: \"default (the only state)\", key default.\nRows (specimen text → key; a key never contains the specimen):\n 1 \"Upcoming\" → upcoming\n 2 \"Due today\" → due-today\n 3 \"Overdue\" → overdue\n 4 \"Paid\" → paid\n 5 \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" → expires\n 6 \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" → declined (past date, date only: 06.A5)\n 7 \"Waiting for your OK\" → waiting\n 8 \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (deadline chip, count first) → deadline\n 9 \"Today\" (deadline chip) → deadline-today\nDark twin: all 27 cells in dark tokens. Chips on dark base and dark app are filled dark surface.raised; chips on the dark raised card are filled dark surface.sunken (B6).\n\nIN CONTEXT (04-in-context: three crops)\n a) f3-bills-list, Home A, iOS 393: \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00 · due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\" and \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\", each with one \"Upcoming\" chip.\n b) f3-members-roster, Home A, web 390: \"Maya Chen · Owner\" and \"Sam Ortega · Member\" with NO chips, and the invite row \"priya@example.com\" with \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n c) f8-seasonal-aha, Place B, Android 412: \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" with the deadline chip \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Under it, a SourceCaption \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of today\" with the official mark and the word \"Official\" printed beside the mark, once on this crop. Label that word \"legend once per surface\".\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): the row \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" with \"Upcoming\". The pair stacks, the chip moves under the title and becomes a wrapping rounded rectangle (radius lg 12) at 40pt with a 24pt glyph. Also draw chip 5 at AX5 to show the longest string wrapping.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same at 24sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): every cell reads \"yes — the word carries the state\". Add a WRONG example: two chips that differ only in fill hue, with the fix \"fix: words, one chip\".\n- Print \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — chip text is already text.strong; glyph hues are decorative because the word carries the state\".\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\n\"StatusChip / <row key> / default / any / <light|dark>\". Publish one name per chip per theme; the three backgrounds are one chip. Examples: \"StatusChip / overdue / default / any / light\" · \"StatusChip / deadline / default / any / dark\".\n\nNOTES (append)\n 06.B1 Invented strings, copied verbatim from this send: grid rows 5, 6 and 8; the three crop a bill rows; the crop b roster rows \"Maya Chen · Owner\" and \"Sam Ortega · Member\"; the crop c caption \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of today\"; the crop c annotation \"legend once per surface\"; and \"fix: words, one chip\".\n 06.C Any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 06.E Every StatusChip name: 9 chips × light and dark = 18 names.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Both grids have 9 rows on three backgrounds with printed keys, and no key contains a fixture string or date.\n- Every future date beyond tomorrow leads with the count, the only past date shows the date only, and no date today carries a weekday; each crop row has at most one chip, the people rows have none, and crop c prints \"Official\" once.\n- Notes has 06.B1, 06.C and 06.E."
          },
