            "promptText": "########## SEND 1 OF 3 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-07: KindGlyph, send 1 of 3. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nTHIS SEND: 00a · KindGlyph · 01-anatomy · light\nThen stop and wait for send 2.\n\nPURPOSE (print): One drawn glyph per dated kind, used in tiles, rows, the pickup card and the widget.\nUSED IN (print): x-date-sheet, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f10-extraction-confirm, f3-household-calendar, x-place-file.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on \"Recycling\" at 24pt, glyph 2, and on the \"Pickup day\" tile, glyph 3)\n① Line icon on a 24pt / 24dp / 24px grid, 2pt stroke, round caps and joins, text.strong. Use the Pantopus design system's icon style; draw any missing glyph in that style.\n② Tile: 42pt rounded square, radius lg 12, fill surface.sunken, 24pt glyph centred.\n③ Tile label 8pt below: label 13/18/600, text.strong, centred, wraps to two lines.\n④ The whole tile-plus-label cell is the target (B13). The kind picker is a 2-column grid with 8pt gaps: cells are 176 wide on iOS 393 (16pt side margins), 186 on Android 412 and 175 on web 390, all 88 tall. Draw the iOS dimension lines.\n⑤ Selected indicator position: 16pt, in the top-right corner of the 176-wide cell, outside the 42pt tile, so it never overlaps the glyph. Mark it on the iOS cell.\n⑥ Selected tile edge: 1.5px primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)) around the 42pt tile, so the tile shape stays visible on its primary.50 fill (primary.50 on base is only 1.07). Mark it on a selected iOS cell beside ⑤.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE\ntext.strong #374151 on base 10.31, on sunken 9.37 · text.primary #111827 (selected label) on primary.50 16.64 · text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled only) · primary.700 #0369a1 on primary.50 5.57, on base 5.93 (selected tile edge) · primary.50 #f0f9ff on base 1.07 (fill, never an edge) · dark text.strong #F1F5F9 on dark raised 13.35 · dark text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 #0c4a6e 7.64 · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (radio, check and edge only), on dark base 8.33 (selected tile edge).\n\nTHE SET (draw all 17 in order; label each \"<row label> · key: <key>\")\n # | kind | row label (exact) | key | drawing\n 1 | garbage | Garbage | garbage | lidded wheeled cart\n 2 | recycling | Recycling | recycling | cart with three chasing arrows on its body\n 3 | garbage+recycling | Recycling and garbage | garbage-recycling | two overlapping carts\n 4 | bulk | Bulk pickup | bulk | armchair\n 5 | move-in | Move-in date | move-in | open box with an arrow entering it\n 6 | lease ends | Lease ends | lease-ends | key over a door outline\n 7 | notice deadline | Notice deadline | notice-deadline | envelope with a small flag\n 8 | insurance renews | Insurance renews | insurance-renews | shield with a circular arrow drawn as an open arc\n 9 | warranty ends | Warranty ends | warranty-ends | tag with a wrench\n 10 | HOA dues | HOA dues | hoa-dues | three adjoining rooftops\n 11 | property-tax appeal | Property-tax appeal | property-tax-appeal | document with an upward arrow\n 12 | property-tax due | Property-tax due | property-tax-due | document with a dollar sign\n 13 | voter registration | Voter registration | voter-registration | ballot entering a slotted box\n 14 | bill | Bill | bill | receipt with a zigzag bottom edge\n 15 | home event | Home date | home-event | house outline with a small calendar page\n 16 | task | Task | task | rounded-square checkbox with a check stroke\n 17 | package | Package | package | parcel with tape\nProperty tax is one kind with two uses; 11 and 12 share the document base. Cart wheels are round sub-parts, which B8 allows. Row 15 is labelled \"Home date\" because the glossary rules out \"event\".\n\nTILE → GLYPH MAP (print)\nPickup day → 3 · Move-in date → 5 · Lease ends → 6 · Notice deadline → 7 · Insurance renews → 8 · Warranty ends → 9 · HOA dues → 10 · Property-tax appeal → 11 · Voter registration → 13 · Bill → 14.\nNo tile (rows, pickup card, widget and tray only): 4, 12, 15, 16, 17, and the pickup glyphs, chosen by which bins go out: \"Garbage only\" → 1; \"Recycling and garbage\" → 3; a recycling-only pickup (a city with its own recycling day; not Home A or Place B) → 2.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print)\n- Decorative (hidden) when a text label is adjacent; otherwise labelled with the row label (\"Recycling\"). Always paired with visible text; widget and tray glyphs carry their word.\n- Each tile is one element: \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\" (iOS: a button with the selected trait; Android: RadioButton semantics; web: role=\"radio\" inside role=\"radiogroup\").\n- Non-colour: shape plus label; selection is the dot or check plus the edge, fill and ink change.\n- Target: the tile cell or row, never the glyph alone (B13).\n\nCOPY (print)\n- Tile labels, exactly: Pickup day · Move-in date · Lease ends · Notice deadline · Insurance renews · Warranty ends · HOA dues · Property-tax appeal · Voter registration · Bill.\n- Row labels, exactly: the \"row label\" column of THE SET. The ones with no tile are Garbage · Recycling · Recycling and garbage · Bulk pickup · Property-tax due · Home date · Task · Package.\n- \"Pickup day\", never \"trash day\", \"garbage day\" or \"bin day\"; \"Date\", never \"event\" or \"deadline item\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print)\n- The same glyph on all three platforms. The widget glyph is silhouette-safe like ProvenanceMark: one ink, inner detail cut out, so it survives one-colour accented rendering.\n- The one-column large-text list: a trailing check on iOS and web; Material 3 radio buttons on Android.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print)\n- Hue-coded glyphs as the only class cue → a silhouette per kind plus a label, because hue alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind users.\n- An unlabelled glyph → the kind's row label beside it, because the glyphs are not universal.\n- Guessing a tile's glyph → the TILE → GLYPH map, because every later picker copies this one.\n- Selection shown with the focus ring → fill + edge + radio dot + label ink, because selection must look different from focus.\n- An empty-ring radio on iOS or web large-text rows → a trailing check on the selected row and nothing on the others, because iOS has no radio control and an empty ring is the unconfirmed mark's shape.\n- Emoji or a second icon set → the Pantopus icon style, because the house style forbids a new icon set.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 01-anatomy shows all 17 glyphs with their row labels and keys, the TILE → GLYPH map, the indicator position outside the tile, the selected tile edge, and every printed block above.\n\n########## SEND 2 OF 3 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-07: KindGlyph, send 2 of 3. Follow the board rules from the setup message. Use the set (with its row labels), map and anatomy on 01-anatomy.\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · light\n 2. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · dark\n 3. 00a · Notes: add the subheading \"07 KindGlyph\" with 07.A1–07.A3, 07.B2 and 07.D below. Leave earlier entries unchanged.\nThen stop and wait for send 3.\n\nPART A (02): 17 glyph rows × 4 variant columns, all in the default state.\n- row (24pt): the glyph with its row label (THE SET, exact) in bodySmall to its right.\n- tile (42pt): tile plus tile label. Glyphs without a tile in the map: \"Does not apply — no picker tile; see the map\".\n- widget (16pt): the glyph with a 1.5pt stroke, its row label beside it in caption.\n- tray: 16pt, one ink, dark text.primary on the dark mail-snap tray (dark surface.raised). Label \"tray: monochrome, one ink\".\n\nPART B (02): the \"Pickup day\" kind (glyph 3). 4 rows (row · tile · widget · tray) × 5 columns (label → key): default → default · selected tile → selected · disabled → disabled · focused, not selected → focus · selected + focused → selected-focus. Every cell is drawn or prints its reason.\n- tile. default: no indicator. selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900) with a 1.5px primary.700 edge around the tile (dark: primary.400 (dark link)); the label stays 13/18/600 with ink text.primary (dark: dark text.primary); in the cell's top-right corner, outside the tile, the 16pt indicator in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)): a 1.5px ring with an 8pt filled centre (B8 exception, 07.A1). Print \"selected = fill + edge + radio dot + label ink\". disabled: glyph and label text.muted, fill surface.muted, caption \"Already on file\" under the label in text.secondary. focus: the B14 ring only, no fill, no edge, no dot. selected-focus: selected plus the B14 ring outside the selected edge.\n- row. default as in Part A. selected: \"Does not apply — rows are not selectable\". disabled: glyph and label text.muted, caption \"Already on file\" in text.secondary. focus and selected-focus: \"Does not apply — the glyph is decorative; its DateRow owns focus\".\n- widget. default only; the other four: \"Does not apply — the widget is read-only\".\n- tray. default only; the other four: \"Does not apply — the tray is read-only\".\nThen draw the 10 tiles, default, as one 2-column picker in map order.\nDark twin: Parts A and B and the picker in dark tokens; the tile fill follows B6.\n\nNOTES (subheading \"07 KindGlyph\")\n 07.A1 Radio indicators vs invariant 1 (\"filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else\"). Two flagged exceptions: (a) the selected tile's corner indicator, a ring with a filled centre (unselected tiles show nothing), from the source spec's \"filled radio dot\"; (b) Android Material 3 radios in the 200% list, whose unselected option is an empty ring, the UNCONFIRMED silhouette. iOS AX5 and web 200% lists use a trailing check instead, because iOS has no native radio control.\n 07.A2 The selected label keeps label 13/18/600 and changes ink from text.strong to text.primary. The source spec's \"bold label\" is shown by the fill, edge, corner dot and ink change instead of an off-scale 700. No type-scale deviation is recorded. Alternative if rejected: record 700 as a deviation.\n 07.A3 Part B has five state columns for every variant (default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus). The source lists default · selected tile · disabled; focus is added to show that selection differs from focus. The selected tile also gains a 1.5px primary.700 edge (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), because its primary.50 fill alone (1.07 on base) would lose the tile shape; this matches ChoiceChip and AddressChip.\n 07.B2 Spoken label: \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\".\n 07.D (1) Radio indicators (07.A1): keep (b) platform-native, or use the trailing check on Android too? Should (a) become a check stroke in the corner? (2) Selected label (07.A2): weight 600 with the ink change, or 700? (3) Widget bill and HOA lines (07.A8, added in send 3): you-added, or official when a bill comes from a verified source?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Part A has 17 × 4 cells with the exact row labels, and Part B 4 × 5, each drawn or carrying its reason; the picker is 2 columns with glyphs from the map.\n- The selected tile has the fill, the 1.5px edge, the corner dot outside the tile and the text.primary label at weight 600; focus is a ring only.\n- Notes has 07.A1–07.A3, 07.B2 and 07.D, with earlier entries unchanged.\n\n########## SEND 3 OF 3 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-07: KindGlyph, send 3 of 3. Follow the board rules from the setup message. Use the glyphs and states already drawn.\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · KindGlyph · 04-in-context · light\n 2. 00a · KindGlyph · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 3. 00a · Notes: append 07.A4–07.A8, 07.B1, 07.B3, 07.C and 07.E under \"07 KindGlyph\".\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04: three crops)\n a) x-date-sheet, iOS 393, Home A: title \"Add a date\", the 2-column picker with \"Warranty ends\" selected (fill, edge, corner dot), a visible \"Close\" and the primary button \"Save\".\n b) f4-today-pickup-card, Home A, Android 412, on surface.base, radius lg. Top to bottom: the 42pt tile with glyph 3; h3 \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\"; \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\"; a SourceCaption with the unconfirmed mark, \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of today\", with \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" printed once beside the mark; two outlined peer buttons of equal weight, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n c) f7-today-widget, iOS home screen, the large 338×354pt widget with 16pt margins (content width 306pt), fill surface.base, top-aligned. Header \"Larkspur Loop\" in label 13/18/600 text.strong, then 8pt, then three entries 12pt apart. Each entry is exactly two lines:\n  line 1: the 16pt glyph, 8pt gap, the title in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary.\n  line 2: indented 24pt to align with the title: the date in caption 12/16 text.secondary, 8pt gap, the XS 12pt provenance mark, 4pt gap, its word in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\n  Entry 1: glyph 3 · \"Recycling and garbage\" / \"Tomorrow\" · unconfirmed mark · \"On record, not confirmed\"\n  Entry 2: glyph 14 · \"Clark Public Utilities\" / \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · you-added mark · \"You added this\"\n  Entry 3: glyph 10 · \"HOA dues\" / \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · you-added mark · \"You added this\"\n  Fit check: each line has 282pt; the longest line 2 (\"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" + mark + \"You added this\") is about 260pt. The content is about 158pt tall (18 + 8 + 3 × 36 + 2 × 12) inside the 322pt content height. No line wraps or truncates; the space below the entries stays empty.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): the picker becomes one column of full-width rows (361pt wide, 12pt inner padding). Inside each row the pair stacks (B9): the tile, grown to 64pt with the glyph at 48pt, sits at the leading edge on top, and the label at 44pt/600 wraps below it across the row width minus the trailing check column (24pt check + 12pt gap), about 301pt. Words never break mid-word; \"Property-tax\" may break only after its hyphen. \"Warranty ends\" is selected: primary.50 row fill, the tile's 1.5px primary.700 edge, text.primary label and a trailing 24pt check stroke in primary.700, aligned to the label's first line. Other rows show no indicator. No ring is drawn on iOS.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same stacked rows with the label at 26sp and a trailing Material 3 radio, the platform control, aligned to the label's first line. The radio is a 24dp ring (the 2× cap of the platform's 20dp control) with a 2px stroke. Selected: primary.700 ring with a 12dp filled centre. Unselected: an empty ring in text.secondary (B8 exceptions, 07.A1).\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the iOS form (stacked rows, trailing check on the selected row, nothing on the others), built as role=\"radio\" rows.\n- GREYSCALE (B10 subset): the 17 row glyphs and all of Part B, verdict \"yes — shape + label\". Selected reads by the dot (tile) or the check (iOS and web rows) plus edge, fill and ink, not by fill hue alone.\n- Print \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — glyphs and labels are already text.strong; on Android, the unselected radio ring becomes text.strong\", and draw that ring.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\n\"KindGlyph / <kind key> / <state key> / <variant key: row · tile · widget · tray> / <light|dark>\". Per theme, publish the 61 drawn Part A cells (68 minus the 7 \"does not apply\" tiles) plus the 5 non-default drawn Part B cells for garbage-recycling (tile selected, disabled, focus, selected-focus; row disabled). Part B defaults reuse the Part A names. Total: 66 per theme, 132 names. Examples: \"KindGlyph / garbage-recycling / selected / tile / light\" · \"KindGlyph / bill / default / widget / dark\".\n\nNOTES (append)\n 07.A4 Widget glyph: 1.5pt stroke at 16pt, with ProvenanceMark's silhouette-safe accented rendering. The source spec has no platform notes for KindGlyph. The widget crop uses the house style's 338×354pt size, because three entries with provenance words do not fit 338×158; each entry is two lines (title; date + mark + word).\n 07.A5 Set and picker decisions: property tax (appeal / due) is two glyphs sharing a document base; glyph 2 has no tile and serves a recycling-only pickup row and the anatomy specimen (neither Home A nor Place B has such a day); the picker is 2 columns (DateSheet anatomy) and \"Pickup day\" uses glyph 3.\n 07.A6 The pickup card crop follows the PickupCard anatomy (42pt tile; \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" once), with the fixture's \"carts out by 6:30 AM\". Its headline names tomorrow's pickup, so it shows the weekday date alone. Its caption says \"as of today\" because a date today carries no weekday (B16).\n 07.A7 Indicator and large-text geometry: the 16pt selected indicator sits in the cell's top-right corner, outside the 42pt tile. At AX5, Android 200% and web 200% the tile grows to 64pt so the glyph can scale to 48pt (B9) with an 8pt margin, and it stacks above its label in each full-width row (B9 \"pairs stack\"); the trailing check or radio aligns to the label's first line; words never break mid-word. The Android radio is 24dp, the 2× cap of the platform's 20dp control.\n 07.A8 Widget provenance: the widget is a standalone surface, so every mark has its word. The pickup entry carries the XS unconfirmed mark with \"On record, not confirmed\". The bill and HOA entries are household entries and carry the XS you-added mark with \"You added this\".\n 07.B1 Invented strings: \"Already on file\" · \"tray: monochrome, one ink\" · \"selected = fill + edge + radio dot + label ink\" · the 17 glyph descriptions and keys · the row labels not in the tile list: \"Garbage\", \"Recycling\", \"Recycling and garbage\", \"Bulk pickup\", \"Property-tax due\", \"Home date\" (for the kind \"home event\"; the glossary rules out \"event\"), \"Task\", \"Package\" · \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of today\" · \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\" (source pattern with the fixture time) · \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\" · the widget lines \"Tomorrow\", \"Clark Public Utilities\", \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", \"HOA dues\", \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\".\n 07.B3 Sourced, not invented: \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\", \"Yes, Tuesday is right\", \"Change pickup day\" (PickupCard); \"Add a date\", \"Save\" (DateSheet); \"On record, not confirmed\", \"You added this\" (ProvenanceMark legend).\n 07.C Any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 07.E All 132 KindGlyph names.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The only rings are the tile corner indicator and the Android radios; no iOS or web frame draws an empty ring.\n- At AX5, Android 200% and web 200%, each 64pt tile (48pt glyph) sits above its label, no word breaks mid-word, and the trailing check or 24dp radio aligns to the label's first line.\n- The widget is 338×354pt; each entry is two lines, no line wraps or truncates, and every entry prints its provenance word beside its mark.\n- No caption puts a weekday on today's date.\n- Notes has 07.A4–07.A8, 07.B1, 07.B3, 07.C and 07.E."
          },
