            ],
            "promptText": "########## SEND 1 OF 2 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-08: AddressChip, send 1 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\nAddressChip is paired with the ScopeChip sentence you drew in 00a-03. Reuse it exactly: \"Only you will see this.\"\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · AddressChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · Notes: add the subheading \"08 AddressChip\" with 08.A1–08.A5, 08.B1, 08.B2 and 08.D. Leave earlier entries unchanged.\nThen stop and wait for send 2.\n\nPURPOSE (print): Shows a held or selected address as a label: never a map, never coordinates.\nUSED IN (print): f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-save-confirmation, f1-add-place-sheet, f8-compare-arrival-header.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on the held chip for Place B)\n① Pill, radius pill, fill surface.raised, with a 1px border.default edge as decoration only (1.24:1 on the base card, 1.18:1 on the chip fill). Surface.raised on base is about 1.05:1, so on a base card this edge is in practice the chip's only visible outline; the pin and text carry the chip, as in ⑨. Meaning never depends on the edge.\n② 16pt pin glyph in text.strong, 8pt gap. Its round hole is a sub-part (B8).\n③ Street \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\": bodySmallMedium 14/20/500, text.primary.\n④ City \"Camas, WA 98607\" on the line below: caption 12/16, text.secondary (4.63:1 on raised). On a selected fill the city turns text.primary (see R1 selected in send 2).\n⑤ Padding 12 horizontal, 8 vertical; minimum height 44pt.\n⑥ At 390 wide, street and city each wrap and are never truncated.\n⑦ Optional \"Save it\", only when the chip is a selectable suggestion row: a text button in label 13/18/600 primary.700, with a target (B13).\n⑧ SCOPE SENTENCE RULE (defined only here; every other mention points to ⑧): \"Only you will see this.\" sits 8pt below every held, recovery and duplicate chip. The sender label (R4) is the one exception: it describes someone else's place, so it carries no sentence, and the sentence goes under the recipient's own address field instead. Print \"no scope sentence: not your place\" on the exception.\n⑨ DARK EDGE RULE: fill dark surface.raised. Dark border.default on dark raised is 1.00:1, so dark mode has no border.default edge; the pin and text carry the chip. The selected state keeps its 1.5px primary.400 (dark link) edge. Draw a light and a dark default chip side by side, labelled \"dark: no border\". The light chip sits on a surface.base card; the dark chip sits on its own dark surface.base card (radius lg 12), never directly on the light artboard.\n\nTOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE\ntext.primary #111827 on raised 16.98, on primary.50 16.64 (selected street and city) · text.secondary #6B7280 on raised 4.63, on primary.50 4.54 (not used on the selected fill) · text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37 · primary.700 #0369a1 on base 5.93, on primary.50 5.57 · border.default #E5E7EB on base 1.24, on raised 1.18 (decoration only) · surface.raised on base 1.05 · dark text.secondary #94A3B8 on dark raised 5.71, on primary.900 3.69 (FAILS, so the selected dark city uses dark text.primary) · primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (edge and check only) · dark text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 7.64.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print)\n- Reads the full address: \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, Washington 98607\". Selected: \"…, selected\". Sender: \"Dana, Camas, Washington\". Expired: \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, no longer held, Search again, button\".\n- Non-colour: selected is the check plus the edge; expired is stated in words.\n- The chip itself is a label. Its actions (\"Save it\", \"Use for Today\", \"Search again\") are targets (B13).\n\nCOPY (print)\n- Scope sentence: see ⑧.\n- Exact strings (each string is everything after the colon; no outer quote marks belong to it):\n  Hold message: We're holding it for 7 days\n  Recovery row: 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\n  Duplicate message: You already saved this as “Mom’s house” (the curly quotes are part of the string)\n  Duplicate action: Use for Today\n  Sender label, compact form: Dana · Camas, WA\n- Glossary: \"Saved place\", never \"bookmark\", \"preview\" or \"draft\".\n\nPLATFORMS (print): no platform differences. Draw the same chip on all three platforms.\n\nINSTEAD OF (print)\n- A blank retype field when the server holds the address → the held AddressChip, because retyping loses people between steps.\n- A map or coordinates → the street and city as text, because a label is enough and a map leaks location.\n- An alarm colour for an expired hold → a neutral sunken chip with \"Search again\", because expiry is not an error.\n- A held or selectable chip without its scope sentence → add it (⑧), because a held address must say who sees it.\n- The sentence under a sender's chip → under the recipient's own field (⑧), because it would be false about the sender's place.\n- A text.secondary city on a selected fill → text.primary (dark: dark text.primary), because dark text.secondary on primary.900 is 3.69.\n\nNOTES (subheading \"08 AddressChip\")\n 08.A1 Dark mode has no border.default edge (1.00:1 on dark raised); the selected 1.5px primary.400 (dark link) edge stays (⑨). In light mode the decorative edge is 1.24 on the base card and 1.18 on the chip fill; with raised on base at about 1.05, it is in practice the only outline, and the pin and text carry the chip.\n 08.A2 The sender label (R4) has no scope sentence (⑧). The source spec says the chip is always paired with the sentence.\n 08.A3 R1–R3 use the Place B address as specimens, although in the fixture story Jordan already saved it on Sat 10 Oct. The duplicate message You already saved this as “Mom’s house” is kept verbatim, with curly inner quotes, for the specimen only.\n 08.A4 The recovery-row example \"1402 NE 3rd Ave, Camas — Save it\" became \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" (the Place B fixture).\n 08.A5 Selected cells set both street and city in text.primary (dark: dark text.primary, 7.64 on primary.900). The city does not keep text.secondary there: dark text.secondary on primary.900 is 3.69, and light text.secondary on primary.50 is only 4.54.\n 08.B1 Invented strings: \"We're no longer holding this address.\" · \"Search again\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\" (the prefilled search) · \"Check your email\" (crop a heading) · \"Your address\" (the recipient's field label, crop c) · \"no scope sentence: not your place\" · \"dark: no border\".\n 08.B2 Spoken labels: \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, Washington 98607\" · \"…, selected\" · \"Dana, Camas, Washington\" · \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, no longer held, Search again, button\" (expired).\n 08.D Sender label without the scope sentence (08.A2): accept?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 01-anatomy has callouts ①–⑨, the light and dark pair (the dark chip on its own dark surface.base card), and every printed block.\n- Notes has 08.A1–08.A5, 08.B1, 08.B2 and 08.D, with earlier entries unchanged.\n\n########## SEND 2 OF 2 (paste on its own; wait for the stop before the next send) ##########\nComponent 00a-08: AddressChip, send 2 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message. Use the anatomy, the scope sentence rule ⑧ and the dark edge rule ⑨ on 01-anatomy.\n\nTHIS SEND (in order)\n 1. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 2. 00a · AddressChip · 04-in-context · light\n 3. 00a · AddressChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 4. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 5. 00a · Notes: append 08.C and 08.E under \"08 AddressChip\".\nThen stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nGRID (02: 4 rows × 3 columns)\nThe addresses are specimens only (08.A3). Columns (label → key): default → default · selected → selected · expired (neutral) → expired. R1–R3 follow ⑧; R4 is its exception. Use the exact strings from COPY on 01-anatomy.\n R1 held → held (f1-email-verify-handoff): the chip, then the hold message We're holding it for 7 days, then the scope sentence.\n   selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900), a 1.5px primary.700 edge (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), and a trailing 16pt check stroke in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)). Street and city are both text.primary (16.64 on primary.50; dark: dark text.primary, 7.64 on primary.900). The city never keeps text.secondary on the selected fill (08.A5).\n   expired: fill surface.sunken, text in text.strong, the caption \"We're no longer holding this address.\" and a text button \"Search again\", which opens search prefilled with \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\". No warning or error hue.\n R2 recovery row → recovery-row (f1-save-confirmation): a full-width 44pt row with the recovery row string 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it, where \"Save it\" is the action; then the scope sentence.\n   selected: the R1 selected treatment (including text.primary for all text), with the check replacing \"Save it\". expired: the R1 expired treatment in row form.\n R3 duplicate → duplicate (f1-add-place-sheet): the chip, then the duplicate message You already saved this as “Mom’s house”, then the duplicate action Use for Today as a 44pt text button; then the scope sentence.\n   selected: the R1 selected treatment (including text.primary for all text), after \"Use for Today\" is chosen. expired: \"Does not apply — a saved place does not expire\".\n R4 sender label → sender (f8-compare-arrival-header): the pin glyph, \"Dana\" in bodySmallMedium and \"Camas, WA\" in caption; compact form Dana · Camas, WA. No scope sentence (⑧).\n   selected and expired: \"Does not apply — a sender label is neither selectable nor held\".\nDark twin: all 12 cells in dark tokens, following ⑨; selected cells use dark text.primary for street and city.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04: three crops)\n a) f1-email-verify-handoff, web 390: the heading \"Check your email\", with R1 default under it.\n b) f1-save-confirmation, iOS 393: R2 default.\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, web 1440 cropped to 720 wide: the R4 sender chip over Dana's column with no sentence, and in the empty second column the recipient's own address field, labelled \"Your address\", with \"Only you will see this.\" under it.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 and R2. Street and city wrap onto several lines, the pill becomes a rounded rectangle (radius lg 12), \"Save it\" moves under the address as a full-width 44pt button, and the pin scales to 32pt.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same, with the button at 48dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390): the same.\n- GREYSCALE (B10): \"yes — pin + text; selected = check + edge\"; expired cells: \"yes — words\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 default with the city line in text.strong; the decorative border is unchanged.\n\nPUBLISH KEYS\n\"AddressChip / <held · recovery-row · duplicate · sender> / <default · selected · expired> / any / <light|dark>\", one name per drawn cell: 9 per theme. Example: \"AddressChip / held / expired / any / light\".\n\nNOTES (append)\n 08.C Any cell you could not draw, or \"none\".\n 08.E Every AddressChip name: 9 cells × light and dark = 18 names.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Both grids have 4 × 3 cells with printed keys, and every \"Does not apply\" cell prints its reason.\n- ⑧ holds in every cell and crop, including crop c; selected has the fill, the 1.5px edge (in dark too) and the check; expired uses no warning or error hue.\n- In every selected cell, light and dark, street and city are text.primary (dark: dark text.primary, 7.64); no text.secondary sits on a selected fill.\n- The COPY strings appear exactly, including the curly quotes in the duplicate message.\n- No street or city is truncated, and no map or coordinates appear."
          }
