              "00b · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-01: ScaleStrip, part 1 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\nPart 1 holds the full specification and the first four artboards. Part 2, my next message, adds artboards 05–08, the dark twins and the Notes, and relies on everything in this part.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN FOR PART 1\nDraw these four, using the exact names and this order. Then stop and wait for part 2.\n1. 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light\n3. 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light\n4. 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The four-layer reading instrument. It draws one row per authority on that authority's own ordered bands, and it never adds up to a grade.\nUSED IN (print it): f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-sheet, f8-og-compare-card.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 640px wide, with 608px of content.\nSPECIMEN CLOCKS\n- Ready Air rows, including the compare \"You\" row, are drawn at 7:10 AM on Mon 19 Oct, so \"observed 7:00 AM\" counts as fresh. Print \"specimen time 7:10 AM\" in the gutter.\n- Stale Air rows use TODAY, 6:10 PM.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy; put a callout on every part)\n- Row order is fixed as Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon, and rows are never re-sorted, because people compare rows by position.\n- A row contains, from top to bottom:\n  - the layer name, in label 13/18/600 text.strong\n  - the value line \"Word · number\", in bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary\n  - the track zone\n  - the band names\n  - 00a · SourceCaption\n- Row padding is 12pt top and bottom. Gaps: name → value 4pt · value → track zone 8pt · track zone → band names 4pt · band names → caption 8pt.\n- Each row is at least 48pt tall and is a single target. Markers and pointers are never targets.\n- Layout:\n  - Below 560pt (phones and web-390), the row is stacked, with a 326pt track.\n  - At 560pt and wider (web-1440), the row has two columns: left 237px, gap 16px, right 355px. The left column stacks the name, the value line and the SourceCaption. The right column holds the track zone and the band names, top-aligned with the value line.\n  - AX5 and 200% are stacked.\n  - Part 2 defines the OG column.\n- Track zone: 24pt tall, with a 12pt track centred in it.\n- Track:\n  - equal-width bands per layer (the layers don't share an axis)\n  - filled surface.raised\n  - 1.5px text.secondary separators (4.63:1 on raised)\n  - a 1px text.secondary keyline with radius xs 4 around the whole track\n  - the least hazard on the left\n- Occupied band: a 2px text.primary outline inside its edges.\n- Marker: a vertical capsule, 4 × 20pt, radius pill.\n  - Core: text.primary. Halo: 2px surface.base, which makes it 8 × 24pt overall. The halo is #0F172A in dark.\n  - It is centred in the occupied band and extends 4pt beyond the track top and bottom.\n  - It is never a disc (G4).\n- Band names, in caption 12/16 text.secondary:\n  - Up to 2 lines each, never truncated.\n  - Flood and Radon print all their names. Wildfire prints the two end names plus the occupied one.\n  - The occupied name is set in captionMedium 12/16/500 text.primary, directly under the marker. If it comes within 8pt of an end name, it replaces that end name.\n  - Air prints \"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\", with the occupied range in captionMedium text.primary.\n- Bands:\n  - Flood, by annual chance: \"Minimal (X)\" · \"0.2% a year (shaded X)\" · \"1% a year or more (A/V zones)\". The value line prints the actual zone code. These FEMA annual-chance names and \"1% chance each year\" are the band names G2 allows.\n  - Wildfire (USFS): \"Very low\" · \"Low\" · \"Moderate\" · \"High\" · \"Very high\".\n  - Radon: \"Zone 3 · low potential\" · \"Zone 2 · moderate potential\" · \"Zone 1 · highest potential\". Never \"N of M\".\n  - Air: the AqiBand instrument-row variant. It is the only coloured track. The next component defines AqiBand; draw this row exactly as follows:\n    - six equal-width 12pt segments in the house-style EPA ColorVision Assist hues\n    - 2px gaps in the host surface\n    - a 1px text.secondary keyline on each segment, with radius xs 4 on the outer corners\n    - on the occupied segment, a 2px text.primary inner outline\n    - the same 4 × 20pt capsule, placed by value within its segment\n    - no reading: segments in surface.sunken with their keylines, and no marker\n    - the value line leaves out the pollutant\n- Fixture rows (HOME A). All are Official; \"●\" stands for the drawn Official mark.\n\n  | Row | Label | Value | Occupied | Caption |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Flood | \"Flood zone\" | \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" | band 1 | \"● FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\" |\n  | Wildfire | \"Wildfire hazard potential\" | \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" | band 3 | \"● USFS · quarter-mile area · 2023\" |\n  | Air | \"Air quality index (AQI)\" | \"AQI 42 · Good\" | 84% of Good | \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\" |\n  | Radon | \"Radon zone\" | \"Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\" | band 3 | \"● EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\" |\n\n- Summary. Print this one sentence under the 01 fixture instrument: \"Flood Zone X, minimal flood hazard; Wildfire Moderate, 3 of 5; Air AQI 42, Good; Radon Zone 1, county-wide.\"\n- Specimen value: a Flood row with \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\" and band 3 occupied.\n\nVARIANTS [row keys]\n- V1 Flood [flood] · V2 Wildfire [wildfire] · V3 Radon [radon] · V4 Air [air].\n- V5 compare [compare]: two identical labelled pointers replace the capsule. Filled vs hollow means provenance only.\n  - Track zone, 60pt tall, from top to bottom:\n    - a 16pt line \"Dana\", in captionMedium text.primary\n    - the 8pt sender pointer\n    - the 12pt track\n    - the 8pt \"You\" pointer\n    - a 16pt line \"You\"\n    Band names sit 4pt below the track zone.\n  - Pointers: triangles 12 wide × 8 tall, in text.primary with a 2px surface.base halo.\n    - The sender pointer points down, with its tip on the track top. The \"You\" pointer points up, with its tip on the track bottom.\n    - Each pointer is centred in its band. On Air, it is placed by value.\n  - Each occupied band is outlined; a band both places share gets one outline. The two pointers share an x position on the non-Air layers, and on Air only when the values are equal.\n  - Value lines: \"Dana: <value>\" and \"You: <value>\". When the band is shared, print one line, \"Both: <value>\".\n  - Chip: \"Same band\" or \"Different band\", right-aligned on the layer-name line.\n    - A 24pt pill in surface.sunken, 8pt side padding, captionMedium text.strong, no glyph and no hue.\n    - On compare rows, the layer-name line is 24pt tall, and the name is vertically centred on the chip. The other row gaps are unchanged.\n  - Header: \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\".\n- V6 no data [no-data] (Flood, Wildfire, Radon): bands in surface.sunken, keyline and separators unchanged, no marker and no outline, value \"Not on record\".\n- V7 not studied (Flood): the same greyed track, with the value \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\".\n- V8 non-burnable (Wildfire): the same greyed track, with the value \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\".\n- V6–V8 must each look different from Wildfire \"Very low\", because missing data is not a low reading.\n- V9 frozen [frozen]:\n  - Captions end \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n  - The Air caption reads \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\", and the Air value reads \"AQI 42 · Good · on Sat 12 Sep\".\n- V10 collapsed [collapsed], for arrival headers below 640px:\n  - one wrapping body row, at least 44pt tall\n  - the whole row is the target, and there are no tracks\n  - text: \"Dana · Camas, WA · Flood X · Wildfire Moderate · Air 42 · Radon Zone 1 ›\"\n\nSTATES [column keys]\n- loading [loading]: 00d · WarmingSkeleton.\n  - Only the track keyline and separators show.\n  - The label and value become surface.sunken bars of 60×12 and 140×16.\n  - The exact row height is reserved.\n- ready [ready].\n- partial, loading [partial-loading]: some rows are ready and others are loading.\n- partial, failed [partial-failed]: the Air row's slot shows 00c · InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with Retry. The other rows are ready.\n- differs [differs]: the \"Different band\" chip (V5).\n- stale [stale], at 6:10 PM:\n  - The Air row keeps its value and marker.\n  - Its caption reads \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", with the 00a stale mark. The age words carry the staleness.\n  - The other rows are unchanged.\n- AX5 [ax5]: text stacked above a full-width track. Part 2 draws this, on 06.\n\nDEVIATIONS FROM THE CONTRACT (part 2 records these on Notes D for my sign-off)\n- The 4 × 20pt two-tone capsule replaces the contract's \"Marker: 12pt two-tone\".\n- The 12 × 8 triangle pointers in V5 replace the contract's \"same marker form\" for compare.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS (part 1; part 2 adds the dark twins)\n01-anatomy:\n- a Wildfire detail row, with every callout\n- the fixture instrument in iOS 393, with the summary under it\n- the same instrument on web-1440 in two columns, with a callout on the 237 / 16 / 355 split [extra key two-column]\n- an R6 table: text.secondary on base and on raised, text.strong on sunken, and the stale mark on base and on raised\n02-layers-by-state: a grid of 5 rows × 6 columns.\n- Rows: flood · wildfire · air · radon · wildfire-very-low (labelled \"Wildfire very low (for contrast)\").\n- Columns: loading · ready · no-data · not-studied-non-burnable · stale · frozen.\n- flood × ready: add the Zone AE specimen under Zone X.\n- flood × not-studied-non-burnable is V7; wildfire × not-studied-non-burnable is V8.\n- air × no-data: use the AqiBand no-reading row (\"No reading for this address right now\"), not V6.\n- These cells are n/a, with these reasons:\n  - air × not-studied-non-burnable: \"n/a — AirNow has no such class; see AqiBand no reading\"\n  - radon × not-studied-non-burnable: \"n/a — EPA zones cover every county\"\n  - flood × stale, wildfire × stale and radon × stale: \"n/a — dated datasets carry their effective date, not an age\"\n- wildfire-very-low × ready: a normal track with band 1 occupied and the value \"Very low · 1 of 5\", aligned with the greyed wildfire cells. The row's other cells read \"n/a — contrast row; only ready is needed\".\n03-compare: a web-390 instrument comparing \"Dana · Camas, WA\" with You (keys \"compare · differs\").\n- Flood: both in band 1; \"Same band\"; \"Both: Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n- Wildfire: \"Different band\"; \"Dana: Moderate · 3 of 5\"; \"You: Low · 2 of 5\".\n- Air: both AQI 42, inside Good; \"Same band\"; \"Both: AQI 42 · Good\". Two caption lines: \"Dana: AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" and \"You: AirNow · observed 7:00 AM\".\n- Radon: both Zone 1; \"Same band\"; \"Both: Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n- Flood, Wildfire and Radon each print one frozen caption, for example \"● FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021 · as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n- Only You's wildfire reading (\"Low · 2 of 5\") is a specimen value; label it so in the gutter.\n- Under the instrument, print the one-sentence compare summary \"Dana's area and yours share 3 of 4 bands; wildfire differs.\", followed by the compare spoken label.\n- Beside the instrument, draw V10 twice. Neither copy may truncate:\n  - at 390 wide (keys \"collapsed · ready\")\n  - at 320 wide, wrapping [extra key collapsed-320]\n- Below the instrument: the compare Wildfire row in two columns on web-1440 [extra key compare-two-column].\n04-instrument-states: the instrument five times in iOS 393, keyed \"instrument · <state key>\", in this order: loading · ready · partial-loading (with Air loading) · partial-failed · stale. Print all four spoken labels under ready, and under each other state print only the labels that change.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (each row is one element; web rows are focusable)\n- Under ready on 04:\n  - \"Flood zone: Zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, effective September 2021. Official.\"\n  - \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate, 3 of 5, scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023. Official.\"\n  - \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM. Official.\"\n  - \"Radon zone: Zone 1, highest potential, scale Zone 3 to Zone 1. EPA, county-wide. Official.\"\n- Changed labels on 04:\n  - loading: \"Loading\", once for the whole container\n  - partial-loading: \"Loading\", on the Air row\n  - partial-failed: \"Air quality: We couldn't reach AirNow just now.\", with the Retry button named \"Retry air quality\"\n  - stale: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago. Official.\"\n- On 03: \"Wildfire hazard potential. Dana: Moderate, 3 of 5. You: Low, 2 of 5. Different band. Scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023.\"\n\nCOPY\n- Use these verbatim: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\" · \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate · 3 of 5\" · \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n- Pair a word with a number on every layer except Radon.\n- Sender rows describe places. Outbound actions start with a verb.\n- \"N of M\" appears only in Wildfire readings, in \"category 1 of 6\", and in the compare summary's \"3 of 4 bands\".\n- Never write: \"100-year floodplain\", \"minimal risk\", \"wildfire risk\", \"better\", \"worse\", \"wins\".\n\nPLATFORMS: web draws it as SVG; iOS (SwiftUI) and Android (Compose) draw it natively. The geometry is identical on all three; only the target minimums differ by platform.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a grade, star, radar chart, cross-layer ramp or shared 0–100 axis, draw each authority's own bands, because the layers never add up to a verdict.\n- Instead of arrows, trophies or better/worse words, print \"Different band\" or \"Same band\", because a difference between places is not a ranking.\n\nCARRY TO NOTES (part 2 writes these, together with its own entries)\n- A: the compare summary \"Dana's area and yours share 3 of 4 bands; wildfire differs.\"\n- D: the two deviations listed above.\n- G: the part 1 extras: two-column, collapsed-320 and compare-two-column.\n\nDONE WHEN (part 1)\n- The four artboards above exist with their exact names.\n- The 02 grid is 5 × 6, with no blank cell.\n- Both V10 widths are drawn.\n- The summary on 01 and the compare summary on 03 are each one sentence."
          },
          {
            "id": "00b-02",
            "component": "AqiBand",
            "artboards": [
              "00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · dark",
              "00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light",
              "00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark",
              "00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light",
              "00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · dark",
              "00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light",
              "00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light",
              "00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light",
              "00b · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-02: AqiBand, part 1 of 2. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\nPart 1 holds the full specification and the first two artboards. Part 2, my next message, adds artboards 03–06, the dark twins, the publish names and the Notes, and relies on everything in this part.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN FOR PART 1\nDraw these two, using the exact names and this order. Then stop and wait for part 2.\n1. 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The one officially coloured scale. It shows the EPA AQI with its category name and is drawn the same way everywhere air appears.\nUSED IN (print it): f1-today-air-band, f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, x-provenance-sheet, f8-og-compare-card, f8-compare-reveal.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 640px wide, with 608px of content.\n\nSPECIMEN CLOCKS\nAirNow readings are hourly, so the age of a reading decides its state. On every artboard that shows one of these specimens, print its specimen time once in the gutter.\n- Ready and offline specimens: 7:10 AM on Mon 19 Oct, so \"observed 7:00 AM\" counts as fresh.\n- Alert and still-above specimens: 4:10 PM.\n- Stale specimens: TODAY, 6:10 PM, which gives \"— 11 hours ago\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy; put a callout on every part)\n- Segments: six equal-width category segments in the EPA ColorVision Assist hues. These are the only non-token colours in the product.\n- Swatch row: show the hues as a row, with each name and RGB value:\n  - aqi.good: Good 158,255,145\n  - aqi.moderate: Moderate 255,201,5\n  - aqi.usg: Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups 255,130,5\n  - aqi.unhealthy: Unhealthy 240,34,0\n  - aqi.veryUnhealthy: Very Unhealthy 137,9,151\n  - aqi.hazardous: Hazardous 100,0,21\n- Segment height: 16pt in the detail variant (Today), 12pt in the instrument row, and 8pt in the widget micro variant.\n- Gaps: 2px between segments, in the host surface. That is surface.base on light cards and surface.raised (dark) on dark cards.\n- Keylines: each segment gets its own 1px text.secondary keyline, because some hues nearly vanish against their surface (Good is 1.22:1 and Moderate 1.54:1 on white; Hazardous is 1.08:1 on dark raised). The outer corners of the first and last segments have radius xs 4.\n- Detail segment width: (326 − 5 × 2) ÷ 6 = 52.7pt. On web-1440: (608 − 10) ÷ 6 = 99.7px.\n- Range labels: centred under each segment, in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\".\n  - The occupied label switches to captionMedium text.primary.\n  - The occupied segment gets a 2px text.primary inner outline.\n- Marker: the ScaleStrip capsule, 4pt wide.\n  - Core: text.primary. Halo: 2px surface.base. In dark mode the halo stays the fixed dark tone #0F172A.\n  - Height is the segment height + 8pt: 24pt in detail, 20pt in the instrument row, 16pt in widget micro.\n  - It is never a disc (G4).\n  - It passes 3:1 on every hue in both themes, because one of its two tones always contrasts.\n- Marker position:\n  - Position within the segment = (value − segment low) ÷ (segment high − segment low).\n  - For position only, the \"301+\" segment spans 301–500.\n  - AQI 42 sits at 84% of Good. AQI 118 sits at 35% of Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups.\n  - Values above 500 clamp to the right end of \"301+\", and the actual number is still printed.\n- Marker contrast table. Print it on 01: core and halo contrast against each hue.\n\n  | Hue | Light core | Light halo | Dark core | Dark halo |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Good | 14.50 | 1.22 | 1.01 | 14.59 |\n  | Moderate | 11.50 | 1.54 | 1.25 | 11.57 |\n  | USG | 7.14 | 2.49 | 2.01 | 7.18 |\n  | Unhealthy | 4.17 | 4.26 | 3.44 | 4.19 |\n  | Very Unhealthy | 2.15 | 8.24 | 6.65 | 2.17 |\n  | Hazardous | 1.31 | 13.52 | 10.92 | 1.32 |\n\n- Value line: above the band, in bodyMedium text.primary.\n  - Fixture: \"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\". Alert: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · PM2.5\".\n  - The category and number always sit on the card in text.primary, never on a fill (text.primary on Hazardous is only 1.31:1).\n  - The value line is the visible summary.\n  - Inside ScaleStrip, the pollutant is left out.\n- Health statement: below the band, in body 16/24 text.primary, verbatim from EPA.\n  - Good: \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups: \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\" Then add the PM2.5 line: \"People with heart or lung disease, older adults, children, and people of lower socioeconomic status are the groups most at risk.\"\n- PANTOPUS NOTE: Pantopus context, labelled as ours. It appears on the alert and still-above specimens only.\n  - It is a separate block below the EPA statement. The EPA statement stays above it, unchanged.\n  - The block holds the overline \"PANTOPUS NOTE\", then, in bodySmall text.primary, \"Your alert level is 101. You can change it in Notifications.\"\n  - On still-above, the block holds a second line directly below that one, also in bodySmall text.primary: \"Still above your alert level (101) since 4:00 PM. No new alert until it drops below 101 and rises again.\"\n- Threshold rule: drawn at the user's chosen threshold (101, 151 or 201), never hard-coded.\n  - A 1.5px dashed vertical rule (3 on, 2 off) in text.primary, extending 6pt beyond the band top and bottom.\n  - When the threshold equals a segment's low value, centre the rule in the 2px gap before that segment. 101 sits in the Moderate/USG gap; 151 sits in the USG/Unhealthy gap.\n  - The threshold number sits above the rule, in caption text.primary (\"101\").\n  - \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\" appears in bodySmallMedium text.primary, with a leading 16pt alert glyph in semantic.warning (on the glyph only).\n  - The fixture threshold is 101, the server default. Also draw one specimen at 151, labelled \"threshold 151 (not crossed)\".\n  - In the instrument row, the threshold number sits to the right of the rule's top end, and the track zone grows from 24pt to 40pt, in the alert cell only.\n- 00a · SourceCaption: \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\". On alert, it reads \"observed 4:00 PM\". \"●\" stands for the drawn Official mark.\n\nVARIANTS [row keys]\n- V1 detail [detail]: the Today card.\n- V2 instrument row [instrument-row]: the Air row inside ScaleStrip, with 12pt segments and no health statement.\n  - In ready, stale and no-reading, it must match the ScaleStrip artboards exactly.\n  - The alert cell (40pt track zone and threshold rule) is an AqiBand-only form that the ScaleStrip artboards don't draw.\n- V3 widget micro [widget-micro]: the block inside the medium widget.\n  - Band: 120 × 8pt, with no range labels and no statement.\n  - Beside the band, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"Air · Good 42\". On alert: \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\".\n  - Under it, a caption line of 11pt or larger: an XS Official mark, then \"Official · AirNow · 7:00 AM\" (G8).\n- V4 no reading, V5 alert and V6 still above threshold (no new push) are drawn in their state columns:\n  - V5 = the threshold rule, \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", the 00a · ScopeChip \"Your household\", and the PANTOPUS NOTE.\n  - V6 = the V5 detail card, unchanged, with the still-above line added as the second line of the PANTOPUS NOTE.\n\nSTATES [column keys]\n- ready [ready], at 7:10 AM.\n- stale [stale], at 6:10 PM:\n  - Hues and marker are unchanged.\n  - The caption reads \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", with the 00a stale mark. The age words carry the staleness.\n- no reading [no-reading] (V4):\n  - Segments are surface.sunken with their keylines, with no marker and no outline. Range labels stay.\n  - The value line becomes \"No reading for this address right now\", in body text.primary.\n  - A second specimen, for a failed provider, adds 00c · InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with Retry [extra key no-reading-provider-failed].\n- alert [alert] (V5), at 4:10 PM.\n- still above [still-above] (V6), at 4:10 PM.\n- offline [offline], at 7:10 AM: the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" sits above the band, which is drawn from cache.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS (part 1)\n01-anatomy:\n- the V1 detail card at AQI 42 on iOS 393, with every callout\n- the swatch row\n- the marker contrast table\n02-variants-by-state: a grid of 3 rows × 6 columns.\n- Rows: detail · instrument-row · widget-micro.\n- Columns: ready · stale · no-reading · alert · still-above · offline.\n- detail row:\n  - ready: V1 at AQI 42\n  - stale: V1 with the stale caption\n  - no-reading: V4, with the no-reading-provider-failed specimen stacked under it\n  - alert: V5 at AQI 118\n  - still-above: V6\n  - offline: V1 under the FreshnessLine\n- instrument-row row:\n  - ready: V2 at AQI 42, \"AQI 42 · Good\", with range labels\n  - stale: V2 with the stale caption\n  - no-reading: V2 greyed, with \"No reading for this address right now\"\n  - alert: V2 at AQI 118 with the threshold rule, and no statement or note\n  - still-above: \"n/a — the still-above line belongs to the detail card; the row keeps its alert form\"\n  - offline: \"n/a — the host instrument shows one FreshnessLine for all four rows\"\n- widget-micro row:\n  - ready: the V3 block, \"Air · Good 42\"\n  - stale: \"n/a — widget age is the widget's own 'As of' line (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - no-reading: V3 greyed, \"Air · No reading\"\n  - alert: V3 at AQI 118, \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\", with no threshold rule\n  - still-above: \"n/a — widgets show only the current reading\"\n  - offline: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n- Under the grid, draw three extras:\n  - threshold 151 (not crossed), at AQI 118 [extra key threshold-151]\n  - a clamp specimen at AQI 612, labelled \"specimen value\", with the marker at the right end and the value \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · PM2.5\" [extra key clamp]\n  - six capsules, one per segment, showing 3:1 in both themes [extra key marker-on-every-hue]\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The summary is the value line. The band is one element. Spell out \"Air quality index (AQI)\" once per surface.\n- \"category N of 6\" is allowed in spoken labels only.\n- Print these labels under their 02 cells:\n  - detail ready: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM.\"\n  - detail stale: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago.\"\n  - detail no-reading: \"Air quality: No reading for this address right now.\"\n  - detail alert: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n  - detail still-above: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. Still above your alert level, 101, since 4 PM. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n  - detail offline: \"You're offline. Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM.\"\n  - instrument-row ready, stale and alert: the matching detail label followed by \" Official.\" (the ScaleStrip Air-row form)\n  - instrument-row no-reading: \"Air quality: No reading for this address right now.\" (no \"Official.\", because no reading is shown)\n  - widget-micro ready: \"Air quality 42, Good. Official, AirNow, 7 AM.\"\n  - widget-micro no-reading: \"Air quality: no reading. Official, AirNow.\"\n  - widget-micro alert: \"Air quality 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups. Official, AirNow, 4 PM.\"\n- Separators and keylines keep the band readable in greyscale. In tinted widgets, the printed name carries the meaning.\n- The band is not a target. Retry and row actions are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY\n- EPA names and health text are verbatim: \"Good\", \"Moderate\", \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", \"Unhealthy\", \"Very Unhealthy\", \"Hazardous\".\n- \"Sensitive groups\" appears only in widgets.\n- Never write: \"satisfactory for everyone\", \"air score\", \"pollution level\".\n\nPLATFORMS: the geometry is identical on iOS, Android and web. The widget differences are defined on 03, in part 2.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a proportional 0–500 track, draw six equal segments ending in \"301+\", because proportional widths squeeze 0–100 and can't place readings above 500.\n- Instead of brand blue or an invented ramp, use the EPA hues, because this is the authority's own scale.\n- Instead of \"Air quality is satisfactory for everyone\", print EPA's exact sentence, because a paraphrase is an EPA reporting error.\n- Instead of hiding the band on a good day, draw it at AQI 42 with \"Good\", because a quiet reading is still a reading.\n\nDONE WHEN (part 1)\n- Both artboards exist with their exact names.\n- The 02 grid is 3 × 6, with no blank cell and one reason per n/a cell.\n- The provider-failed specimen and the three extras are drawn.\n- Every spoken label above is printed under its cell."
          }
