            "promptText": "Component 00b-03: FourteenDayStrip. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): The next two weeks at this address, drawn as a shape. The strip sits above list rows, and those rows are the real tap targets.\nUSED IN (print it): f5-today-calendar-strip, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, f1-today-tab, x-place-file.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 648px wide (616px of content), so each cell is 44px.\nTYPE (two styles this component adds to the house scale; use them only as named):\n- captionMedium 12/16/500. iOS AX5 → 43, Android 200% → 24.\n- widgetCaption 11/16/400, widgets only. At AX sizes the widget drops to its text fallback (05), so widgetCaption has no AX5 or 200% size.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Header: the 00a · ScopeChip \"Your household\" (HOME A), then the summary label \"Next 14 days: 6 items\" in label 13/18 text.strong. The summary is the strip's one-sentence summary.\n- Strip: 14 equal cells across the content width, today on the left. At 326pt the pitch is 23.3pt.\n  - One track: radius sm 6, a 1px text.secondary keyline, and 1px text.secondary separators between cells.\n  - Cell height 76pt, top to bottom: 6pt padding · up to 3 XS (12pt) ProvenanceMarks stacked with 4pt gaps (44pt) · a 4pt gap · a 16pt line reserved for \"+N\" · 6pt padding.\n  - \"+N\" appears when a cell has 4 or more mark items (3 marks, then \"+N\"). It is in caption 12/16 text.strong (#F1F5F9 dark), because text.secondary on sunken is only 4.39:1. Otherwise the reserved line stays empty.\n  - All marks use one ink, text.secondary at full opacity, centred in the cell. Marks never dim, in any state (C11).\n- Cell fill: weekdays surface.sunken at 100%, weekends surface.sunken at 40%. Opacity marks the weekend, never hue, and the initials also name it (or \"Sat–Sun\" where there are no initials).\n- Civic, state or county rule: a solid 4pt bar, full cell height, in text.strong. The bar is centred if the cell has no other marks. Otherwise it sits 2pt from the cell's left edge and the marks shift 3pt right. A bar never counts toward the 3-mark limit or \"+N\". A rule is never a dot. YearBand uses the same bar rule.\n- Holiday move: the mark sits on the moved day. The usual day gets a struck ghost: the same shape at full text.secondary ink, crossed by a 1.5px diagonal strike in text.primary (#E5E7EB dark). The strike carries the meaning, and the DateRow names the move in words.\n- Labels under the strip:\n  - Row 1: weekday initials under every cell, in caption text.secondary: \"M T W T F S S M T W T F S S\". Draw them only where the pitch is 20pt or more. They are never spoken.\n  - Row 2: anchors in captionMedium text.strong: \"Today\" left-aligned under cell 1 and \"Mon 26 Oct\" left-aligned under cell 8.\n- Below the strip: one 00c · DateRow per item. The foot is a persistent 48pt row \"+ Add a date\", with the glyph and label in primary.700 (#38BDF8 dark).\n- Fixture window, HOME A, Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov:\n\n  | Cell | Day | Item (DateRow title) | Mark |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 2 | Tue 20 Oct | Recycling and garbage | hollow (city schedule, not confirmed) |\n  | 5 | Fri 23 Oct | Clark Public Utilities bill | tick |\n  | 8 | Mon 26 Oct | Voter registration, online or mail, must arrive by | state bar |\n  | 9 | Tue 27 Oct | Garbage only | hollow |\n  | 10 | Wed 28 Oct | City of Vancouver water bill | tick |\n  | 14 | Sun 1 Nov | HOA dues | tick, weekend cell |\n\n  DateRow line 2 dates (R11): \"Tomorrow\"; \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\"; \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\"; \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\".\n- Two extras for 01. Each is a separate specimen outside the window, labelled \"specimen\" in the gutter:\n  - Overflow cell [extra key overflow-cell], Mon 2 Nov: the county rule \"Property tax 2nd half\" as the bar 2pt from the left, plus four tick items (Comcast bill, \"Swap furnace filter\", \"Library books due\", \"Drop off old paint\"). Draw 3 marks shifted 3pt right, then \"+1\". Callout: \"Bar = county rule, not counted in +N; 4 marks → 3 + '+1'; 6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6 = 76pt\".\n  - Holiday-move pair [extra key holiday-move], PLACE B: the Thanksgiving notice moves the usual Thu 26 Nov pickup to Fri 27 Nov. Draw a hollow mark on Fri 27 Nov and a struck ghost on Thu 26 Nov. DateRow: \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\", line 2 \"in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov\".\n\nVARIANTS (row keys in brackets)\n- V1 Today card [today-card]: as above.\n- V2 widget medium [widget-medium], for the 338×158 widget (306 × 126pt content). Widget fill: surface.base in light and dark raised #1E293B in dark, so the sunken cells stay visible.\n  - The strip spans 306pt, so the pitch is 21.9pt.\n  - Cell height 60pt: 6pt · up to 2 XS marks with a 4pt gap (28pt) · 4pt · a 16pt \"+N\" line · 6pt. With 3 or more mark items, draw 2 marks, then \"+N\" (N = items − 2).\n  - Under the strip, one 16pt line in widgetCaption: the anchors \"Today\" and \"Mon 26 Oct\" in text.strong (no initials), plus \"Sat–Sun\" in text.secondary, centred under cells 6–7 and 13–14.\n  - Then one 16pt legend line in widgetCaption text.secondary with inline S marks. The widget is a standalone surface (C14), so the legend prints a word for each shape drawn in that specimen, and the bar is always keyed as an official rule. HOME A: \"○ On record · ✓ You added · ▮ Official rule\". PLACE B: \"○ On record · ▮ Official rule\".\n  - Height used: 60 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16 = 100pt. The remaining 26pt holds f7-today-widget's header line, which carries both the place label and the widget's \"As of\" text. f7-today-widget owns that line's layout. Print this budget in the gutter.\n  - No rows and no add row.\n- V3 year-band window crop [x-place-file]. Label it \"window crop — YearBand defines the band\". It has two forms, each copied from YearBand (00b-04):\n  - Phone form (on 03, inside an iOS 393 frame): YearBand's phone anatomy. 326pt wide, 12 columns of 27.2pt (\"Oct\"–\"Sep\"), four labelled 24pt lanes with the HOME A month groups, bars, count numerals (captionMedium text.primary) and Tuesday ticks.\n  - Desktop form (on 07 crop (c), web-1440): a crop of YearBand's exact-day band (00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day). It shows the 128px label column plus the Oct and Nov columns (60px each). Items sit on exact days under YearBand's collision rule, so the You lane shows one tick at 23 Oct with \"4\". The state bars are at 26 Oct and 3 Nov, and the county bar is at 2 Nov.\n  - Both forms, per lane, paint in this order: lane fill · window wash · keyline and separators · ticks · today rule · marks, bars and numerals. Marks, bars and numerals carry a 1pt halo that matches the fill beneath them, so the today rule stops short of them and never cuts through the Oct You tick. Light: base lanes and a surface.sunken wash. Dark: base #0F172A lanes and a raised #1E293B wash.\n  - The today rule is at 19 Oct. The wash covers 19 Oct–1 Nov and carries the window, with the legend \"Shaded: next 14 days\". A 1px dashed text.secondary edge marks the end of 1 Nov. In the phone form, that edge sits about 1.8pt from the Oct/Nov separator, so it also rises 4pt above the top lane as a tick.\n  - Batch 3 of YearBand checks the phone form against YearBand's phone anatomy and the desktop form against YearBand 03-desktop-exact-day.\n- V4 empty: the cells with no marks, then the 00d · QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\", then \"+ Add a date\". Summary: \"Next 14 days: nothing on file\".\n  - QuietDayReceipt stand-in: a 16pt bare stroked check in text.secondary (no disc) and the sentence in bodySmall text.primary, always starting with \"Checked\". The check never sits at a mark position. This is the one exception to grammar rule 4 (Notes E).\n\nSTATES (column keys in brackets)\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with 14 cell outlines on surface.sunken and a bar for the header, with no marks or text. It reserves the full height and is static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready [ready].\n- empty [empty]: V4.\n- stale [stale]: the strip is unchanged. The 00a · FreshnessLine \"Updated 2h ago\" appears under the header, and its words carry the staleness.\n- permission-denied [permission-denied]: the viewer may not add dates. The add row is absent, with no ghost row. The strip and rows are unchanged.\n- T1 [t1]: PLACE B, with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - One hollow mark on Thu 22 Oct only (frequency Not set), with the DateRow \"Pickup day · frequency not set\", line 2 \"in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\", source City of Camas.\n  - The state bar on Mon 26 Oct, with its DateRow line 2 \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n  - Summary: \"Next 14 days: 2 items\". The add row is present, and dates added here stay Only you.\n- error [error]: no strip. The slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load your dates just now\" + Retry. This is an error row, not an absence.\n- highlighted row [highlighted-row]: after the push \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\", the Tue 20 Oct DateRow is highlighted and accessibility focus moves to it. The strip is unchanged. Light: an infoBg wash with a 1px semantic.info outline. Dark: per C6. The highlight fades over 300ms after 4s. Under Reduce Motion it appears and disappears without animation.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light:\n- V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including the 76pt cell budget.\n- The overflow cell and the holiday-move pair, each magnified 4× and labelled.\n- R6 contrast table: text.secondary on base, on sunken and on a weekend cell; text.strong on sunken; primary.700 on base. Note under it: \"Stale marks use the same ink.\"\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n- Rows: today-card · widget-medium. Columns: loading · ready · empty · stale · permission-denied · t1 · error · highlighted-row.\n- Layout (fits 1440): three stacked grids of up to 3 columns. Each grid has its own header row and a 160-wide header column. Columns are 358 wide with 24 gaps. The grids hold (loading · ready · empty) / (stale · permission-denied · t1) / (error · highlighted-row). The highlighted-row cell holds the start frame. Under the grids, one extra row labelled \"highlighted-row · start and end frames\" draws both frames side by side.\n- today-card row: as in STATES.\n- widget-medium row:\n  - loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n  - ready: V2, HOME A\n  - empty: V2 cells with no marks, and \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" in widgetCaption in place of the legend line\n  - stale: \"n/a — widget age is the 'As of' text in f7-today-widget's header line\"\n  - permission-denied: \"n/a — the widget has no rows or add row\"\n  - t1: V2, PLACE B (Thu 22 Oct hollow, state bar on Mon 26 Oct, PLACE B legend)\n  - error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - highlighted-row: \"n/a — the widget has no rows\"\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light and · dark:\n- V2 at true size inside a 338×158 outline. Label the rest \"owned by f7-today-widget\" and print the 100pt budget in the gutter.\n- Beside it, the V3 phone form with a leader line to a V1 strip: \"same data\". The state bar on 26 Oct matches in both.\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light (this artboard is the accessibility and platform spec):\n- iOS: the strip is one adjustable element with one focus outline; its label is the summary. Draw four consecutive steps (one day per swipe), each in a speech bubble:\n  - \"Tuesday 20 October: Recycling and garbage, city schedule, on record, not confirmed\"\n  - \"Wednesday 21 October: nothing on file\"\n  - \"Thursday 22 October: nothing on file\"\n  - \"Friday 23 October: Clark Public Utilities bill, you added this\"\n  - Annotate: \"A tap on the strip scrolls to the rows. Cells are not targets; rows follow DateRow.\"\n- Android: the same element, with the TalkBack custom actions \"Next day\" and \"Previous day\".\n- Web-390: annotate \"Hidden from assistive tech because the rows duplicate it; otherwise a list of full-date labels.\"\n- Web-1440: the only per-cell targets. Each cell is a 44px button with its own focus ring (C12). Its accessible name is the native day readout, for example \"Tuesday 20 October: Recycling and garbage, city schedule, on record, not confirmed\". Empty days read \"Wednesday 21 October: nothing on file\". Activating a cell moves focus to that day's first row. Hover reveals nothing new.\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5:\n  - The cells keep their size.\n  - The initials are dropped, because 43pt initials do not fit a 23.3pt pitch.\n  - The anchors become wrapped lines above the strip (\"Today · Mon 19 Oct\", \"Mon 26 Oct\").\n  - A caption under the strip keeps the weekend cue: \"Lighter cells are Sat and Sun\".\n  - The summary, rows and add row wrap and grow.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- V2 at AX sizes falls back to text: \"Next 14 days: 6 items · Tomorrow: Recycling and garbage (on record, not confirmed)\".\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light: the light 02 artboard, desaturated. Per C8, print one caption under each grid row:\n- today-card: \"Provenance by shape; rules by bar; weekends by opacity plus initials; moves by strike; empty by the word 'Checked'.\"\n- widget-medium: \"Provenance by shape plus legend words; rules by bar plus 'Official rule'; weekends by opacity plus 'Sat–Sun'; empty by the word 'Checked'.\"\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f5-today-calendar-strip on iOS 393: V1 with its rows and the legend line \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n- (b) f1-today-tab on Android 412: the strip card inside Today, with its ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- (c) x-place-file on web-1440: V1 with per-cell buttons, above the V3 desktop form (the exact-day crop defined in V3).\n- Under the crops, in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet → V2 widget medium · f7-widget-tap-landing → V1 with the highlighted row.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY: see 04. Non-colour cues: see the 06 captions.\n\nCOPY: \"Next 14 days: N items\". Dates always show the weekday, and DateRow line 2 adds the relative count beyond tomorrow. Pickup rows name the bins. Deadlines say \"must arrive by\". The add row reads exactly \"+ Add a date\".\n\nPLATFORMS: see 04.\n\nINSTEAD OF (contract doNot)\n- No class hue as the only cue: one ink, with the DateRow KindGlyph carrying the class.\n- No 6pt dots with ticks: 12pt XS marks, the smallest size where the shapes stay distinct.\n- No 14 tiny tap targets on phones: 23pt cells fail 44pt / 48dp (04).\n- No statewide or county dot: a full-height bar, because a rule is not an item at this address.\n- No even rhythm through a holiday week: the moved day plus a struck ghost.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"FourteenDayStrip / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: overflow-cell and holiday-move (01, light), highlighted-row-frames (02, light and dark), year-band-window (03, light and dark), web-1440-cell-buttons (04, light), widget-text-fallback (05, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a FourteenDayStrip part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: list every quoted string above that is not in the fixtures or the contract.\n- B. Assumptions:\n  - The cell is 76pt (6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6).\n  - The widget cell is 60pt, with up to 2 marks, then \"+N\" (N = items − 2), within 100pt of the 158pt widget. The other 26pt is f7-today-widget's header line, which carries the label and the \"As of\" text.\n  - The widget fill is base in light and raised in dark. The widget legend keys only the shapes drawn, and a bar is always keyed \"Official rule\".\n  - PLACE B's frequency is Not set, so only Thu 22 Oct is drawn. The Thanksgiving move is drawn because the City of Camas notice covers every Thursday route.\n  - The overflow cell is outside the window.\n  - The strip counts pickups as items; YearBand does not.\n  - The dark window wash is raised #1E293B, because dark sunken equals the dark lane fill.\n  - In the window crop, the today rule paints under marks, bars and numerals, which carry a 1pt halo. The wash carries the window, and on phones the dashed edge also rises 4pt above the lanes.\n  - captionMedium 12/16/500 and widgetCaption 11/16/400 are added to the type scale for this component.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract's \"Next 14 days: 9 items\" → the fixture count \"6 items\". The empty line follows QuietDayReceipt (\"next two weeks\").\n- D. Deviations: stale marks and holiday ghosts stay at full ink (C11); the contract's 50% opacity is not used.\n- E. Open question for 00d: QuietDayReceipt uses a bare stroked check, while grammar rule 4 reserves the ticked disc for \"You added this\". Should the exemption stay (bare stroke, no disc, always followed by \"Checked\"), or should its CheckItems get a glyph that is not a check?\n\nDONE WHEN (checks not stated above)\n- All 9 artboards and the Notes append exist with the exact names below.\n- The 02 grid is complete (2 × 8), with one reason per n/a, and fits 1440.\n- V1–V4, all eight states and both extras are drawn. The 76pt, 60pt and 100pt budgets add up.\n- The window wash is visible in dark.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light\n4. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light\n5. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light\n6. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light\n8. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n9. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark\n10. 00b · Notes (append FourteenDayStrip)"
