            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-04: YearBand. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): Twelve months of dated rules in four source lanes. It shows the same data as FourteenDayStrip at a longer zoom.\nUSED IN (print it): x-place-file, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery.\nWEB-1440 CARD: 880px wide (848px of content).\nTYPE (two styles this component adds to the house scale; use them only as named):\n- captionMedium 12/16/500. iOS AX5 → 43, Android 200% → 24.\n- widgetCaption 11/16/400, widgets only. At AX sizes the widget drops to its text fallback (05), so widgetCaption has no AX5 or 200% size.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy-phone, with a callout on every part)\n- Scope: the 00a · ScopeChip \"Your household\" (HOME A), above the summary header.\n- Summary header, in label 13/18 text.strong: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates. Next, in 4 days: Clark Public Utilities bill due Fri 23 Oct.\" The pickup rhythm is not counted as dates.\n- Top line (16pt): \"Today\" in caption text.primary above the today rule, and \"2027\" above \"Jan\".\n- Month columns: 12, current month first, in caption text.secondary: \"Oct Nov Dec Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep\". Phone: 326pt, so each column is 27.2pt.\n- Lanes, in order: \"You\" · \"Your city\" · \"Your county\" · \"Your state\".\n  - Phone stack per lane: a 16pt label line (captionMedium text.strong) · a 24pt lane · a 4pt gap. At 768px and wider, the labels sit in a 128px left column.\n  - Lane track: surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary keyline, radius xs 4, and 1px text.secondary month separators.\n  - Paint order in each lane: lane fill · window wash · keyline and separators · rhythm ticks · today rule · marks, bars and numerals.\n  - Marks, bars and numerals carry a 1pt halo that matches the fill beneath them, so the today rule stops short of them. On phones the rule (≈16.7pt) would otherwise cut across the Oct You tick (7.6–19.6pt). Callout this.\n- Marks on phones: one group per month per lane.\n  - Each group is an XS 12pt ProvenanceMark centred in the column. When the group has 2 or more items, add a count numeral in captionMedium text.primary, 1pt to the right of the mark.\n  - A mixed-provenance group shows the hollow mark, and the rows list each item.\n- Rules: county and state rules are solid 4pt bars, full lane height, in text.strong (the same rule as FourteenDayStrip). On phones a bar is centred in its month column, with a numeral when there are 2 or more.\n- Collision rule (768px and wider only; exact-day placement happens only there):\n  - Use drawn extents: a mark is 12px wide and a bar is 4px wide. Once a cluster holds 2 or more items, its numeral adds 1px plus the numeral's width (about 7px for one digit in captionMedium).\n  - Work left to right within each lane. An item joins the current cluster if its left edge is less than 2px from the cluster's right edge (its mark or bar, plus the numeral once there is one). Otherwise the item starts a new cluster.\n  - A cluster is drawn as one item at its earliest day, with its count numeral 1px to the right. Mixed provenance shows the hollow mark.\n  - Rhythm ticks are not items and never merge.\n  - Item centres: x = 128 + 60 × (month index + (day − 0.5) ÷ days in month), where Oct is month index 0.\n- Today rule: 1.5px text.primary through all four lanes at 19 Oct (19/31 into Oct).\n- Shaded 14-day window: 19 Oct–1 Nov across all lanes.\n  - Wash: light surface.sunken; dark raised #1E293B (dark lanes are base #0F172A, so a sunken wash would vanish).\n  - The wash carries the window, and the legend line under the band names it: \"Shaded: next 14 days\".\n  - A 1px dashed text.secondary edge marks the end of 1 Nov. On phones that edge sits about 1.8pt past the Oct/Nov separator, so it also rises 4pt above the top lane as a tick, to tell it apart.\n- Pickup rhythm, \"Your city\" lane:\n  - Label line: \"Your city\", an XS hollow mark, and the caption \"Pickup every Tuesday · city schedule\" in caption text.secondary. At 768px and wider these sit in the label column under \"Your city\".\n  - Ticks: 1.5 × 8pt in text.secondary, one per service week, centred vertically.\n  - After the last published city calendar (Dec 2026), the Jan–Sep keyline turns dashed (3 on, 2 off). The caption \"Projected after Dec 2026 (last published city calendar)\" sits on its own 16pt caption line directly under the Your city lane.\n  - Holiday moves on phones: that week's tick is 11pt tall with a 1.5px strike.\n  - Holiday moves at 768px and wider: if the moved day is at least 14px from the usual day, the tick moves to the real day and a struck ghost (same shape, full ink) sits on the usual day. Otherwise use the phone form.\n- The band reserves its full height while loading.\n- Caption under the band, in text.secondary: \"The same dates are listed below.\" Then come 00c · DateRow and 00c · FactRow rows, which are the table.\n- Fixture data, HOME A:\n  - You (all ticks): Oct \"2\" (Clark Public Utilities bill Fri 23 Oct; City of Vancouver water bill Wed 28 Oct) · Nov \"2\" (HOA dues Sun 1 Nov; Comcast bill Mon 2 Nov) · Dec (water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec) · Mar \"2\" (lease notice deadline Mon 1 Mar; lease ends Wed 31 Mar).\n  - Your city: the weekly Tuesday rhythm, on record, not confirmed. There is no holiday move in the published window.\n  - Your county: a bar in Nov (property tax 2nd half due Mon 2 Nov; the row may add \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\").\n  - Your state: bars in Oct (online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct) and Nov (in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov).\n  - Total: 10 dates (7 + 1 + 2).\n\nVARIANTS (row keys in brackets)\n- V1 place file, HOME A [place-file-home-a]: as above.\n- V1 place file, PLACE B [place-file-place-b], with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\":\n  - You: empty.\n  - Your city: no rhythm (frequency Not set). One tick on Thu 22 Oct, and the Thanksgiving move in Nov (\"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", from the published 2026 calendar).\n  - City label line: an XS hollow mark and \"Pickup day Thursday · frequency not set\". The keyline stays solid and there is no projected caption line, because there is no rhythm to project.\n  - Your county: a bar in Nov. Your state: bars in Oct and Nov.\n  - Summary: \"Next 12 months: 3 dates. Next, in 7 days: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- V2 widget large [widget-large], 338×354pt, with 306×322 of content. Every V2 specimen uses HOME A. Fill: surface.base in light, raised #1E293B in dark (the lanes stay base).\n  - 12 columns of 25.5pt. Lane labels are place names: \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\".\n  - The city label line reads \"Vancouver\", then the hollow mark, then \"On record\".\n  - Numerals sit 1pt right of the mark, as on phones, in widgetCaption text.primary. The mark and numeral are centred as a group (a 25.5pt column leaves about 6.75pt).\n  - The widget draws the today rule (with the same paint order and 1pt halos as V1) but no shaded window.\n  - Legend line in widgetCaption text.secondary with inline S marks: \"○ On record · ✓ You added · ▮ Official rule\". The widget is a standalone surface (C14), so the legend keys only the shapes it draws, and a bar is always keyed as an official rule.\n  - All text is at least 11pt.\n  - Height budget (print it in the 04 gutter), 268pt in total:\n    - label \"Larkspur Loop\" 20 · gap 4 · top line 16 · month labels 16 · gap 4\n    - lanes: 4 × (16 + 24) + 3 × 4 = 172\n    - projected caption line 16 (\"Projected after Dec 2026\") · gap 4 · legend 16\n  - The remaining 54pt belongs to f7-today-widget's \"As of\" line and padding.\n  - At AX sizes the widget drops to text (05).\n- V3 gallery sample [gallery-sample]: V2 with the HOME A data, static, inside a gallery preview frame no wider than 358.\n- V4 empty checked [empty-checked]: the lanes, month labels and today rule, with no marks, bars or rhythm. Under them, the 00d · QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" (the bare stroked check stand-in defined in FourteenDayStrip V4).\n\nSTATES (column keys in brackets)\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with four lane outlines on surface.sunken, at the exact final height. Static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready [ready].\n- empty checked [empty-checked]: V4.\n- error [error]: no band. The slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load the next 12 months just now\" + Retry. This is an error row, not an absence.\n- offline [offline]: the band drawn from cache under the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\".\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light:\n- V1 HOME A on iOS 393 with every callout. Include callouts on the county bar (\"county rule = bar, same as FourteenDayStrip\"), the lane stack (16 · 24 · 4) and the today rule's halo.\n- R6 contrast table: text.secondary on base and on sunken; text.strong on base and on sunken; text.secondary on dark raised (the dark window wash).\n- Native readouts, in speech bubbles. The band is one element with adjustable month cells, one month per swipe:\n  - \"October: 3 dates. Clark Public Utilities bill due Friday 23 October, you added this. Voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October, Washington, official. City of Vancouver water bill due Wednesday 28 October, you added this. Pickup every Tuesday, city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n  - \"November: 4 dates. HOA dues due Sunday 1 November, you added this. Comcast bill due Monday 2 November, you added this. Property tax 2nd half due Monday 2 November, Clark County, official. Voting in person until 8 PM Tuesday 3 November, Washington, official. Pickup every Tuesday, city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n- Rows: place-file-home-a · place-file-place-b · widget-large · gallery-sample · empty-checked. Columns: loading · ready · empty-checked · error · offline.\n- Layout (fits 1440): two stacked grids, each with its own header row and a 160-wide header column. Columns are 358 wide with 24 gaps. The grids hold (loading · ready · empty-checked) / (error · offline).\n- place-file rows: as in STATES. The empty-checked cell is V4 under that place's header.\n- widget-large:\n  - loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n  - ready: V2\n  - empty-checked: V2 with no marks, and \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" in place of the legend\n  - error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n  - offline: V2 under \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (the 00a widget-horizon form)\n- gallery-sample: ready is V3. Loading, empty-checked, error and offline print \"n/a — the gallery shows a static sample\".\n- empty-checked:\n  - loading: the HOME A skeleton\n  - ready: \"n/a — V4 is the empty state\"\n  - empty-checked: V4\n  - error: \"n/a — an error is not a checked result; see the place-file rows\"\n  - offline: V4 under the FreshnessLine\n00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light:\n- V1 on web-1440 in the 880px card: a 128px label column + 12 × 60px months = 848px. Marks and bars sit on exact days under the collision rule.\n- Clusters, each with a callout:\n  - You: 23 Oct (≈171.6), 28 Oct (≈181.2), 1 Nov (≈189.0) and 2 Nov (≈191.0) become one tick at 23 Oct with \"4\". Callout: \"each next left edge is less than 2px from the cluster's mark-plus-numeral edge (≈185.6) → one mark + count numeral\".\n  - You: 12 Dec, 1 Mar and 31 Mar stay separate.\n  - State: the 26 Oct bar (≈177.4) and the 3 Nov bar (≈193.0) stay separate, about 12px clear.\n  - County: a bar at 2 Nov (≈191.0).\n  - Tuesday ticks sit on exact Tuesdays, about 13.5px apart.\n- Below it, a PLACE B inset band. The Thanksgiving move (about 2px) uses the phone form. Callout: \"moved day under 14px from usual day → phone form\".\n- Annotate: \"Marks are not targets; the rows below are.\"\n00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light and · dark:\n- V2 at true size inside a 338×354 outline. Label the rest \"owned by f7-today-widget\" and print the budget in the gutter.\n- V3 in two previews:\n  - inside an iOS gallery preview;\n  - inside an Android widget-picker preview: a 4×3-cell picker tile showing the 338×354 widget scaled to 75% (254×266).\n- V2 under iOS tinted rendering: marks keep their silhouettes, and the legend words carry the meaning.\n00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5:\n  - The lanes keep their geometry.\n  - The month labels drop to \"Oct\", \"Jan\", \"Apr\", \"Jul\" on a line above the band.\n  - \"Today\" and \"2027\" (43pt) wrap onto their own line above the month-label line. The today rule and the Jan column keep their positions.\n  - Lane labels, captions and the summary wrap.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- V2 at AX sizes drops to text, with no amounts:\n  - \"Next 12 months: 10 dates\"\n  - \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Clark Public Utilities bill · You added\"\n  - \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Voter registration must arrive by · Official\"\n  - \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct · City of Vancouver water bill · You added\"\n00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light: the light 02 artboard, desaturated. Per C8, print one caption under each grid row:\n- place-file rows: \"Lanes by label; rules by bar; city provenance by hollow mark and caption; projected by dashed keyline and caption; window by wash plus legend.\"\n- widget-large and gallery-sample: \"Lanes by place name; provenance by shape plus legend words; rules by bar plus 'Official rule'.\"\n- empty-checked: \"Empty by the word 'Checked'.\"\n00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) x-place-file on iOS 393: the band under the place file header, with its rows.\n- (b) x-place-file on Android 412: PLACE B with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- (c) f7-widget-gallery on iOS: V3 in the gallery.\n- Under the crops, in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget → V2 widget large.\"\nConsistency check (batch 3). Update only a crop that differs, and nothing else on those artboards. Check the paint order, 1pt halos, dark raised wash, dashed edge and numeral token.\n- The V3 phone-form crops on 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window (light and dark) must match 01-anatomy-phone.\n- Crop (c) on 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context must match the 03-desktop-exact-day form: a 128px label column, 60px Oct and Nov columns, and the You cluster at 23 Oct with \"4\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The summary sentence is the label. The rows are the table, and the caption says so.\n- Native: one element with adjustable month cells (readouts on 01).\n- Web: one image, with the summary as its text alternative.\n- Marks are never targets. Provenance is shown by shape, rules by bar.\n\nCOPY: Lane labels are exactly \"You · Your city · Your county · Your state\"; widgets use place names. Deadlines say \"must arrive by\". Dates show the weekday, and summaries and widget lines add the relative count beyond tomorrow.\n\nPLATFORMS: Phones group items by month; at 768px and wider, items sit on exact days. Everything else is identical.\n\nINSTEAD OF (contract doNot, plus the bar rule)\n- No heatmap: marks with count numerals in labelled lanes, because intensity hides what the dates are and who set them.\n- No collapsing the lanes: the source of a rule matters as much as its date.\n- No day-accurate dots on phones: one group per month with a count, because 27pt columns cannot place days.\n- No dot for a county or state rule: a full-lane bar, because the strip and the band must encode the same data the same way.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"YearBand / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: desktop-exact-day and desktop-place-b-inset (03, light), widget-large-tinted (04, light and dark), gallery-android (04, light and dark), widget-text-fallback (05, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a YearBand part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: list every quoted string above that is not in the fixtures or the contract. Include the October and November readouts, the widget text lines, \"Projected after Dec 2026\" (widget), and the specimen items \"lease notice deadline\" and \"water-heater warranty ends\".\n- B. Assumptions:\n  - The rhythm is not counted in \"N dates\" (the strip counts pickups).\n  - County rules are bars.\n  - The desktop label column is 128px.\n  - The desktop collision rule uses drawn extents (mark or bar plus numeral) with a 2px gap, so the four Oct–Nov You items become one mark with \"4\". The holiday-move threshold stays at 14px.\n  - The today rule paints under marks, bars and numerals, which carry a 1pt halo.\n  - The wash carries the window. On phones the dashed edge also rises 4pt above the lanes.\n  - PLACE B shows only its next Thursday plus the Thanksgiving move (the Camas notice covers every Thursday route).\n  - The dark window wash is raised #1E293B.\n  - Every widget specimen is HOME A. The widget draws no shaded window. Its legend keys only the shapes it draws (no \"● Official\" in the fixture), and the bar is keyed \"Official rule\".\n  - The widget budget is 268 of 322pt. The Android picker preview is the widget at 75% in a 4×3-cell tile.\n  - captionMedium 12/16/500 and widgetCaption 11/16/400 are added to the type scale for this component.\n- C. Normalisations:\n  - The contract summary \"Next 12 months: 9 dates. Next: Furnace warranty ends Nov 14.\" → the fixture data.\n  - The contract's widget lanes used Camas (PLACE B's city); HOME A uses Vancouver.\n  - Summaries and widget lines carry the relative count, and the widget line reads \"Voter registration must arrive by\".\n  - \"As of Mon 7:40 AM\" → \"As of 7:40 AM\", matching 00a.\n- D. Deviations: the contract draws only statewide rules as bars; county rules are bars too, to match FourteenDayStrip.\n- E. Open question: native month readouts give absolute dates only (\"due Friday 23 October\"). Should they stay absolute, or add \"in 4 days\"?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 9 artboards exist with the exact names below. The 02 grid is complete (5 × 5, drawn as two grids, one reason per n/a) and fits 1440.\n- V1 (HOME A and PLACE B), V2–V4 and all five states are drawn.\n- The 848px desktop grid and the 268pt widget budget add up.\n- No mark, bar or numeral overlaps another, and the today rule never crosses a mark.\n- Rules are bars in every lane and at every size. Every mark is at least 3:1. The window wash is visible in dark.\n- Widget text is at least 11pt and prints provenance words, including in the AX lines.\n- The FourteenDayStrip crops match their stated forms. Notes holds the YearBand entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light\n2. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light\n4. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light\n5. 00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light\n6. 00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light\nBatch 2:\n7. 00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light\n8. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n9. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · dark\n10. 00b · Notes (append YearBand)\nBatch 3 (consistency check; update an artboard only if its crop differs):\n11. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light (phone form)\n12. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark (phone form)\n13. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light (crop (c), desktop exact-day form)"
          },
          {
            "id": "00b-05",
            "component": "SlotMeter",
            "artboards": [
              "00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light",
              "00b · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00b-05: SlotMeter. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): An honest, dated Founding Neighbor window. When anything is uncertain, it fails closed.\nUSED IN (print it): f9-founding-meter-preview, f9-block-founders-panel, f9-nearby-cells-map, f9-verification-promise-copy, f9-invite-rewards-card.\nTYPE (one style this component adds to the house scale): bodyMedium 16/24/500. iOS AX5 → 53, Android 200% → 28.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part)\n- Heading \"Founding Neighbor\" in bodyMedium text.primary.\n- Segments: five bounded capsules, each 40 × 12pt, radius pill, with 4pt gaps (216pt in total). Taken segments come first, from the left.\n  - Taken: solid primary.600 fill with a 1.5px primary.700 edge (#38BDF8 dark, per C6).\n  - Open: surface.base fill with a 45° diagonal hatch (1.5px lines every 4pt) in text.secondary, and a 1.5px text.secondary edge.\n  - Fixture: 2 taken, 3 open.\n- Numeral label, 8pt right of the segments, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"3 of 5 open\". This count of open slots is the one sanctioned \"N of M\" here. It counts what is left and never measures progress.\n- Elapsed bar, 8pt below the segments: 4 × 216pt, radius pill.\n  - The elapsed part is solid text.secondary. The remaining part is an unfilled 1px text.secondary outline (never a border token).\n  - The window opened Mon 5 Oct and closes Tue 27 Oct. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct, so the elapsed part is 138pt. Callout: \"elapsed 138pt of 216pt; decorative\".\n  - The bar is decorative and hidden from assistive tech; the date pill carries the meaning.\n- Date pill, 8pt below the bar: a neutral 24pt pill with a surface.sunken fill, holding a 12pt calendar glyph and \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" in label 13/18, both in text.strong.\n- RankBadge (part of this specimen, published only with SlotMeter). It appears only in V2 (HOME A), because a Block Founder rank cannot exist on an unclaimed place.\n  - It always sits below the meter, at least 24pt away, never in the same row or sentence as the tier.\n  - It is a separate squared shape: 128 × 64pt, radius md 8, surface.sunken fill, a 1px text.secondary edge, 12pt horizontal padding (104pt of text width) and 8pt vertical padding.\n  - It holds the overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\" in overline 11/16/600 caps +0.5 text.strong, then \"#3\" in h2 24/32/600 text.primary.\n  - At default size the overline sits on one line (it measures about 91–100pt, inside 104pt). It breaks as \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\" only at AX sizes, where the badge grows vertically.\n- R6 contrast table on 01: primary.600 fill on base, primary.700 on base, text.secondary on base, text.strong on sunken.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys in brackets)\n- V1 preview card [preview-card] (f9-founding-meter-preview, PLACE B): the heading, meter and date pill, plus the caption \"A badge — no money or fee change. You can still claim this address.\" in bodySmall text.secondary. No RankBadge.\n- V2 Block Founders panel [block-founders-panel] (f9-block-founders-panel, HOME A): the meter and date pill in the tier section, and the RankBadge \"#3\" in a separate rank section below.\n- V3 wall line replacement [wall-line]: body text.primary only, with no meter: \"3 Founding Neighbor slots are still open on this block.\"\n\nSTATES (column keys in brackets)\n- open [open].\n- closed [closed]: the meter is absent. Zero open slots counts as closed, so an empty meter is never drawn. In V2, only the tier section is removed. The rank section with \"#3\" stays, because the RankBadge is a separate earned shape that the founder already holds.\n- lookup failed [lookup-failed]: the entire card is absent. In V2, both the tier and rank sections are removed, because the rank comes from the same failed lookup. In V3, the line is absent.\n- Closed and lookup-failed cells are absence specimens per C5: draw the host context around the gap, plus the dashed gutter annotation box beside each removed section.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light:\n- V1 at true size, with every callout.\n- Below the V1 card, the RankBadge as a separate labelled part, with the gutter note \"RankBadge · shown in V2 (HOME A) only\".\n- A taken segment and an open segment, magnified 4×.\n- The contrast table.\n00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n- Rows: preview-card · block-founders-panel · wall-line. Columns: open · closed · lookup-failed.\n- Absence cells:\n  - preview-card (closed and lookup-failed): the PLACE B preview without the card.\n  - block-founders-panel, closed: the panel without its tier section, with the rank section and \"#3\" still drawn.\n  - block-founders-panel, lookup-failed: the panel without its tier and rank sections.\n  - wall-line (closed and lookup-failed): the cells-map wall without the line.\n- Under the grid, one extra absence specimen [extra key zero-open], with the gutter label \"0 of 5 open → treated as closed\".\n- Dark:\n  - The taken fill stays primary.600 (3.57:1 on dark raised), with a #38BDF8 edge.\n  - The open fill becomes dark base #0F172A. The hatch uses dark text.secondary, at 6.96:1 on that open fill.\n  - The open edges and the elapsed bar use dark text.secondary, at 5.71:1 on dark raised.\n00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light: one frame with three labelled encodings side by side:\n- The SlotMeter (solid vs hatched, plus \"3 of 5 open\").\n- The PublicPointMap cells-map bucket labels: four small rectangles with a 1px text.secondary outline and a 70% surface.base fill, printing \"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" and \"16+\" in label 13/18 text.primary.\n- The 00a · ProvenanceMark legend \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\", with drawn marks.\n- Caption: \"Solid vs hatched means taken vs open. Filled vs hollow means provenance only.\"\n00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5, with the RankBadge drawn as a separate part below it:\n  - The segments keep their size, and the numeral label moves below them.\n  - The date pill grows and wraps, becoming a rounded rectangle (radius lg 12).\n  - The RankBadge grows vertically, with \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\" on two lines.\n- The same at Android 200%.\n- V1 and V2 desaturated, captioned \"Taken vs open by texture plus numeral.\"\n00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light: five mini crops.\n- (a) f9-founding-meter-preview on web-390: V1 on the PLACE B preview.\n- (b) f9-block-founders-panel on iOS 393: V2.\n- (c) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 as the wall line.\n- (d) f9-verification-promise-copy on iOS 393 and (e) f9-invite-rewards-card on iOS 393: each is one line naming the tier, \"Founding Neighbor · 3 of 5 open · Closes Tue 27 Oct\", and never the rank in the same sentence.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The meter is one element. Its spoken label, printed on 01: \"Founding Neighbor slots: 3 of 5 open, closes Tuesday 27 October.\"\n- The RankBadge reads \"Block Founder number 3\".\n- Taken vs open is shown by solid vs hatched, plus the numeral.\n- The meter is not a target. Any card action is 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- Absent states are silent: nothing is announced.\n\nCOPY\n- Never write \"permanent\" unless the data model guarantees it.\n- Rank (\"Block Founder #3\") and tier (\"Founding Neighbor\") never share a sentence.\n- Closing dates are dates, never \"closes in 6 days\" or hh:mm.\n\nPLATFORMS: identical on iOS, Android and web; only the target minimums differ.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of hollow segments for open slots, draw hatched segments with an ink edge, because hollow means \"on record, not confirmed\".\n- Instead of a warning-tinted pill, draw a neutral surface.sunken pill, because a badge deadline is not an alarm.\n- Instead of an hh:mm or \"closes in 6 days\" countdown, print \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because live countdowns manufacture urgency.\n- Instead of a border-token fill for the remaining time, draw a text.secondary outline, because border tokens are never the only edge of a segment.\n- Instead of a 2px elapsed bar, draw a 4pt bar, because a 1px outline cannot be drawn around a 2px shape.\n- Instead of an empty meter at 0 open, or a meter after a failed lookup, render nothing, because the meter must never promise a slot the system cannot honour.\n- Instead of a disc or ring for the rank, draw the squared RankBadge, because discs and rings mean provenance.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list on Notes G)\n- Each 02 cell: \"SlotMeter / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\". Absence cells are published too, as the rule that nothing renders.\n- Extras: zero-open (02, light and dark), rank-badge (01, light), ax5 (04, light).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a SlotMeter part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: list every quoted string above that is not in the fixtures or the contract, including the normalised \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" and the normalised spoken label.\n- B. Assumptions:\n  - The window opened Mon 5 Oct and closes Tue 27 Oct, with 2 of 5 slots taken.\n  - The RankBadge is 128 × 64pt so the overline fits one line at default size (104pt text width). It breaks and grows only at AX sizes.\n  - The RankBadge appears only in V2 (HOME A).\n  - When the window is closed, the panel keeps the rank section. When the lookup fails, the rank section is removed too, because it comes from the same lookup.\n  - bodyMedium 16/24/500 is added to the type scale.\n- C. Normalisations: the contract's \"Closes Tue, Sep 22\" → \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because Tue 22 Sep is before TODAY and that window would be closed. The spoken \"closes Tuesday September 22\" follows it.\n- D. Deviations: the contract's \"2px elapsed bar\" is drawn 4pt tall with an outlined remaining part, because a 1px outline cannot surround a 2px bar.\n- E. Open question (add it to YearBand's relative-count question): \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" has no relative count, although dates beyond tomorrow normally add one (\"in 8 days\"). This follows the no-countdown rule. Should it stay that way?\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 6 artboards exist with the exact names below, and the 02 grid is complete (3 × 3).\n- In the closed, lookup-failed and 0-open cells, the meter renders nothing, and each is drawn as an absence specimen. Only the closed V2 cell keeps the RankBadge.\n- Taken vs open is solid vs hatched with an ink edge. No segment is hollow, and nothing is warning-tinted.\n- \"N of M\" appears only as \"3 of 5 open\" and in the \"0 of 5 open\" annotation. No countdown appears.\n- The RankBadge overline is on one line at default size, and the RankBadge never appears with V1. Rank and tier never share a row or sentence.\n- 05 shows five crops, each in a named frame. Notes holds the SlotMeter entries.\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light\n4. 00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n5. 00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light\nBatch 2:\n6. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n7. 00b · Notes (append SlotMeter)"
