            "promptText": "Component 00b-06: PublicPointMap. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print it): Shows exactly where neighbours see a post, drawn at true scale from the server's stable public point.\nUSED IN (print it): f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map.\n\nFRAMES: 02 cells are drawn at iOS 393 geometry (326pt content). Controls reserve 96pt (148pt for V3). The Android values, 104dp (160dp for V3), apply on 03.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy, with a callout on every part; the address is HOME A and the viewer is Maya Chen)\n- V1 stack, top to bottom: map thumb · 8pt · caption · 8pt · controls. In context only, the hidden-from-neighbors row sits between the caption and the controls, with 8pt above and below it.\n- Map thumb: 16:9, 326 × 183pt, radius md 8, 1px text.secondary edge. The frame is centred on the public pin.\n  - Base map, neutral tokens only, no brand tint: land is surface.sunken; streets are 4pt surface.base lines with 1px text.secondary casing.\n  - Street labels: caption 12/16 text.strong with a 2px surface.base halo: \"NE 18th St\", \"NE 138th Ave\", \"NE 23rd St\".\n- Public pin: one 24pt teardrop in text.primary, 2px surface.base halo, 6pt surface.base centre.\n- Pin label chip, above the pin: a pill in surface.base, 1px text.secondary edge, shadow md, reading exactly \"What neighbors see\" in label 13/18 text.primary.\n- Scale bar, bottom left, on an 80% surface.base plate: a 1.5px text.primary line with end ticks; labels \"0\", \"0.1\", \"0.2 mi\" in caption 12/16 text.primary on the plate. The thumb spans about 0.8 mi, so 0.2 mi = 81pt.\n- Caption, bodySmall text.primary, the map's one-sentence summary, used exactly: \"Neighbors see your posts at this spot, the same spot every time, about 0.3 mi from your address.\"\n- Hidden-from row (f9-privacy-mirror; draw only in context): \"Hidden from neighbors: your street address, your home on the map\".\n- Controls:\n  - Each button is 44 × 44pt on iOS and web and 48 × 48dp on Android: radius md 8, surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary edge, 20pt text.primary glyph. The accessible names are the words below.\n  - One two-row cluster at every size. Left edge of the content width: a zoom column, \"Zoom in\" (+) above \"Zoom out\" (−), 8pt apart. Right edge: a 3 × 2 arrow pad with 8pt gaps. Top row: \"Move map up\" (↑) in the middle slot. Bottom row: \"Move map left\" (←), \"Move map down\" (↓), \"Move map right\" (→).\n  - Size: the pad is 148pt wide on iOS and web (3 × 44 + 2 × 8) and 160dp on Android. The cluster needs at least 208pt (224dp) with a 16pt minimum gap between column and pad, so it fits 326pt. It is 96pt tall on iOS and web and 104dp on Android.\n  - Disabled buttons: fill unchanged, still focusable, with a reason. Light: glyph and edge in text.muted. Dark: glyph and edge in #475569 (an added dark value, listed on Notes D), so disabled stays distinct from the enabled #94A3B8 edge. Disabled controls are exempt from the contrast minimums; the reason text carries the meaning.\n  - Focus order: Zoom in, Zoom out, Move map up, Move map left, Move map down, Move map right, then List cells when present.\n- Cells-map parts (V3):\n  - V3 stack, top to bottom: map 326 × 326 (the same base map at the same zoom, with streets and street labels, no pin, no chip, scale bar bottom left) · 8pt · summary line · 4pt · FreshnessLine · 8pt · controls · 8pt · List cells.\n  - Grid: three columns and three rows of 108/110/108pt, no gaps; neighbouring cells share one 1px text.secondary outline. Each cell has a 70% surface.base fill over the base map.\n  - Each cell prints its bucket label centred in label 13/18 text.primary: \"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" or \"16+\".\n  - The user's cell gets a 2px primary.600 inner outline inside its rectangle (the contract calls it a ring; #38BDF8 in dark mode), and \"Your cell\" in caption text.primary, centred 4pt below its bucket label.\n  - \"List cells\": a text button (primary.700; #38BDF8 in dark mode), left-aligned, 44pt tall (48dp on Android). The V3 controls block is therefore 148pt tall on iOS and web (96 + 8 + 44) and 160dp on Android (104 + 8 + 48).\n- Contrast table on 01, R6 rows, each labelled with its kind and threshold:\n  - text.secondary on base · text (\"Simplified map\") and edges · 4.5:1\n  - text.secondary on sunken · outline (map edge, street casing) · 3:1\n  - text.strong on sunken · text (street labels) · 4.5:1\n  - text.primary on sunken · text and pin · 4.5:1\n  - primary.700 on base · text (\"See the spot\", \"List cells\") · 4.5:1\n  - primary.600 on the 70% base cell fill (light) · outline · 3:1\n  - #38BDF8 on the dark cell fill · outline · 3:1\n\nPENDING DECISION: range box R (not a variant)\n- The ±0.005° box is centred on the home by definition, so drawing it may reveal the home. Until the founder answers the range-box question on Notes E, draw R only on 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light, inside a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation frame labelled \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\". Draw it on no other artboard and never publish it.\n- How to draw it: the real box, about 1.11 km tall × 0.78 km wide (about 0.69 × 0.49 mi), as a 1.5px dashed text.secondary rectangle with no fill. Use a zoom where the 326pt thumb spans about 1.6 mi, so the box is about 141 × 99pt and fits the 183pt-tall thumb with a margin. The scale bar reads \"0\", \"0.25\", \"0.5 mi\" (0.25 mi = 51pt). The box sits off-centre in the frame.\n\nVARIANTS (row keys in brackets)\n- V1 privacy mirror [privacy-mirror]: as in ANATOMY.\n- V2 composer one-liner [composer-one-liner]: a row at least 44pt tall with a 16pt pin glyph in text.secondary, the bodySmall text.primary line \"Neighbors see this post at the same spot as your other posts, about 0.3 mi from your address.\", and a trailing 44pt text button \"See the spot\" (primary.700; #38BDF8 in dark mode) that opens V1. No map is drawn.\n- V3 cells map [cells-map]: the V3 stack from ANATOMY.\n  - Cell names and buckets, user's cell in the centre:\n    - top row: North-west 0 · North 1–5 · North-east 1–5\n    - middle row: West 6–15 · Your cell 6–15 · East 16+\n    - bottom row: South-west 0 · South 0 · South-east 1–5\n  - Summary line, bodySmall text.primary: \"14 neighbor posts in your cell in 30 days. 3 Pantopus posts not counted.\"\n  - 00a · FreshnessLine: \"Updated 12m ago\".\n\nSTATES (column keys in brackets)\n- ready [ready].\n- loading [loading]: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton panel: a surface.sunken 16:9 block (square for V3), with the controls drawn as outlines at their reserved height. V1 loading shows the caption as text. V2 shows its text immediately. Static under Reduce Motion.\n- vector fallback [vector-fallback]: when tiles fail, land is surface.base and streets are 1px text.secondary lines. \"Simplified map\" in caption text.secondary sits 4pt above the map. Everything else stays: on V1 the street labels, pin, chip, scale bar and caption; on V3 the same cells, bucket labels, \"Your cell\" outline, scale bar and text lines.\n- offline [offline]:\n  - With a cache: the cached map. The pan and zoom buttons are disabled, with the reason caption \"Moving the map needs a connection.\" in caption text.secondary.\n    - V1 stack: map · 4pt · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · 8pt · caption · 8pt · controls · 4pt · reason caption.\n    - V3 stack: the V3 stack with \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" in place of \"Updated 12m ago\", and the reason caption 4pt below the controls, then 8pt, then \"List cells\", which stays enabled and lists the cached buckets.\n  - With no cache: the reserved map slot (16:9, square for V3) is a surface.sunken block with the centred line \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\" in body text.strong. All buttons are drawn disabled, including \"List cells\"; the centred line is their reason.\n    - V1: the caption stays (map slot · 8pt · caption · 8pt · controls).\n    - V3: the summary line and FreshnessLine are not drawn, because there are no counts without data (map slot · 8pt · controls · 8pt · List cells).\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light: V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including the controls cluster geometry and the contrast table. Beside it, the pending-decision frame holding R.\n00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark: a grid.\n- Rows: privacy-mirror · composer-one-liner · cells-map. Columns: ready · loading · vector-fallback · offline.\n- privacy-mirror × offline and cells-map × offline: the cached form above the no-cache form in the cell.\n- composer-one-liner: loading shows the line as in ready; vector-fallback prints \"n/a — no map drawn\"; offline shows the line unchanged (the composer owns the offline notice).\n- Print the map text equivalents (see ACCESSIBILITY) under the V1 and V3 ready cells.\n- Dark base map: land is dark surface.raised; streets are dark surface.base with dark text.secondary casing; the pin core is #E5E7EB with a #0F172A halo; cell fill is 70% dark surface.base; the user's cell outline is #38BDF8; disabled buttons use #475569.\n00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light: V3 on Android 412 with its controls. Beside it, the \"List cells\" view: nine 48dp rows, each giving cell name · bucket · lock state. The locked tier states only its requirement.\n- \"Your cell · 6–15 · Detail open\"\n- \"North-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"North of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"North-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"West of your cell · 6–15 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"East of your cell · 16+ · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n- \"South-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n- V1 at iOS AX5. The map keeps its 326 × 183 size, and the caption grows and wraps. The chip moves under the map as the text line \"What neighbors see: the pin on this map\". Street labels and scale-bar labels stay at their base size, because map labels are graphic geometry under the AX5 rule. The glyph buttons keep their size and the two-row cluster.\n- V3 at iOS AX5: the map, cells, bucket labels and \"Your cell\" stay at base size; the summary line, FreshnessLine and \"List cells\" grow and wrap. The List cells view carries the scaled text.\n- V1 at Android 200%, with the same rules.\n- V1 and V3 desaturated, captioned \"Pin by shape and label; buckets by printed numbers; your cell by outline width and words.\"\n00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light: three mini crops.\n- (a) f9-privacy-mirror on iOS 393: V1 with the hidden-from-neighbors row, below a neighbour-view feed-card header reading \"Maya C. · near NE 18th St · 2h\".\n- (b) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 with the summary line.\n- (c) the f9-privacy-mirror composer entry on web-390: V2 above a post field.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Map text equivalents:\n  - V1: \"Map. One pin marks where neighbors see your posts, about 0.3 miles from your address. Your home is not shown. Scale bar 0.2 miles.\"\n  - V3: \"Cells map. Your cell: 6 to 15 posts in 30 days.\" It is followed by the List cells view.\n- On web, the focused map also accepts +, − and the arrow keys.\n- Buttons never auto-hide while assistive tech is on. The pin and cells are not targets.\n\nCOPY\n- Never write \"re-rolled every time you post\".\n- Cells-map counts say \"Pantopus posts\", never \"curator\".\n\nPLATFORMS: identical geometry on all three; only the button minimums in Controls differ.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a 150 m ring around the home, draw the single public pin, because the real offset area is about 12 times larger and a ring centred on the home reveals it.\n- Instead of a home marker \"for orientation\", show street labels only, because a screenshot must never locate the home.\n- Instead of a blurred, fogged or locked map or list, draw everything and state the requirement in words, because a hidden map is a carrot, not information.\n- Instead of a lightness-only density ramp, print the bucket label in every cell, because adjacent ramp steps are only 1.16 to 1.66:1 apart.\n- Instead of one long controls row, draw the zoom column and arrow pad, because six 48dp buttons do not fit in 326pt.\n- Instead of pinch and drag only, give every movement a labelled button, because gestures alone exclude switch and keyboard users.\n\nPUBLISH NAMES (list them on Notes G)\n- Each drawn 02 cell: \"PublicPointMap / <row key> / <column key> / <light|dark>\". The two offline cells with a no-cache form also publish \"PublicPointMap / <row key> / offline-no-cache / <light|dark>\".\n- Extras: \"PublicPointMap / list-cells / light\" (from 03) and \"PublicPointMap / ax5 / light\" (from 04).\n\nNOTES (last batch: append a PublicPointMap part to each section of 00b · Notes)\n- A. Invented strings: the street labels; \"0.1\", \"0.2 mi\", \"0.25\", \"0.5 mi\"; the V2 line; \"See the spot\"; \"Your cell\"; \"List cells\"; the six control names; the summary line; the nine List cells rows; \"Simplified map\"; \"Moving the map needs a connection.\"; \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\"; \"What neighbors see: the pin on this map\"; both map text equivalents; \"Hidden from neighbors: your street address, your home on the map\"; the feed-card header \"Maya C. · near NE 18th St · 2h\"; \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\"; the FreshnessLine strings \"Updated 12m ago\" and \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" (the pattern comes from 00a; these values are invented); the greyscale caption \"Pin by shape and label; buckets by printed numbers; your cell by outline width and words.\"\n- B. Assumptions: the nine cell names and buckets; the two-row controls cluster with an arrow pad (the contract names only zoom buttons; pan buttons follow the brief's rule that pan and zoom work by buttons); the no-cache offline line; with no cache, V3 drops the summary line and FreshnessLine; offline \"List cells\" lists cached buckets and is disabled with no cache; the summary counts only the user's cell; map and cell labels do not scale at AX5.\n- C. Normalisations: none for PublicPointMap.\n- D. Deviations: the added pan buttons (see B). The cells map is square (326 × 326), not the contract's 16:9 thumb, so the 3 × 3 grid has square cells. Dark disabled buttons use #475569, a value added to the C6 dark list because C6 has no dark text.muted.\n- E. Open question: the optional ±0.005° range box has the home at its geometric centre, even when the frame is off-centre. Should it exist at all? Until this is answered, it appears only in the pending-decision frame on 01 and is not published.\n- F. n/a: composer-one-liner × vector-fallback — no map drawn.\n- G. The PublicPointMap publish names above.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 6 artboards exist with the exact names below; the 02 grid is complete in light and dark (3 × 4, one reason per n/a, both offline forms for V1 and V3).\n- None of the INSTEAD OF forms appears anywhere, and R appears only inside the pending-decision frame on 01.\n- V1 and V3 follow their stacks in every state; no counts or freshness appear in V3 with no cache; the controls match the 01 callout; the List cells view has nine rows matching the nine cells.\n- Notes holds the PublicPointMap entries in A–G (C reads \"none\").\n\nARTBOARDS AND BATCH PLAN (6 artboards plus the Notes update, exact names, in drawing order; draw one batch, then stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n1. 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light\n2. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light\n3. 00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light\n4. 00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n5. 00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light\nBatch 2:\n6. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n7. 00b · Notes (append PublicPointMap)"
