            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-01: DateRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: DateRow. This message is the complete DateRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). One dated fact in a list. Its row grammar is shared by the 14-day strip list, the calendar agenda, the place file Dates section and reminder rows.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f5-today-calendar-strip · f3-household-calendar · x-place-file · x-date-sheet · f3-household-notifications · f7-today-widget.\n\nEXTRA STAND-INS FOR THIS COMPONENT (label each \"stand-in\", per R11)\n- KindGlyph: a 24pt line icon with a 2pt stroke in text.strong, with one distinct drawing per kind: garbage, recycling, garbage+recycling, notice deadline, warranty ends, HOA dues, property-tax due, property-tax appeal, voter registration. Never one generic calendar icon.\n- SourceCaption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"authority · scope · as-of\". It wraps and never ellipsises the authority.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V3a at 2x for callouts ①–⑦ and ⑩. Beside it, draw V3c in S3 (done) at 2x for callouts ⑧ and ⑨.\n① Row: minimum height 56pt, padding 16pt horizontal and 12pt vertical, on surface.base. The whole row is the target: draw the dashed target rectangle around it.\n② Leading KindGlyph, 24pt, text.strong, top-aligned with the title, with a 12pt (spacing.3) gap after it.\n③ Title: body 16/24/400, text.primary. It wraps and is never truncated.\n④ Line 2: caption 12/16 text.secondary, the relative date then the absolute date, e.g. \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" stand alone, with no absolute date after them. An approximate date reads \"about Dec 2026\".\n⑤ SourceCaption short form (authority · scope). It continues line 2 after a middot, or wraps to line 3.\n⑥ Trailing ProvenanceMark S (16pt), vertically centred, with 8pt (spacing.2) between it and the text. It is not a target.\n⑦ Optional chip after the title reading \"Statewide — WA\", in ScopeChip geometry (24pt pill, surface.sunken fill, label 13/18 text.strong) with a 12pt state-outline glyph. It states coverage, not visibility.\n⑧ Annual rows and self-entered rows: a 2px identity.home rule on the leading edge, full row height, plus a recurrence caption on the last line in caption text.secondary (\"Every year\", \"Every month\" or \"Does not repeat\").\n⑨ Done tick: a 16pt stroke check before the title. It is a bare stroke, not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark.\n⑩ Web menu callout: \"web menu: a row menu button (20px ellipsis, 44px target) after the mark, holding Edit · Remind me · Where this comes from · Mark done\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\nV1 pickup. Home A as of TODAY, before Maya confirmed her pickup day. The title names the bins.\n- V1a · pickup-both: garbage+recycling glyph · title \"Recycling and garbage\" · line 2 \"Tomorrow · Waste Connections · city schedule\" · hollow mark.\n- V1b · pickup-garbage: garbage glyph · \"Garbage only\" · \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct · Waste Connections · city schedule\" · hollow mark.\n- V2 · holiday-moved (Place B, Camas): garbage glyph · \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\" · \"in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\" · hollow mark.\nV3 deadline. The weekday is always shown, and received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n- V3a · deadline-voter: voter registration glyph · \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · chip \"Statewide — WA\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Washington Secretary of State · statewide\" · filled mark.\n- V3b · deadline-notice: notice deadline glyph · \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · last line \"Does not repeat · Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V3c · deadline-tax: property-tax due glyph · \"Property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov · Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\" · last line \"Every year\" · filled mark · identity.home rule.\n- V4 · conditional-rule: property-tax appeal glyph · \"Property-tax appeal window\" · \"Closes Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Clark County Board of Equalization · county-wide\" · last line \"Every year\" · filled mark · identity.home rule.\n- V5 · reminder: warranty glyph · \"Reminder: Water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec\" · \"in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec · You added this\" · last line \"Does not repeat\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V5x · reminder-approx (fixture delta: the warranty date was entered as approximate): warranty glyph · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"about Dec 2026\" · last line \"Does not repeat\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n- V6 · money: HOA dues glyph · \"HOA dues\" · amount \"$285.00\" in bodyMedium with tabular figures, right-aligned and placed before the mark · \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov · You added this\" · last line \"Every month\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2a, S2b, SF, S3, S4)\n- S1 · default.\n- S2 · highlighted: arrival from a notification, per R8 (dark: D1), with accessibility focus moved onto the row. Drawn as two columns:\n  - S2a · highlighted-arrival: infoBg wash, 4pt leading bar, and the focus ring 2px outside the row.\n  - S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; the focus ring remains.\n- SF · focused: the R8 focus ring on the whole row.\n- S3 · done: the ⑨ tick before the title; title and line 2 in text.secondary; line 2 prefixed \"You marked this done ·\". Done is personal. On every row, including the civic V3a row, it stays Only you and is never shown to the household.\n- S4 · permission-hidden: the row is not rendered at all.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 26 cells)\n- S1 and S3: V1a, V1b, V2, V3a, V3b, V3c, V4, V5, V5x and V6 (20 cells).\n- S2a and S2b: V1a and V3a (4 cells).\n- SF: V3a, so it sits directly beside V3a S2a and V3a S2b (1 cell).\n- S4: one cell, in the V6 row: a three-row list of V1a, [absent V6], V3a. The rows above and below close the gap, with no placeholder and no ghost row. An annotation arrow outside the list reads \"row absent: viewer lacks permission\" (1 cell).\n- Outside the V3a S3 cell, annotate: \"done stays Only you\".\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. Highlight uses D1. The \"Statewide — WA\" chip fill uses D4. Marks and the done tick use dark text.secondary; each KindGlyph uses dark text.strong.\n- The identity.home rule keeps its hue (D7). Beside the first one, caption \"identity.home on dark base 5.42:1\".\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V3a and V6 in both columns.\n- The title wraps to as many lines as it needs.\n- The \"Statewide — WA\" chip drops below the title.\n- Line 2 wraps at middots.\n- The amount and the mark move below the text block: the amount first, then the mark, scaled to about 28pt.\n- The KindGlyph scales to 32pt and stays top-aligned.\n- The identity.home rule stays full height.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- provenance = disc vs ring vs disc with knocked-out tick.\n- done = stroke tick + \"You marked this done\".\n- highlighted = 4pt leading bar.\n- annual = 2px rule + \"Every year\".\n- kind = KindGlyph shape.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The whole row is one element and one target (minimum 56pt), read in visual order. The mark and the glyph are not targets.\n- Spoken pattern: \"<title>, <line 2 as shown>, <authority, scope>, <mark name>\". The label speaks only the dates the row shows, so \"Tomorrow\" is spoken as \"tomorrow\" with no absolute date. Example: \"Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Waste Connections city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- Done rows start with \"You marked this done\". Done stays Only you.\n- Custom actions: Edit · Remind me · Where this comes from · Mark done. On web they sit in the ⑩ row menu button.\n- Non-colour encoding: the glyph shape carries the kind, the mark shape carries provenance, the leading bar carries highlight, and the words carry done.\n- Contrast: text at least 4.5:1; mark at least 3:1 (text.secondary on base, 4.83:1).\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- For deadlines, the title names the action: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\n- Received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n- Dates are spelled out with the weekday (\"Mon 26 Oct\"), never 10/26/2026.\n- Beyond tomorrow, the relative count comes first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Conditional rules (V4) are exempt from the relative count.\n- Source captions carry a scope word: \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\".\n- Pickup titles use exactly \"Recycling and garbage\" or \"Garbage only\".\n- Holiday moves read \"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", never \"delayed\" or \"cancelled\".\n- \"I did this\" reads \"You marked this done\" and stays Only you.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences, except that web adds the ⑩ row menu button (R12).\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of red text or an overdue chip on an annual date that has passed, draw the next occurrence with its \"Every year\" caption. Annual dates never inherit overdue red.\n- Instead of one generic calendar icon for every row, draw the specific KindGlyph. The glyph is what tells kinds apart without colour.\n- Instead of a greyed placeholder row for a date the viewer may not see, draw nothing. A ghost row leaks that something exists.\n- Instead of a numeric date like 10/26/2026, draw \"Mon 26 Oct\". The weekday is what people plan by.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops, each with the legend line and the ScopeChip (R13).\n1. f5-today-calendar-strip · ios, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; a card (radius lg) holding a 14-cell strip drawn only as a plain outline (the strip is specified on another board), above rows V1a, V3a and V6; a foot row \"+ Add a date\"; the legend line. Annotate the strip: \"strip cells are not targets; the rows below are\".\n2. x-place-file · web-1440, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; section overline \"DATES\"; rows V3b, V4 and V5, each with its ⑩ row menu button; the legend line.\n3. f3-household-calendar · android, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; an agenda with the day header \"Tue 20 Oct\" and row V1a in S2a; the legend line.\n\nNOTES (add a \"DateRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"city schedule\" · \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide\" · \"Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" as a caption · the \"Reminder:\" title prefix · \"Every year\" · \"Every month\" · \"Does not repeat\".\n- Fixture deltas: V1a and V1b show Home A as of TODAY, before Maya confirmed Tuesday (hollow) · V5x: the warranty date was entered as approximate (\"about Dec 2026\") instead of Sat 12 Dec 2026 · V6: HOA dues appears both as a household bill (BillRow) and as a self-added monthly date.\n- Contract conflicts: \"Statewide — WA\" drawn in ScopeChip geometry as a coverage chip, instead of one of ScopeChip's two exact strings · highlighted drawn as a wash plus a leading bar, instead of contract \"wash + outline\", so it never looks like focus.\n- Assumptions: V2 has a hollow mark on an official city holiday move, because Place B's schedule is unconfirmed · V5x carries the identity.home rule and \"Does not repeat\", like every other self-entered row.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · DateRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (created in this component's Turn 2)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then create 00c · Notes with its board section (R14) and the DateRow section above. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five DateRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label, and 00c · Notes exists as the last artboard.\n- 01 shows callouts ①–⑩ with size and token, the dashed row target, and the five panels with the text above.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 26 listed cells, with every row and column labelled \"<code> · <key>\" plus its printed key, and every cell captioned \"DateRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- V3a SF sits beside V3a S2a and S2b, and bar, ring and wash are each distinct. S2a shows bar and ring without touching.\n- The done tick is a bare stroke check; the YOU ADDED mark is a disc with a knocked-out tick; every mark is at least 12pt with a 1.5px ring stroke.\n- Every row has its own KindGlyph, and no row is red or carries an overdue chip.\n- The S4 cell shows no ghost row and carries its annotation arrow; the V3a S3 cell carries \"done stays Only you\".\n- 03 shows V3a and V6 in both columns, following the AX5 rules above, and the greyscale grid with its five captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops, each with the legend line and ScopeChip; the web crop shows the row menu button on every row.\n- 05 uses D1, D4 and D7 (with its 5.42:1 caption) and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string on the board is in this message or listed on Notes."
          },
