            "promptText": "Component 00c-02: FactRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: FactRow. This message is the complete FactRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). One row per fact in the place file and in settings. The fact is known, missing, or not available at this tier.\n\nUSED IN (panel): x-place-file · f6-home-basics-rows · f1-today-tab · f3-household-block · f9-verification-promise-copy · f4-notification-settings.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw three specimens at 2x, stacked: V1a (known, chevron), V2a (missing, \"Add\") and the ⑦ disclosure row.\n① Row: minimum height 56pt, padding 16pt horizontal, on surface.base, content vertically centred.\n② Label: bodySmall 14/20, text.secondary, above the value.\n③ Value: body 16/24, text.primary.\n④ ProvenanceMark S (16pt) after the value, with an 8pt (spacing.2) gap. It is not a target.\n⑤ Trailing element: either a chevron (16pt, text.secondary) or a text action in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), e.g. \"Add\".\n⑥ Missing form: the label, then an ask sentence in body text.primary, then the text action \"Add\".\n⑦ Disclosure row \"More you can add (5)\" with a chevron, 44pt minimum. At most 3 promoted asks show per screen; the rest sit under this row.\n⑧ Target rule callout. On rows with a chevron, the whole row is the target. On rows with a text action (missing, declined, permission-disabled), the text action is a separate 44pt / 48dp / 44px button and the row itself is not a target. Rows with neither (V3 and V8) are not targets. Draw the dashed target on each specimen accordingly: around the V1a row, and around \"Add\" only on V2a.\n⑨ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Each cell belongs to the place named.\nV1 known:\n- V1a · known-flood (any address): label \"Flood zone\" · value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · filled mark · chevron.\n- V1b · known-pickup-unconfirmed (Home A as of TODAY): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · hollow mark · chevron.\n- V1d · known-pickup-confirmed (Home A, fixture delta: after Maya confirmed Tuesday): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · filled mark · chevron.\n- V1c · known-pickup-saved-place (Place B): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Thursday · City of Camas\" · hollow mark · chevron.\nV2 missing, drawn as an invitation, never in red:\n- V2a · missing-dates: label \"Dates\" · ask \"Add one date that matters\" · action \"Add\".\n- V2b · missing-frequency (Place B): label \"Pickup frequency\" · value \"Not set\" in text.secondary · action \"Add\".\n- V3 · not-at-tier (Place B): label \"People who live here\" · value \"Claim this address first\" in text.secondary · no action, no chevron and no mark.\n- V4 · done-ask (Home A, same fixture delta as V1d), drawn quiet: a 16pt bare stroke check (not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark) · \"Pickup day set · Tuesday\", all in text.secondary · chevron.\nV5 declined (Home A before Sam joined; fixture delta):\n- V5a · declined-undo: the moment after the decline, as the InlineUndo \"Just you, then. · Undo\".\n- V5b · declined-later: later and re-openable: label \"People who live here\" · value \"Just me\" · action \"Add the people you live with\".\n- V5c · declined-skip: label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Skipped\" · action \"Set your pickup day\".\n- V6 · permission-disabled: label \"Reminders\" · the reason inline in bodySmall text.primary, \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · action \"Open Settings\".\n- V7 · receipt (Home A): label \"What moved when you claimed\" · value \"2 dates and your pickup day\" · chevron.\nV8 \"Your reports\": three rows, each with the label \"Your reports\", the value \"Pickup schedule\", one StatusChip and a caption line in caption text.secondary:\n- V8a · reports-checking: chip \"Checking\" · caption \"We'll check by Mon 26 Oct\".\n- V8b · reports-fixed: chip \"Fixed\" · caption \"Fixed Fri 16 Oct\".\n- V8c · reports-no-change: chip \"No change\" · caption \"City of Camas confirmed Thursday\".\nRow order: V1a, V1b, V1d, V1c, V2a, V2b, V3, V4, V5a, V5b, V5c, V6, V7, V8a, V8b, V8c. V1b and V1d sit in adjacent rows so the hollow-to-filled change reads side by side.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · default.\n- SF · focused.\n- S2 · loading: a WarmingSkeleton exactly 56pt high, with a 144pt-wide label bar above a 253pt-wide value bar (at 361pt content width) and no text.\n- S3 · offline. The value stays readable. A text action that needs the network is disabled per R8 (text.secondary, focusable) with the reason caption \"You're offline. You can add this when you're back.\" under it. A chevron row (V1a, V7) stays readable and opens cached content, so it looks like S1. On V6, \"Open Settings\" stays enabled, because it opens the system settings and needs no connection: draw V6 unchanged with the annotation \"Open Settings works offline\".\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 25 cells)\n- S1: all 16 variants.\n- SF: V2a, with the focus ring on \"Add\" only, because the row is not a target (1 cell).\n- S2: V1a, V2a, V3 and V8a (4 cells).\n- S3: V1a, V2a, V6 and V7 (4 cells).\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows stay on dark surface.base. The skeleton bars and StatusChip fills use D4. Marks, the chevron and the V4 check use dark text.secondary. \"Add\" and the other text actions use dark border.focus.\n- No D7 hue appears on this component. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1a and V2a in both columns.\n- The label wraps, and the value wraps below it.\n- The mark and the chevron, or \"Add\", drop below the value.\n- \"Add\" keeps its 44pt / 48dp target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- missing = ask sentence + \"Add\", not colour.\n- not-at-tier = the words \"Claim this address first\".\n- unconfirmed vs confirmed = ring vs disc (V1b next to V1d).\n- done = stroke check + \"Pickup day set\".\n- loading = skeleton bars in the row's geometry.\n- report status = chip words.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Targets follow ⑧. A row with a chevron is one target (44pt / 48dp / 44px; 56pt visual). A text action is a separate button, and its row is not a target.\n- Known rows merge their label: \"<label>, <value>, <mark name>\". Example: \"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, official.\"\n- Asks are read as text, then a verb-first button: \"Pickup frequency, not set.\" then \"Add. Button.\"\n- V5a is announced with role=status (\"Just you, then. Undo.\"), and Undo is focusable.\n- The loading skeleton is announced once as \"Loading\".\n- A disabled offline action reads its reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The approved asks are \"Set your pickup day\" · \"Add one date that matters\" · \"Add the people you live with\".\n- \"Not set\" is in text.secondary.\n- Hazard values put the plain meaning first: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n- Declines are neutral: \"Just me\", \"Skipped\".\n- Offline reasons open with \"You're offline\".\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a red X or red text for a missing fact, draw the ask sentence with \"Add\". Missing is an invitation, not an error.\n- Instead of a score, percentage or \"3 of 6\" on the place file, draw plain rows and the \"More you can add (5)\" disclosure. Counts of completion create pressure.\n- Instead of more than 3 promoted asks, draw 3 and fold the rest under \"More you can add (5)\".\n- Instead of hiding a not-at-tier fact, draw it grey with \"Claim this address first\" and no button, so the path is named without a dead control.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. x-place-file · ios, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; then V1a, V1c, V2b, V2a, V3 and the disclosure \"More you can add (5)\"; the legend line. Do not use V1b or V1d here: the Tuesday rows are Home A's.\n2. f4-notification-settings · android: V6 at the top of the settings group. No mark, so no legend.\n3. f6-home-basics-rows · web-1440, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; V7 and V8a. No row menu button (no custom actions).\n\nNOTES (add a \"FactRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"People who live here\" · \"Reminders\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · \"Just you, then.\" · \"Pickup day set · Tuesday\" · \"Skipped\" · \"2 dates and your pickup day\" · \"Pickup schedule\" · \"We'll check by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Fixed Fri 16 Oct\" · \"City of Camas confirmed Thursday\" · \"You're offline. You can add this when you're back.\" · \"Open Settings works offline\" (annotation).\n- Fixture deltas: V1b shows Home A as of TODAY (hollow); V1d and V4 show the later state after Maya confirmed Tuesday (filled) · V1c, V2b and V3 belong to Place B · V5a–V5c show Home A before Sam joined.\n- Contract conflicts: V3 drawn with the contract string \"Claim this address first\" on a Place B row, although ScopeChip's copy rule says a saved place never uses the word \"claim\" · the contract's \"the whole row is the target\" narrowed: rows with a text action expose a separate button and the row is not a target · V6 offline drawn with \"Open Settings\" still enabled, instead of the contract's generic \"offline\" treatment.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · FactRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · FactRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · FactRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · FactRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · FactRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · FactRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · FactRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the FactRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five FactRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the three specimens with callouts ①–⑨ and the targets drawn per ⑧, plus the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 25 listed cells, labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"FactRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- V1b and V1d are adjacent rows; V1b is hollow and V1d filled.\n- The V2a SF cell rings \"Add\" only.\n- No red, no score, no percentage and no fraction appears; \"More you can add (5)\" is a plain disclosure.\n- V4 uses a bare stroke check, never a disc.\n- The S2 cells are 56pt skeletons with no text. The S3 cells follow the offline rules above, including the V6 annotation.\n- 03 shows V1a and V2a in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops; the Place B crop has the legend line and \"Saved place · Only you\" and no Home A rows.\n- 05 uses D4 and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
          }
        ],
        "clean": true
      },
