            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-03: FirstWeekRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: FirstWeekRow. This message is the complete FirstWeekRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). The single pointer on Today to the next first-week ask. It comes from a bounded set of steps that the person has already started.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f1-today-tab · x-place-file · f4-briefing-optin-card. (f4-briefing-optin-card is not cropped on 04: it only hosts the row, so it adds nothing beyond the f1-today-tab crop.)\n\nFIXTURE DELTA (applies to every FirstWeekRow specimen). The specimens show Place B (Jordan Lee) on Tue 13 Oct 2026, 3 days after the Sat 10 Oct save. The 7-day activation window runs Sun 11 Oct through Sat 17 Oct and closes after Sat 17 Oct. The hidden variant (V2) shows Mon 19 Oct, when the window has closed. Place B's pickup day is known (Thursday, City of Camas); its pickup frequency is Not set.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1a at 2x.\n① One row, 48pt high at default sizes: padding 16pt horizontal and 12pt vertical (12 + 24 + 12 = 48), on surface.base. At default sizes the step text is one line; if it wraps, the row grows and the dismiss button stays top-aligned.\n② Text in bodyMedium 16/24, text.primary: \"Next: set your pickup day →\". The arrow is part of the link. The whole row except the dismiss button is the link target: draw its dashed target.\n③ Trailing dismiss button: a 16pt close glyph in text.secondary inside a 44pt / 48dp target, with 8dp between it and the link target. Draw its dashed target too.\n④ Callout listing the bounded set: \"Save (already done) · Pickup day · Reminder or widget · One date or person\".\n⑤ Callout: \"Only steps reachable at the current tier are counted. Verify, profile and photo are never steps.\"\n⑥ Callout: \"Shown for 7 days (the activation window).\"\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"the visible dismiss button is the only extra action; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1a · next-pickup: \"Next: set your pickup day →\". For Place B this step means confirming the known day and setting the frequency.\n- V1b · next-widget: \"Next: put today on your home screen →\" (invented). It may wrap at 361pt; if it does, apply the ① rule.\n- V2 · hidden (set complete, dismissed, or window closed): draw an outline of the Place B Today section stack (ScopeChip, pickup section, air section) with no FirstWeekRow and no gap where it would be, plus the annotation \"hidden: set complete, dismissed, or 7 days passed\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SFl, SFd, S2)\n- S1 · default.\n- SFl · focused-link: the focus ring around the link target only.\n- SFd · focused-dismiss: the focus ring around the dismiss button only.\n- S2 · dismissed (stored on the server): the row collapses in place to the InlineUndo \"Hidden from Today · Undo\" (invented). Undo has a 44pt target and stays until the user leaves Today. There is no countdown.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 7 cells)\n- S1: V1a, V1b and V2 (V2 is one cell, in the S1 column).\n- SFl and SFd: V1a, side by side, each ringing only its own target (2 cells).\n- S2: V1a and V1b (2 cells).\n\nDARK (05)\n- The row sits on dark surface.base. Text is dark text.primary, the close glyph dark text.secondary, and \"Undo\" dark border.focus.\n- No substitutes beyond the token swap are needed. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1a in S1 and V1a in S2, in both columns.\n- The text wraps to two or more lines, and the arrow stays at the end of the text.\n- The dismiss button stays top-aligned at the trailing edge and keeps its target (overrides R9: a dismiss control stays top-trailing).\n- The row grows beyond 48pt.\n- In S2, \"Undo\" wraps below \"Hidden from Today\" and keeps its 44pt / 48dp target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- next step = the words; no colour is used.\n- dismissed = \"Hidden from Today · Undo\".\n- hidden = absence, carried by the annotation.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The row is one link: \"Next: set your pickup day. Link.\"\n- Dismiss is a separate button, \"Dismiss next step\" (invented), and is also offered as a custom action on the link.\n- Undo is announced with role=status and is focusable.\n- Targets: the link row is 48pt; the dismiss button is 44pt / 48dp / 44px, 8dp from the link.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Name only the next step, in sentence case, verb first. Never show a count or fraction of steps.\n- The row shows for 7 days, matching the activation window.\n- Step strings come from the set: \"set your pickup day\", \"put today on your home screen\" (invented), \"add one date that matters\" (invented).\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of \"3 of 6\" or any denominator, draw \"Next: <step> →\". Naming the next step moves people without pressure.\n- Instead of counting verify, profile or photo, draw only the four set steps reachable at the viewer's tier. A step you cannot do is not a step.\n- Instead of a checklist card, draw this single 48pt row. The full list lives in the place file.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): two crops (R13).\n1. f1-today-tab · ios, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; then V1a; then the pickup section outline, showing \"Pickup day\" with a hollow mark, and the legend line.\n2. x-place-file · web-390, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; the same step drawn as two published FactRow variants: V1c (label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Thursday · City of Camas\" · hollow mark · chevron), then V2b (label \"Pickup frequency\" · value \"Not set\" in text.secondary · action \"Add\"). Annotation: \"same set, same storage\". Add the legend line (R13). No row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add a \"FirstWeekRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: every string marked (invented) above.\n- Fixture deltas: specimens on Tue 13 Oct 2026, 3 days after the Sat 10 Oct save; the 7-day window runs Sun 11 Oct through Sat 17 Oct · V2 on Mon 19 Oct, after the window closed · the pickup step for Place B covers both confirming the known day (FactRow V1c) and setting the frequency (FactRow V2b) · the set step \"One date or person\" is drawn as \"add one date that matters\" because the person half is locked for Place B at T1 (\"Claim this address first\") and is not counted.\n- Contract conflicts: the contract lists a \"fraction\" variant (a done-count in front of the next step); not drawn, because house invariant 6 and the research brief rejected it. The contract's \"no-fraction\" variant is drawn as V1a and V1b · link target drawn as the whole row minus the dismiss button (contract: whole-row link), so dismiss can have its own target.\n- Assumptions: at AX5 / 200% the dismiss button stays top-trailing, overriding R9 (trailing elements move below the text) because a dismiss control belongs at the top-trailing corner.\n- Not cropped: f4-briefing-optin-card, because it only hosts the row.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · FirstWeekRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · FirstWeekRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · FirstWeekRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · FirstWeekRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · FirstWeekRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03, 04 and 05 as named above. Then add the FirstWeekRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five FirstWeekRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows callouts ①–⑦, both dashed targets and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 7 listed cells, each captioned \"FirstWeekRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- No fraction, step count or percentage is drawn on any specimen, callout, annotation or crop (INSTEAD OF names \"3 of 6\" only as the pattern to avoid).\n- If V1b wraps, its row grows and its dismiss button is top-aligned.\n- Both 04 crops show Place B's pickup day as known (\"Thursday · City of Camas\", hollow mark), each with the legend line; the only missing Place B pickup item is \"Pickup frequency · Not set · Add\".\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
