            "promptText": "Component 00c-04: BillRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: BillRow. This message is the complete BillRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (top of 01). A household bill with payer attribution, so two people don't pay the same bill.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-bills-list · f3-member-home-dashboard · f3-bill-detail-web · f10-mail-piece-photo.\n\nFIXTURE ROWS (Home A, viewer Maya unless stated; strings given only here)\n- Clark Public Utilities · Upcoming · $142.18 · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n- City of Vancouver water · Upcoming · $84.00 · \"Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\".\n- HOA dues · Upcoming · $285.00 · \"Due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\".\n- Comcast · Upcoming · $79.99 · \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n- Paid (invented): Comcast · Paid · $79.99 · \"Due Fri 2 Oct\" · \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\".\n- Overdue (invented): Waste Connections · Overdue (error glyph in chip) · $38.75 · \"Due Thu 15 Oct\".\n- Due today (invented; shown on Fri 23 Oct): Clark Public Utilities · Due today · $142.18 · line 2 left \"Due today\". The repetition is intended: the chip is the status and line 2 keeps the due-date column filled. Today stands alone; the date is only spoken.\n- Header ⑧: Maya sees \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Sam can see these\"; Sam sees \"… · You and Maya can see these\".\n\nANATOMY (01, at 2x): Maya's header over the Clark upcoming and paid Comcast rows.\n① Row: 12 + 24 + 20 + 12 = 68pt at default sizes (min 68pt), padding 12pt vertical, 16pt horizontal, surface.base. The whole row opens bill detail (dashed target).\n② Line 1 left: provider, bodyMedium 16/24 text.primary. The ONLY field that truncates (default sizes only).\n③ Line 1: one StatusChip after the provider.\n④ Line 1 right: amount, bodyMedium tabular, one right-aligned column.\n⑤ Line 2 left: due date, bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary.\n⑥ Line 2 right: attribution, bodySmall text.secondary, never truncated.\n⑦ Overflow (dashed target): 20pt ellipsis, 44pt / 48dp, 8dp from the row target: Mark paid · I paid this · Paid a different amount · Skip this month.\n⑧ Header, bodySmall text.strong. Finance access differs, so it names people.\n⑨ Not on 01; it sits on the V1 · S3 cell: \"the household notification is held until the user leaves the screen without undoing\".\n⑩ Web menu: \"the ⑦ overflow is the web row menu button; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · manage (Maya): the Clark upcoming row.\n- V2a · member-overflow (Sam): same row; overflow holds \"I paid this\" only.\n- V2b · member-no-overflow (Sam): same row, no overflow; \"Maya can mark this paid\" (invented) replaces line 2 right. Its S4 cell has no bill row; it keeps the R7 label and caption, with a separate annotation beside the cell: \"viewer: Sam, before Maya shared bills\".\n- V3 · only-me: same row, lines 1–2 unchanged. Line 3, leading-aligned: 12pt person glyph + \"Only you will see this.\" in bodySmall text.secondary.\n- V4 · former-member (later state, after Sam left): the paid Comcast row with \"Paid by Sam (no longer here) · Thu 1 Oct\".\n- C1 · chip-upcoming, C2 · chip-due-today, C3 · chip-overdue (hue on glyph only), C4 · chip-paid: the Clark upcoming, due-today, overdue and paid fixtures.\n\nSTATES (columns: S1, S2a, SF, S2b, S3, S4, S5)\n- S1 · default. V1 · S1 draws its menu open with all four items.\n- S2a · highlighted-arrival (R8; dark D1), focus moved here: infoBg wash, 4pt leading bar, ring 2px outside.\n- SF · focused: the R8 ring on the whole row. It sits between S2a and S2b so the ring can be compared with both.\n- S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; ring remains.\n- S3 · marked-paid: InlineUndo \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\" (invented), role=status. Beside it, the row after the user left: line 1 \"Clark Public Utilities · Upcoming · $142.18\"; line 2 left \"Next due in 35 days · Mon 23 Nov\" (invented).\n- S4 · permission-denied (Sam before Maya shared bills): header is just \"Bills\"; the body is one locked row: 16pt text.secondary lock glyph, \"Maya can give you access to bills\" (invented), bodySmall text.secondary, no link, min 44pt, border.subtle hairline above.\n- S5 · offline: FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" (invented) above the rows; rows still open cached detail. V1 · S5 draws the menu open, all four items disabled, with one shared reason under the item group: \"You're offline. You can mark bills paid when you're back.\" (invented). (Overrides R8 for menus: one shared reason under the group, not one per item.)\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 15): V1: S1, S2a, SF, S2b, S3, S5 · V2a: S1 · V2b: S1, S4 · V3: S1 · V4: S1 · C1–C4: S1.\n\nDARK (05): D1 highlight; D4 chip fills; D7 overdue glyph, caption \"error on dark raised 3.03:1\"; D8 keyline on open menus, caption \"5.71:1\"; Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): C1 and C4 in both columns. Provider wraps (no truncation); chip drops below it, then amount; due date and attribution stack, attribution last; overflow stays top-trailing (overrides R9: an overflow control stays top-trailing).\n\nGREYSCALE (03): status = chip words · overdue = glyph + \"Overdue\" · payer = \"Paid by Sam\" · highlighted = leading bar · marked paid = \"marked paid · Undo\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Merged label: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday 23 October, upcoming.\" Due today: \"…, due today, Friday 23 October.\" Paid: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99 cents, paid by Sam, Thursday 1 October.\"\n- S3 is a live region (\"Clark Public Utilities marked paid. Undo.\"); Undo is focusable.\n- Overflow items are also custom actions; offline-disabled ones keep the shared reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel): notifications say \"marked paid\", not \"paid\" · \"Paid by <first name> · <weekday day month>\" · future dates beyond tomorrow add the relative count; past dates show the date only (\"Due Thu 15 Oct\", \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\") · former member \"Sam (no longer here)\" · the header names who can see · never monitoring language (\"still hasn't paid\").\n\nPLATFORMS (panel; added by this board): the overflow is native: iOS pull-down menu, Android M3 DropdownMenu, web menu button with keyboard support.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- One-tap \"Mark paid\" on the row or dashboard → in the overflow; a mis-tap must not notify the household.\n- Avatar without a name → \"Paid by Sam\"; the name is the point.\n- Budget meter → the header total.\n- Truncated attribution → truncate the provider.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; R13)\n1. f3-bills-list · ios, Maya: her header, the four upcoming rows.\n2. f3-member-home-dashboard · android, Sam: a Bills card (radius lg), his header, two V2b rows (Clark, City of Vancouver water).\n3. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440: V1 in S2a as the header summary, overflow as the web menu.\nPlatform strip: the V1 menu in the three PLATFORMS forms; web shows keyboard focus on item one.\n\nNOTES (add a \"BillRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: all marked (invented) above.\n- Fixture deltas: C2 on Fri 23 Oct · S4 is Sam before sharing · V4 shows a later state after Sam left · HOA dues is also a self-added monthly date (DateRow V6).\n- Contract conflicts: header names people, not \"… Everyone at Maple St can see these\" (ScopeChip doNot) · V3 uses ScopeChip's sentence · native menus added here · V2a drawn per contract, but the brief did not adopt member-recorded payments (finance.view decision), so crops use V2b.\n- Board-rule overrides: a menu gets one shared offline reason under its item group (overrides R8's per-action caption) · at AX5 / 200% the overflow stays top-trailing (overrides R9).\n- Copy decisions: C2 repeats \"Due today\" in the chip and on line 2 on purpose · past dates show the date only, with no relative count.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · BillRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · BillRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03, 04 and 05 as named above, then add the BillRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five artboards exist with exact visible names.\n- 01 shows ①–⑧ and ⑩; ⑨ sits on V1 · S3 in 02 and 05.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 15 cells, in column order S1, S2a, SF, S2b, S3, S4, S5, captioned \"BillRow · <variant key> · <state key>\"; the S4 viewer note is a separate annotation, not part of the caption.\n- Default rows are 68pt.\n- No header says \"Everyone\".\n- \"Mark paid\" appears only inside overflow menus.\n- Every string is in this message or on Notes."
