            "promptText": "Component 00c-05: MemberRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: MemberRow. This message is the complete MemberRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (top of 01). A person in the household. It carries no trust badge and no status badge.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-members-roster · f3-member-home-dashboard · f3-household-block · f3b-owner-attestation · x-place-file · f3b-invitation-decision.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw a MEMBERS group at 2x: the ⑥ heading, the V3 row and the ⑦ disclosure. Beside it, draw V1 at 2x to show ⑧.\n① Row: 56pt minimum, padding 16pt horizontal and 8pt vertical (8 + 40 + 8 = 56; text block 24 + 16 = 40), on surface.base. V1, with the ⑧ caption, grows to 72pt. The row is one element: draw its dashed target.\n② A 40pt initials avatar: a surface.sunken circle (dark: D4) with initials in label 13/18 text.strong. Neutral, with no identity hue.\n③ Name: body 16/24, text.primary.\n④ Caption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" (invented) or \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" (invented).\n⑤ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) holding Change role · Confirm lives here · Remove. On the viewer's own row, the only item is \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". Draw its dashed target.\n⑥ Group heading in overline 11/16, text.secondary: OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS.\n⑦ Group disclosure: a 44pt / 48dp row under its heading, with a chevron. MEMBERS \"What can members do?\", ADMINS \"What can admins do?\" (invented), GUESTS \"What can guests do?\" (invented). OWNER has no disclosure.\n⑧ Optional second caption naming method and date: \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 15 Oct 2026\" (date invented), caption text.secondary, no badge shape. Only on the viewer's own row, so members never look different from one another.\n⑨ Web menu callout: \"the ⑤ overflow is the web row menu button; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Home A, viewer Maya. Role variants reuse Sam Ortega, so no new people are invented. Draw V1–V5 with their group heading above the row inside the cell.\n- V1 · owner: OWNER · \"Maya Chen (you)\" (\"(you)\" invented) · \"joined Mon 21 Sep 2026\" (invented) · ⑧ · overflow (closed). This is the owner's own row. The owner as seen by another member (e.g. Sam on f3-member-home-dashboard) is the V2 layout under an OWNER heading: \"Maya Chen\", join caption, no ⑧, and no overflow.\n- V2 · admin: ADMINS · \"Sam Ortega\" · \"joined Tue 22 Sep 2026\" · overflow.\n- V3 · member: MEMBERS · the same content as V2.\n- V4 · guest: GUESTS · \"Sam Ortega\" · \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" · overflow.\n- V5 · you: V1's content (OWNER heading, \"Maya Chen (you)\", join caption, ⑧) with the overflow open, showing only \"Leave Larkspur Loop\".\n- V6a · roster-line: a 44pt / 48dp row \"Maya and Sam live here · View\". \"View\" is a text button in primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus).\n- V6b · roster-count (Priya's view before she accepts; count only): a 44pt / 48dp row \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\", no action.\n- V7 · empty (fixture delta: Home A before Sam joined): a 44pt / 48dp row \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\". \"Invite someone\" is a text button in primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus).\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · default.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the whole row.\n- S2 · loading: a WarmingSkeleton in the row's final geometry, no text, announced once as \"Loading\". Per row type:\n  - V3: 56pt high, a 40pt circle and two bars.\n  - V6a: 44pt / 48dp high, one text bar and one short trailing bar, no circle.\n- S3 · offline: the overflow opens and its items are disabled. A menu gets one shared reason under its item group (overrides R8 for menus). The V3 menu (Change role · Confirm lives here · Remove) carries \"You're offline. You can manage people when you're back.\" (invented). On V5, \"Leave Larkspur Loop\" carries \"You're offline. You can leave when you're back.\" (invented).\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 13 cells)\n- S1: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6a, V6b, V7 (8).\n- SF: V3 (1).\n- S2: V3, V6a (2).\n- S3: V3, V5 (2), each with its menu open.\n\nDARK (05): rows stay on dark surface.base; D4 on avatar circles and skeleton shapes; D8 keyline on open menus, caption \"5.71:1\"; Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): V3 and V6a in both columns. The avatar grows to 48pt and stays top-aligned; name and caption wrap; V6a moves \"View\" to its own line, keeping its target; the overflow stays top-trailing (overrides R9: an overflow control stays top-trailing).\n\nGREYSCALE (03): role = the group heading words, never colour · own row = \"(you)\" and the ⑧ words · loading = skeleton shapes in the row's geometry.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The avatar is decorative; the name is read.\n- Pattern: \"Sam Ortega, member, joined Tuesday 22 September 2026. Actions available.\"\n- Overflow items are also custom actions. Row and overflow targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- V6b is read as text, with no action.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Verification is shown on actions, through LockedActionRow, never on names. The only exception is ⑧ on the viewer's own row, naming method and date.\n- Roles are Owner, Admin, Member, Guest. Never \"resident\".\n- Before someone accepts, show only a count: \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\".\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a \"Verified\" or \"Household member\" chip, draw the plain ⑧ caption on the viewer's own row only. A badge on a person reads as a trust score.\n- Instead of a check-badge shape on the avatar, draw the plain initials circle.\n- Instead of names for someone who has not accepted, draw the count line.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3-members-roster · ios, viewer Maya: OWNER with V1 (showing ⑧, no disclosure), MEMBERS with V3 and its disclosure, then the overline \"PENDING\" over a labelled grey outline reading \"InviteRow (00c-06)\" with no internal detail. InviteRow is specified in its own later message; do not draw its contents here.\n2. f3-household-block · android: V7.\n3. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440, viewer Priya: V6b. No row menu button (no actions).\n\nNOTES (add a \"MemberRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: every string marked (invented) above.\n- Fixture deltas: V7 shows Home A before Sam joined · V6b shows Priya's view before she accepts · V2 and V4 reuse Sam Ortega in other roles · join dates set in September so that \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\" (BillRow) falls after Sam joined.\n- Contract conflicts: ⑧ drawn on the viewer's own row only, instead of never (contract \"never on names\") · \"What can members do?\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary lists \"members (in user copy)\" under Not for \"Your household\".\n- Owner seen by others: the V2 layout under an OWNER heading (\"Maya Chen\", join caption, no ⑧, no overflow). V1 and V5 are the owner's own row only.\n- Board-rule overrides: a menu gets one shared offline reason under its item group (overrides R8's per-action caption) · at AX5 / 200% the overflow stays top-trailing (overrides R9).\n- Assumptions: the neutral avatar colour (surface.sunken with text.strong initials) · the avatar grows from 40pt to 48pt at AX5 / 200%.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · MemberRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · MemberRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03, 04 and 05 as named above. Then add the MemberRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five artboards exist with exact visible names.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 13 listed cells, each captioned \"MemberRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- The V3 · S2 skeleton is the same height as V3 · S1 (56pt), and the V6a · S2 skeleton is the same height as V6a · S1 (44pt / 48dp) with no circle.\n- No row carries a badge, chip, check shape or identity hue.\n- ⑧ appears only on Maya's own row.\n- The 04 PENDING group is a grey outline labelled \"InviteRow (00c-06)\" with no InviteRow strings.\n- Every string is in this message or on Notes."
