              "00c · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-06: InviteRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: InviteRow. This message is the complete InviteRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). A pending invitation or invite link, with its expiry and a one-tap fix.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-members-roster · x-place-file · f3-invite-composer · f3-invite-banner.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 at 2x under its \"PENDING\" overline.\n① Row: minimum 56pt, in a \"PENDING\" group (overline 11/16 text.secondary) that only managers see. Quieter than people rows: no avatar on any variant.\n② Leading mail glyph, 16pt, text.secondary.\n③ Line 1, the recipient: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, \"priya@example.com\" or a username such as \"@priya\".\n④ Line 2, the caption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". It runs the full text width under ⑤ and ⑥ and wraps at a middot when it has to.\n⑤ \"Resend\" text button, bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), trailing and aligned to line 1, with a 44pt target. Draw its dashed target.\n⑥ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) holding Cancel · Extend, trailing, 8dp after Resend. Draw its dashed target.\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"the ⑥ overflow is the web row menu button; rows without an overflow use their visible buttons; no second menu\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · pending-email: as in the anatomy.\n- V1u · pending-username: V1 with the recipient \"@priya\".\n- V2 · expiring (fixture delta: shown on Sun 25 Oct): V1 with the caption \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\". The expiry is words in text.secondary, not tinted.\n- V3 · needs-reissue: a 16pt warning glyph replaces the mail glyph (hue on the glyph only; dark: D7). Line 1: the recipient, with ⑥ trailing. Line 2: \"Needs reissue — your household's invite rules changed\" in bodySmall text.primary, wrapping within the text width. Line 3: the caption \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" leading, and the \"Reissue\" text button trailing with a 44pt target.\n- V4 · declined (fixture delta: Priya declined): the 16pt mail glyph; line 1 the recipient; line 2 a StatusChip \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\". ⑥ holds only \"Remove\". No Resend.\n- V5 · link-active: a 16pt link glyph; line 1 \"Invite link\" in bodySmall text.primary; line 2 the caption \"Works once · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". \"Turn off link\" is a trailing text button with a 44pt target. No overflow.\n- V6 · awaiting-approval (Priya joined by link, so the link is used and no expiry applies): the 16pt mail glyph; line 1 \"priya@example.com\"; line 2 the caption \"Waiting for your OK\". \"Approve\" and \"Remove\" are equal-weight text buttons, trailing, 8dp apart, each with its own 44pt target. No overflow.\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2, S3)\n- S1 · default.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the Resend button only.\n- S2 · sending: \"Resend\" becomes \"Sending…\" and \"Reissue\" becomes \"Reissuing…\", each with a 12pt spinner before it (dark: D6; static text under Reduce Motion). Not re-tappable.\n  - Follow-on (V1 only): inside the V1·S2 cell, under the sending row, draw a second stacked frame sub-labelled \"then\": the caption gains \" · Sent\" at the end and the button returns to \"Resend\". \"Sent\" is a role=status region whose accessible text is \"Invitation resent\". It stays one cell.\n- S3 · offline: each action is disabled per R8, with a reason under it that names it: \"You're offline. You can <resend | reissue | turn off the link | approve | remove this> when you're back.\" The ⑥ overflow stays enabled and opens; Cancel and Extend inside it are disabled with \"You're offline. You can change this invite when you're back.\" On V4, Remove inside it uses the remove reason.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 14 cells)\n- S1: V1, V1u, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6 (7).\n- SF: V1 (1).\n- S2: V1 with its \"then\" frame, and V3 (2). V4 in S2: \"n/a — declined invites cannot be resent\" (1).\n- S3: V1, V5, and V6 with both buttons disabled, each with its own reason (3).\n- Every other position stays empty canvas.\n\nDARK (05): rows on dark surface.base. The V3 warning glyph keeps its hue (D7), captioned \"warning on dark base 5.60:1\". StatusChip fill uses D4. Spinners use D6. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V6 in both columns. The recipient wraps at the \"@\". Captions wrap at middots. Resend drops below the caption and keeps its target. The overflow stays top-trailing (an icon button, not a text action). Approve and Remove stack below the caption, each full width with its own target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions): expiring = \"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\" words · needs reissue = warning glyph shape + \"Needs reissue\" · declined = chip word \"Declined\" · link = link glyph + \"Works once\" · sending = \"Sending…\" words.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Pattern: \"Invitation to priya@example.com, member, expires in 7 days, Monday 26 October. Resend. Button.\"\n- A successful resend is announced as \"Invitation resent\" (the visible word is \"Sent\").\n- Expiry is always in words. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps.\n- Overflow items are also custom actions. Disabled offline actions stay in the tree with their reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The expiry is shown on every pending invite (including expiring and needs-reissue rows) and on every active link. The awaiting-approval row shows none, because its link is already used.\n- Dates show the weekday; beyond tomorrow, the relative count comes first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- The link warning (\"Works once\") appears at the point of choice.\n- Every email uses @example.com. Each offline reason names the action it blocks.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a \"Remind them\" action on a declined invite, draw only \"Remove\". A decline is an answer.\n- Instead of a real email domain, draw @example.com.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted expiring row, draw the expiry in text.secondary words. Urgency comes from the date, not colour.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f3-members-roster · ios, viewer Maya: the PENDING group with V1 and V5, below the MEMBERS group outline.\n2. f3-invite-banner · android: V3 as the banner's single slot.\n3. f3-invite-composer · web-1440: V5 under the link choice. \"Turn off link\" is visible, so there is no row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add an \"InviteRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"@priya\" · \"sent Mon 12 Oct\" · \"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" on the link and reissue rows · \"Sending…\" · \"Reissuing…\" · \"Sent\" · \"Invitation resent\" · the accessibility pattern above · the five offline reasons and the overflow reason.\n- Notes only (not in the grid): the Reissue and V4 Remove offline reasons, and the Cancel · Extend offline reason.\n- Fixture deltas: V2 on Sun 25 Oct · V4 Priya declined · V6 Priya joined by link and awaits approval.\n- Contract conflicts: \"Approve\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary lists \"approve member\" under Not · expiry omitted only on the awaiting-approval row (its link is used), narrowing \"the expiry is always shown\" · contract \"Expires Sep 23\" drawn with the house relative count · link row drawn with an expiry the contract string omits · \"Reissue\" drawn as a trailing button on line 3 instead of after a middot, so it has a full target.\n- Assumptions: V3 keeps the Cancel · Extend overflow · only V1 has a drawn S2 success frame.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · InviteRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · InviteRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the InviteRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five InviteRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1 with callouts ①–⑦, both dashed targets and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 14 listed cells (including the n/a cell and its reason), labelled \"<code> · <key>\", each captioned \"InviteRow · <variant key> · <state key>\". The V1·S2 cell holds its \"then\" frame.\n- V3 and V5 show an expiry; V5 and V6 have the line 1 / line 2 split and trailing buttons as specified; V4 and V6 have the mail glyph.\n- No row has an avatar or a tint. Every drawn S3 action carries the reason that names it. Every email ends in @example.com.\n- 03, 04 and 05 match their sections, including the D7 ratio and Increase Contrast captions.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
