            "promptText": "Component 00c-07: NotificationRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: NotificationRow. This message is the complete NotificationRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). The in-app twin of every push. Tapping it lands on the exact object.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f3-household-notifications · f4-notification-settings.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 (unread) and V4 (unread, system) at 2x, stacked, and V7 expanded beside them.\n① Row: minimum 64pt on surface.base; padding 12pt vertical, 16pt leading (before the dot column) and 16pt trailing. The whole row is the target: draw its dashed target.\n② A fixed 12pt leading column holding a 6pt unread dot in primary.700 (dark: D6), labelled \"Unread\". Read rows keep the empty column, so text never shifts. The dot is not a provenance mark and not a target.\n③ A 28pt initials avatar: surface.sunken circle, initials in label 13/18 text.strong (dark: D4). System rows have no avatar; their text keeps the same leading alignment.\n④ Line 1: body 16/24 text.primary, a sentence with the actor first.\n⑤ Line 2: caption 12/16 text.secondary, joined by middots: date and time · home label (only for readers with more than one home) · for reminders, a trailing ProvenanceMark S.\n⑥ Grouped row: a chevron disclosure that expands to the individual rows. The chevron is part of the row target. Expanded rows have no avatar, are indented to the text column, and each has line 2 \"Today · 5:40 PM\".\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Home A, viewer Maya, today Mon 19 Oct. Each variant is an independent specimen. Times are invented; 7:00 AM is assumed to be the morning briefing time.\n- V1 · bill-paid: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid · $142.18\" · \"Today · 5:40 PM\".\n- V2 · task-completed: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked \"Carts out\" done\" · \"Today · 5:55 PM\".\n- V3 · event-created: Sam avatar · \"Sam added a date: Gutter cleaning, in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov\" · \"Yesterday · 8:12 PM\".\n- V4 · date-reminder (system): \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive in 7 days · by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · filled mark.\n- V5 · bill-reminder (system): \"Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · $142.18\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · YOU ADDED mark.\n- V6j · member-joined (fixture delta: Priya accepted): Priya avatar · \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\" · \"Today · 4:20 PM\".\n- V6l · member-left (fixture delta: Sam left): Sam avatar · \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\" · \"Today · 4:25 PM\".\n- V7 · grouped: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" · \"Today · 5:40 PM\" · chevron. Grid cells draw it collapsed; only 01 shows it expanded into three rows (Clark Public Utilities $142.18, City of Vancouver water $84.00, Comcast $79.99).\n- V8 · gone-target: the landing after tapping a removed bill: the bill screen's header outline with a visible Back, and a plain body line \"That bill was removed.\" in the bill's slot. Back returns to the notifications list.\n- V9 · multi-home (fixture delta: Maya has a second home): V1 with line 2 \"Today · 5:40 PM · Larkspur Loop\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2, SF, S3, S4, SL)\n- S1 · unread: dot present.\n- S2 · read: no dot; identical text weight and fill.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the whole row.\n- S3 · push-off: a banner row at the top of the list, minimum 44pt: \"Push is off. You'll still see these here. · Turn on\", bodySmall text.strong on surface.sunken (dark: D3). The text wraps; \"Turn on\" stays trailing as a text button in primary.700 (5.39:1 on sunken; dark: dark border.focus, 6.83:1 on raised). An unread V1 sits under it.\n- S4 · offline: the FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" above the list. Rows stay readable and unread. Tapping a row whose object is not cached shows \"You're offline. This opens when you're back.\" under that row.\n- SL · landing: the column for V8 only, which has no unread state.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 21 cells)\n- S1 and S2: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6j, V6l, V7 collapsed (16).\n- S1: V9 (1). SF: V1 (1).\n- S3: V1 row: the banner above an unread V1 (1).\n- S4: V1 row: the FreshnessLine above unread V1 and V4, with the reason under V4 (1).\n- SL: V8 (1).\n- Every other position stays empty canvas.\n\nDARK (05): rows on dark surface.base. Unread dot D6, avatars D4, S3 banner D3 with \"Turn on\" in dark border.focus, marks in dark text.secondary. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V7 (collapsed) in both columns. The sentence wraps fully; line 2 wraps at middots. The dot column stays 12pt, top-aligned with line 1. The avatar stays 28pt. The V7 chevron moves below the text and stays part of the row target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03): captions: unread = dot presence + \"Unread\" spoken first · reminder provenance = mark shape · grouped = chevron + \"3 bills\". Add one extra cell: an unread V1 above a read V1, differing only by the dot, captioned \"unread is also spoken first\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Merged label, \"Unread\" first: \"Unread. Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid, 142 dollars 18 cents. Today, 5:40 PM.\"\n- Reminder rows end with the mark name: \"…Today, 7:00 AM, official.\"\n- The row is the target and lands on the exact object.\n- Grouped row: \"Sam marked 3 bills paid, collapsed, button\".\n- The S3 banner reads as text, then \"Turn on. Button.\"\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Amounts appear in-app only, never in pushes.\n- Use \"marked paid\", not \"paid\". The actor comes first.\n- Dates show the weekday; beyond tomorrow the relative count comes first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- A landing whose object is gone says \"That bill was removed.\"\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of bold text or a tinted background for unread rows, draw the 6pt dot plus the spoken \"Unread\". Weight and tint make read rows look disabled.\n- Instead of landing on a generic list when the object exists, land on the object: the bill row highlighted (BillRow highlighted-arrival).\n- Instead of an avatar on system rows, leave the slot empty and keep the text aligned.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): two crops (R13).\n1. f3-household-notifications · ios, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; the S3 banner; then V1 (unread), V4 (unread) and V3 (read); the legend line.\n2. f4-notification-settings · web-1440: the \"Household activity\" settings group with a sample V1 row. No row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add a \"NotificationRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"5:40 PM\", \"5:55 PM\", \"8:12 PM\", \"4:20 PM\", \"4:25 PM\" · \"Carts out\" · \"Gutter cleaning, in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov\" · \"Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · $142.18\" · \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\" · \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\" · \"You're offline. This opens when you're back.\" · \"Household activity\".\n- Fixture deltas: V1 shows Clark Public Utilities marked paid (BillRow shows it upcoming) · V6j Priya joined (fixture: pending) · V6l Sam left · V7 three bills marked paid · V9 Maya has a second home.\n- Contract/house conflicts: grouped row \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" instead of contract \"Sam paid 3 bills\" · \"Push is off…\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary limits \"push\" to technical settings copy · V4 reorders the fixture deadline to \"must arrive in 7 days · by Mon 26 Oct\" so the relative count comes first.\n- Assumptions: 7:00 AM is the morning briefing time (the house fixture uses 7:00 AM only as the AirNow observed time) · V5 carries YOU ADDED (household bills are entered by the household; the contract requires a mark but not which) · V8 sits in its own \"SL · landing\" column · V7 grid cells are collapsed.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · NotificationRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the NotificationRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five NotificationRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1, V4 and expanded V7 with callouts ①–⑦, the dashed row target and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 21 listed cells in columns S1, S2, SF, S3, S4, SL, labelled \"<code> · <key>\", each captioned \"NotificationRow · <variant key> · <state key>\" (V8: \"NotificationRow · gone-target · landing\"). V7 cells are collapsed.\n- The home label appears only on V9. Every relative count comes before its weekday date.\n- 03 shows V1 and V7 in both columns, the greyscale grid, its captions and the extra unread/read cell.\n- 04 shows both crops; the iOS crop has the legend line and \"Your household\".\n- 05 uses D3, D4, D6 and dark border.focus on \"Turn on\", with the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
