            "promptText": "Component 00c-08: TextActionRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: TextActionRow. This message is the complete TextActionRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). Tertiary actions that spread the product: share, compare and outbound links. They never outrank the primary action.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f8-native-share-compare · f8-compare-sheet · f8-seasonal-aha · f6-place-section-details · f8-compare-reveal.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 at 2x, and V2b at 2x below it.\n① Two text buttons side by side: \"Share this address\" and \"Compare with a friend\". Each is bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), with a 44pt / 48dp / 44px target, 8dp apart, no fill and no border. Draw both dashed targets and the 8dp gap.\n② Caption under the buttons: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"The card shows your city and your readings — never your address, and no name.\"\n③ Outbound variant: a bordered row, 48pt minimum, radius md 8, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal, with a 1px text.secondary edge (4.83:1 on base; a border token would fail as the only edge). It holds the destination text in bodySmall text.primary and a trailing 16pt external-link glyph \"↗\" in text.secondary. The whole row is the target. The \"↗\" at the end of each variant string below is this glyph: draw it once, as a vector, not as a text character.\n④ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · share-compare: ① plus ②.\n- V2a · outbound-test-kits: \"Free test kits · Washington Dept of Health ↗\".\n- V2b · outbound-votewa: \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, SF)\n- S1 · idle.\n- S2 · minting: on \"Compare with a friend\", a 12pt spinner (dark: D6) replaces the start of the label, which reads \"Making a link…\". Not re-tappable. Under Reduce Motion the spinner is removed and the words stay.\n- S3 · copied: the caption \"Link copied\" (role=status) sits between the buttons and the ② caption, and stays until the user leaves the screen.\n- S4 · cancelled: nothing changes. Draw the idle row again with the annotation \"share sheet dismissed: neutral, no message\".\n- S5 · offline: \"Compare with a friend\" is disabled per R8, with the reason \"You're offline. Compare needs a connection.\" \"Share this address\" stays enabled (the system share sheet works offline). Outbound rows are disabled: the destination text turns text.secondary (glyph unchanged), the edge stays, and \"You're offline. You can open this when you're back.\" sits under the row.\n- SF · focused: the ring 2px outside the V2b row.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 16 cells)\n- V1: S1, S2, S3, S4, S5 (5).\n- V2a and V2b: S1 and S5 (4).\n- V2a and V2b in S2, S3 and S4: \"n/a — outbound links open the browser\" (6).\n- V2b: SF (1).\n\nDARK (05): rows on dark surface.base. Buttons use dark border.focus. The outbound edge is a 1px dark text.secondary keyline (6.96:1 on dark base). Spinners use D6. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V2b in both columns. The two buttons stack, each full width with its own target. The caption wraps. The outbound row wraps its destination text; the glyph stays trailing, top-aligned.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions): actions = verbs and position, not colour · outbound = text.secondary edge + destination name + ↗ glyph · minting = \"Making a link…\" words · copied = \"Link copied\" words · offline = reason captions.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- Links name their destination: \"Check or update at VoteWA, opens in browser\".\n- \"Link copied\" is a status message.\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px, with 8dp between the two buttons.\n- The minting button is announced as \"Making a link\" and cannot be re-activated.\n- Disabled offline controls stay in the tree with their reason as a hint.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The V1 buttons start with a verb. Outbound rows name the destination as the contract gives it.\n- The caption states what the card reveals.\n- Use \"Compare with a friend\", never \"challenge\" or \"vs\".\n- Offline reasons open with \"You're offline\".\n\nPLATFORMS (panel)\n- Only the system share sheet is used. iOS supplies LPLinkMetadata; Android supplies EXTRA_TITLE to the system chooser; web uses the browser's share, falling back to copying the link (S3).\n- System UI is never redrawn by us: in 04 it is a surface.sunken frame with a 1px text.secondary keyline, labelled \"system UI\" in caption text.secondary.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of placing these actions inside the sticky WallBar, draw them on the page surface under the content card. The wall's single primary action must stay single.\n- Instead of an app-drawn Android chooser, draw the system chooser frame.\n- Instead of filled or bordered buttons for share and compare, draw text buttons, so they never outrank the primary.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops plus a platform strip (R13).\n1. f8-native-share-compare · ios: V1 under a seasonal card outline.\n2. f6-place-section-details · android, Place B: the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\" at the top; a radon row (\"Radon zone\" · \"Zone 1 — highest potential\" · filled mark · SourceCaption \"EPA · county-wide · as of 1993 map\") with V2a under it; the legend line.\n3. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390: V2b under the voter deadline line, which is plain text with no mark. No row menu button.\nPlatform strip: the iOS share sheet header and the Android system chooser header, each as the \"system UI\" frame described in PLATFORMS.\n\nNOTES (add a \"TextActionRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"The card shows your city and your readings — never your address, and no name.\" · \"Making a link…\" · \"Link copied\" · \"You're offline. Compare needs a connection.\" · \"You're offline. You can open this when you're back.\" · \"as of 1993 map\" in the radon SourceCaption.\n- Fixture gap: the house fixture gives the radon source as \"EPA, county-wide\" with no as-of; the crop adds an invented as-of so the caption has all three parts (invariant 5). Replace it when the real map date is confirmed.\n- Contract conflicts: outbound row edge drawn in text.secondary instead of a border token, because the house style forbids a border token as a meaningful edge · contract \"minting (spinner on the URL row)\" drawn on \"Compare with a friend\", because V1 has no URL row · V2a drawn as the contract gives it, without a leading verb.\n- Assumptions: \"Share this address\" stays enabled offline · outbound rows are disabled offline · the seasonal-aha voter deadline line carries no mark in this crop.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · TextActionRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · TextActionRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · TextActionRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · TextActionRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · TextActionRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 01-anatomy · light and 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the TextActionRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five TextActionRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1 and V2b with callouts ①–④, the dashed targets, the 8dp gap and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 16 listed cells (including six n/a cells with their reason), labelled \"<code> · <key>\" (outbound-test-kits, outbound-votewa), each captioned \"TextActionRow · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- Share and compare have no fill and no border; the outbound edge is text.secondary ink; each ↗ is drawn once, as the vector glyph.\n- The S3 \"Link copied\" sits between the buttons and the caption; the S4 cell looks like S1 and carries its annotation.\n- 03 shows V1 and V2b in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops and the two \"system UI\" frames; the Place B crop has the ScopeChip, the legend line and the three-part radon SourceCaption; the voter line has no mark.\n- 05 uses D6 and the dark keyline, with the Increase Contrast caption.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
