            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00c-11: InlineErrorRow. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: InlineErrorRow. This message is the complete InlineErrorRow specification.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). Shows a partial failure in one component. It names what failed and keeps everything else live.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f1-today-tab · f1-claim-receipt · f10-mail-day-triage · f10-snap-capture-tray · f10-bill-trend · f4-briefing-optin-card · f4-notification-settings · f6-home-basics-rows · f11-keeper-naming · f11-keeper-strip.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw V1 at 2x, sitting in the slot of an air section between two live section outlines. Beside it, draw V4 at 2x.\n① The row sits in the failed component's own slot and height, and keeps its position in the list. Minimum 44pt, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal.\n② Leading glyph, 16pt: an exclamation mark in a circle, in error hue (glyph only; dark: D7).\n③ Message: bodySmall 14/20, text.primary.\n④ Trailing \"Retry\" text button: bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), 44pt target. Draw its dashed target.\n⑤ Surface: surface.base. It is errorBg only when a write failed (V4; dark: D2). On errorBg, nothing uses text.secondary (R4). The error-on-errorBg pair is not in the R6 table, so write the measured caption \"error on errorBg 4.41:1\" beside the V4 glyph.\n⑥ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\")\n- V1 · provider-unreachable: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now · Retry\".\n- V2 · carry-failed: \"We couldn't move your water-heater warranty · Retry\".\n- V3 · upload-failed: \"Upload failed · Retry\".\n- V4 · save-failed, on errorBg, value preserved: above the row, the field it belongs to still shows \"Pickup day\" with the value \"Tuesday\" and a hollow ProvenanceMark (the confirm did not save). Maya tapped Tuesday to confirm the city schedule and the save failed. The row reads \"We couldn't save your pickup day. Your choice is still here. · Retry\".\n- V5 · fail-closed: draw an f9-block-founders-panel card (radius lg; dark: D8 edge) with its title \"Block Founders\" and a LockedActionRow in its card-header form directly under the title (\"Address verification needed to earn a Block Founder rank · Verify address\"). The founding meter, the invite banner and the Earn row are absent, with no gap and no error row. Outside the card, draw dashed annotation brackets where each would have been, labelled \"founding meter\", \"invite banner\" and \"Earn row\", plus the annotation \"fail-closed: nothing rendered, no error row\".\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, SF, S2)\n- S1 · failed.\n- SF · focused: the ring on \"Retry\" only.\n- S2 · retrying: \"Retry\" becomes \"Retrying…\" in bodySmallMedium (text.secondary on base, text.strong on errorBg), with a 12pt primary.700 spinner before it (dark: D6), or the static text under Reduce Motion. It is not re-tappable. The target stays in place and the message stays.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 11 cells)\n- S1: V1, V2, V3, V4 and V5 (5 cells). The V4 cell carries the caption \"error on errorBg 4.41:1\" beside its glyph.\n- SF: V1 (1 cell).\n- S2: V1, V2, V3 and V4 (4 cells). V5 in S2: \"n/a — nothing to retry\" (1 cell).\n\nDARK (05)\n- V1–V3 sit on dark surface.base; the error glyph keeps its hue (D7): caption \"error on dark base 3.70:1\" beside the first one.\n- V4 uses D2 (dark raised plus a 1.5px error border); its glyph measures 3.03:1 on dark raised, so caption that too.\n- V5's card uses D8: caption \"keyline 5.71:1\". Its LockedActionRow follows its own dark rules (dark text.secondary reason, dark border.focus link).\n- Spinners use D6. Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V4 in both columns.\n- The message wraps.\n- \"Retry\" drops below it, on its own line, and keeps its target.\n- The glyph scales with the text and stays top-aligned.\n- V4's field above keeps \"Tuesday\" and its hollow mark visible.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- failure = glyph shape (exclamation in a circle) + the words.\n- V4 = the words and the kept \"Tuesday\"; errorBg is not needed to understand it.\n- focused = ring.\n- retrying = \"Retrying…\" words.\n- fail-closed = absence, carried by the annotations.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- A polite live-region announcement when the row appears.\n- Retry names its target: V1 \"Retry air quality\"; V2 \"Retry moving your water-heater warranty\"; V3 \"Retry upload\"; V4 \"Retry saving pickup day\".\n- Retry targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- The retrying state is announced as \"Retrying\".\n- V5 announces nothing, because nothing is rendered.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- Messages are specific and blameless.\n- Name the source or the thing that failed, and say what to do next.\n- Typed and chosen input is kept.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): No platform differences.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of \"Oops, something went wrong\", draw \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now · Retry\". The user needs to know what failed.\n- Instead of hiding a failed row among successful ones or dropping it, draw it in its own slot and order, so nothing silently disappears.\n- Instead of an error row for a fail-closed component, draw nothing. A broken meter must never promise a slot.\n- Instead of clearing the field on a failed save, keep \"Tuesday\" in it.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f1-today-tab · ios, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; the pickup section above, still live, with its hollow mark (the confirm in crop 3 did not save); the air section replaced by V1; the legend line.\n2. f10-snap-capture-tray · android: a tray of three mail-photo items (56pt thumbnail slots drawn as outlines), with V3 under one item. The failed item's slot shows a 16pt retry glyph on surface.sunken, as ThumbnailRail's failed form.\n3. f6-home-basics-rows · web-390, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; V4 under its \"Pickup day\" field, which shows \"Tuesday\" with a hollow mark; the legend line.\n\nNOTES (add an \"InlineErrorRow\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"We couldn't save your pickup day. Your choice is still here.\" · \"Retrying…\" · \"Retry moving your water-heater warranty\" · \"Retry upload\" · \"Retry saving pickup day\" · \"Retrying\" (spoken).\n- Fixture deltas: V4 and crop 3: Maya tapped Tuesday to confirm the city schedule and the save failed, so the mark stays hollow (this keeps crop 1's hollow pickup mark consistent).\n- Contract conflicts: V2 drawn as \"water-heater warranty\" instead of contract \"furnace warranty\", to match the fixture · V3 \"Upload failed\" drawn as the contract gives it, although the glossary lists \"upload\" under Not for mail photos.\n- Assumptions: the \"Retrying…\" colour (text.secondary, or text.strong on errorBg) · the primary.700 spinner in light · error glyph on errorBg measured at 4.41:1 (a pair not in the R6 table; passes the 3:1 graphic check), captioned on 01 and 02.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · InlineErrorRow · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · InlineErrorRow · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then add the InlineErrorRow section to 00c · Notes and update its board section. Stop and wait for the next component message.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five InlineErrorRow artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows V1 in its slot and V4 with callouts ①–⑥, the Retry target and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 11 listed cells (including one n/a cell with its reason), labelled and captioned per R7.\n- Error hue appears only on the glyph (and the D2 border in dark); message text is text.primary.\n- Only V4 uses errorBg; its field still shows \"Tuesday\" with a hollow mark; its row names the pickup day; the \"error on errorBg 4.41:1\" caption sits on 01 and 02.\n- S2 cells show a primary.700 spinner in light and D6 in dark.\n- The V5 cell shows the card with no gap and no error row, plus the three dashed brackets and the annotation.\n- 03 shows V1 and V4 in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops; the Today crop and the home-basics crop each have the legend line, \"Your household\" and a hollow pickup mark; the tray crop's failed slot shows the retry glyph on surface.sunken.\n- 05 uses D2, D6, D7 and D8 with their captions.\n- Every string is in this message or listed on Notes."
          }
        ],
