            "promptText": "Component 00c-12: ThumbnailRail. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPUBLISH NAME: ThumbnailRail. This message is the complete ThumbnailRail specification. It is the last component on this board, so its Turn 2 also finishes 00c · Notes.\n\nPURPOSE (print at the top of 01). The optional leading photo slot on mail rows and in the capture queue.\n\nUSED IN (panel): f10-mail-day-triage · f10-snap-capture-tray · f10-mail-piece-photo · f10-mail-snap-privacy · f10-bill-provenance.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy)\nDraw the three sizes side by side at 2x, then V1 in S2, S3, S4 and SX at 2x below them, then V5 with the rail collapsed.\n① Thumbnail sizes, all radius md 8: triage 56×56pt · drawer 40×52pt · privacy list 32×32pt. The thumbnail sits 12pt (spacing.3) before the row text.\n② Photo content: a neutral envelope on a grey table, with no legible name, address or amount.\n③ No photo: the rail collapses. The text moves to the leading margin, with no empty square.\n④ Uploading: a determinate ring inside the thumbnail, 2pt stroke, primary.700 on a border.strong track (4.03:1; dark: D6), plus the text \"Uploading 2 of 3\" beside the row in caption text.secondary. This is transfer progress, not a score, and it never carries a percentage.\n⑤ Failed: a 16pt retry glyph in text.strong, centred on a surface.sunken thumbnail (dark: D4), plus the row caption \"Upload failed · Retry\". That caption is InlineErrorRow's upload-failed variant, drawn as specified in the previous message.\n⑥ Deleted: a quiet 16pt document glyph in text.secondary on surface.sunken (dark: D4), plus the words \"photo deleted Mon 12 Oct\" in caption text.secondary.\n⑦ Selected: a primary.50 fill behind the row plus a leading check glyph (dark: D5). Below it, a visible action row of three text buttons, each with a 44pt / 48dp target, 8dp apart: \"Retake\" · \"Delete\" · \"Same letter as previous\". Draw their dashed targets. The progress ring never sits under or next to the Delete target.\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"the visible action row holds the actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows; label each \"<code> · <key>\"). Mail fixtures: Clark Public Utilities, Comcast.\n- V1 · triage: 56pt thumbnail · \"Clark Public Utilities\" (bodyMedium, text.primary) · \"Bill · $142.18\" (bodySmall, text.secondary).\n- V2 · drawer: 40×52pt thumbnail · \"Comcast\".\n- V3 · privacy: 32pt thumbnail · \"Photo of your mail · Mon 19 Oct\".\n- V4 · queue: two joined pieces drawn as a stacked thumbnail (two 56pt rectangles, offset 4pt) plus the label \"2 pages\".\n- V5 · no-photo: V1 with the rail collapsed (③).\n\nSTATES (columns, in this order: S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, SX, SF)\n- S1 · default.\n- S2 · uploading: the ④ ring plus \"Uploading 2 of 3\".\n- S3 · failed: ⑤.\n- S4 · deleted: ⑥.\n- S5 · offline: the thumbnail is a surface.sunken slot (dark: D4) with a 16pt cloud-off glyph in text.strong, and the caption \"You're offline. This photo isn't saved on this device.\"\n- SX · selected: ⑦, with the action row.\n- SF · focused: the ring on the whole row.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05; 15 cells)\n- V1: S1, S2, S3, S4 and S5 (5 cells).\n- V2: S1, S2 and S4 (3 cells).\n- V3: S1 and S4 (2 cells).\n- V4: S1 and S2 (2 cells).\n- V5: S1 (1 cell).\n- V1: SX with its action row, and SF directly beside it (2 cells).\n\nDARK (05)\n- Rows sit on dark surface.base. Thumbnail slots use D4. The ring uses D6 on a dark border.strong track (4.81:1). Selection uses D5, with the action row buttons in dark border.focus.\n- Add the Increase Contrast caption (R5).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 in S2 and V1 in SX, in both columns.\n- The thumbnail stays 56pt, top-aligned.\n- The title and the progress text wrap below one another.\n- The action row stacks into three full-width buttons, each with a 44pt / 48dp target.\n\nGREYSCALE (03 captions)\n- uploading = ring + \"Uploading 2 of 3\".\n- failed = retry glyph + \"Upload failed\".\n- deleted = document glyph + \"photo deleted\".\n- offline = cloud-off glyph + the caption.\n- selected = check glyph + the visible action row.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel)\n- The thumbnail is part of the row element: \"Clark Public Utilities, bill, photo, uploading 2 of 3\".\n- Retake, Delete and Same letter as previous are visible buttons and also custom actions.\n- No action is long-press-only or hover-only.\n- Upload progress is a polite status (live region).\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel)\n- The contract lists none. Use \"Photo of your mail\" for the stored image, never \"scan\" or \"document\".\n- Upload progress reads \"Uploading 2 of 3\", with no percentage.\n\nPLATFORMS (panel): web converts HEIC to JPEG before rendering; add a callout on the web crop. iOS and Android render natively.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel)\n- Instead of a broken-image icon, draw the ⑥ deleted glyph with words, or the ⑤ retry glyph.\n- Instead of placing the progress ring under or near the Delete target, keep the ring inside the thumbnail and the action row separate, so a tap meant for Delete never lands on progress.\n- Instead of an empty square when there is no photo, collapse the rail.\n- Instead of a percentage beside the ring, draw \"Uploading 2 of 3\". Percentages are banned by house invariant 6.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04): three crops (R13).\n1. f10-mail-day-triage · ios: V1, V5, then V1 selected with its action row.\n2. f10-snap-capture-tray · android: V4, then V1 in S2.\n3. f10-mail-snap-privacy · web-1440: ScopeChip \"Your household\" at the top; V3 rows, one of them in S4 (deleted); a callout \"web converts HEIC to JPEG before rendering\". No row menu button.\n\nNOTES (add a \"ThumbnailRail\" section to 00c · Notes)\n- Invented strings: \"Bill · $142.18\" · \"Photo of your mail · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"2 pages\" · \"Uploading 2 of 3\" · \"photo deleted Mon 12 Oct\" · \"You're offline. This photo isn't saved on this device.\"\n- Contract conflicts: the contract's uploading string (a count plus a percentage) is not drawn, because house invariant 6 and the research brief rejected percentages; drawn as \"Uploading 2 of 3\" with a determinate ring · \"Uploading\" and \"Upload failed\" drawn as specified, although the glossary lists \"upload\" under Not for mail photos.\n\nARTBOARDS (exact names)\n- 00c · ThumbnailRail · 01-anatomy · light\n- 00c · ThumbnailRail · 02-grid · light\n- 00c · ThumbnailRail · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n- 00c · ThumbnailRail · 04-in-context · light\n- 00c · ThumbnailRail · 05-grid · dark\n- 00c · Notes (final update)\n\nBATCH PLAN\n- Turn 1 (now): 00c · ThumbnailRail · 01-anatomy · light and 00c · ThumbnailRail · 02-grid · light. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\n- Turn 2 (after \"continue\"): 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light, 04-in-context · light and 05-grid · dark. Then finish 00c · Notes: add the ThumbnailRail section, then complete the board section (every D1–D8 use across all twelve components with its captions, the Increase Contrast note, the stand-ins you drew, any string you added, and any state you could not draw). Keep Notes as the last artboard. Then list, in your reply, every artboard on the board (61 in total: 60 component artboards and Notes) and confirm each one exists.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The five ThumbnailRail artboards exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- 01 shows the three sizes, the collapse and the four state specimens with callouts ①–⑧, the action-row targets and the five panels.\n- 02 and 05 hold exactly the 15 listed cells, labelled \"<code> · <key>\" with printed keys, each captioned \"ThumbnailRail · <variant key> · <state key>\".\n- No percentage is drawn on any specimen, callout, crop or Notes line; progress reads \"Uploading 2 of 3\".\n- No empty square appears on V5, and no broken-image icon appears anywhere.\n- SX and SF sit side by side and look different; the ring is never near Delete.\n- 03 shows V1 in S2 and SX in both columns and the greyscale grid with its captions.\n- 04 shows the three crops, with the HEIC callout on the web crop.\n- 05 uses D4, D5 and D6 and carries the Increase Contrast caption.\n- 00c · Notes is complete: its board section and twelve component sections, each item on one line.\n- Every string on the board is in these messages or listed on Notes."
          }
        ],
        "clean": true
      },
      {
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "00d-00",
            "promptText": "Foundations board 00d: States, feedback and asks. BOARD SETUP.\n\nUse the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is one Foundations board. This message sets the board rules and draws nothing. Eight component prompts follow, one per turn: 1 QuietDayReceipt, 2 WarmingSkeleton, 3 InlineUndo, 4 DestructiveConfirm, 5 LandingBannerSlot, 6 NotificationAsk, 7 PushCopy, 8 ReminderLeadControl. Each opens with \"Component 00d-NN: <Name>. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\" and carries that component's complete specification.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nA NEW component specimen board with no screens. These components cover the moments when the product must be honest about time and consent: nothing is wrong, something is loading, something can or can't be taken back, something is waiting, and the product wants to interrupt now or on dates you chose. Each has a quiet default; none nags. Later, 59 surfaces are designed in separate projects with no memory of this one, using these components by exact name from the published Pantopus design system. So every size, token, string and state in a component prompt is literal: draw each component once, precisely, with every variant and state listed.\n\nHOW THIS PROJECT RUNS\n1. Each component prompt has an ARTBOARDS list and a BATCH PLAN of at most 6 artboards per turn. Draw batch 1 and stop; the founder types \"continue\" before each later batch. After a component's last batch, wait for the next component prompt.\n2. Before every batch, re-read R1–R19 and the whole current component prompt. Don't carry details between components unless a prompt says so.\n3. Component order replaces the house-style priority order: finish each component, dark twin included, before the next. A named attachment arrives with its component prompt.\n4. Ask a question only if two readings would give materially different specimens. Otherwise decide, and record it on Notes (R19).\n\nPUBLISH (a founder step)\nThe founder adds each accepted component to the Pantopus design system under its exact name, with each specimen under the name printed beneath it (R7). Notes F lists every name.\n- Every drawn specimen except the review aids below is published in light. Every specimen on a dark artboard is published in dark; every variant × state cell has a dark twin there.\n- Light-only frames (platform strips, large-text frames, web-1440 crops, anything a prompt marks light only) are published in light only and listed on Notes E. A later dark surface takes their geometry from the light frame and their colours from R9.\n- Review aids, never published: greyscale copies, \"Not applicable\" cells, \"Not this\" thumbnails, IN CONTEXT crops, and anything a prompt calls a review aid.\n\nBOARD RULES\n\nR1. Artboard names. \"00d · <Component> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\", exactly as the ARTBOARDS list gives it. This replaces the house-style name format on this board, because one artboard can hold several platforms; the platform goes in each specimen name (R7). The Notes artboard is \"00d · Notes\", with no suffix. Print the name above the frame in label 13/18/600 text.strong.\n\nR2. Artboard format. 1600px wide, as tall as needed, on surface.app (dark: dark app). Top left: the component name in h2 24/32/600 text.primary, then the artboard's subject in body text.secondary. Each 01 artboard also prints PURPOSE (body text.secondary) and \"Used in:\" (caption 12/16 text.secondary). Section headings are overline 11/16/600 caps text.strong.\n\nR3. Platforms. Specimens are 1x at real width: iOS 393pt, Android 412dp, web-390 390px, web-1440 1440px (cropped to the relevant column, labelled \"web-1440 crop\"). Content width inside 16 margins: 361pt iOS, 380dp Android, 358px web-390.\n\nR4. Units and type. pt, dp and px have equal values, except targets (R11). Spacing uses only the 4px scale. Type uses only the house-style scale, plus bodyMedium 16/24/500, bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 and the R17 large-text sizes. Other dimensions appear only where a prompt states them.\n\nR5. Callouts. A numbered SQUARE marker (20×20, radius xs 4, surface.sunken fill, 1px text.strong outline, numeral in label 13/18/600 text.strong, centred), joined to its part by a 1px text.secondary leader. The key sits beside the specimen in caption 12/16 text.strong as number · size · token (\"1 · 16pt tick glyph · text.secondary\"). Markers are never circles (circles mean provenance). Dimension rulers are 1px text.secondary with 4px end ticks and the number in caption text.secondary.\n\nR6. Grids. A \"variants-by-states\" artboard is a table: rows are variants, columns are states, in the order given. Headers are label 13/18/600 text.strong in sentence case (\"V1 · Removed row\"). Each cell holds one specimen unless the prompt lists more. Draw every cell. A combination that doesn't apply is a surface.sunken cell with \"Not applicable: <the prompt's reason>\" in caption text.strong, never blank.\n\nR7. Keys and names. Each grid row and column prints \"key: <key>\" under its label in caption 12/16 text.secondary: lowercase, hyphenated, no \"/\", never a fixture string, name, amount or date. Use each prompt's keys exactly. Under every specimen, print its published name in caption 12/16 text.strong:\n  <Component> / <variant-key> / <state-key> / <platform> / <light|dark>\nfor example \"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo / ios / light\". Platform keys: ios, android, web-390, web-1440; large text: ios-ax5, ios-ax2, ios-ax-widget, android-200, android-150; \"any\" where a prompt calls a specimen platform-neutral. An anatomy specimen that repeats a grid cell carries that cell's name.\n\nR8. Tokens. Label every colour by token name; hex appears only in R9 and R10. The house-style TOKEN USAGE rules apply: semantic hues on glyphs and borders only; text.muted for disabled labels only; readable secondary text is text.secondary on base, raised or app, and text.strong on sunken; borders are decoration, never the only edge of a control, segment or card.\n\nR9. Dark mapping. Each dark artboard redraws its light twin:\n  surface.base → #0F172A (dark base) · surface.raised → #1E293B (dark raised) · surface.app → #020617 (dark app) · surface.sunken → dark base (same colour, separates nothing)\n  text.primary → #E5E7EB · text.strong → #F1F5F9 · text.secondary → #94A3B8 · text.muted → #64748B · text.inverse → #111827\n  border.default → #1F2937 · border.strong → #374151 · border.focus and primary.700 → #38BDF8 · primary.50 (selected fill) → primary.900 #0c4a6e with #E5E7EB text\n  semantic.error #DC2626 and semantic.warning #D97706 keep their hue.\n  A dark card's edge is the fill step (raised on app), never a border, with no shadow. Dialogs and sheets are dark base. Print the container surface each prompt names in the dark frame's subject line.\n\nR10. Contrast figures. The only figures on the board; prompts cite them as \"(R10)\". Print the figure beside the part; never compute a new one.\n  Light on base: text.secondary 4.83:1 · primary.700 5.93:1 · text.inverse on primary.700 5.93:1 · semantic.error 4.83:1 · semantic.warning 3.19:1 · text.muted 2.54:1.\n  Light on sunken: text.strong 9.37:1 · primary.700 5.39:1 (text.secondary is only 4.39:1 here).\n  Light selection: primary.700 border on primary.50 5.57:1.\n  Dark on raised: #94A3B8 5.71:1 · #38BDF8 6.83:1 · #D97706 4.59:1 · #DC2626 3.03:1 (glyphs only) · #64748B 3.07:1 · #1F2937 1.00:1 (never an edge).\n  Dark on base: #94A3B8 6.96:1 · #38BDF8 8.33:1 · #F1F5F9 16.30:1 · #DC2626 3.70:1 · #64748B 3.75:1 · #111827 on #38BDF8 8.28:1.\n  Dark selection: #E5E7EB on primary.900 7.64:1 · #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42:1 (checks and borders only) · primary.900 on dark base 1.89:1 (a fill; the #38BDF8 border is the edge).\n\nR11. Targets. Minimum hit areas: 44×44pt iOS, 48×48dp Android with 8dp gaps, 44×44px web, each drawn as a dashed 1px text.secondary rectangle labelled with its size. A glyph is never a target on its own.\n\nR12. Focus and selection. Focus: a 2px border.focus ring with a 2px gap. Selection: primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, 16pt primary.700 check, 600-weight text.primary label (dark per R9). They never look alike. A prompt may define one further treatment, in full.\n\nR13. Glyphs and circles. Pantopus icon set only, 16pt unless stated, 1.5px stroke. Filled vs hollow circles mean provenance only, so no glyph, tick, bullet, marker or control is a plain disc or ring; the one exception is an avatar circle (MemberRow or its skeleton), which is never a mark. A tick is a bare check stroke. No control uses a radio circle, on any platform or text size: at large sizes, the brief's \"radio rows\" are list rows with the R12 selection check.\n\nR14. Strings. Use the house-style FIXTURES exactly (TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific). Every string comes from the house style or the current prompt; any string you add goes on Notes D. Print character counts where given. No string ends in an ellipsis unless a prompt says so. Dates show the weekday.\n\nR15. Other boards' components. FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, KindGlyph, AqiBand, ScaleStrip, PickupCard, MemberRow and the Pantopus app icon come from the published design system. If one isn't published yet, draw a surface.sunken box at this size with its name in caption text.strong, and list it on Notes C: FourteenDayStrip 361×40pt · YearBand 361×120pt, four 24pt lanes · AqiBand 361×48pt · ScaleStrip row 361×48pt · PickupCard 361×196pt · MemberRow 361×56pt · KindGlyph 16pt or 42pt square, as stated · app icon 20pt square. Never draw a fallback where the published component exists.\n\nR16. Disabled controls. A disabled control stays focusable and reads \"<label>, unavailable, <reason>\". Its label is text.muted, and the reason is also written nearby in readable text. No button is silently dead.\n\nR17. Standard artboards.\n  - \"01-anatomy\" (light): the default specimen with callouts, sizes, tokens and R10 figures.\n  - \"variants-by-states\" (light and dark): the R6 grid.\n  - \"ax5-200-greyscale\" (light), three required columns. (a) iOS AX5: caption 12 → 43pt, label 13 → 44pt, bodySmall 14 → about 46pt, body 16 → 51pt (Callout), h3 20 → 55pt. (b) Android 200%, Android 14 non-linear: caption 12 → 24sp, label 13 → 25sp, bodySmall 14 → 26sp, body 16 → about 28sp, h3 20 → about 34sp. (c) Greyscale copies of the light default and the most state-heavy light cell, captioned \"Reads without colour: <cue>\". Extra frames a prompt lists go in labelled rows below. At these sizes pairs stack, text wraps instead of truncating, sheets may scroll (sticky buttons reserve padding), glyphs scale with text up to 2×, and hit areas grow.\n  - \"in-context-and-rules\" (light), five panels in order. IN CONTEXT: two or three crops (393pt or 390px wide, about 300pt tall), each labelled with its surface id and captioned \"host illustrative, not a spec\", then \"Also consumed by: <ids>\"; draw undesigned hosts only as far as needed. ACCESSIBILITY. COPY. PLATFORMS. INSTEAD OF: \"Instead of X, draw Y — because Z\", with a struck-through thumbnail of X labelled \"Not this\" beside one of Y.\n\nR18. Motion. Transitions have a purpose and last 300ms or less; idle loops stop within 5 s. Wherever something moves, draw its Reduce Motion form (cross-fade or static). Nothing is gesture-only or hover-only.\n\nR19. Notes. \"00d · Notes\" is shared by all eight components: create it in QuietDayReceipt's last batch, extend it in each later last batch, never drop entries. Body 16/24 text.primary on surface.base, overline headings, grouped by component:\n  A. Decisions and contract conflicts for the founder, numbered 1.1 … 8.n: each prompt's items plus anything you decided. A opens with:\n     0.1 Dark selection is a primary.900 fill with a #38BDF8 border and check, the same everywhere. Confirm.\n     0.2 Dark text.strong, text.muted, text.inverse and border.strong (#F1F5F9, #64748B, #111827, #374151) are board assumptions; the house style lists none. Confirm or map them to published dark tokens.\n     0.3 The brief turns long segmented controls into \"radio rows\" at large sizes; this board draws list rows with the R12 check, never radio circles. Confirm.\n  B. Assumptions.\n  C. Missing dependencies: every R15 fallback box, and any named attachment that didn't arrive.\n  D. Invented strings: each prompt's list plus any you added. Board chrome, once: \"host illustrative, not a spec\" · \"Not this\" · each \"Not applicable: <reason>\" · \"key: <key>\" · \"Reads without colour: <cue>\" · \"web-1440 crop\" · \"Also consumed by:\" · callout key texts. Row labels and component callouts go in each component's list.\n  E. Omitted, with reason, plus each component's light-only frames and review aids.\n  F. Publish index: every specimen name per component, light first, then dark.\n\nReply 'ready' and wait for the first component.",
