            "promptText": "Component 00d-01: QuietDayReceipt. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Makes silence readable: a finished \"nothing needs you\" state that lists the checks that were run.\nUsed in (print on 01): f1-today-tab, f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file, f7-today-widget, f4-briefing-optin-card, f4-notification-settings, f11-keeper-strip\nATTACH: none. This component hasn't shipped yet.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then create Notes)\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (create it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Today full = today-full · V2 Widget one-liner = widget-one-liner · V3 Briefing settings row = briefing-settings-row · V4 Strip empty = strip-empty · V5 Year band empty = year-band-empty.\nStates: S1 All ticked = all-ticked · S2 One pending = one-pending · S3 One failed = one-failed.\nExample: \"QuietDayReceipt / today-full / all-ticked / ios / light\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: the V1 S1 specimen on iOS 393 with callouts)\n1. Card: surface.base, radius lg 12, padding 16, shadow sm. Width is the host's content width: 361pt iOS, 380dp Android, 358px web-390, 560px max in the web-1440 Today column.\n2. Heading: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, \"Nothing needs your attention today\". It appears only in S1.\n3. Receipt line, 8pt below the heading: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Checked 6:00 PM\" (R10: 4.83:1).\n4. CheckItem row, 12pt below the receipt line: four CheckItems with 16pt gaps, \"weather\", \"air\", \"alerts\", \"your calendar\", in that order, wrapping to a second row if the width runs out.\n5. CheckItem: a 16pt tick glyph (bare check stroke) in text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1), a 4pt gap, then the label in caption 12/16 text.secondary. An optional source time follows in the same style after \" · \". Draw one such item as an inset beside the card: \"air · 7:00 AM\" (the AirNow observation time), named \"QuietDayReceipt / checkitem-with-time / all-ticked / ios / light\".\n6. No illustration, no keeper, no colour fill and no semantic tint.\nCallout on the card: \"The whole receipt reads as one line: Checked 6:00 PM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\".\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 Today full: the card above (f1-today-tab).\nV2 Widget one-liner: a 338×158pt medium widget on surface.base (radius per the widget family) holding only one caption 12/16 text.secondary line, top-left inside 16pt margins, with no card and no place label (the label belongs to f7-today-widget, shown in IN CONTEXT). Widget text is never below 11pt.\nV3 Briefing settings row: a settings row under the Briefings group, bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary (f4-notification-settings, f4-briefing-optin-card).\nV4 Strip empty: a FourteenDayStrip (R15) with 14 empty day cells in one ink colour, then a caption line (f5-today-calendar-strip).\nV5 Year band empty: a YearBand (R15) with 12 month columns and the lanes You / City / County / State left empty, then a caption line (x-place-file).\nV4 and V5 are fixture-free: no address, place label or scope. Their failed state names the City of Vancouver calendar.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 All ticked: the only state that shows the heading (V1) or the all-clear phrase (V2–V5).\nS2 One pending: no heading. The \"air\" CheckItem shows a pending mark instead of a tick: three 3pt rounded squares in a row inside the 16pt glyph box, text.secondary, never a single dot or circle. Its label reads \"air · not back yet\". The receipt line still reads \"Checked 6:00 PM\". Nothing animates.\nS3 One failed: no heading. The \"air\" CheckItem becomes a line: a 16pt error glyph (semantic.error, R10: 4.83:1), then \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, then a \"Retry\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44×44pt hit area. The other three items keep their ticks.\n\nGRID CELLS (every string on this component is here or in ANATOMY)\n- V1: S1, S2, S3 as above.\n- V2. S1 \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\" · S2 \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\" · S3 \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\", with no Retry, because tapping the widget opens Today, where Retry lives.\n- V3. S1 \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\" · S2 \"Not applicable: the row appears only after tonight's check has finished\" · S3 error glyph, then \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\", Retry a 44pt text button.\n- V4. S1 the empty strip plus \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" · S2 \"Not applicable: the strip shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\" · S3 no strip; the slot shows the error glyph, then \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\", Retry a 44pt text button.\n- V5. S1 the empty band plus \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" · S2 \"Not applicable: the year band shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\" · S3 no band; the error glyph, then \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\", Retry a 44pt text button.\n\nGRIDS\n02 light: the 5 × 3 grid, iOS specimens (platform key ios).\n03 dark: the same grid per R9. Container: the V1 card and V3 settings group are dark raised on dark app; the V2 widget is dark raised; V4 and V5 sit on dark raised. Print beside the parts: ticks and pending squares #94A3B8 (R10: 5.71:1), error glyph #DC2626 (R10: 3.03:1), Retry #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1).\n\n04-ax5-200-greyscale (light, per R17)\n- (a) iOS AX5, V1 at S1, S2, S3: the heading wraps (about four lines) and never truncates. CheckItems become a vertical list, one item per line. Retry drops under \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" onto its own line, at least 44pt tall. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) Android 200%, V1 at S1, S2, S3: the same vertical list with 48dp rows. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 at S1, S2, S3. Caption: \"Reads without colour: glyph shape (check / three squares / error glyph) and words ('not back yet', 'Couldn't reach')\".\n- Row \"Widget at AX sizes\": V2 at S1, S2, S3, text only, no glyphs. Widget text caps at 20/28 (the widget's large-text cap) and wraps to at most three lines in the 306×126pt content area. Names: \"QuietDayReceipt / widget-one-liner / <state-key> / ios-ax-widget / light\".\n- Row \"Platforms\": V1 S1 on Android 412 (\"QuietDayReceipt / today-full / all-ticked / android / light\") and as a 560px web-1440 crop (\"QuietDayReceipt / today-full / all-ticked / web-1440 / light\").\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The card is read as a list. S1: \"Nothing needs your attention today. Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" S2: \"Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, alerts, your calendar. Air: not back yet.\" S3: \"Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, alerts, your calendar. Couldn't reach AirNow.\" followed by the button \"Retry air quality\".\n- Every tick is paired with a word; state is carried by glyph shape plus words. Retry is 44pt iOS, 48dp Android, 44px web; CheckItems are not targets.\n- S2 → S1 is announced politely, once, without moving focus.\n\nCOPY. The heading appears only when every check succeeded. Never \"All caught up\", \"Inbox zero\" or \"You're all set\". Print the strings from ANATOMY and GRID CELLS.\n\nPLATFORMS. The same everywhere; width is the host's content width (ANATOMY 1). Only target size and the text-only AX widget differ.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05, per R17). All crops show PLACE B, viewer Jordan Lee, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. His pickup is Thursday, so nothing is due tonight and the quiet state is true.\n- f1-today-tab: Today for PLACE B with the scope string \"Saved place · Only you\", the AqiBand (R15) and the V1 card under it.\n- f7-today-widget: the medium widget with the place label \"Birchfield Ct\" above the V2 line.\n- f4-notification-settings: Jordan's Briefings group with \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" and the V3 row under it.\nAlso consumed by: f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file, f4-briefing-optin-card, f11-keeper-strip\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"All caught up\", \"Inbox zero\" or \"You're all set\", draw the heading with the four checks — because people need to see what was checked, not a mood.\n- Instead of the heading while a provider is loading, draw S2 — because an early all-clear teaches people to stop trusting it.\n- Instead of an illustration or keeper pose, draw the plain card — because silence is a fact, not a celebration.\n- Instead of ticks in circles, draw bare check strokes — because filled vs hollow means provenance.\n- Instead of \"Something went wrong\", draw \"Couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" — because a failed check names its provider.\n\nNOTES (create 00d · Notes per R19 and add)\nA. 1.1 V4 caption: the contract says \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\"; brief section 4 says \"next 14 days\". This board uses the contract. Confirm.\n   1.2 Pending mark: the contract says one pending dot. This board draws three 3pt rounded squares so it can't read as a filled provenance mark. Confirm.\n   1.3 Spoken label: the contract says \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" This board adds the heading (S1) and the time. Confirm.\n   1.4 IN CONTEXT uses PLACE B, because HOME A has pickup Tue 20 Oct, so its Monday evening is not quiet.\n   1.5 At AX sizes the widget is text only, capped at 20/28 and at most three lines in 306×126pt (key ios-ax-widget). Confirm the cap.\nB. Jordan's last briefing was Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM, the night before his Thursday pickup. The V2 grid widget carries no place label.\nC. AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip or YearBand, if drawn as a fallback box.\nD. Every string in GRID CELLS and ANATOMY that is not in the contract or house style, plus: \"air · 7:00 AM\" · the S1–S3 spoken labels · \"Retry air quality\" (spoken) · \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" · \"Birchfield Ct\" (from the fixture street) · chrome: row labels \"Widget at AX sizes\" and \"Platforms\", the one-line receipt callout.\nE. Light only: the 04 ios-ax5, android-200, ios-ax-widget, android and web-1440 frames, and the checkitem-with-time inset. Omitted: none.\nF. Light: the 12 drawn grid cells, the inset, and the light-only 04 frames. Dark: the same 12 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 5 artboards and 00d · Notes (sections A–F) exist with the exact names.\n- The heading appears only in V1 S1; no S2 or S3 cell shows an all-clear.\n- No tick or pending mark is a circle or sits in one.\n- Retry has a dashed hit area everywhere except the widget.\n- The dark grid prints its container and figures.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02 light, 03 dark. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04, 05, 00d · Notes (create it). Stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read R1–R19 and this whole message."
