            "promptText": "Component 00d-02: WarmingSkeleton. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Content-shaped placeholders that sit in their final slots during cold loads of 1–10 s, so nothing jumps when the data arrives.\nUsed in (print on 01): f1-today-tab, x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f1-your-places, f3-members-roster, f3-household-block, f3-member-home-dashboard, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map, f10-bill-trend, f11-keeper-strip, f7-widget-tap-landing\nATTACH (optional, tone only): docs/screenshots/hub-v2-skeleton-ios.png, hub-v2-skeleton-android.png, hub-v2-skeleton-web.png. Their layout is not a spec.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion · light\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Section skeleton = section-skeleton · V2 Row skeleton = row-skeleton · V3 Instrument skeleton, four sub-specimens with their own keys: a = instrument-skeleton-strip · b = instrument-skeleton-year-band · c = instrument-skeleton-scale-strip · d = instrument-skeleton-bill-trend · V4 Panel skeleton = panel-skeleton.\nStates: S1 Shimmer = shimmer · S2 Static = static · S3 Replaced progressively = replaced-progressively.\nExamples: \"WarmingSkeleton / section-skeleton / shimmer / ios / light\" · \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument-skeleton-bill-trend / static / ios / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 at S1 on iOS 393 with callouts, plus V3d at S1 beside it, named \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument-skeleton-bill-trend / shimmer / ios / light\")\n1. Shapes are surface.sunken fills on surface.base cards, matching the final geometry: strip cells, track shapes, row bars, avatar circles. A count of facts is a number bar plus pill chip bars (the count is an integer plus chips, so there is no ring skeleton). Each shape takes the radius of the part it stands in for. Shapes are filled, never outlined, because an outline-only skeleton reads as an empty state. The avatar circle is placeholder geometry and carries no meaning (R13).\n2. The skeleton reserves the exact final height. Beside it, draw a height ruler; beside a loaded version, a second ruler; caption both \"same height\". The loaded version is a review aid, not published: AqiBand (AQI 42 Good), PickupCard for HOME A (recycling and garbage, Tue 20 Oct) and the V3a loaded strip below, as R15 components or fallback boxes.\n3. No text, no glyphs and no \"checking…\" inside a skeleton.\n4. Shimmer: a soft band 30% of the shape's width, surface.base at 60% opacity, sweeping left to right. 1.2 s per pass; it stops after 4 passes (4.8 s) and holds static. This is an idle loop under the 5 s rule, not a 300ms transition (Notes 2.4). Draw the band mid-sweep with the callout \"1.2 s per pass · stops after 4 passes\".\n5. Container: one accessibility element labelled \"Loading\" (callout).\n6. Print on the board: \"Skeleton shapes are decorative and have no contrast requirement.\"\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows), all iOS 393. Strip geometry everywhere: 14 cells, each (361 − 52) / 14 ≈ 22.07pt wide, 4pt gaps, 361pt overall, radius xs.\nV1 Section skeleton (f1-today-tab), three blocks in one column:\n  - Air band: a 48pt row with a 12pt filled track shape (radius pill) and a 96×12pt label bar.\n  - Pickup card: a card with a 42×42pt square (radius md) in the KindGlyph slot, two bars (200×20pt and 240×14pt, radius xs) and two 44pt button shapes of equal width (radius md).\n  - Fourteen-day strip: the strip geometry, 40pt tall.\nV2 Row skeleton (lists): three rows, each as tall as the final row it stands in for, drawn at 56pt (the MemberRow height) with the caption \"height = the consuming row's final height\". 16pt horizontal padding; a 40pt avatar circle and two bars (60% width × 14pt, 40% width × 12pt, 4pt apart), all vertically centred in the 56pt row.\nV3 Instrument skeleton, four labelled sub-specimens stacked in the cell:\n  a. 14-day strip: the strip geometry at 40pt tall (the R15 fallback height; if the published FourteenDayStrip is taller, match it and note it on Notes B).\n  b. Year band: 361×120pt, 12 month columns × 4 lanes of 24pt, with lane-label bars.\n  c. Scale strip: 4 rows of 48pt, each a 12pt filled track shape with a 72×14pt reading bar beside it.\n  d. Bill trend: a 160×14pt summary bar above 12 columns, 16pt wide, 8pt gaps, radius xs, bottom-aligned, heights 40, 56, 48, 64, 52, 44, 60, 72, 56, 48, 64, 52pt.\nV4 Panel skeleton (f9-nearby-cells-map): on a surface.base card, a 361×240pt surface.sunken panel, radius lg, with a 6×4 grid of 1px border.default lines (decoration), and a 120×14pt caption bar below it.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Shimmer (default): the band mid-sweep.\nS2 Static (Reduce Motion): the same shapes, no band. Loaded content replaces it with a 200 ms cross-fade.\nS3 Replaced progressively: each replacement is a 200 ms cross-fade in place; the height ruler shows no change. Loaded content:\n  - V1: the air band is AqiBand (R15): AQI 42 Good, AirNow, observed 7:00 AM. Pickup card and strip stay skeletons.\n  - V2: row 1 is MemberRow (R15, owner variant) \"Maya Chen\" with caption \"Owner\". Rows 2–3 stay skeletons.\n  - V3: a is FourteenDayStrip (R15) for HOME A from Mon 19 Oct 2026, with marks exactly as the published HOME A strip specimen: Tue 20 Oct recycling and garbage, hollow (city schedule, not confirmed) · Fri 23 Oct Clark Public Utilities bill, tick (you added) · Mon 26 Oct voter registration must arrive by, full-height state bar · Tue 27 Oct garbage only, hollow · Wed 28 Oct City of Vancouver water bill, tick · Sun 1 Nov HOA dues, tick, weekend cell. b, c, d stay skeletons, each with its own name.\n  - V4: \"Not applicable: the panel lands as one piece\".\n\nGRIDS\n02 light: 4 rows × 3 columns, iOS; the V3 cells hold sub-specimens a–d, each named.\n03 dark: the same grid per R9. Container: V1–V3 cards are dark raised on dark app, with shapes in #374151 (border.strong) and a shimmer band of dark raised at 60%. V4: the panel is dark raised on a dark base card, grid lines #374151, band of dark base at 60%. (Dark sunken equals dark base, so it would vanish.) Loaded content uses its own dark tokens.\n\n04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion (light, per R17)\n- (a) iOS AX5, V1 and V2 at S1: bar heights follow the R17 AX5 line heights of the text they stand in for, so V1 grows to its AX5 final height and the two pickup button shapes stack; V2 rows grow to their AX5 heights. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) Android 200%, V1 and V2 at S1: the same, with 48dp minimum rows. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V3 S3. Caption: \"Reads without colour: yes — no text, and the shapes are content-shaped, so it still reads as a placeholder.\"\n- Row \"Reduce Motion\": V1 and V3 static, captioned \"no shimmer; replacements cross-fade\". They repeat the S2 cells and are not published again.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken \"Loading\", once, on the container (VoiceOver container label; Android contentDescription; web aria-busy=\"true\" plus visually hidden \"Loading\"). Shapes are hidden from assistive tech.\n- Skeletons carry no data, so need no non-colour encoding. They are not interactive; controls can't be tapped until content lands. Reduce Motion: no shimmer.\n\nCOPY. The only string is the spoken \"Loading\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- All platforms skip skeletons for loads under about 1 s. Callout: \"under 1 s: show nothing new; keep the old content\".\n- Warm screens (the widget path, f7-widget-tap-landing) never show a skeleton; they refresh in place with no hairline.\n- Android uses its existing shimmer component with these shapes and ANATOMY 4; iOS and web match it.\n- Fail-closed components never get a skeleton: the founding meter (f9-founding-meter-preview), the Earn row (f9-earn-removal) and LandingBannerSlot render nothing until their data is confirmed. Print this list here.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05, per R17)\n- f1-today-tab: a cold load, V1 under the header \"Larkspur Loop\" and the scope string \"Your household\".\n- f3-members-roster: V2 with three rows.\n- f10-bill-trend: V3d inside the bill trend card.\nAlso consumed by: x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f1-your-places, f3-household-block, f3-member-home-dashboard, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map, f11-keeper-strip, f7-widget-tap-landing (as the warm path with no skeleton)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a full-page spinner, draw skeletons in their final slots — because a spinner hides the wait and the page jumps.\n- Instead of an empty card frame, draw filled shapes — because a frame-only skeleton looks empty.\n- Instead of \"Checking air…\", draw text-free shapes — because a skeleton must not claim a check is running.\n- Instead of a ring for a count, draw a number bar and chip bars — because the count is an integer plus chips.\n- Instead of a skeleton for the founding meter, the Earn row or LandingBannerSlot, draw nothing — because they fail closed.\n- Instead of an endless shimmer, stop after 4 passes — because idle loops stop within 5 s.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 2.1 Dark shapes: dark sunken equals dark base, so shapes are dark raised on dark base and #374151 on dark raised cards.\n   2.2 Shapes: the contract says \"track outlines\" and \"ring outline\". This board draws filled shapes (per the contract's \"no frame-only skeletons\") and drops the ring, because brief section 4 replaced the count ring with an integer plus chips. Confirm.\n   2.3 Threshold: the contract says 1–10 s; brief P11 says about 2–10 s. This board follows the contract. Question: skeleton or nothing between 1 and 2 s?\n   2.4 The shimmer is an idle loop (1.2 s per pass, 4 passes, 4.8 s) under the 5 s idle-loop rule, not the 300 ms transition rule. Confirm.\n   2.5 The V3a loaded marks copy the published HOME A FourteenDayStrip specimen (hollow pickups, ticked bills and HOA, state bar for the voter deadline). Confirm.\nB. The V3a window runs Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov; Comcast and property tax (both Mon 2 Nov) fall outside it. Record here if the published strip is taller than 40pt.\nC. AqiBand, PickupCard, MemberRow or FourteenDayStrip, if drawn as a fallback box; the three optional screenshots, if they didn't arrive.\nD. \"Loading\" (spoken) · \"Owner\" (MemberRow caption) · the bar sizes and bill-trend heights · chrome: every quoted callout, caption and row label in this prompt.\nE. Light only: the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames on 04. Review aids: the 01 loaded version, V4 S3, greyscale copies, crops, thumbnails; the Reduce Motion row repeats S2. Omitted: skeletons for fail-closed components (by rule).\nF. Light: every drawn grid cell (V3 as a–d; the 01 V3d specimen shares its cell's name), the 04 large-text frames. Dark: the same grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 5 artboards exist with the exact names, and Notes carries 2.1–2.5 and B–F.\n- No skeleton holds text, a glyph or a ring; every shape is filled.\n- Every skeleton has a \"same height\" ruler pair, and S3 shows no height change.\n- S3 shows only the loaded content listed.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02 light, 03 dark. Stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04, 05, 00d · Notes (extend it). Stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read R1–R19 and this whole message."
          }
