            "promptText": "Component 00d-03: InlineUndo. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Reversible removals and declines, with no timers and no dialogs.\nUsed in (print on 01): x-date-sheet, f1-your-places, f3-household-block, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f6-home-basics-rows, x-place-file, f3-bills-list, f10-snap-capture-tray\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · InlineUndo · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · InlineUndo · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · InlineUndo · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Removed row = removed-row · V2 Declined ask = declined-ask · V3 Triage decision = triage-decision · V4 Undo all = undo-all · V5 Bill + photo deleted = bill-and-photo-deleted · V6 Fan-out hold = fan-out-hold.\nStates: S1 Pending undo = pending-undo · S2 Undone = undone · S3 Committed = committed.\nSpecimens outside the grid (drawn in the 04 \"Platforms\" row):\n\"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo-with-echo / android / light\" (in-row line plus snackbar; the 01 inset repeats it and carries this name)\n\"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo-with-echo / web-390 / light\" (in-row line plus toast)\n\nHOST CONTENT (TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026. Every cell draws its target row with the neighbours named here; invent no other rows.)\n- Row: 361pt on surface.base, padding 12/16, 1px border.default divider (decoration). Line 1 bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary, amounts right-aligned in tabular figures. Line 2 bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary.\n- Maya's places (V1), in order: \"Larkspur Loop\" / \"Your household\" · \"The Blairmont rental\" / \"Saved place · Only you\" · \"Dad's place\" / \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- Household block (V2): a card (surface.base, radius lg 12, padding 16, shadow sm): title \"Who lives here with you?\" in h3 20/28/600 text.primary; then \"They see the same pickup day, calendar and bills. Nothing about your home is shared with anyone else.\" in bodySmall text.secondary; then three 44pt actions: \"Invite by email\" (primary.700 fill, text.inverse label), \"Share a link\" (outlined like \"Finish day\") and \"Just me\" (text button, primary.700). Above and below the card, a surface.sunken 361×56pt box labelled \"Today section (host)\" in caption text.strong.\n- Mail day (V3, V4): six pieces in this order. Line 2 shows the kind while unsorted and the decision once sorted:\n  1 \"Clark Public Utilities\": \"Bill\" / \"Kept\" · 2 \"City of Vancouver water\": \"Bill\" / \"Kept\" · 3 \"Comcast\": \"Offer\" / \"Recycled\" · 4 \"HOA dues\": \"Bill\" / \"Kept\" · 5 \"Clark County Elections\": \"Voter guide\" / \"Kept\" · 6 \"Waste Connections\": \"Flyer\" / \"Recycled\".\n  Under the list, a \"Finish day\" button: outlined, surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border (R10: 4.83:1), bodyMedium text.primary label, 44pt tall, radius md 8.\n- Bills list (V5, V6), by due date: \"Clark Public Utilities\" $142.18 / \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"City of Vancouver water\" $84.00 / \"Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\", with a 40pt surface.sunken thumbnail slot labelled \"photo\" at its leading edge · \"HOA dues\" $285.00 / \"Due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Comcast\" $79.99 / \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n  Paid form (V6 S3 only): line 2 keeps the due date, and a line 3 carries \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" in bodySmall text.secondary, right-aligned, never truncated (Notes 3.7).\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393 with callouts, plus one Android inset)\n1. Collapse. The removed row collapses in place into a line on surface.base; its height animates to 56pt over 200 ms (Reduce Motion: no animation, the line replaces the row). The line reads 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\"' in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, then \" · \", then an \"Undo\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a dashed 44×44pt hit area.\n2. Lifetime. The line stays until the person leaves the screen (V3 and V4: until \"Finish day\" or leaving, whichever comes first). No countdown, no progress bar, no auto-dismiss. Callout: \"stays until you leave this screen\".\n3. Echo, Android and web only (iOS has no native snackbar). It repeats the line's text and Undo and is never the only record.\n   Geometry, light only: surface.base fill, radius md 8, shadow md, 1px text.secondary edge (R10: 4.83:1), min height 48dp (48px web), 16 horizontal padding; message in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary; action \"Undo\" in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1) with a 48dp (44px web) hit area. It sits 8 above the bottom tab bar, with scroll padding reserved. Web-1440 places it bottom left with the same geometry (not drawn; Notes E).\n   Duration: indefinite while a screen reader runs; otherwise the default Material long duration, because the in-row line remains. The web toast is in a polite live region and doesn't auto-hide while focus is inside it.\n   On 01, draw it as an Android 412 inset beside the iOS anatomy, labelled \"android only\".\n4. Fan-out hold. A write that notifies the household (Mark paid) holds its notification until the undo line closes. Draw it on a V6 line with a callout, and the caption \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary under the undo line.\n5. Restore highlight, this component's one further R12 treatment: a fill only, with no border, no check and no weight change, fading to the row surface within 300 ms (Reduce Motion: static, no fade). Callout: \"restore highlight: fill only, not selection\".\n   Light: primary.50 fill; line 2 stays text.secondary (4.54:1 on primary.50) and links stay primary.700 (5.57:1).\n   Dark: primary.900 fill. Every text on it is #E5E7EB (R10: 7.64:1), including line 2 and the \"Just me\" link, which is underlined while highlighted (#38BDF8 on primary.900 is only 4.42:1). Each returns to its dark raised colour when the fill fades.\n   Buttons keep their own fills and label colours. Captions under a restored row (V6 \"No notification sent\") sit below the highlight, on the row surface.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; viewer Maya Chen at HOME A)\nV1 Removed row (f1-your-places). S1: the line 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\" · Undo' between Larkspur Loop and Dad's place. S2: The Blairmont rental returns. S3: Larkspur Loop and Dad's place touch.\nV2 Declined ask (f3-household-block). S1: \"Just you, then. · Undo\" in the card's slot between the host boxes (contract string, Notes 3.1). S2: the card returns. S3: the host boxes touch; no card.\nV3 Triage decision (f10-mail-day-triage). S1: pieces 1–2 unsorted, the line \"Comcast · Recycled · Undo\" in piece 3's place, pieces 4–6 unsorted, then \"Finish day\". S2: Comcast returns unsorted (\"Offer\"); \"Finish day\" stays. S3 (after \"Finish day\"): pieces 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 unsorted, 2 touching 4; no undo line, no \"Finish day\".\nV4 Undo all (f10-mail-day-triage). S1: the line \"6 pieces sorted · Undo all 6\" at the top, all six pieces sorted, then \"Finish day\". S2: all six return unsorted; \"Finish day\" stays. S3 (after \"Finish day\"): only kept pieces 1, 2, 4, 5 (\"Kept\"), 2 touching 4; recycled 3 and 6 are gone; no undo line.\nV5 Bill + photo deleted (f10-bill-provenance, f3-bills-list). S1: \"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\" in the water bill's place, between Clark Public Utilities and HOA dues. S2: the water row returns with its photo slot. S3: Clark Public Utilities and HOA dues touch.\nV6 Fan-out hold (f3-bills-list; Notes 3.2). S1: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\" in the first row's place, with the anatomy 4 caption under it, above the water row. S2: Clark Public Utilities returns unpaid, with \"No notification sent\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary under it. S3 (override, nothing removed): Clark Public Utilities stays at the top in its paid form; no undo line or caption. In the table margin right of the V6 row, outside the cell, draw a thumbnail at most 120pt wide (title only, \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\", captioned \"sent to Sam\"), joined to the cell by a 1px text.secondary leader. It is board chrome, not a PushCopy specimen, and not published.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Pending undo: the collapsed line with its action, among its neighbours.\nS2 Undone: the row returns at full height with the anatomy 5 highlight. \"Restored\" is announced, not written.\nS3 Committed: the person left the screen (V3, V4: tapped \"Finish day\") and came back. The row is gone, the gap closed, no trace or banner. V6 is the exception above.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 6 rows × 3 columns, iOS. Every cell applies.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9), including the V6 margin thumbnail. Container: rows and the household card are dark raised on dark app. On dark raised: Undo and \"Just me\" #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1); line 2, the paid attribution, the captions and outlined-button borders #94A3B8 (R10: 5.71:1); \"Invite by email\" is a #38BDF8 fill with the dark text.inverse label (R10: 8.28:1); outlined buttons are dark raised with #E5E7EB labels. S2 follows the anatomy 5 dark rule.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V4 at S1: the message wraps and the action moves to its own line below, left-aligned, at least 44pt tall. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 and V4 at S1: the same, with a 48dp action. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V6 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: Undo is a word with a heavier weight (500 vs 400); Restored is announced, and the row returns at full height.\"\n- Extra row, labelled \"Platforms\": V1 S1 three ways. iOS: the in-row line only (\"InlineUndo / removed-row / pending-undo / ios / light\", the grid cell repeated). Android and web-390: the two pending-undo-with-echo specimens (anatomy 3).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: when a line appears, role=status announces \"Removed The Blairmont rental. Undo, button.\" Undo is focusable; focus stays where it was. After Undo, the status reads \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\"\n- Non-colour: Undo is a word with a weight change, not only a link colour. The highlight is never the only sign of a change.\n- Targets: Undo 44×44pt / 48×48dp / 44×44px. \"Finish day\" and the household actions are 44pt tall.\n\nCOPY. Pattern: \"<what happened> · Undo\". Never \"(4s)\" or \"Undo in 5…\". Use only the strings under HOST CONTENT, ANATOMY, VARIANTS, STATES and ACCESSIBILITY, plus the 04 row label \"Platforms\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17), four labelled crops:\n- f1-your-places: Maya's places with V1 in place of the removed row.\n- f10-mail-day-triage: two side-by-side crops, V3 S1 and V4 S1, each ending with \"Finish day\".\n- f3-household-block: V2 in the block's slot on Today for HOME A.\nAlso consumed by: x-date-sheet, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f6-home-basics-rows, x-place-file, f3-bills-list, f10-snap-capture-tray\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a \"Remove this place?\" dialog for a cheap delete, draw the V1 line — because routine actions are reversible and dialogs teach click-through.\n- Instead of \"Undo (4s)\" with a countdown, draw \"Undo\" with no timer — because undo stays until the person leaves the screen.\n- Instead of a toast as the only trace, draw the in-row line, with the toast only as an echo — because toasts vanish before some people can reach them.\n- Instead of sending \"marked paid\" to the household at once, hold it until the undo line closes — because a notification can't be taken back.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 3.1 V2 \"Just you, then.\": the glossary forbids \"just you\" as a stand-in for \"Only you\" and names \"Just me\" as the household decline. Kept as the contract string. Question: switch to \"Just me, then.\"?\n   3.2 V6 is a sixth variant; the contract lists five. It comes from the contract anatomy rule \"Household-notifying writes (Mark paid) hold their fan-out until undo closes\". Confirm it as a published variant.\n   3.3 Echo platforms, duration and geometry are this board's choice (anatomy 3); the contract gives no platform notes. Confirm.\n   3.4 Restore highlight (anatomy 5): confirm it reads apart from selection. In dark, line 2 switches to #E5E7EB and \"Just me\" is underlined while on primary.900, because #94A3B8 (3.69:1) and #38BDF8 (4.42:1) fail there.\n   3.5 V6 paid form \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" is the brief's attribution form (\"Paid by Sam · 15 Oct\") plus the R14 weekday. Confirm.\n   3.6 After \"Finish day\", recycled pieces leave the list; kept and unsorted pieces stay. Confirm.\n   3.7 Bill due dates use the house relative form (\"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"). With it, the paid attribution no longer fits beside the due date in 329pt, so the paid form puts it on a right-aligned line 3. Confirm.\nB. Viewer Maya Chen at HOME A; TODAY Mon 19 Oct. The Blairmont rental and Dad's place are Maya's saved places (Only you). The mail-day pieces and decisions are as listed under HOST CONTENT.\nC. None expected.\nD. \"Dad's place\" · \"Who lives here with you?\", \"They see the same pickup day, calendar and bills. Nothing about your home is shared with anyone else.\", \"Invite by email\", \"Share a link\" (from f3-household-block) · \"Offer\", \"Voter guide\", \"Flyer\", \"Kept\", \"Recycled\", \"Clark County Elections\", \"Waste Connections\" · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", \"Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\", \"Due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\", \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"6 pieces sorted\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid\" · \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" · \"No notification sent\" · \"Restored\" and \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\" (spoken) · \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\", \"sent to Sam\" (thumbnail) · chrome: \"Today section (host)\", \"photo\", \"stays until you leave this screen\", \"android only\", \"restore highlight: fill only, not selection\", \"Platforms\".\nE. Light only: the two echo specimens and the large-text frames. Not drawn: the web-1440 toast (anatomy 3). Not published: the V6 S3 thumbnail. Omitted: an iOS echo; visible \"Restored\" text.\nF. Light: all 18 grid cells, the two pending-undo-with-echo specimens, and the 04 large-text frames. Dark: all 18 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 5 artboards with the exact names above; Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Both grids are 6 × 3 with keys, every cell drawn with its HOST CONTENT.\n- No countdown, timer, progress bar or dialog. Every Undo shows its dashed hit area.\n- Every S2 row follows anatomy 5 in its theme; no dark line 2 in #94A3B8 sits on primary.900.\n- The iOS anatomy has no echo; the 01 Android inset is labelled \"android only\".\n- 04 has (a), (b), (c) and the Platforms row; 05 has the four crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message.\n"
