            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-04: DestructiveConfirm. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The confirm for real losses. It names what goes and what stays.\nUsed in (print on 01): f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-mail-snap-privacy, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f3-members-roster\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (6, then extend Notes)\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 03-platforms · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 04-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 06-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 One photo = one-photo · V2 All photos = all-photos · V3 Keeper = keeper · V4 Leave home sheet = leave-home-sheet.\nStates: S1 Open = open · S2 Deleting = deleting · S3 Done = done.\nSpecimens outside the grid, named in full:\n\"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open-keep-focused / ios / light\" (the focus specimen on 01)\n\"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open / android / light\"\n\"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open / web-390 / light\"\n\"DestructiveConfirm / one-photo / open / web-1440 / light\" (the 01 web-1440 crop repeats this specimen and carries its name)\n\"DestructiveConfirm / leave-home-sheet / open / android / light\"\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393, plus the web-1440 crop of the same dialog, with callouts)\n1. Container.\n   - Dialogs (V1–V3): surface.base, radius xl 16 on all corners, padding 24, shadow lg. Width: 320pt on iOS; 364dp on Android (a Material 3 basic dialog, 24 from each screen edge; Notes 4.8); 400px on web-1440; 358px on web-390 (16px each side). Dialogs have no Close.\n   - Sheet (V4): surface.base, radius xl 16 on the top corners, large detent, a visible \"Close\" text button in the top bar above the title.\n   - Scrim, both kinds: text.primary #111827 at 40%, in both themes (board assumption, Notes B). In S1, tapping the scrim cancels.\n2. Title: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, a question that names the object (\"Delete this photo?\").\n3. Body: one sentence in body 16/24 text.primary, naming what survives.\n4. Buttons: two buttons of equal size and type, 44pt tall (48dp on Android), radius md 8, horizontal padding 12, labels that describe outcomes. Both labels are bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary.\n   - Destructive: surface.base fill, 1.5px semantic.error border (R10: 4.83:1), a leading 16pt trash glyph in semantic.error, glyph-to-label gap 8. Red only on the border and glyph. Callouts: \"no red fill\" and \"no red text\".\n   - Keep: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border (R10: 4.83:1), no glyph.\n   - Side by side: equal-width pair filling the content width, Keep leads, Delete trails, gap 8. Widths: 154dp on Android, 151px on web-390, 172px on web-1440. Stacked (iOS at every size, every platform at AX5 and 200%): Delete on top, Keep below, gap 8.\n   - If a label doesn't fit on one line at its side-by-side width, stack the pair instead of wrapping or truncating, and log it on Notes A.\n5. Initial focus: screen readers start on the title. Keyboard focus lands on Keep, never on the destructive button. Draw the R12 focus ring on \"Keep it\" in a second iOS specimen beside the first (\"…/open-keep-focused/…\").\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; viewer Maya Chen for V1–V3, Sam Ortega for V4)\nV1 One photo (f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-bill-provenance). Title \"Delete this photo?\" Body \"The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed.\" Buttons \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\".\nV2 All photos (f10-mail-snap-privacy). Title \"Delete all 17 photos?\" Body \"The bills and their amounts stay; only the photos are removed.\" Buttons \"Delete 17 photos\" / \"Keep them\".\nV3 Keeper (f11-keeper-naming). Title \"Remove Ollie?\" Body \"Today goes back to no keeper. You can add one again any time.\" Buttons \"Remove Ollie\" / \"Keep Ollie\".\nV4 Leave home sheet (f3-members-roster). Title \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" Two labelled lists, each heading in label 13/18/600 text.primary; each item is a 16pt glyph in text.secondary plus words in bodySmall text.primary:\n  \"What goes\" (minus-stroke glyph): \"The household calendar and bills\" · \"Household activity notifications\" · \"Your access to this home's place file\".\n  \"What stays\" (check-stroke glyph): \"Dates you added that are Only you\" · \"Your saved places\" · \"Bills you marked paid still show 'Sam (no longer here)'\".\n  Buttons \"Leave this home\" / \"Stay in this home\". The destructive button uses the icon set's door-exit glyph (an arrow leaving a doorway) in semantic.error instead of the trash. If the set has none, use the trash glyph and log it on Notes C.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Open: as above.\nS2 Deleting: the title stays. The body becomes a progress line in body 16/24 text.primary with a 4pt determinate bar under it (primary.700 on surface.sunken, R10: 5.39:1; Reduce Motion: the bar steps with no easing). V1 \"Deleting the photo…\", bar 50% · V2 \"Deleting 5 of 17…\", bar 5/17 · V3 \"Removing Ollie…\", bar 50% · V4 \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\", bar 50%. Only these lines end in an ellipsis. Both buttons are hidden until the action finishes. Escape, Back, the scrim and swipe-to-dismiss do nothing.\n  V4 only: the top-bar \"Close\" stays visible but disabled per R16 (text.muted label, focusable, read as \"Close, unavailable, Close is available when this finishes.\"), and \"Close is available when this finishes.\" is written under the bar in caption 12/16 text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1).\nS3 Done: the dialog or sheet has closed. Draw the host status line that replaces it, in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary with a 16pt check glyph in text.secondary: V1 \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · V2 \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · V3 \"Ollie removed.\" · V4 Sam's Place tab: \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" at the top, above a surface.sunken 361×200pt box labelled \"Place tab (host)\" in caption text.strong. No Undo, because the loss is real.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 4 rows × 3 columns, iOS. Every cell applies.\n04-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid in dark tokens (R9). Every dialog and sheet is dark base over the scrim, never dark raised; S3 lines sit on a dark raised host card. Destructive border and glyph stay #DC2626 (R10: 3.70:1 on dark base; non-text only). Labels are dark text primary. Keep border #94A3B8 (R10: 6.96:1). S2 bar #38BDF8 on a dark raised track (dark sunken would vanish on dark base). Disabled Close #64748B (R10: 3.75:1); its written reason #94A3B8 (R10: 6.96:1).\n\nPLATFORMS (03-platforms · light only). V1 S1 four ways, per anatomy 1 and 4:\n- iOS 393: the grid cell repeated (a custom in-app dialog, not the system alert, so the outlined treatment shows).\n- Android 412: a Material 3 basic dialog, buttons side by side. Back cancels in S1.\n- web-390: a dialog, not a sheet: anchored 16px above the tab bar, no Close; Escape and the scrim cancel in S1.\n- web-1440 crop: a centred modal, buttons side by side. Escape cancels in S1. Focus is trapped inside and returns to the opening control on close.\nAlso V4 S1 on Android: a bottom sheet with a drag handle and a visible \"Close\" (48dp). V4 on iOS is the grid cell.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (05-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V4 at S1: both become scrollable sheets with the top-bar \"Close\" (it cancels like Keep), so V1 gains a Close. Buttons stack full width, pinned at the bottom, with scroll padding reserved so the last body line is never hidden. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 at S1: the dialog content scrolls and the buttons stack. Name uses android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V4 S1. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the destructive button has its outcome label, its glyph and its heavier 1.5px border; the V4 lists differ by glyph shape and heading word.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Delete this photo?, dialog. The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed. Delete photo, button. Keep it, button.\" While deleting, a polite live region reads progress at most every 5 items: \"Deleting 5 of 17\", \"Deleting 10 of 17\", \"Deleting 15 of 17\", then \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\"\n- Each title is unique. Cancel and S2 behaviour follow S1 and S2 above.\n- Non-colour: the destructive action is named by its label and marked by its glyph and heavier border, never by red alone. The glyph is decorative for screen readers.\n- Targets: buttons 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8 gaps. Close 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY. Titles are questions naming the object, bodies name what survives, buttons name outcomes. Never just \"Are you sure?\" or \"This can't be undone\". Use only the strings under VARIANTS, STATES and ACCESSIBILITY, plus \"Close\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (06-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f10-mail-piece-photo: the photo viewer with V1 open over it.\n- f10-mail-snap-privacy: the \"Mail snaps\" card with V2 open.\n- f3-members-roster: Sam's member view with the V4 sheet.\nAlso consumed by: f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Are you sure?\" / \"OK\" / \"Cancel\", draw \"Delete this photo?\" / \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\" — because people decide faster when the buttons say what happens.\n- Instead of \"This can't be undone\", draw the sentence naming what stays — because people fear losing more than they will.\n- Instead of a filled red button, a red slab above the content, or red label text, draw the outlined button with a semantic.error border, the glyph and a text.primary label — because a red fill shouts, semantic hues go on glyphs and borders only, and red text drops below readable contrast in dark mode.\n- Instead of default focus on the destructive button, put keyboard focus on Keep — because Enter must never destroy something.\n- Instead of this dialog for a cheap removal, use InlineUndo — because dialogs are only for losses that can't be undone.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 4.1 Label: the contract asks for a red label (\"text.error\", not a token); the house style puts semantic hues on glyphs and borders only. This board follows the house style: both labels share bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary (no R4 exception), and the destructive button carries the border and glyph. The alternative (a semantic.error label, 4.83:1 on base) would need a dark error text token, since #DC2626 is 3.70:1 on dark base. Question for the founder.\n   4.2 Dark: no dark error token and no accent token. #DC2626 stays on border and glyph only. Dialogs and sheets stay on dark base, where it measures 3.70:1 (3.03:1 on dark raised).\n   4.3 S2 ignores Escape, Back, the scrim and swipe-to-dismiss, and the V4 Close stays visible, disabled and focusable with its written reason. The contract only says \"Escape / Back cancels\". Confirm.\n   4.4 S2 progress is announced every 5 items, so V2 is drawn at \"Deleting 5 of 17…\". V1, V3 and V4 are single actions, drawn at a 50% mid-action pose.\n   4.5 V4 uses the door-exit glyph because nothing is deleted. Confirm.\n   4.6 At AX5, V1 becomes a sheet and gains \"Close\", because every sheet needs one. Confirm.\n   4.7 The S2 count and bar are operation progress for a real loss, not a completion score (house invariant 6); kept because the contract asks for \"deleting (progress count)\". Confirm.\n   4.8 The Android dialog is 364dp wide instead of 312dp so the side-by-side buttons (154dp) fit \"Delete photo\" with its glyph and padding. Confirm.\nB. Sam Ortega is the member who leaves in V4. Ollie is HOME A's keeper. HOME A has 17 mail photos. The scrim (text.primary at 40%, both themes) is a board assumption.\nC. The door-exit glyph, if the icon set lacks it.\nD. \"The bills and their amounts stay; only the photos are removed.\" · \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" · \"What goes\" · \"What stays\" and all six items · \"Leave this home\" · \"Stay in this home\" · \"Remove Ollie\" · \"Keep Ollie\" · \"Deleting the photo…\" · \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" · \"Removing Ollie…\" · \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\" · \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · \"Ollie removed.\" · \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Close\" · \"Close is available when this finishes.\" (written and spoken) · \"Deleting 10 of 17\", \"Deleting 15 of 17\" (spoken) · chrome: \"Place tab (host)\", \"no red fill\", \"no red text\".\nE. Light only: 03-platforms, the open-keep-focused specimen, and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames (including the V1 AX5 sheet). A later dark surface takes their colours from the 04 grid note. Omitted: the red-label alternative (4.1).\nF. Light: all 12 grid cells, the open-keep-focused specimen, the four 03 specimens that aren't grid repeats, and the 05 large-text frames. Dark: all 12 grid cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 6 artboards with the exact names above; Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Both grids are 4 × 3 with keys, every cell drawn.\n- Red only on the destructive border and glyph; both labels share one type style.\n- Keyboard focus on Keep. Side-by-side pairs are equal width and fit on one line.\n- S2 hides both buttons and draws each bar at its stated fill; V4 Close is disabled with its reason written.\n- Every sheet, including the V1 AX5 sheet, has a visible Close. Every button and Close shows its dashed hit area.\n- 03 shows V1 on four platforms and V4 on Android, each with its full name.\n- 05 has (a), (b), (c); 06 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-platforms. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-variants-by-states dark, 05-ax5-200-greyscale, 06-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message.\n"
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-05",
            "component": "LandingBannerSlot",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-05: LandingBannerSlot. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The single arrival slot at the top of Place and /start. It shows exactly one banner at a time.\nUsed in (print on 01): f3-invite-banner, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-founding-meter-preview, x-place-file, f1-claim-receipt\nATTACH: a screenshot of the shipped mailbox-arrival pill at the top of the Place tab (iOS, Android and web-390). LandingBannerSlot copies its geometry exactly. If it is missing, use the fallback in anatomy 1 and write \"mailbox-arrival pill screenshot missing; fallback geometry used\" on Notes C.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then extend Notes)\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 One invite = one-invite · V2 Count = count · V3 Expiring = expiring · V4 Sender reissue = sender-reissue · V5 Expired compare link = expired-compare-link · V6 Sync merge = sync-merge · V7 Claim receipt = claim-receipt.\nSecondary specimens inside rows: V1 degraded = one-invite-degraded · V3 seven days out = expiring-early.\nStates: S1 Hidden = hidden · S2 Shown = shown · S3 Offline = offline.\nExamples: \"LandingBannerSlot / expiring / shown / ios / light\" · \"LandingBannerSlot / expiring-early / offline / ios / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy-and-precedence: V1 S2 on iOS 393 with callouts, then the ladder and fetch frames)\n1. Geometry: copy the attached pill exactly (height, radius, padding, fill, edge). Fallback: min height 44pt, radius pill, padding 16 horizontal and 12 vertical, surface.base on surface.app, shadow sm, 1px border.default as decoration.\n2. Leading 16pt glyph, top-aligned with line 1, 8pt before the sentence; not a target. Colour text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1) unless noted:\n   envelope: V1, V1 degraded, V2, V4, the seven-days-out specimen · warning, in semantic.warning (R10: 3.19:1, glyph only): V3 only, replacing the envelope · link: V5 · sync: V6 · home: V7.\n   No specimen carries a second glyph; V3's line 2 has none of its own.\n3. Sentence: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary. Where there is an actor, the actor's name comes first.\n4. One trailing action: a text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (R10: 5.93:1), dashed 44×44pt hit area, 12pt after the sentence, top-aligned with its first line. The \" · \" before the action in the strings below is notation only and is not drawn.\n5. Placement: full content width (361pt iOS, 380dp Android, 358px web-390, 640px max in the web-1440 Place column). Shown: 16pt below the navigation title and 16pt above the first section. Hidden (S1, or a pending or failed fetch): the slot is 0pt, and the gaps collapse into one 16pt gap.\n6. Shape. One-line pills on iOS 393: V1, V2, V4, V7. Two-line, radius 2xl 20 so corners never clip text: V1 degraded, V3 and its seven-days-out specimen, V5, V6, and any specimen that wraps at large text. Callout: \"two lines → radius 2xl\". If a listed one-line specimen doesn't fit in 361pt (V1 is borderline), let it wrap, use radius 2xl, and log it on Notes A.\n7. Precedence ladder: a vertical list of nine labelled steps joined by \"wins over\" connectors: invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival (includes V5) > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify > founding-meter preview. Beside it, a scenario: an invite and a compare arrival are both pending, and only the invite banner shows. Caption: \"Never two banners.\" (Notes 5.3.)\n8. Fetch frames: three stacked iOS 393 frames of the Place top, each with the navigation title \"Place\" and a surface.sunken 361×120pt box labelled \"First section (host)\" in caption text.strong:\n   (i) \"before the fetch resolves (slot 0pt)\" and (ii) \"after the fetch failed (slot 0pt)\", with identical section positions and one 16pt gap, captioned \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\";\n   (iii) \"banner arrives: content below moves down once, 300 ms or less (Reduce Motion: no animation)\", with V1 in the slot.\n   No error banner in any frame.\nItems 7 and 8 are documentation, not published specimens.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026)\nV1 One invite (viewer: Priya): \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\". In the same S2 and S3 cells, a small secondary specimen, the degraded form: \"Someone invited you to a home in Vancouver · Review\" (when the name or address can't be shown).\nV2 Count (viewer: Priya, with two further invitations assumed; Notes B): \"You have 3 invitations · Review\". Callout: \"→ Invitations list\".\nV3 Expiring (viewer: Priya, viewed on Sun 25 Oct, the day before the Mon 26 Oct expiry): line 1 \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\"; line 2 \"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\" in caption 12/16 text.primary. In the same S2 and S3 cells, the seven-days-out secondary specimen viewed on TODAY: line 2 \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", envelope glyph.\nV4 Sender reissue (viewer: Maya): \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\".\nV5 Expired compare link: \"That comparison link has expired. Type an address to see your own place.\" with the action \"Close\".\nV6 Sync merge: \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\".\nV7 One-time claim receipt (viewer: Maya): \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\". Callout: \"→ the persistent receipt in the place file, 'What moved when you claimed'\".\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Hidden: the 0pt slot, drawn as a dashed annotation outline captioned \"hidden = 0pt\" (chrome). Every row; secondary specimens have no hidden cell.\nS2 Shown: as above.\nS3 Offline: the action is disabled per R16: text.muted label, focusable, reason read aloud. The readable reason is a caption line under the banner in caption 12/16 text.secondary:\n  V1, V1 degraded, V2, V3, the seven-days-out specimen, V6: \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\"\n  V4: \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\"\n  Spoken \"<action>, unavailable, <caption>\", e.g. \"Review, unavailable, You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\"\n  V5 and V7 keep their action live (Close and the local receipt work offline): the S2 banner with the chrome caption \"action works offline\".\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 7 rows × 3 columns on iOS, secondary specimens in the V1 and V3 rows. Every cell applies.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid, secondary specimens included, in dark tokens (R9). The banner is dark raised on dark app, with no shadow and no edge. Actions #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1), glyphs #94A3B8 (R10: 5.71:1), warning glyph #D97706 (R10: 4.59:1, glyph only), disabled actions #64748B (R10: 3.07:1). The offline caption sits on dark app in #94A3B8.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 and V3 at S2 and V4 at S3, in the anatomy 6 two-line shape: the sentence wraps as needed and the action moves below it, left-aligned, at least 44pt tall. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, the same three, with a 48dp action. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S2 and V3 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: V3 still reads as expiring from the words 'Expires tomorrow' and the warning glyph shape.\"\n- Extra row, labelled \"Platforms\": \"LandingBannerSlot / one-invite / shown / android / light\", \"LandingBannerSlot / one-invite / shown / web-1440 / light\", and V5 on /start at 358px, \"LandingBannerSlot / expired-compare-link / shown / web-390 / light\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: role=status once, when the banner appears: \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop. Review, button.\" Expiry is spoken in words: \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\" / \"Expires in 7 days, Monday 26 October.\"\n- Non-colour: expiry is carried by words plus the warning glyph, never by a tinted pill.\n- Targets: the action is 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- The slot never takes focus when it appears.\n\nCOPY. Actor name first. Degrade to \"Someone invited you…\" or \"…a home in <city>\" (HOME A: Vancouver). Expiry in words, with the weekday. Use only the strings under VARIANTS, STATES and ACCESSIBILITY, plus the 04 row label \"Platforms\".\n\nPLATFORMS. The same geometry on iOS, Android and web. Place shows every variant. /start (web, anonymous) shows only the compare-arrival step: a live compare arrival or V5. Both come from the same link, so only one is ever pending.\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f3-invite-banner: the Place tab for Priya with V1 at the top (iOS, 393pt crop).\n- f8-compare-arrival-header: /start on web-390 (390px crop) with V5 above the address field.\n- f1-claim-receipt: the Place tab for Maya with V7 at the top.\nAlso consumed by: x-place-file, f9-founding-meter-preview (shares the slot at the ladder's last step and fails closed the same way)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of stacking an invite banner over a compare banner, draw only the ladder's winner — because two banners split attention and push content down.\n- Instead of a red \"Couldn't load invitations\" banner on a fetch failure, render nothing — because a failed optional fetch must not look like an alert.\n- Instead of an amber-tinted pill for expiry, draw \"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\" in text.primary with the warning hue only on the glyph — because tinted text fails contrast and colour alone doesn't carry meaning.\n- Instead of \"You've been invited!\", draw \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" — because the actor comes first.\n- Instead of a dead action while offline, keep it focusable with its reason read out and written — because silent dead buttons leave people guessing.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 5.1 V1: the contract example \"Sam Ortega invited you to the Payne St house\" uses a non-fixture street and \"house\", which the glossary forbids. This board uses the V1 strings, degrading to Vancouver (the contract's example city is Camas).\n   5.2 V6 uses \"synced\", a glossary-forbidden freshness word. Kept as the contract string; its \"Review\" action is this board's addition. Question for the founder.\n   5.3 Precedence: the contract ladder (invite > reissue > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > setup > verify) omits sync merge, the claim receipt and the founding-meter preview, and doesn't place V5. This board proposes the anatomy 7 order. Confirm.\n   5.4 Glyphs are this board's choice (anatomy 2); the contract names none. Confirm.\n   5.5 V5 and V7 keep their actions live offline (S3). Confirm.\n   5.6 The contract says \"one line\"; two-line content uses the anatomy 6 shape. The contract's V5 has no action; this board adds \"Close\". Confirm both.\n   5.7 A pending fetch reserves no height, so an arriving banner moves content down once (anatomy 8 iii). Only a pending, failed or empty fetch is guaranteed not to shift layout. Confirm.\n   5.8 The contract's expiry caption is \"Expires tomorrow\"; this board adds the weekday (\"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\") per R14. Confirm.\nB. Priya is the invitee for V1–V3 (priya@example.com, invite expires Mon 26 Oct). V2 assumes Priya holds two further invitations. V3 \"Expires tomorrow\" is viewed on Sun 25 Oct; everything else on TODAY.\nC. The mailbox-arrival pill screenshot, if it didn't arrive.\nD. \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" · \"Someone invited you to a home in Vancouver\" · \"Expires tomorrow · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\" and \"Expires in 7 days, Monday 26 October.\" (spoken) · \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" · \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" · \"· Review\" on V6 · \"Close\" on V5 · \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\" · \"What moved when you claimed\" · chrome: \"Never two banners.\", \"wins over\", \"hidden = 0pt\", \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\", the three fetch-frame captions, \"Place\", \"First section (host)\", \"two lines → radius 2xl\", \"→ Invitations list\", \"action works offline\", \"Platforms\".\nE. Light only: the Platforms row and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Not published: the ladder, scenario and fetch frames. Omitted: the compare-arrival, mailbox-arrival, setup, verify and founding-meter-preview banners (in the ladder only; their strings belong to their own surface prompts).\nF. Light: 7 × 3 grid cells, one-invite-degraded and expiring-early at shown and offline, the three Platforms specimens and the large-text frames. Dark: the same grid cells and secondary specimens.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- 5 artboards with the exact names above; Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Both grids are 7 × 3 with keys, secondary specimens in S2 and S3.\n- 01 shows anatomy items 1–8, with fetch frames (i) and (ii) at identical section positions.\n- Every banner has one glyph, one action with its dashed hit area, and the anatomy 6 shape; no \" · \" is drawn.\n- No pill is tinted.\n- Every S3 cell follows S3.\n- 04 has (a), (b), (c) and the Platforms row; 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy-and-precedence, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message.\n"
          }
