            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-06: NotificationAsk. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The in-context notification permission ask and its denial states. It is never a second \"Yes\".\nUsed in (print on 01): f4-notification-primer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f4-today-pickup-card, f4-notification-settings, f3-household-notifications\nATTACH: none. The OS permission dialog is never drawn.\nTAG: a string followed by (new) is not in the house style or the contract. Draw it without the tag and log it on Notes D.\n\nARTBOARDS (7, then extend Notes)\n00d · NotificationAsk · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 02-card-row-states · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 04-card-row-states · dark\n00d · NotificationAsk · 05-primer-and-denial-by-platform · dark\n00d · NotificationAsk · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · NotificationAsk · 07-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\nWidth: 02 and 04 are 2400px wide (the one exception to R2) so five 393pt columns fit at 1x.\n\nKEYS (R7)\nGrid variants (02 and 04): V1 Card row = card-row · V7 Time chips = time-chips.\nGrid states: S1 Never asked = never-asked · S2 Granted = granted · S3 Declined = declined · S4 OS blocked = os-blocked · S5 Save status = save-status. The S5 cell holds three specimens, stacked, with the state keys saving, saved and save-failed.\nSpecimen outside the grid (in its own row below the grid on 02 and 04, labelled \"Settings row · OS blocked\" (new)): \"NotificationAsk / settings-row / os-blocked / ios / <theme>\".\nSheets (03 and 05): V2 = primer-ios, V3 = primer-android, their household twins, V4 = ios-denied, V5 = android-denied-once, V6 = android-blocked. The seven sheet names are exactly:\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-ios / never-asked / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-android / never-asked / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-ios-household / never-asked / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / primer-android-household / never-asked / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / ios-denied / denied / ios / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / android-denied-once / denied-once / android / <theme>\"\n  \"NotificationAsk / android-blocked / blocked / android / <theme>\"\n<theme> is light on 02 and 03, dark on 04 and 05.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: the card row and the pickup primer on iOS 393, with callouts)\nA. Card row form (on f4-briefing-optin-card). The briefing card is surface.base (radius lg 12, shadow sm) on surface.app, so the R10 \"on surface.base\" figures apply.\n  1. Question in body 16/24 text.primary: \"The night before pickup?\"\n  2. \"Yes\" and \"Not now\", side by side, equal weight. Both outlined: 1px text.secondary border (R10: 4.83:1), surface.base fill, bodyMedium text.primary label, radius md 8, 44pt tall, equal widths, 8pt gap. Callout: \"Yes fires the OS prompt directly. The OS prompt is not drawn.\" (new)\n  3. Granted collapse: the row becomes \"6:00 PM · Change\"; \"Change\" is a primary.700 text button (R10: 5.93:1) with a 44pt hit area.\n  4. Time chips, shown after Change: \"5:00 PM\", \"6:00 PM\", \"7:00 PM\", \"8:00 PM\". Each chip: 44pt tall, radius pill, 12pt horizontal padding, 8pt gaps, bodySmall 14/20 text.primary label (600 when selected). Unselected: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border. Selected: the R12 selection (fill + 16pt check + 600 weight), 4pt between check and label. Wrap to a second line if the width runs out.\n  5. Status slot at the row's trailing edge, caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"Saving…\" / \"Saved\" / \"Couldn't save · Retry\" (new: \"Retry\"), where Retry is a primary.700 text button with a 44pt hit area. \"Saving…\" is the only string on this component that ends in an ellipsis.\n  Callout on the card row: \"Appears only after an action that shows the purpose\" (new).\nB. Primer sheet form, only for the contract's two indirect entries: the first confirmed pickup and household activity from Mail. Draw the pickup entry; the household entry differs only in items 2–4.\n  1. iOS sheet: surface.base, radius xl 16 on the top corners, 24pt side padding (345pt content). Height: a custom detent sized to content, not the medium detent (pickup about 514pt, household 538pt). Stack, top to bottom: 8 · Close row 44 (\"Close\" (new) text button at top right, 44pt hit area) · 8 · title 28 · 16 · tray panel about 144 · 16 · body 72 (3 lines; household: allow 4 lines = 96 even if the text wraps to 3, and keep the sheet at 538pt) · 12 · silence contract 40 (2 lines) · 24 · Continue 44 · 8 · caption 16 · home-indicator inset 34. Continue and its caption are pinned to the bottom at every size; at default size nothing scrolls. Print the stack as a spacing callout.\n  2. Unique title, h3 20/28/600 text.primary. Pickup: \"Pickup reminders on this phone\" (new). Household: \"Household updates on this phone\" (new).\n  3. The PushCopy tray preview (drawn exactly as here; PushCopy comes later), then 8pt, then \"This is the whole thing.\" It is an in-app illustration, never a system alert: a surface.raised inset card (radius lg 12, padding 12) on a surface.sunken panel (radius lg, padding 16), holding the Pantopus app icon at 20pt (R15), \"Pantopus\" and \"now\" (new) in caption text.strong, the title in bodySmallMedium text.primary and the body in bodySmall text.primary. The caption is caption text.strong on the panel (R10: 9.37:1). Pickup: \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\". Household: \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" / \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\".\n  4. Body, body 16/24 text.primary. Pickup: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Nothing else unless you turn it on.\" Household: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" (new: the last sentence)\n  5. Silence contract, bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\"\n  6. iOS only: one forward button, \"Continue\": primary.700 fill, text.inverse label (R10: 5.93:1), full width, 44pt, radius md.\n  7. Under it, caption text.secondary: \"Your phone will ask next.\"\n  8. Android only (on 03): a Material 3 bottom sheet sized to content. Geometry: a 24dp drag-handle row (a 32×4dp handle, centred) above the Close row; 24dp side padding (364dp content); Close hit area 48dp; the bottom inset is the 24dp gesture-navigation inset in place of 34. Otherwise the same order and gaps. In place of item 6: \"Continue\" and \"Not now\", both outlined (surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border, bodyMedium text.primary label, 48dp tall, equal widths, 8dp gap, radius md). Neither is filled; the filled button is iOS-only. Item 7 follows the button row.\n\nGRID (02-card-row-states · light, iOS): rows V1 and V7 × columns S1–S5, then the settings row specimen in its own row below.\n- V1 Card row. S1: the row as drawn in A1–A2. S2: \"6:00 PM · Change\". S3 Declined: the card slot collapses (200 ms; static under Reduce Motion) and is replaced, once, by \"Put Today on your home screen\" (new) with an \"Add the widget\" (new) text button (primary.700, 44pt). That row never returns after this visit. S4: \"Not applicable: shown on the settings row specimen\". S5: \"Not applicable: the card row saves only through the chips\".\n- V7 Time chips. S1: \"Not applicable: chips appear only after granted\". S2: the four chips, 6:00 PM selected. S3: \"Not applicable: chips are hidden after a decline\". S4: \"Not applicable: shown on the settings row specimen\". S5: three stacked chip-row specimens with the slot reading \"Saving…\", \"Saved\" and \"Couldn't save · Retry\"; in \"Couldn't save\", the chip Maya picked (7:00 PM) stays selected.\n- Settings row specimen (os-blocked), below the grid: the f4-notification-settings Briefings group row, a surface.base group on surface.app. The Briefings switch shows on; beneath it, a 16pt warning glyph (semantic.warning, glyph only, R10: 3.19:1), then \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" (new) in bodySmall text.primary, then an \"Open Settings\" text button (primary.700, 44pt).\n\nSHEETS (03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light): seven full sheets at platform width, each with its exact name and, under it, a caption (new) naming its entry.\n- primer-ios: B, pickup. Caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\".\n- primer-android: B with item 8, pickup. Caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\".\n- primer-ios-household: B, household. Caption \"after household activity from Mail\".\n- primer-android-household: B with item 8, household. Caption \"after household activity from Mail\".\n- ios-denied (V4): the pickup iOS primer, same title and tray. Items 4 and 5 become \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" (new) in body text.primary; item 6 becomes \"Open Settings\" in Continue's filled style; item 7 becomes \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" (new). No Continue. Close stays. The sheet shrinks to its content. Caption \"after the iOS prompt was declined\".\n- android-denied-once (V5): the pickup Android primer unchanged: outlined \"Continue\" (asks again) and \"Not now\", then \"Your phone will ask next.\" Caption \"after the Android prompt was declined once\".\n- android-blocked (V6): the pickup Android sheet, same title and tray. Items 4 and 5 become \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\"; item 8 becomes \"Open Settings\" and \"Not now\" as equal outlined 48dp buttons; item 7 becomes \"Opens the notification settings for Pantopus.\" (new). No \"Your phone will ask next.\" and no Continue. Close stays. Caption \"after the Android prompt was declined twice\".\n\nDARK (04 and 05, R9)\n04-card-row-states · dark (2400px): the full 02 grid, Not applicable cells included, and the settings row specimen below it. The briefing card and settings group are dark raised on dark app. Outlined buttons and chips: #94A3B8 border (R10: 5.71:1). Selected chip: R12 dark selection. Change, Add the widget, Retry and Open Settings: #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1). Warning glyph: #D97706 (R10: 4.59:1).\n05-primer-and-denial-by-platform · dark: all seven 03 sheets on dark base; the tray inset is dark raised on a dark base panel. iOS Continue and Open Settings: #38BDF8 fill, dark text.inverse label (R10: 8.28:1). Android buttons are all outlined: dark base fill, 1px #94A3B8 border (R10: 6.96:1), dark text primary label.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (06-ax5-200-greyscale · light, R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: V1 S1 (\"Yes\" then \"Not now\", stacked full width, each at least 44pt), V7 S2 (one chip per line), and primer-ios (content scrolls behind the pinned Continue and caption, with scroll padding). Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android: V1 S1, V7 S2 and primer-android, with 48dp buttons and chips and 8dp gaps. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 (the light default), V7 S2 and the settings row os-blocked specimen (the most state-heavy cell). Caption: \"Reads without colour: Yes and Not now are the same outline; the selected chip has its check glyph and weight; the blocked row reads as a problem from its words and glyph shape.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken, card row: \"The night before pickup? Yes, button. Not now, button.\" Chips: \"6:00 PM, selected, 2 of 4.\" (new). Status is announced in a polite live region (\"Saved\") without moving focus. Each primer title is unique and read first. Sheets trap focus; Close dismisses them (also swipe-down on iOS, Back on Android).\n- Non-colour encoding: a selected chip has fill + check + weight; the blocked state has a glyph + words.\n- Targets per R11: buttons and chips 44pt iOS, 48dp Android.\n\nCOPY: every string is given above; use it exactly.\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: one filled button per sheet (Continue; Open Settings when denied, opening the app's Notifications page). Android: every button outlined; after one denial, Continue asks again.\n- Web: not drawn (Notes 6.7). All platforms: never at cold launch, sign-up or save.\n\nIN CONTEXT (07-in-context-and-rules · light, R17)\n- f4-briefing-optin-card: the briefing card on Today for HOME A, with V1 at S1.\n- f4-notification-primer: primer-ios over f4-today-pickup-card (PickupCard, R15), just after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\". This crop is 393 × 600pt so the whole sheet shows (an R17 exception).\n- f4-notification-settings: the Briefings group with the settings row os-blocked specimen.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card, f3-household-notifications (the household primer, drawn on 03)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a primer button labelled \"Yes\" or \"Allow\", draw \"Continue\" with \"Your phone will ask next.\" — because the decision already happened on the card.\n- Instead of imitating the iOS or Android system dialog, draw the in-app sheet with the tray illustration — because a fake system dialog deceives.\n- Instead of a permanent amber banner after Not now, close the slot and offer the widget row once — because \"Not now\" never asks again.\n- Instead of a filled \"Yes\" beside a grey \"Not now\", or a filled Continue beside an outlined Not now on Android, draw both outlined — because declines are equal weight.\n- Instead of the ask at launch or sign-up, draw it only after the first confirmed pickup, household activity from Mail, or a card tap — because people grant what they understand.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 6.1 The contract writes \"Open Settings\" (variants) and \"Open settings\" (S4). This board uses \"Open Settings\" everywhere, which breaks house-style sentence case. Question for the founder.\n   6.2 V1: the glossary pairs \"Not now\" with a lasting decline, but the contract's card row has only \"Yes / Not now\"; \"Yes\" also breaks the house-style rule that buttons start with a verb. This board draws the contract. Questions: add \"No thanks\"? Replace \"Yes\" with a verb (for example \"Remind me\")?\n   6.3 Entry points follow the contract (primer after the first confirmed pickup or household activity from Mail). Research brief section 2 item 8 instead asks inline after the first \"That's my day\" (\"Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM\") and goes straight to the OS dialog. Question: primer sheet, or inline row?\n   6.4 The household primer title and body are invented; \"arrive quietly\" means iOS Passive / Android LOW. Confirm, and say whether this entry switches household activity on after the grant.\n   6.5 \"Put Today on your home screen\" uses the tab name; the glossary calls the widget \"Today at your address\". Question: \"Add Today at your address to your home screen\"?\n   6.6 V4 and V6 keep the pickup title and tray and replace the body, silence contract, buttons and caption. V6 has its own caption because \"Your phone will ask next.\" is false once Android has blocked the app. The contract is silent. Confirm.\n   6.7 Web: no web push in scope, so no web NotificationAsk is drawn. Question for the founder.\n   6.8 OS blocked is a settings row specimen outside the grid, because it lives on f4-notification-settings. 02 and 04 are 2400px wide so the grid stays at 1x.\nB. The primers are for HOME A (Maya), so the tray shows \"Larkspur Loop\". \"Couldn't save\" is drawn after Maya picked 7:00 PM. The detent heights (about 514pt and 538pt) come from the B1 stack; the household body is allowed 4 lines even if it wraps to 3.\nC. The Pantopus app icon or PickupCard, if drawn as a fallback box.\nD. Every string tagged (new) above, including the spoken chip label, and the chrome: the two anatomy callouts, the seven entry captions and the \"Settings row · OS blocked\" row label.\nE. Light only: the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Review aids, never published: the greyscale copies. Omitted: NotificationAsk on web (6.7) and the OS permission dialog (never drawn).\nF. Light: the 4 applicable grid cells (V1 S1–S3, V7 S2), the three S5 status specimens, the settings-row os-blocked specimen, the seven sheets, and the 06 ios-ax5 and android-200 frames (not the greyscale copies). Dark: the same grid cells and specimens, and the seven sheets.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 7 artboards exist with the exact names above (02 and 04 at 2400px), and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Both grids have the five Not applicable cells with reasons, and the settings row specimen in its labelled row below the grid.\n- 03 and 05 each show seven named sheets with entry captions. V4 has no Continue; V6 has no \"Your phone will ask next.\"\n- No Android button is filled.\n- No \"(new)\" tag is printed anywhere.\n- Every button, chip and text button shows its dashed hit area.\n- 06 has columns (a), (b) and (c); 07 has three labelled crops (the primer crop 393 × 600pt), the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-card-row-states light, 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform light, 04-card-row-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 05-primer-and-denial-by-platform dark, 06-ax5-200-greyscale, 07-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message, including DONE WHEN."
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-07",
            "component": "PushCopy",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · PushCopy · 05-android-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · PushCopy · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · PushCopy · 07-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-07: PushCopy. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): The canonical push strings and tray-preview artwork, so every surface draws the same notification.\nUsed in (print on 01): f4-notification-primer, f4-today-pickup-card, f1-today-air-band, f3-household-notifications, f4-notification-settings\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (7, then extend Notes)\n00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light\n00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light\n00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light\n00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · PushCopy · 05-android-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · PushCopy · 06-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · PushCopy · 07-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Unconfirmed pickup = unconfirmed-pickup · V2 Confirmed pickup = confirmed-pickup · V3 Air, Time Sensitive = air-time-sensitive · V4 Air, below 151 = air-below-threshold · V5 Bill marked paid = bill-marked-paid · V6 Household roll-up = household-roll-up · V7 Date reminder = date-reminder · V8 Hidden-preview placeholders = hidden-preview.\nStates: S1 Collapsed = collapsed · S2 Expanded = expanded · S3 Lock screen public = lock-screen-public.\nV8 cells hold four specimens each, one per placeholder group, with these state keys: collapsed-pickup, collapsed-air, collapsed-household, collapsed-date (S1) and lock-screen-public-pickup, lock-screen-public-air, lock-screen-public-household, lock-screen-public-date (S3).\nLevels table rows (platform-neutral, light only): \"PushCopy / levels / pickup-briefings-dates-bills / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / household / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / air-151-and-above-and-noaa / any / light\" · \"PushCopy / levels / air-below-151 / any / light\".\nExample: \"PushCopy / air-time-sensitive / expanded / android / dark\".\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy-and-levels: V1 S2 on iOS 393 with callouts, then the levels table)\n1. The tray preview is an in-app illustration: a surface.raised inset card (radius lg 12, padding 12) on a surface.sunken panel (radius lg, padding 16). It is never drawn as a system alert, over a wallpaper, or with system chrome. In the grids, the panel spans the full device width (393pt on iOS, 412dp on Android), so the inset is the real notification width: 361pt on iOS (337pt of text) and 380dp on Android. Inside a host sheet (IN CONTEXT, and the NotificationAsk primers) the panel fits the sheet's content width and the inset shrinks with it.\n2. Inside the inset, the top row: the Pantopus app icon from the design system at 20pt (R15; if it isn't published, use the R15 fallback box and log it on Notes C), then \"Pantopus\" in caption 12/16 text.strong, then \"now\" in caption text.strong, right-aligned. (Secondary words on the raised inset inside a sunken frame use text.strong.) R10 has no light-raised row, so print no contrast figure for these words. On Android, the row uses the Android small-icon form of the same app icon, in the same illustrated style.\n3. Title: bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 text.primary, 30 characters or fewer, caveat first. Under the string, draw a ruler marked in characters: one small tick per 5 characters, a labelled tick at 30, and the part after the last character shaded as the remaining room.\n4. Body: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, 40 characters or fewer on its first line. Draw the same character ruler, with the labelled tick at 40.\n5. Place label: the street name only (\"Larkspur Loop\"), and only when the person has more than one place. Callout: \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\".\n6. Caption under the panel: \"This is the whole thing.\" in caption text.strong (it sits on the sunken panel, R10: 9.37:1).\n7. Actions (expanded only): title-case text buttons inside the inset in bodySmallMedium primary.700, separated from the body by a 1px border.default rule (decoration). Print no contrast figure for them (no light-raised row in R10). They are drawn for illustration; real tray actions belong to the system.\n8. Levels table, on the same artboard: four rows, each printed with its name from KEYS.\n   - pickup, briefings, dates, bills: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   - household: iOS Passive / Android LOW, one thread per home.\n   - air at AQI 151 or above, and NOAA warnings: iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH.\n   - air below AQI 151: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   Under the table, print: \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" and \"Android: the air group holds two channels, one HIGH (AQI 151 or above, and NOAA warnings) and one DEFAULT (below 151). Every other group has one channel.\"\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows; the viewer is Maya, HOME A, who also has a saved place, so street labels show). Print each string's character count beside it, and each row's level in words under the row label.\nV1 Unconfirmed pickup. Title \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35). Action \"That's My Day\". iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV2 Confirmed pickup. Title \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\" (32). No action. iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV3 Air, Time Sensitive. Title \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" (22). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH (176 is 151 or above). In V3 S1 and S2 only (not S3), draw the words \"Time Sensitive\" as a caption word inside the inset beside \"now\" (caption text.strong), not as copied system chrome.\nV4 Air, below 151 (the fixture alert; a variant this board adds, Notes 7.5). Title \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" (25). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). iOS Active / Android DEFAULT (the air group's below-151 channel).\nV5 Bill marked paid (the actor is Sam). Title \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" (25). Body \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\" (30). No amount. iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV6 Household roll-up. Title \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" (23). Body \"Larkspur Loop\" (13). One notification that updates in place. iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV7 Date reminder. Title \"Lease notice due in 14 days\" (27). Body \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\" (31). Action \"Done\". iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV8 Hidden-preview placeholders: \"Pickup reminder\" (15) · \"Air quality alert\" (17) · \"Household update\" (16) · \"Date reminder\" (13). Android public versions: \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\" (26) · \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\" (28) · \"Pantopus · Household update\" (27) · \"Pantopus · Date reminder\" (24).\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Collapsed tray at true truncation. On iOS, drawn at 393pt device width (inset 361pt); on Android, at 412dp (inset 380dp). Title on one line, body on one line. None of these strings truncates at real width: draw them whole, and show the shaded remaining room on the ruler. An ellipsis is allowed only where a string actually overflows. V8 S1: four collapsed trays, unlocked with previews hidden: the top row as in item 2, and one text line holding the placeholder. Under each V8 S1 specimen, print the board caption \"Unlocked, previews hidden\".\nS2 Expanded: the full body. V1 and V7 add their action row (\"That's My Day\", \"Done\"). V2–V6 are drawn with the board caption \"No action\" under the inset. V8 S2: \"Not applicable: a hidden preview does not expand until the device is unlocked\".\nS3 Lock screen public version, still the inset illustration, never on a wallpaper. The placeholder follows the variant's group (V1, V2 → \"Pickup reminder\"; V3, V4 → \"Air quality alert\"; V5, V6 → \"Household update\"; V7 → \"Date reminder\").\n  - iOS S3: the top row keeps the icon, \"Pantopus\" and \"now\"; the single text line is the placeholder.\n  - Android S3: the top row keeps the icon and \"now\" only; the single text line reads \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\", so the name appears once.\n  - V8 S3: the four public forms for that grid's platform. Under each V8 S3 specimen, print the board caption \"Locked, public version\".\n  Addresses, names, amounts and \"Time Sensitive\" never appear in S3.\n\nGRIDS\n02-ios-variants-by-states · light: 8 rows × 3 columns, iOS.\n03-android-variants-by-states · light: the same 8 × 3 grid on Android.\n04-ios-variants-by-states · dark: the full 02 grid in dark tokens (R9).\n05-android-variants-by-states · dark: the full 03 grid in dark tokens (R9).\nDark container: the inset is dark raised on a dark base panel. Inset top-row words are #F1F5F9 (R10: 13.35:1 on dark raised). Title and body are dark text primary. Action buttons are #38BDF8 (R10: 6.83:1). The caption \"This is the whole thing.\" is #F1F5F9 on the dark base panel (R10: 16.30:1). Rulers, counts and the V8 captions stay board chrome in dark text.secondary.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (06-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) AX5 iOS, V1 S2 and V3 S2: in the in-app illustration, the title and body wrap fully and never truncate; the caption \"This is the whole thing.\" wraps; the illustration grows taller and never scales down. Names use ios-ax5.\n- (b) 200% Android, V1 S2 and V3 S2: the same. Names use android-200.\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S2 (the light default) and V3 S2 (the most state-heavy cell). Caption: \"Reads without colour: the Time Sensitive marker on V3 reads by its words; levels are labelled in words, never by colour.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The in-app illustration is read as one element: \"Example notification. Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow. Recycling + garbage · city schedule. This is the whole thing.\" (each variant reads its own title and body).\n- No house numbers and no full addresses in any string. Actions are title case.\n- Non-colour encoding: levels are labelled in words on the board.\n- Targets: the illustration is not interactive. Real tray actions belong to the system.\n\nCOPY: all strings are given in ANATOMY, VARIANTS and STATES; use them exactly. Never \"Open Pantopus to…\". No keeper name or voice. No marketing, Founding or referral pushes. No pickup reminder alongside the briefing for the same pickup.\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: Active / Passive / Time Sensitive, as in the levels table. Hidden previews show the placeholder. Provisional authorization is never used for pickup.\n- Android: DEFAULT / LOW / HIGH channels, one per group, except the air group's two (levels table). The public version is \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\".\n- Web: no push on this board.\n- Actions: no tray \"Mark paid\" action on any platform, because it notifies the household and can't show an Undo.\n\nIN CONTEXT (07-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- f4-notification-primer: V2's tray illustration inside the pickup primer sheet (a NotificationAsk sheet, drawn only as far as the crop needs).\n- f4-notification-settings: the \"Air & weather alerts\" group row with V3 as its example and the level spelled out (\"Time Sensitive at AQI 151 or above\").\n- f3-household-notifications: the notification list row that V5 opens: \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" in body text.primary, with \"Today 6:10 PM\" under it in bodySmall text.secondary.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card (where V1 and V2 land), f1-today-air-band (where V3 and V4 land)\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow — not yet confirmed\", draw \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" — because at 30 characters a caveat at the end is the part that gets cut.\n- Instead of \"Bins out tonight. 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\", draw \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\" — because a house number doesn't belong on a lock screen.\n- Instead of \"Sam paid Clark PUD $142.18\", draw \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" — because amounts stay inside the app, and \"marked paid\" is the product's word.\n- Instead of the notification over a phone wallpaper, as a system alert, or with a copied Time Sensitive badge, draw the inset illustration captioned \"This is the whole thing.\" — because an imitation of system UI misleads.\n- Instead of \"Open Pantopus to see today's pickup\", draw the fact itself — because the notification is the whole message.\n- Instead of Time Sensitive for a pickup reminder, draw Active — because pickup is never Time Sensitive.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes)\nA. 7.1 The contract's example strings use \"Lacamas Dr\", \"Maple St\", \"Due Sep 20\" and \"Sun 31 Jan\". This board uses the fixture-aligned strings from research brief section 3 (\"Larkspur Loop\", \"Due Fri 23 Oct\", \"Mon 1 Mar\").\n   7.2 V1: the contract body \"Recycling + garbage · City of Camas schedule. Bins out tonight.\" is 63 characters, over the 40 limit. This board uses \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35).\n   7.3 V6: the contract's \"Sam paid 3 bills\" conflicts with the glossary rule \"marked … paid\". This board uses \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\", with the body \"Larkspur Loop\".\n   7.4 Title case: the contract says push actions are title case (\"That's My Day\"), while research brief section 3 writes \"That's my day\" and the house style requires sentence case everywhere. \"Open Settings\" (6.1) is also title case. This board follows the contract for both. Question: keep title case, or switch to sentence case (\"That's my day\", \"Open settings\")?\n   7.5 V4 is a variant this board adds: the contract lists one air variant. It comes from the contract's \"Time Sensitive only at 151 or above\" and research brief section 3 (air: HIGH / DEFAULT), and covers the fixture's AQI 118 alert, which is below the threshold. Its title \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" is invented. Confirm the added variant and its title.\n   7.6 V1 body: the glossary allows \"Recycling + garbage\" only in 30-character push titles. It is kept in the body to fit 40 characters. Question for the founder.\n   7.7 Levels: the contract has no row for air below AQI 151. This board adds \"air below 151: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT\" (research brief section 3, \"HIGH / DEFAULT\"), so the Android air group has two channels. Confirm.\n   7.8 V5 level: research brief section 3 makes bill_paid Active for members who still see the bill as unpaid and due within 3 days. Clark Public Utilities is due Fri 23 Oct, 4 days after TODAY, so V5 is drawn Passive.\n   7.9 V8 adds a \"Date reminder\" placeholder; the contract lists only three.\n   7.10 The contract says the body carries the source, but the brief's canonical bodies for V2, V5, V6 and V7 carry none. This board draws the brief's bodies. Question: add a source to those bodies?\nB. Maya also has a saved place (The Blairmont rental), so street labels show. V3's AQI 176 reading at 4:00 PM is the contract's example, not the fixture reading. The f3-household-notifications row time \"Today 6:10 PM\" is invented (it is the same day as TODAY, so \"Today\" stands alone without a weekday, per research brief section 6).\nC. The Pantopus app icon, if it isn't published yet (the R15 fallback box).\nD. Invented strings: \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" · \"now\" · \"Time Sensitive\" (as a word inside the illustration) · \"Date reminder\" · \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\" · \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\" · \"Pantopus · Household update\" · \"Pantopus · Date reminder\" · \"Larkspur Loop\" as the V6 body · \"Time Sensitive at AQI 151 or above\" · \"Today 6:10 PM\" · the spoken \"Example notification…\" labels · \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" · the Android air-channel line under the levels table · chrome: \"No action\" · \"Unlocked, previews hidden\" · \"Locked, public version\" · \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\" · the character counts and ruler ticks.\nE. Light only: the levels table (documentation, platform-neutral) and the ios-ax5 and android-200 frames. Review aids, never published: the greyscale copies. Omitted: web push (none in scope). Omitted from the levels table: the brief's Account & security group (sign-in, invitations; Time Sensitive / HIGH), because it is not a PushCopy variant.\nF. Light: 23 iOS cells and 23 Android cells (every cell except V8 S2), with V8's four specimens per cell, plus the four levels rows and the 06 ios-ax5 and android-200 frames (not the greyscale copies). Dark: the same 46 cells.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 7 artboards exist with the exact names above, and Notes carries this component's entries.\n- Four grids each have 8 rows × 3 columns with keys; V8 S2 carries its reason, and V8 S1 and S3 each hold four named specimens with their captions (\"Unlocked, previews hidden\" / \"Locked, public version\").\n- Every title and body has its character count printed, over a character ruler with its labelled 30 or 40 tick.\n- S3 cells show only the icon, \"Pantopus\", \"now\" and a placeholder; on Android the name appears once, in the text line.\n- In the tray illustrations, \"Time Sensitive\" appears only in V3 S1 and S2.\n- No ellipsis appears anywhere except where a string actually overflows in S1.\n- 06 has columns (a), (b) and (c); 07 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy-and-levels, 02-ios-variants-by-states light, 03-android-variants-by-states light, 04-ios-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 05-android-variants-by-states dark, 06-ax5-200-greyscale, 07-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend it). Then stop and wait for the next component prompt.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message, including DONE WHEN."
          },
          {
            "id": "00d-08",
            "component": "ReminderLeadControl",
            "artboards": [
              "00d · ReminderLeadControl · 01-anatomy · light",
              "00d · ReminderLeadControl · 02-variants-by-states · light",
              "00d · ReminderLeadControl · 03-variants-by-states · dark",
              "00d · ReminderLeadControl · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light",
              "00d · ReminderLeadControl · 05-in-context-and-rules · light",
              "00d · Notes"
            ],
            "promptText": "Component 00d-08: ReminderLeadControl. Follow the board rules from the setup message.\n\nPURPOSE (print on 01): Shows every reminder that will actually fire, on a small timeline running back from the date the person must act.\nUsed in (print on 01): x-date-sheet, f10-extraction-confirm\nATTACH: none.\n\nARTBOARDS (5, then finish Notes)\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 01-anatomy · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 02-variants-by-states · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 03-variants-by-states · dark\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 05-in-context-and-rules · light\n00d · Notes (extend and finish it)\n\nKEYS (R7)\nVariants: V1 Date sheet = date-sheet · V2 Extraction confirm = extraction-confirm · V3 Lease = lease-notice.\nStates: S1 Default = default · S2 Lead already passed = lead-passed · S3 Disabled = disabled.\nSpecimens outside the grid, named exactly:\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default-one-day / ios / <theme>\" (light on 02, dark on 03)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default-focused / ios / light\" (01)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / segment / chosen-then-passed / ios / light\" (the inset on 01)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / ios-ax5 / light\" (04)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / android-200 / light\" (04)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / ios-ax2 / light\" (04)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / android-150 / light\" (04)\n  \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / web-1440 / light\" (04)\n\nPASSED-LEAD RULE (stated once here; everything below refers to it)\nTODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026. A lead whose date is before TODAY has passed. A passed lead gets exactly one of two treatments:\n- Passed (never chosen): disabled per R16. Label in text.muted (disabled only), no check, still focusable, read as \"<N> days, unavailable, <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" Its reason is also written in readable text: the passed-lead line, 8pt below the control and above the timeline, in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1; dark #94A3B8, R10: 6.96:1). It names only never-chosen passed leads: \"60 days has passed for this date.\" (V1) or \"60 and 30 days have passed for this date.\" (V2). With no such lead, there is no line. Activating a passed segment shows the explanation line and suggestion instead of selecting it.\n- Chosen-then-passed (the lead was selected, then the date was edited so it has now passed): a primary.50 fill, a 1.5px primary.700 border, NO check, the label in bodySmall 14/20 at weight 400 in text.primary, and the word \"passed\" under the label in caption 12/16 text.primary; both lines fit inside the 44pt segment. Dark: a primary.900 fill, a 1.5px #38BDF8 border, no check, label and word in dark text primary. Read as \"<N> days, selected, passed. <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" It keeps this treatment, with the explanation line and suggestion under the control, until the person picks another lead. This is the one extra treatment R12 allows.\nThe suggestion is always the longest lead still ahead. Nothing is saved until the person taps the suggestion or picks a live segment. The timeline never draws a tick for a passed lead.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy: V1 S1 on iOS 393 with callouts; the example date is the water-heater warranty ending Sat 12 Dec 2026)\nLead dates: 60 days = Tue 13 Oct 2026 (passed) · 30 days = Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 7 days = Sat 5 Dec 2026 · 1 day = Fri 11 Dec 2026.\n1. Label above the control: label 13/18/600 text.primary, \"Remind me\".\n2. Segmented control, 361pt × 44pt (Android 380 × 48dp), four equal segments: \"60 days\", \"30 days\", \"7 days\", \"1 day\". Container: 1px text.secondary outline (R10: 4.83:1), radius md 8, 1px text.secondary dividers. Unselected segment: surface.base, label in bodySmall text.primary. Selected: the R12 selection treatment (fill + check + 600 weight).\n   - \"60 days\" is passed (rule). Callout: \"passed: Tue 13 Oct; focusable, reason read out and written below\".\n   - The passed-lead line, 8pt below the control: \"60 days has passed for this date.\"\n   - Chosen-then-passed: drawn once as a small inset beside the control (rule). Callout: \"chosen before a date edit; no check; 'passed' written\".\n   - Focus: the R12 ring on the unselected live segment \"7 days\", in a second full specimen beside the first (\"default-focused\").\n3. Mini timeline, 361pt wide, not to scale. It starts below the passed-lead line (or below the control when there is no line). Vertical order, top to bottom:\n   a. Event line (16pt), right-aligned to the 361pt edge: KindGlyph (16pt, R15), 4pt, then the event label in caption text.primary (\"Water-heater warranty ends\"). On the same line, left-aligned, the caption \"not to scale\" in caption text.secondary.\n   b. 4pt, then the timeline: a 2px text.secondary horizontal line from x 0 to 361, with three ticks (12pt tall, 2px wide) centred at x 54, 180 and 307. A two-slash break mark sits on the line at x 117. A 1px text.secondary leader line drops from under the event label to the top of the tick at 307.\n   c. 4pt, then under each tick, centred on it: the date in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary (\"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" · \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\" · \"Sat 12 Dec 2026\"), and under that the role in caption 12/16 text.secondary (\"30 days before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\"). Tick dates use the contract's absolute form, with no relative count (Notes 8.6).\n4. Caption, 8pt below the role labels: \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\" in caption text.secondary.\n5. When \"1 day\" is selected, the lead and the day before are the same day, so only two ticks are drawn, at x 54 and 307 (\"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\"), with no break mark (the ticks are one day apart), and the caption reads \"We'll also remind you on the day.\" The passed-lead line still shows. This is the one-day specimen, drawn in its own labelled row, \"V1 · one day selected\", directly below the grid on 02 and 03.\n\nVARIANTS (grid rows)\nV1 Date sheet (x-date-sheet): the anatomy example: 30 days selected, 60 days passed, with the passed-lead line.\nV2 Extraction confirm (f10-extraction-confirm): 7 days is the default. The date is the City of Vancouver water bill, due Wed 28 Oct 2026. Passed: 60 days (Sat 29 Aug 2026) and 30 days (Mon 28 Sep 2026), so the passed-lead line reads \"60 and 30 days have passed for this date.\" 1 day = Tue 27 Oct 2026. Ticks: \"Wed 21 Oct 2026 · 7 days before\", \"Tue 27 Oct 2026 · Day before\", \"Wed 28 Oct 2026 · Day of\". Event label: \"Water bill due\".\nV3 Lease, anchored to the notice deadline (x-date-sheet, lease kind). Event label: \"Notice deadline\" (the Day-of tick carries the date). Never anchor to the lease end. 30 days is selected. No lead has passed, so there is no passed-lead line (60 days = Thu 31 Dec 2026, 7 days = Mon 22 Feb 2027, 1 day = Sun 28 Feb 2027). Ticks: \"Sat 30 Jan 2027 · 30 days before\", \"Sun 28 Feb 2027 · Day before\", \"Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Day of\". Below the role labels, 8pt, two right-aligned lines in caption text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1, readable, never text.muted): \"Wed 31 Mar 2027\", then \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\". The item 4 caption follows 8pt below them.\n\nSTATES (grid columns)\nS1 Default: as drawn per variant, with passed segments disabled and the passed-lead line under the control (V1: 60 days; V2: 60 and 30 days; V3: none, no line).\nS2 Lead already passed (suggested alternative). Print the scenario label above each cell in caption text.secondary. Under the control, top to bottom: the passed-lead line if any, then 8pt, the explanation line and suggestion, then the timeline.\n  - V1. Scenario: \"date first entered as Sat 16 Jan 2027 with 60 days chosen (Tue 17 Nov 2026), then edited to Sat 12 Dec 2026\". \"60 days\" is chosen-then-passed; 30, 7 and 1 days are live and unselected. No lead is passed and never chosen, so there is no passed-lead line. Under the control: a 16pt info glyph (primary.700), then \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" in bodySmall text.primary, then a suggestion button \"Use 30 days instead\" (outlined: surface.base, 1px text.secondary border, bodySmallMedium text.primary, 44pt tall, radius md). The timeline shows the suggested series (the V1 ticks), captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V2. Scenario: \"the extraction first read Sun 22 Nov 2026 and 30 days was chosen (Fri 23 Oct 2026); the date was then corrected to Wed 28 Oct 2026\". \"30 days\" is chosen-then-passed, \"60 days\" is passed, and 7 and 1 days are live and unselected. Passed-lead line: \"60 days has passed for this date.\" Explanation: \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\", then \"Use 7 days instead\". The timeline shows the V2 ticks, captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V3: \"Not applicable: no lead has passed for Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\nS3 Disabled (the date field is empty): the segment container is on surface.sunken; the 1px text.secondary outline and dividers stay; all four labels are text.muted; no selection, no passed-lead line, no timeline, and the item 4 caption is hidden. Segments stay focusable and read \"<N> days, unavailable, Add the date first to set reminders.\" The line \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" sits under the control on the sheet (surface.base), in bodySmall text.secondary (R10: 4.83:1). Applies to all three variants.\n\nGRIDS\n02-variants-by-states · light: 3 rows × 3 columns on iOS, then, in its own row directly below the grid, labelled \"V1 · one day selected\", the one-day specimen. The control sits on a surface.base sheet.\n03-variants-by-states · dark: the same full grid and one-day row in dark tokens (R9). The control sits in a dark base sheet. Selected segment: the R12 dark selection; chosen-then-passed: its dark form. Container outline, dividers, ticks and leader lines are #94A3B8 (R10: 6.96:1). Passed labels are #64748B (R10: 3.75:1 on dark base). The info glyph is #38BDF8. In S3, the segment container is dark raised (dark sunken would vanish on the dark base sheet), so its #64748B labels are 3.07:1 (R10, dark raised); the reason line stays on the dark base sheet in #94A3B8.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (04-ax5-200-greyscale · light, per R17)\n- (a) iOS AX5, V1 S1: the segments become four selectable rows, each at least 44pt tall. The selected row has the R12 selection treatment (primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, 16pt check glyph, 600-weight label). Unselected rows have no glyph, and there are no circles. Line one is the role and line two is the date. For a passed row, only line one is text.muted; line two carries the date and the word \"passed\" in text.secondary. The rows read:\n  \"60 days before\" (text.muted) / \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" (text.secondary) · \"30 days before\" / \"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" (selected) · \"7 days before\" / \"Sat 5 Dec 2026\" · \"1 day before\" / \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\".\n  The timeline becomes a vertical list of three rows: \"Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 30 days before\", \"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\", preceded by the event line. Name: \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / ios-ax5 / light\".\n- (b) Android 200%, V1 S1: the same selectable rows at 48dp. Name: \"ReminderLeadControl / date-sheet / default / android-200 / light\".\n- (c) Greyscale of V1 S1 and V1 S2. Caption: \"Reads without colour: the selected segment has its check and weight; a passed lead has its lighter label, no check, the passed-lead line, and the word 'passed' in the AX rows; the chosen-then-passed segment has the word 'passed' and no check; S2 has its explanation line.\"\n- Extra row below, V1 S1 each: iOS AX2 (bodySmall 14 → about 28pt, caption 12 → about 26pt; a 2×2 grid of 44pt cells; ios-ax2) · Android 150% (bodySmall 14 → about 22sp, caption 12 → 18sp; a 2×2 grid of 48dp cells; android-150) · a web-1440 crop inside the date sheet's 480px side panel (44px segments; web-1440). Use the full names from KEYS.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Remind me, 30 days before, selected, 2 of 4.\" The segment's accessibility label intentionally expands \"30 days\" to \"30 days before\". Passed and chosen-then-passed segments read as the rule says; the passed-lead line is plain text read in order after the control. The timeline is one element with a summary: V1 \"Reminders on Thu 12 Nov, Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec.\" · V1 one day \"Reminders on Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec.\" · V2 \"Reminders on Wed 21 Oct, Tue 27 Oct and Wed 28 Oct.\" · V3 \"Reminders on Sat 30 Jan, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar.\" The same facts appear as a list at AX sizes. The S2 explanation line is announced politely when it appears.\n- Non-colour encoding: selection is a text label plus a fill change plus a check, never colour alone.\n- Targets: segments (disabled ones included) are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. The suggestion button is 44pt. Ticks are not targets.\n\nCOPY: all strings are given in the rule, ANATOMY, VARIANTS, STATES and AX rows; use them exactly. Dates always show the weekday.\n\nPLATFORMS: the same on all platforms apart from target sizes and the large-text layouts above. On web-1440, the control sits in the date sheet's 480px side panel (04 extra row).\n\nIN CONTEXT (05-in-context-and-rules · light, per R17)\n- x-date-sheet: the Date sheet for \"Water-heater warranty\", with V1 below the date field.\n- x-date-sheet (lease): the Date sheet for the lease, with V3.\n- f10-extraction-confirm: \"Confirm what we read\" for the water bill, with V2.\nAlso consumed by: none beyond these two surfaces.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a single \"Remind me 30 days before\" row, draw all three reminders with their real dates — because three will fire, and the person should see each one.\n- Instead of anchoring the lease reminder to Wed 31 Mar 2027, anchor it to the notice deadline Mon 1 Mar 2027 — because the notice is what the person must act on.\n- Instead of silently accepting, hiding or greying a passed lead, apply the PASSED-LEAD RULE, with its written passed-lead line — because a reminder dated in the past never fires, and silent dead controls leave people guessing.\n- Instead of keeping the check on a lead that passed after a date edit, draw the chosen-then-passed segment — because a check says a reminder will fire.\n- Instead of radio circles at large text, draw selectable rows with a check — because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance.\n- Instead of showing selection by colour alone, draw fill + check + weight — because colour alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind people.\n- Instead of a timeline drawn to scale, draw fixed tick positions with a \"not to scale\" break — because a to-scale 60-day line squashes the last two ticks together.\n\nNOTES (extend 00d · Notes, then finish it)\nA. 8.1 V3: the fixture's lease reminder is Mon 15 Feb 2027 (14 days before the notice deadline; PushCopy V7 says \"due in 14 days\"), but the contract's leads are 60 / 30 / 7 / 1. This board draws 30 days (Sat 30 Jan 2027). Question: add a 14-day option, or change the fixture?\n   8.2 Passed leads: the contract gives no rule. The PASSED-LEAD RULE, including the written passed-lead line, is this board's invention (following OfflineNotice's \"Disabled controls stay focusable\" and R16). Confirm.\n   8.3 Large text: the contract says \"radio rows\". This board draws selectable rows with a check and no circles, because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance only.\n   8.4 Selection: segments use the R12 treatment, the same as NotificationAsk chips.\n   8.5 S3 dark: the disabled container uses dark raised, because dark sunken equals the dark base sheet.\n   8.6 Tick dates follow the contract's absolute form (\"Thu 12 Nov 2026\") and drop the house-style relative count (\"in 24 days\"), because the timeline already shows the relation. Confirm.\n   8.7 The one-day specimen sits in its own row below each grid so the grid stays at 1x within R2's 1600px width.\nB. The S2 starting dates (Sat 16 Jan 2027 for the warranty; the misread Sun 22 Nov 2026 for the water bill) are invented so the chosen leads were still ahead before the edit. Tick x-positions (54, 180, 307) are layout choices. The AX2 and Android 150% type sizes are approximate.\nC. KindGlyph, if drawn as a fallback box.\nD. Invented strings: \"Remind me\" · \"60 days before\" · \"30 days before\" · \"7 days before\" · \"1 day before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\" · \"passed\" · \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"Water bill due\" · \"Notice deadline\" (as an event label) · \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\" · \"60 days has passed for this date.\" · \"60 and 30 days have passed for this date.\" · \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" · \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\" · \"Use 30 days instead\" · \"Use 7 days instead\" · \"Suggested\" · \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" · \"We'll also remind you on the day.\" · the passed and chosen-then-passed spoken labels · the V1 one-day, V2 and V3 timeline summaries · chrome: \"not to scale\" · \"V1 · one day selected\" · the two S2 scenario labels · the two segment callouts.\nE. Light only: the default-focused and chosen-then-passed insets on 01 (their dark forms are defined in R9, R12 and the rule, and appear in the dark grid), and the 04 ios-ax5, android-200, ios-ax2, android-150 and web-1440 frames. Review aids, never published: the greyscale copies. Omitted: a 14-day lead (Notes 8.1).\nF. Light: 8 grid cells (V3 S2 is Not applicable), the one-day specimen, the two 01 insets, and the 04 ios-ax5, android-200, ios-ax2, android-150 and web-1440 frames (not the greyscale copies). Dark: the same 8 grid cells and the one-day specimen.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The 5 artboards exist with the exact names above, and 00d · Notes is complete for all eight components.\n- Both grids have 3 × 3 cells with keys, plus the one-day specimen in its labelled row directly below the grid (no break mark); V3 S2 carries its reason.\n- S1 shows the passed-lead line (V1 and V2); S3 keeps the outline and dividers and hides the item 4 caption.\n- The V1 and V2 S2 cells are real specimens with scenario labels, explanation lines, suggestion buttons and \"Suggested\" timelines.\n- Nothing on the timeline overflows 361pt; the event label sits on its own line above the ticks.\n- No radio circles anywhere, and every specimen name is written in full.\n- Every segment (disabled ones included) and the suggestion button show their dashed hit area.\n- 04 has columns (a), (b) and (c) and the extra row; 05 has three labelled crops, the \"Also consumed by\" line and all five panels.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn)\nBatch 1 (this turn): 01-anatomy, 02-variants-by-states light, 03-variants-by-states dark. Then stop and wait for \"continue\".\nBatch 2: 04-ax5-200-greyscale, 05-in-context-and-rules, 00d · Notes (extend and finish it). Before finishing Notes, check that Notes A–F cover all eight components in order, 0.1 first, and that F lists every printed name. Then stop: the board is complete.\nBefore each batch, re-read the board rules R1–R19 and this whole message, including DONE WHEN."
          }
        ],
        "clean": false
      }
    ]
